window.FWN_HERO_SUMMONING_PEACE_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_HERO_SUMMONING_PEACE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2301,"title":"Chapter 2301: Miyama Kaito’s Birthday Celebration Party Continues 45","paragraphs":["According to Alice, this was supposed to be the highest-difficulty challenge, reading Shiro-san's expressions, but honestly, I'm pretty good at picking up on subtle changes in her expressions. In fact, just a glance was enough for me to figure out exactly what kind of expression each of the four choices represented.","\"Alright. Time’s up for answering...... The atmosphere among the Gods sure is intense. It’s like a verdict is about to be passed......\"","\"Well, in truth, the verdict is about to be passed. Judging from their almost desperate expression, they probably didn’t know the answer and ended up relying on luck in the end...... Just imagining myself in their position gives me chills.\"","\"I see. So it really was a brutal question...... but someone still managed to answer correctly...... and at an overwhelming speed, at that. Actually, Kaito-san was the fastest to answer and got it right, so let’s have him reveal the answer.\"","\"Eh? Kai-chan, you can tell?\"","Just as I was thinking the conversation was going off in a strange direction, Ein-san quietly handed me a Loudspeaker Magic Tool. I accepted it and began to speak.","\"Errr, well, since we’re at it, I’ll go through them one by one...... or rather, all four expressions this time were actually variations of a smile.\"","\"They were!?\"","\"Yes. First, number 1. The corners of the mouth are raised the most out of the four, but there’s a slight tilt to the head, so this is a doya...... errr, a triumphant smile.\"","There were probably a fair number of people who got tripped up by expression #1. In terms of how high the mouth corners are raised, it’s the most prominent. But the slight change in the angle of the face gives it away, this is a doya.","Just to add a side note, this smug look isn’t the one she makes when she’s all hyped up with the 3D doyas. It’s more the face she makes when she’s teasing Kuro or someone. When she’s in the mood for flashy effects like 3D letters, her face tilts even more.","\"Now, expression #2. The mouth corners are just slightly upturned, but the outer corners of the eyes droop a bit, especially more on the right side than the left. This is the face she makes when she’s giving a wry smile, like when she’s slightly exasperated.\"","This is the kind of face she shows when talking about things like Kuro’s baby castella obsession or some topic she clearly doesn’t care about. Technically, her mouth is shaped almost the same as when she’s genuinely smiling. But the way her eyes move, especially the eye corners, gives it away. So it’s actually quite identifiable.","\"Expression #3 is the one most easily mistaken for a genuine smile. It’s nearly identical, but when the right side of the mouth is raised just slightly more than the left, that’s the face she makes when she finds something amusing.\"","She sometimes wears this expression when we’re watching plays or something like that. All things considered, it’s actually kind of rare. If her mood goes up just a bit more, she shifts into what you'd call a proper smile. So this one falls into a narrow zone between a smile and laughter, making it uncommon.","To describe it, I’d say this is the face she makes when she’s feeling mildly entertained by something not directly related to me. If it is something related to me, she tends to go straight into a full-on smile pretty easily.","\"And so, the correct answer, the true gentle smile, is expression #4. The mouth corners are evenly raised on both sides, and the eyes are just slightly narrowed. That’s the giveaway.\"","\"I- I see...... That was actually really informative. Thanks for the detailed explanation and tips for telling them apart! I mean, honestly, I still can’t really see the micro-angle differences even after all that, but I’ll do my best to learn. You really are amazing, Kai-chan.\"","\"That was a great answer. I mean, seriously, the changes are only a matter of millimeters, and yet you caught them al...l... Anyhow, the correct answer is #4. So...... Shallow Vernal-sama? You look like you have a comment?\"","[I quite like that confident air you carry, as if declaring that no one knows me better than you. You may go ahead and proclaim \"Shiro-san is mine.\", you know? I shall permit it.]","\"If you two want to flirt, do it later. Moving on.\"","Shiro-san’s declaration, with a nod that radiated deep satisfaction, was immediately and thoroughly dismissed by Alice, who quickly moved on to the next question.","As the conversation moved on to the next question, Olivia remained in the audience, gazing at Kaito with sparkling, deeply moved eyes.","(What a magnificent and noble soul...... For me to be unable to read even the expressions of Shallow Vernal-sama, I’m overwhelmed by my own inadequacy. I feel like burying my face in my hands. But how merciful and wonderful Miyama Kaito-sama is...... Not only does he possess the insight to perfectly understand Shallow Vernal-sama’s heart, but the way he guides the ignorant masses, myself included, with his words...... I can’t hold back my tears. Shouldn’t his words just now be recorded in the holy scriptures?)","Olivia, unfortunately, hadn’t been able to distinguish Shallow Vernal’s expression and had made a random guess, which turned out to be wrong, plunging her into self-loathing. But the fact that Kaito not only gave a near-perfect answer, but also shared tips on how to read Shallow Vernal’s expressions, moved her as though she had received divine revelation.","Just as she was about to shift into a posture of prayer, tears in her eyes as if gazing upon a great being, her movement came to a sudden halt at the sound of a nearby voice.","\"Milady, that was amazing. You got it right.\"","\"It was just luck.\"","Turning her gaze, she saw Lilia, Lunamaria, and Sieglinde. Lunamaria was praising Lilia, who had answered the question correctly, and Lilia responded with a wry smile.","(What? Lilia Albert got that impossible question right......? Was it just a lucky one-in-four guess? No, Lilia Albert is someone who has received the True Blessing of God of Time and Space Chronois and even Shallow Vernal-sama has acknowledged her. In that case, perhaps she was able to discern the expression just like Miyama Kaito-sama...... It seems my evaluation of her must be revised upward.)","Of course, Lilia had not read Shallow Vernal’s expression at all. She had merely guessed at random and happened to get it right. Olivia’s belief that Lilia had perceived the expression was a complete misunderstanding.","(......Should Godism Church strengthen its relationship with Lilia Albert? Favoring a specific nation may be problematic, but if it's only toward Lilia Albert as an individual...... Even at this party, she was treated separately from the three rulers of the Human Realm, given the status of a representative of Humans...... Yes. Going forward, Godism Church should work to deepen its ties with Lilia Albert.)","Once again, this was a total misunderstanding. But tragically, since Olivia was only thinking all of this to herself, there was no way for Lilia to notice it, quietly sealing her fate to yet another future case of stomachache.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [To be able to distinguish expressions that perfectly, guess I have to say, as expected of him...... And meanwhile, completely unrelated to that, the strongest Stomachache Warrior has just sealed her fate for future stomachache......]"]},{"number":2302,"title":"Chapter 2302: Miyama Kaito’s Birthday Celebration Party Continues 46","paragraphs":["The quiz progressed, and we had just finished the 20th question, leaving only five more to go. Up to this point, with a bit of luck on my side, I had managed to keep a perfect score. If things continued like this, I might even have a shot at taking the top spot.","However, I couldn't afford to let my guard down just yet. That's because out of the remaining five questions, two were still marked as high difficulty. I'd only managed to get through Shiro-san's question because it happened to be in a category I was good at...... Whether or not I could answer these difficult ones would likely be the key.","“Now then, we're down to the last five questions...... and here's some information for you all...... Currently, there are 10 participants who have answered 18 or more questions correctly, so the race for the top 10 seems to be narrowing down. Well, unless all 10 of them completely miss the rest, there's still a chance for an upset.”","“Huh? You're not saying perfect score, but 18 or more?”","“I left it a bit vague on purpose, makes it more fun trying to guess who's managed a perfect score or not.”","Only ten people have answered 18 or more...... That's more narrow than I thought. Indeed, this quiz doesn't just demand in-depth knowledge, but rather a broad and shallow kind of knowledge across many topics, which makes it quite tricky.","I get the feeling that a lot of people were probably filtered out by the Otherworld-related questions.","“Let's see, next up is...... oh, high-difficulty, Question 3.”","“Ahh, here it comes. This is one of the two remaining high-difficulty questions that are likely to greatly affect the standings. For those who've gotten 18 or more correct, whether you answer this one correctly or not might be what determines if you stay at the top, so give it your all.”","It's definitely an important question, but these high-difficulty ones really are tough. What kind of question will it be this time......?","“Now then, here is the question. The Dragon King, Magnawell-san, is known as the largest creature in the world, with a total length of around 30,000 meters...... So, what is Magnawell-san's approximate weight? 1. Around 150 billion tons, 2. Around 200 billion tons, 3. Around 250 billion tons, 4. Around 300 billion tons ...... Just as before, you have three minutes to answer.”","“That's insane!? Dragon King's weight, even he himself probably wouldn't know about it......”","“Indeed, he doesn't. I took the measurements myself when making this question, and for fairness, I haven't even told Magnawell-san.”","This is absurdly hard. I mean, none of the choices seem impossible, they're all incredibly heavy, and the question is just about guessing the correct ballpark figure...... Is this really going to come down to blind guessing?","Hmmm...... wait. Hold on. I think...... a while ago, when Alice was telling me about Magnawell-san's total length, she said something...... Errr......","————-30,000 meters is 30 kilometers...... at that size, even walking must be a challenge.","————-Well, Magnawell-san takes care not to stress the ground too much by floating a little. His exact weight hasn't been precisely measured, but it's estimated to be around 200 billion tons. Without counteracting techniques, he'd be cracking the earth everywhere he went.","————-That scale is just ridiculous.","I remembered! That's right, Alice said it was around 200 billion tons...... Of course, that wasn't an exact measurement at the time, but I seriously doubt someone like Alice would be off by as much as 50 billion tons, even if it was an estimate. In that case...... could the correct answer be option 2: around 200 billion tons?","“......And the correct answer is: 2, around 200 billion tons. It might sound insanely heavy, but considering Magnawell-san's size, it wouldn't be strange for him to weigh several trillion tons. However, high-ranking Dragons are mostly made up of special cells called dragon cells, which are composed of high-density magic power, so despite their size, they're actually much lighter than you'd expect. That's why even those ridiculously massive Colossal Dragons can still fly with their wings.”","Now that she mention it, 200 billion tons does sound like a crazy number, but given Magnawell-san's sheer size, that might actually be on the lighter side.","Apparently, Magnawell-san used to be able to fly with wings too, so I guess that technically makes him a Flying Dragon. Alice's explanation definitely makes sense.","Anyway, that makes 21 correct answers for me...... Depending on what the next high-difficulty question is, there might actually be a chance I can get a perfect score.","<Afterword>","? ? ? : [By the way, aside from Kaito-san, there's one other person who has gotten every question right so far. It might be fun to guess who that is. Ah, just to clarify, those with omniscience like Makina aren't participating, and that perfect scorer didn't just get lucky, they've properly answered everything.]","Serious-senpai : [You're not gonna say it's Alice just as a punchline, right?]","? ? ? : [Alice-chan isn't participating either. That's all the hints you get. But if they've answered all the high-difficulty questions correctly up to this point, that means this person must be well-versed about the Kruels (or something related to magic crystal mining), familiar with the latest Quoits Elite rankings, able to distinguish Shallow Vernal-sama's facial expressions, and have a rough idea of how much Magnawell-san weighs.]"]},{"number":2303,"title":"Chapter 2303: Miyama Kaito’s Birthday Celebration Party Continues 47","paragraphs":["The quiz competition had reached question 23, with only two questions remaining. Aside from the high-difficulty ones, the questions weren’t particularly extreme, and somehow, relying on bits and pieces of conversations and experiences from various people, I had managed to answer correctly so far.","Since it’s a four-choice format, even if you don’t remember the official name exactly, as long as it sounds familiar, you can narrow it down, and even make educated guesses. You could say the format itself has helped a lot.","\"Now then, only two questions remain. Let’s give a progress update, currently, there are only two participants who have answered every question correctly so far.\"","\"Whoa, a perfect score? That’s impressive. A pretty wide range of knowledge is required for that, and there were a lot of questions about the Otherworld that I’d never even heard of before. The high-difficulty ones were insanely tough too.\"","\"Indeed. And there’s a reason I’m mentioning this now. The person in second place currently has 20 correct answers...... which means the competition for the top spot is between just two people. I’ll reveal who they are at the end, but the ones with perfect scores should already know it’s them, so do give it your all for the last two questions.\"","Wow, it’s a head-to-head fight for the top spot...... Also, whoever has answered everything correctly so far is seriously amazing. The high-difficulty questions were, of course, extremely tough, but for people from Trinia, the Otherworld-related questions must’ve been just as difficult.","Of course, it could be an Otherworlder like me who’s gotten a perfect score. But even in that case, they’ve correctly answered tricky questions like identifying Shiro-san’s expressions, names of the Kruels, and the Quoits Elite ranking...... That’s still seriously impressive.","\"Alright, next up is...... oh! High-Difficulty Question 4. It’s the last of the high-difficulty questions.\"","\"Which means the final question will automatically be Otherworld Question 1. Now, will one of the perfect scorers drop out here......? High-Difficulty Question 4: In the Otherworld, there’s a type of pottery used at a Zen Buddhist temple on Tianmu Mountain in a country called China. These tea bowls are called “Tenmoku chawan”. Among them, there’s a class considered to be the finest, and all existing examples are designated as national treasures. What are these called? 1. Yohen Tenmoku Chawan, 2. Yuteki Tenmoku Chawan, 3. Konoha Tenmoku Chawan, Haikatsugi Tenmoku Chawan...... As usual, you have three minutes to answer.\"","\"No, this is so hard! Can the Otherworlder kids even answer something like this?\"","\"If they have any knowledge of pottery, it wouldn’t be surprising if they know.\"","Whoa, I didn’t expect a question that’s so favorable to me to show up here. I actually remember this one because it came up when we brought some pottery made by Nebula to Shigenobu-san’s place. Aoi-chan explained it to me at the time.","The correct answer is 1: Yohen Tenmoku Chawan. However, isn’t this question way too difficult for someone from Trinia......? I mean, I didn’t even know it until Aoi-chan told me...... Well, the previous four high-difficulty questions were all related to Trinia...... Wait a minute, the high-difficulty questions in general...... There was one about the Kruels from the Human Realm, one about Shiro-san’s expressions from the God Realm, one about Magnawell-san’s weight from the Demon Realm, and now this one from the Otherworld...... RINGTOSS is kind of its own category, but it seems the quiz topics are structured in the same way as the question categories.","\"......Alright, the answers are in, and both of the perfect scorers answered instantly without hesitation, and they got it right. Looks like both of them still have a shot at a perfect score.\"","\"Eh? That’s amazing......\"","That other perfect scorer is really something...... Could it be Aoi-chan or Shigenobu-san? If so, it wouldn’t be surprising for them to answer that question instantly.","\"Now then, the final question is from the \"Otherworld\" category...... Ahhh, of all things, this question had to be the last one huh......\"","\"Is it difficult?\"","\"Difficult...... well, not exactly. Hmmm...... anyway, let’s go. Here is the final question: In the home country of the past Hero Actors, including Kaito-san, what is most commonly consumed as a staple food? 1. Bread, 2. Rice, 3. Noodles, 4. Baby Castellas...... You have three minutes to answer.\"","\"......Eh? Isn’t this easy? Even I know the answer to this one.\"","It really is an incredibly simple question, the answer is 2, rice. The question specifies it’s about the home country we come from, so rice is definitely the correct choice.","In fact, it’s widely known that Hero Actors prefer rice, and that’s why, even if only in small quantities, rice is cultivated in various countries. It wouldn’t be strange if everyone got this one right.","\"......Alright, time’s up. And look at that, exactly what I expected. Who the heck answers faster than anyone else and gets it completely wrong...... especially when you had a perfect score up to this point, Kuro-san?\"","[......Well, you know, maybe not right now, but in the future it could become a staple food. Baby castellas hold limitless potential, after all......]","\"This isn’t about potential.\"","Wait...... the other perfect scorer was Kuro?! And thanks to Alice’s exasperated tone, it’s painfully clear that Kuro chose that answer.","To knowingly pick the wrong answer faster than anyone else, as to be expected of the Baby Castella Demon. And somehow, I get the feeling she looks oddly satisfied about being wrong, like she’s at peace with it.","<Afterword>","? ? ? : [There you have it. And so, while many of you guessed correctly, the other person with a perfect score was Kuro-san. She’s the honorary president of the world’s greatest magic tool trading company, naturally well-versed in things like magic crystals and the Kruels, and since she herself appears in the Quoits Elite Rankings, she checks the biannual updates. While she’s not quite on Kaito-san’s level, she’s been able to somewhat interpret Shallow Vernal-sama’s expressions for a while now, which is why she's capable of saying things like \"that smug look is really annoying\". She also has a rough grasp of her family member Magnawell-san’s approximate weight.]"]},{"number":2304,"title":"Chapter 2304: Miyama Kaito’s Birthday Celebration Party Continues 48","paragraphs":["Kuro, who had answered all the questions correctly up until the last one, ended up getting that final question wrong, going all in on the baby castella answer, and as a result, I was the only one who answered every question correctly. In other words, that makes me the winner of this quiz competition.","\"Well then, let’s move on to the results announcement. First place, with a perfect score of 25 out of 25, goes to...... today’s star, Kaito-san!\"","\"Ooooh! So Kai-chan was the one who got them all right! That’s amazing!\"","\"Well, I’ll admit, as the question writer, I may have made the questions slightly favorable toward Kaito-san, but as you can all see from the lineup of participants, Kaito-san has a wide social network, so he’s heard stories from people in all sorts of fields. That means he has a broad range of general knowledge, which makes him really strong in a quiz like this that tests across many topics.\"","\"Ahh, now that you mention it, since he’s an Otherworlder, he knows a lot about that too, and compared to Humans and Demons, he’s also got a ton of knowledge about the God Realm. And he’s always going around to different places and events, so his knowledge is really broad.\"","\"Exactly. While he did have a favorable foundation, I still made sure the harder questions were difficult, so to get every single one right is truly impressive.\"","It’s true that I’ve had interactions with all three realms to some extent, and I do know quite a bit about Otherworld info, which definitely gave me an advantage. Some of the questions were even about my own home......","\"Now then, since we have the opportunity, let’s hear a few words from Kaito-san. How was the whole event for you?\"","As Alice said that, Ein-san held out the Loudspeaker Magic Tool to me, just like when I explained Shiro-san’s question earlier.","\"......Let’s see. Honestly, the high-difficulty ones were really tough, and there were times I got lucky. There were moments where I had to desperately recall things I’d only vaguely heard about, or try to eliminate answers based on what I did know. In the end, I really enjoyed the quiz, and I’m happy I was able to get every question right.\"","\"Thank you very much. As the first-place winner, Kaito-san will receive this commemorative trophy and a bonus prize!\"","\"Kai-chan! It’s me! Congratulations~~!\"","As Alice explained, the monitor displayed the commemorative trophy: it was a design of the cat mascot costume she often wears, wearing a silk hat and giving a thumbs-up...... Couldn’t they have done something a little better with the design......? Well, either way, I’m happy, so I’ll go ahead and display it in my room.","\"Next, in second place, with 24 out of 25 questions correct, is the Underworld King herself, Kuro-san! Honestly, Kuro-san dabbles in a wide range of things, and her knowledge runs deep, so it’s no surprise she's good at this kind of quiz.\"","\"But Kurorin, didn’t you answer the last high-difficulty question without hesitation? How did you know that one~~?\"","\"Yeah, the Hero Actor from 29 terms ago had parents who were potters of what Otherworlders call bizenyaki, and he himself liked pottery and studied a lot about it. He told me about all kinds of things, including yohen tenmoku. You know, I’ve talked to most of the past Hero Actors to some extent.\"","\"Ah, I see. That’s why you’re so strong with questions related to the Otherworld too.\"","Come to think of it, just like with Kaori-san and Akane-san, it seems that Kuro has spoken with most of the previous Hero Actors, so it’s fair to call her an expert on Otherworld topics.","Sometimes she misremembers things in weird ways, but among the people living in Trinia, she’s probably head and shoulders above the rest in terms of knowledge about the Otherworld. When you look at it that way, her good performance in this quiz tournament might have been inevitable.","\"Now then, let’s hear a comment from Kuro-san as well...... How was it?\"","\"It was fun. A lot of the questions were really interesting, and the way the quiz helped broaden your knowledge while you enjoyed yourself, very fitting of Shalltear. But that trap in the final question was just mean.\"","\"Just so we're clear, Kuro-san was the only one who would get that last question wrong, okay? You ran full speed into a clearly marked landmine, okay?\"","\"The moment I saw \"baby castella\" as an option, I hit the buzzer before I could even think. I don’t regret it. Even if I were asked the same question again and again, I would still choose baby castella!\"","\"Okay...... shall we move on now?\"","\"You could at least show a little more interest......\"","\"No thanks. Do you know how many times I’ve had to listen to your ridiculous baby castella obsession? When it comes to anything baby castella-related, treating you roughly is the right approach.\"","When it comes to baby castella, Alice is seriously dependable, she says exactly what I want to say, and it feels so satisfying.","Well, Kuro and Alice get along well, so I’m sure there’s a bit of playful banter in there too......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [All the performances are over, so I guess Kaito’s birthday party is finally wrapping up? This time, we probably won’t have any stomachache-inducing drama like we did with Lilia last time...... though someone’s still probably going to get their gut punched...... no, more like get smacked by a berserk gorilla first......]"]},{"number":2305,"title":"Chapter 2305: Miyama Kaito’s Birthday Celebration Party Continues 49","paragraphs":["I got all the questions right, while Kuro got 24 out of 25, missing just one...... That much was already clear by the final question, so what I’m really interested in now is the ranking from this point on.","\"Well then, starting from third place, since the comments will get long, we’ll just add brief explanations as I go. Third place...... there’s a tie, so I’ll announce them together. With 22 correct answers out of 25: Tre-san and Eris-san!\"","\"Oh~~ 22 correct answers is pretty amazing!\"","\"Indeed. Eris-san used her broad knowledge well, answering the Otherworld-related and high-difficulty questions with a lot of consistency. She seemed to have a hard time distinguishing between Shallow Vernal-sama’s expressions, but she got every question right that was within the range of what a marquis’ daughter could study and learn about.\"","Eris-san getting 22 right is something I can understand. This quiz did require broad knowledge, but not necessarily super in-depth knowledge, so it wasn’t just a matter of having lived a long time. It felt more like the kind of challenge where having a wide range of knowledge across various fields was key, and Eris-san seems quite strong in that area.","What was more surprising was Tre-san. True, Tre-san is clever in her own way, and she once mentioned that she has a habit of getting interested in many things, trying them out, and quickly getting bored, so she might’ve accumulated a wide breadth of knowledge that way.","Still, I really can’t help getting this ditzy vibe from her. It might be rude, but it really did feel unexpected.","\"As for Tre-san, she basically lucked her way into third place. No, well, about half of her answers were ones she genuinely knew, but for around 10 of them, she just guessed randomly and happened to get them right. She even guessed Shallow Vernal’s expressions correctly by pure chance.\"","\"Well, luck’s a form of skill too, right~~\"","So apparently Tre-san made it to third place thanks to her sharp instincts, lucky guesses, basically. Honestly, she does seem like the type to excel in things that rely on intuition or chance...... she gives off a strong “good luck” vibe.","Well, like Fate-san said, luck is part of ability too. And half her answers were correct through her own merit, so I’d say that’s impressive enough.","\"Next, we have a three-way tie for fourth place. With 21 correct answers out of 25: Isis-san, Magnawell-san, and Zwei-san.\"","\"That makes sense, they all seem like they’d be knowledgeable across a wide range of fields.\"","Just as Fate-san said, the people announced in fourth place gave off a smart and well-read impression.","Isis-san has read an incredible number of books, so she has knowledge in a wide range of fields. Magnawell-san also knows a lot of things, and Zwei-san gives off the vibe of an intellectual as well, so you could say it's a convincing lineup.","\"First, Isis-san, her hobby is reading, so she has a broad base of knowledge, but due to her personal circumstances, she hasn’t interacted much with Otherworlders, so she missed a few of the Otherworld-related questions. Magnawell-san, as expected, has great general knowledge, but before he got his clone body, he couldn’t travel around much, so he missed some geography-related questions about the Human Realm and God Realm. Zwei-san was steady overall, but seemed to struggle a bit with God Realm topics. That said, all three got 21 questions right, so these are just minor differences, really.\"","It’s true that, unlike Kuro, Isis-san probably hadn’t had much interaction with Otherworlders, so when it came to those topics, she might’ve had to rely on secondhand knowledge.","As for Magnawell-san, that makes sense too. Given his enormous size, his movement would’ve been restricted, and as he mentioned before, after gaining a clone body, even familiar places looked completely different. Originally, with his size, he would’ve only ever seen things from a towering, top-down perspective, so I can imagine he might’ve struggled on questions like identifying tourist landmarks in the Human Realm.","Zwei-san might simply not have had many chances to visit God Realm. She seems busy managing their territory, and it doesn’t look like she has any acquaintances among the Gods, so that’s understandable to some extent.","Still, looking at it overall, the people with high scores mostly make sense, they’re the types you’d expect. Well, there were some like Ein-san who didn’t participate, but if they had, they likely would’ve placed near the top too.","\"Now then, we’ll conclude the ranking announcements at 5th place. Honestly, there are too many ties beyond this point, so it would just go on forever. So, tied for 5th place, with 20 correct answers out of 25, we have: Megiddo-san, Lillywood-san, Lilia-san, Blossom-san, Fafnir-san, Chronois-san, Life-san, Gaia-san, Akane-san, Aoi-san, Fors-san, and Chris-san.\"","\"That’s a lot of people......\"","\"Well, the average number of correct answers was around 15 to 18, so the people in 5th place did quite well overall. Also, everyone from 1st to 5th place will receive trophies. They’re made of platinum, gold, silver, bronze, and iron, respectively, kind of like the hard currency. And with that, the quiz tournament is officially over. Everyone, thank you for participating!\"","And so, the quiz tournament, which turned out to be quite a hit, came to an end. My birthday party, which had grown into a fairly large event, was also finally drawing to a close.","<Afterword>","? ? ? : [So we pace things here, wrap it up at 50, then throw in a bonus round of gut-punching for the Stomachache Warriors, something like that, yeah?]","Serious-senpai : [Can you not treat hitting their stomachs like some side activity......]"]},{"number":2306,"title":"Chapter 2306: Miyama Kaito’s Birthday Celebration Party Continues 50","paragraphs":["With the end of the quiz tournament, all the side events came to a close, and a sense that the long birthday party was finally wrapping up began to settle in.","\"Well then, now that the timing feels right, and it’s a good stopping point, we’ll be ending the party here...... but before that, just like last time, I’d like to take a group photo.\"","\"Well, last time it was a drawing, though~~\"","\"This time, we have the recorder magic tool, so we can take an actual photo. For those who didn’t attend last time, we’ll all line up and capture the moment, that’s basically the idea.\"","\"But, Shall-tan, with this many people in the photo, won’t each person end up looking really tiny?\"","\"Yeah, well, last time that's also the case last time with Magnawell-san being in the photo, so we had to pull the camera way back for the composition...... but don’t worry, I’ve already considered that.\"","It was true that compared to last time, there were a lot more participants this time, nearly 500 people. That meant the photo would have to be taken from quite a distance, and individual faces likely wouldn’t be very clear.","Still, as a memento, even a distant group photo would be totally fine...... or so I thought, but it seemed Alice had a plan to solve that issue.","\"So with that in mind, Makina, make it so the photo can be zoomed in or out nicely with a finger swipe or something.\"","[.......That’s so sloppy. Your instructions to me are extremely sloppy. And it really feels like you're just throwing it at me assuming I can solve everything with my omnipotence.]","\"Make it a photo-frame-sized image, suitable for placing on a table, and allow it to be operated by touch through the frame’s cover. Make sure it doesn’t malfunction if touched accidentally. Also, let Kaito-san be able to zoom in if he wants to look closer. Make it operable not just by touch, but also remotely through thought. While you’re at it, since saving state data is a pain, make sure it doesn’t degrade over time. Also, let the frame’s outer design be changeable for fun. Oh, and one more thing, use that feature you included in the photo you gave as a gift, where it triggers a mental image. I want it so that when someone picks it up, they’re flooded with vivid memories of today’s birthday party.\"","[......No, can we go back to that sloppy one instead!? No, well, I can do it, yeah, but aren’t you treating me like a tool way too casually!?]","As it turned out, her plan was simply to have the omniscient and omnipotent Makina-san add a bunch of convenient features to the photo. Well, I guess if it’s Makina-san, she really can do anything......","\"......Well, you see, I got my dependable best friend Makina after all. When I need something complicated done, you’re naturally the first one I want to rely on.\"","[S- Seriously? Well, then I guess it can’t be helped~~ Yeah, that makes sense. When you're in trouble, of course you’d turn to your best friend. And I am omniscient and omnipotent, so I can totally do it no problem. I guess I don’t have a choice~~ If my best friend’s asking, there’s no way I could say no~~]","Easy! You're way too easy! Just moments ago, she looked so grumpy, but Makina-san’s expression instantly brightened into a happy smile as she accepted Alice’s request.","Makina-san, by nature, was clearly indulgent on Alice, doting her on her whims, so it probably made it easy for Alice to ask for complicated things. Though, to be fair, I’m sure a lot of that is because she genuinely trusts her as a best friend......","Now that the issue with the photo composition had been resolved, it was time to take the group picture. Last time, we’d gone outside the castle and lined up based on Alice’s instructions, but this time, since there were Gods who could literally do anything, it seemed we were going to be teleported directly into our preassigned positions.","It looked like I’d be surrounded by my lovers, with Shiro-san and Kuro on either side of me, the rest forming a circle around us. Everyone else was arranged based on things like body size and height.","『Well then, this unit shall be taking the photo.』","[Arehh? Electrone-san, aren’t you going to be in the photo too?]","『May I be included as well?』","[Of course.]","『Emotion output...... <My oshi's fansa is just overwhelming, I’m crying. If it’s an invitation from Kaito-sama, I’d be delighted~~!> ......And so, this unit will handle the photography.』","Even though she’d joined midway through the event, Electrone-san had helped with the concert effects and such, so I had hoped she’d be in the photo too. When I invited her, she gladly accepted and joined the group photo, leaving behind her cat ear device to float in the air and handle the camera.","『A countdown will now appear above this unit. The photo will be taken at zero, so please prepare yourselves.』","As Electrone-san said this, a giant digital number 10 appeared above the cat ear device in the air, beginning the countdown.","Just beneath it, a message read: \"Look in this direction for the best photo\", so I turned my gaze to match.","Before long, the count reached zero, and the photo was taken...... Thanks to Makina-san, the photo was instantly developed, placed in a photo frame, and delivered right to my hands.","As I held it in my hand, the memories of today’s lively yet fun party vividly came to mind, and I felt a warm sensation in my heart.","And since the moment called for it, I borrowed a Loudspeaker magic tool from Alice and briefly addressed the crowd gathered here.","\"Everyone, thank you so much for throwing such a grand party today. There were many confusing moments, but even more than that, it was a joyful and happy day.\"","Yeah. There really were a lot of surprises and moments of confusion, but I had the chance to talk with each person who came, and it was truly a fun, happy time...... well, uh, except for the scale of it all...... I kind of wish it had been just a little more modest...... But that’s no longer an option, is it? I mean, they made an entire world just for this. They’re definitely going to use it again for the next one, aren’t they?","......U- Unn. Well, I’ll worry about that when the time comes. For now, I’m just glad to have made such a wonderful, happy memory today.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [The party’s over, but there are still a few things I'm curious about...... the additional attacks on the Stomachache Warriors, the almost certain assault on Electrone by the gorilla, and that modest celebration Nebula mentioned......]"]},{"number":2307,"title":"Chapter 2307: After the Birthday Party 1","paragraphs":["The birthday party had come to an end, but there was still this lingering atmosphere, like the party was continuing just a bit longer. It felt like one of those moments where you’d go around saying goodbye to acquaintances before heading home.","Incidentally, regarding going home, it seemed that a special gate had been set up near the exit of the venue, and passing through it would take each person back to their respective homes.","With that in mind, although I had spoken to most people when receiving their presents, I decided to have a proper conversation with a few others, and first, I went to visit Electrone-san.","[Electrone-san, thanks for all the help today, one way or another.]","『Please don’t mention it. Outputting emotion...... <Actually, for me, not only was I allowed to attend the party, but getting to be involved in so many ways, it was the best!> ......Truly a stroke of luck.』","[Hearing that means a lot. By the way, there’s something I wanted to ask, Electrone-san, would it be possible for you to deliver something to the other four World Creators who gave me birthday presents aside from you?]","『It’s possible, but...... a delivery?』","For my birthday, five World Creators had sent me presents through Canalis-san. I had asked her to pass along my thanks, but I was wondering if I could do something more in return.","After all, considering that lottery draw, there must have been over 170 billion World Creators who tried to send me a gift. If I don’t make a move myself, I don’t even know when I’ll next have a chance to get in touch with the ones who actually succeeded in sending something.","And so, thinking if there was anything I could give in return, I remembered something I’d left inside my magic box. When I attended Archlesia Empire's Founding Festival, I made some Wingeds' accessories with Amel-san’s guidance. But since there were more products than expected, and other Winged stalls were participating too, we decided to pass those accessories to them. That said, since I’m not a member of the Winged like Amel-san, it didn’t feel right to display a beginner’s handmade work among theirs. In the end, the accessories I made remained in my magic box.","Amel-san had told me I could do whatever I liked with the accessories, so I’d thought I’d give them to someone eventually...... As luck would have it, I had exactly five of them, perfect for this occasion.","And so, I figured I’d ask Canalis-san later, but if Electrone-san could contact the other four as well, it’d be faster to give all five to her and ask her to deliver them.","[So, here are the accessories...... I know they’re just handmade by an amateur, but if it’s alright with you, could you please accept them as a token of my gratitude for today?]","『......Outputting emotion...... <Hawawa, t- that’s just...... it’s like a tidal wave of fansas?! If anything, I should be the one giving thanks for being allowed to attend the party, and now I’m even getting a handmade accessory from Kaito-sama...... it’s too precious, too precious...... my brain’s about to burst into a festival of reverence! Kaito-sama really is the overwhelmingly number one! Love love L-O-V-E love!> ......I am deeply grateful for your thoughtfulness, Kaito-sama. I’ll gladly accept it.』","[Ah, yeah.]","Her mood swings were as intense as ever, like a hardcore idol fan one second, and then suddenly returning to a blank expression. Even though I’d seen it plenty of times by now, I still couldn’t help but be caught off guard.","『Please leave the deliveries to the other World Creators to me. This unit swears on my name that they will be delivered without fail.』","[Thank you very much. I really appreciate it.]","『Today was truly a wonderful day for me as well. In fact, I’ve received permission from Shallow Vernal to visit Trinia again, so if it’s convenient for Kaito-sama, I would love to come visit you again sometime.』","[Oh, really? I’d be happy to have you over again. I feel like we haven’t had the chance to really talk yet, but I can already tell that you’re incredibly kind and a genuinely good person. I’d love to get the chance to talk more with you.]","『Outputting shock...... <Hawaaa!? That smile, my oshi’s smile is so dazzling!? It’s literally sunshine! To be blessed with such a MAXIMUM PRECIOUS smile...... This happiness is overwhelming! I’m so glad I came! I’m really, really glad I cameeeee!!! Even if I get beaten to a pulp by some irrational, jealous gorilla afterward, I’ll have no regrets!!!> ......I too look forward to the day I can meet with you again, Kaito-sama.』","Honestly, her personality is pretty strong, but unlike Makina-san, she doesn’t go off the rails. Even when she gets excited, she maintains a respectful distance, which makes her feel reliable, and I definitely think she’s a good person. That’s why I wanted a chance to talk with her more leisurely.","When she comes to visit again, I hope we can have a relaxed conversation with some others like Nebula and Canalis-san.","......That aside, for that so-called \"irrational gorilla\" who can apparently beat up someone like Electrone-san, who should be Omnipotent and Omniscient, what in the world......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Once again, he’s frying the brains of the World Creators on high heat...... and I’m starting to feel like that berserk gorilla might start radiating a golden aura any moment now.]"]},{"number":2308,"title":"Chapter 2308: After the Birthday Party 2","paragraphs":["The main events had all concluded, and in the slightly more relaxed atmosphere of the venue, Lady Eris of the Hamilton Marquisdom sat quietly lost in thought.","(This really was an extraordinary party, but what I gained from it was even more valuable than I expected. There’s the connection to the Lord Trading Company, of course, and though luck certainly played a role, I was able to score well in the quiz tournament and even win a trophy. Looking ahead, that’s quite advantageous. A trophy crafted by Phantasmal King-sama carries enough prestige for a noble...... That said, I’ve been receiving far too many benefits lately for someone who is merely an heir, and I fear it may invite unwanted envy...... I would really like to restrain this a bit but......)","For a noble like Eris, interacting with high-ranking individuals, essentially the upper echelons of the world, was undoubtedly beneficial. And in fact, thanks to recent events involving Kaito, Eris’ name had begun spreading rapidly among the nobility.","It wasn’t just her reputation as the capable heir of the Hamilton family, but the name “Eris Dia Hamilton” itself that was gaining recognition at a remarkable pace. While she was grateful, she also understood it could easily lead to jealousy and the emergence of new political rivals.","As the saying goes, “The nail that sticks out gets hammered down”, and being too prominent isn’t always ideal.","(Well, if it's someone like Kaito-sama, operating on a literally different dimension of existence, things like envy or enemies don’t even apply anymore, so that technically isn't a problem, but I’m just a candidate heir of a great noble family and haven’t even been granted a title in my own right yet. I’ve long thought that now would be a good time to ease off and settle down a little...... but nothing ever goes the way I plan.)","Eris had intended to keep a low profile after reaping the benefits from her involvement with Nifty until rumors in high society died down, but events involving Kaito kept unfolding beyond her expectations, making that impossible.","(I can’t imagine anyone would be foolish enough to openly move against the Hamilton family, but just in case, I should probably increase my security detail...... and if possible, I’d also like to secure some kind of personal backing. That, however, is easier said than done. I do have impressive social ties, the Seven Princesses, Founder-sama, the Lord Trading Company, and even Kuromu-sama, whom I was permitted to greet this time,but these are all just social connections. None of them would be people I would say would be my backing.)","Given her future promise to invite Kaito to a tea party, the chances of drawing envy were only going to increase. What she wanted was some kind of backing that would make others hesitant to act against her. That was her honest wish.","But of course, such things can’t be obtained easily or on a whim.","(If I were to consider possibilities...... perhaps through the matter Satania-sama brought up this time, or that gemstone mining opportunity Rasal-sama mentioned before. If I could have Father appoint me as the person in charge of those Hamilton family dealings, and from there build trust through meaningful interaction...... No, that’s difficult. Desires like that are easy to see through, and if I act with such intentions in mind, I might end up offending them instead...... It’s best to keep those ambitions quietly to myself and engage with sincerity.)","Though she desired a powerful supporter, Eris also understood that acting solely to obtain one would be insincere and could tarnish her reputation. She resolved to interact in good faith and chose not to put herself forward as the person in charge of any dealings.","Just as she reached that decision, someone suddenly called out to Eris.","[......May I have a moment of your time?]","[Eh? Ah, yes. I apologize for not noticing——- hhyu!?]","Eris, who had been deep in thought, turned around to apologize for her delayed reaction, only to freeze upon seeing who had addressed her. After all, standing before her was none other than one of God Realm's Supreme Gods, God of Life, Life herself......","[I had been meaning to speak with you during the party, but the opportunity never presented itself. I’m sorry it had to be after the event concluded.]","[N- No! I am honored beyond words that you would even speak to me!]","[I'm glad to hear that. Since we have the chance, allow me to introduce myself as well. I am one of God Realm's Supreme Gods, God of Life...... my name is Life.]","[I offer my greetings to the great God of Life-sama. I am Eris Dia Hamilton, heir to Hamilton Marquisdom in the Archlesia Empire.]","Though Life spoke in a calm yet dignified voice, Eris returned the introduction with a deep bow, her mind in utter chaos.","(W- Why? Why would God of Life-sama speak to me......? N- No, more than that, she introduced herself by name? Why would something like this even happen? I- I mean, I can guess. It’s safe to assume Kaito-sama is somehow involved, but this is completely outside anything I could’ve expected...... W- Why is this happening!?)","While Eris did her utmost to keep her expression composed, inside her mind was total panic. Her stomach, as always in moments like these, throbbed with intense pain.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I don’t know the details, but one thing’s for sure...... This definitely happened because Kaito said something unnecessary when he was receiving presents or something around that time.]","? ? ? : [No doubt about it.]"]},{"number":2309,"title":"Chapter 2309: After the Birthday Party 3","paragraphs":["To begin with, the question arises, why did Life decide to approach Eris in the first place......? The reason goes all the way back to the moment when Kaito was receiving gifts in the parallel worlds.","When Kaito received his gifts, he had some spare time, so he made small talk with each person to a certain extent, and Life also chatted with him in a similar way.","[Still, I feel that having more opportunities to attend events involving those outside the God Realm is a good thing. At the same time, it’s made me painfully aware of my own immaturity.]","[Wasn’t it after the White God Festival that the Gods started interacting more with the Human Realm and Demon Realm? I think it’s a good thing, but yeah, the shift in environment must be a bit overwhelming, right?]","[Yes, though it’s still only in relative terms compared to before, more people have begun to broaden their perspectives beyond the God Realm. I myself had the chance to reference Human Realm festivals during the White God Festival and realized just how narrow my outlook was. That in itself isn’t a problem. Immaturity is something to be ashamed of, yes, but I believe that expanding one’s horizons like this is the kind of growth that Shallow Vernal-sama wishes to see in us. Still...... I can’t help but feel a little anxious when I compare myself to the God of Time and Space and God of Fate. I feel like I’ve fallen far behind.]","[You mean compared to Chronois-san and Fate-san? Just out of curiosity, what makes you feel that way, Life-san?]","Before they realized it, the conversation had turned into something like a consultation with Kaito, who waited attentively for Life’s reply. Life went quiet, seemingly organizing her thoughts, before she finally began to speak.","[......Indeed. God of Fate is, needless to say, the one who grew the most among us Supreme Gods, and there were many times during the White God Festival when I felt I couldn’t match the depth of her thinking. As for the God of Time and Space, I thought we were somewhat similar, but she is quite close to Lilia Albert, and it seems her ties to the Human Realm are deeper than mine. Especially when it was decided that we would reference Human Realm festivals for the White God Festival, I didn’t really have anyone I could talk to about that kind of thing...... The only Human I had any real connection to was the Emperor of the Archlesia Empire, the country I oversee. I realized that was a problem I needed to address.]","[Ah, I see. So basically, you’d like to make more acquaintances among the Humans?]","[Exactly. It’s a bit tricky given my position as a Supreme God, but like God of Time and Space, I do think it would be beneficial to have a close relationship with certain individuals among the Humans. Do you know anyone suitable, Miyama-san?]","[Hmmm, do you have any preferences or conditions?]","Hearing Life say she wanted to connect with more Humans, Kaito found the intent to be a very good one. If he could help in any way, he wanted to.","[Let’s see. Ideally, someone who lives in Archlesia Empire would be best. Symphonia is the country under the care of God of Time and Space, and Hydra is under God of Fate...... It’s not that I’m forbidden from interacting with their residents, but there are certain considerations and precautions I’d have to take. It would be easier if they were from the country I’m responsible for.]","[Got it. If we’re talking about people from Archlesia Empire, the first names that come to mind are Amel-san and Eris-san. I do know a few others, but considering you’d be interacting with them, they’d probably need to be someone of fairly high status......]","If it were just about being a Human resident of Archlesia Empire, people like Chapel or Anne would qualify, but when it came to dealing with a Supreme God, a certain level of status was necessary. With that in mind, the names that came to Kaito were Amel, the leader of the Wingeds, or Eris, heir to a marquisdom.","[Fumu...... Amel was the leader of the Wingeds, correct? The Wingeds are known for their strong faith, so my presence might make them feel too self-conscious. And this Eris person is?]","[Errr, you remember that time when Shiro-san and Eden-san were glaring at each other? The woman with dark indigo hair who was standing behind me at the time, does that ring a bell?]","[Yes, I remember. The one with the air of a noblewoman, yes?]","[She’s the heir to the Hamilton Marquisdom.]","[Hamilton Marquisdom...... If I recall correctly, they’re one of the four great noble houses of Archlesia Empire, and currently hold the position of Prime Minister. I see, considering the God of Time and Space’s ties with Duchess Lilia, building a connection with Eris might indeed be appropriate for me. By the way, Miyama-san, what’s your impression of this Lady Eris?]","Prompted by Kaito’s words, Life developed an interest in Eris and went on to ask for Kaito’s personal impression of her. She also held Kaito’s insight into people in high regard and was eager to hear what he thought.","[Eris-san is incredibly kind and a really good person. She’s probably quite intelligent and knowledgeable, so she’s really good at naturally stepping in and supporting the conversation. She’s also very sincere and trustworthy as a person.]","[If she’s someone you rate that highly, Miyama-san, then I’d very much like to speak with her at least once.]","[Sure, I’ll introduce you if the opportunity comes up.]","At the time, Kaito’s assumption was simply to explain to Eris that Life wished to interact more with Humans, and then introduce Life while being present himself.","However, what Kaito didn’t anticipate was that Life was unexpectedly quick to act. Seeing that Eris herself was present at the party, Life decided to directly approach her and initiate contact on her own.","That slight misalignment in expectations would, quite ironically, end up causing Eris a considerable amount of stomachache.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [She usually gives off the impression of being sleepy and inactive, but when Kaito visited the God Realm, she immediately decided to accompany him. When she found out Kaito was interested in the God of Fertility, she summoned her right away. And when Epsilon used Taboo Magic, she instantly moved to deal with it herself...... Life’s actually the type who acts the moment something crosses her mind, isn’t she......]"]},{"number":2310,"title":"Chapter 2310: After the Birthday Party 4","paragraphs":["In the God Realm, the position of the Supreme Gods, second only to the Creator God Shallow Vernal, is immensely significant, especially to Humans.","Normally, outside of the Festival of Heroes, one wouldn't even catch a glimpse of them. Even mere rumors of a Supreme God possibly visiting the Human Realm are enough to draw massive crowds. Naturally, the influence of such a God is on an entirely different level, completely incomparable to that of a marquis's daughter.","That's particularly so in Archlesia Empire, where the environment makes it difficult for crops to grow, the Divine Protection of the God of Fertility is a major lifeline. As such, the influence of Gods in this country is even more pronounced than in the other two nations.","Of course, even without those contextual elements, it's an undeniable fact that she is one of the pinnacles in the world. For Eris, she was someone whose displeasure she could never afford to incur.","(T- That’s right, even if the Hamilton Marquisdom is one of the Four Great Noble Houses, if God of Life-sama were to speak a single word, it wouldn't be strange for us to be literally erased from Archlesia’s history. In any case, I must not be disrespectful...... B- But what could God of Life-sama possibly want with me? I'm certain it has something to do with Kaito-sama, but without knowing her purpose, I can’t act recklessly......)","While Eris could say with absolute certainty that Kaito was the cause, she had no idea what business someone like Life could possibly have with a mere noble’s daughter like her.","The only person in Archlesia Empire who had ever spoken directly with Life was likely the Emperor, Chris. Even her own father, Marquis Hamilton, had probably never had such an opportunity.","[There’s no need to cower. You have caused no wrongdoings at all, I reached out entirely on my own accord. It is not an issue of disrespect. However, I understand how not knowing the purpose may cause unease, so let me begin by explaining it.]","[Y- Yes. My gratitude for God of Life-sama's consideration......]","[Ahh, you may address me by name, call me Life. From now on, please refer to me as such.]","[Huh? Yesh, t- then...... Life-sama......]","While Life continued the conversation calmly, Eris was in complete turmoil, her mind thrown into a full-blown panic.","(Eh? Ehhh? S- She permitted me to call her by name? T- That can’t be...... Just being granted the honor of hearing the Supreme God’s name is already beyond comprehension, and now I’m allowed to refer to her as such? E- Even Her Majesty Chris isn’t granted that right, is she? W- Why? W- Where in the world did I earn such an overwhelming excessive level of recognition......?)","Among the Gods, names were considered treasures directly bestowed by Shallow Vernal and were held as supremely important. Even among themselves, Gods would refrain from using names, instead referring to one another as \"God of XXX\", showing how much reverence they had for names.","In Eris’ understanding, the names of the Gods were only allowed to be spoken by those whom the Gods held in the highest regard. For someone like herself, a mere marquis's daughter, to be permitted to speak the name of a Supreme God like Life was an earth-shattering honor.","[First, let me explain my purpose. Are you aware that we Gods have recently increased our interactions with both the Human Realm and the Demon Realm?]","[Y- Yes, I’m aware. Since the White God Festival, the low-ranking Gods, and even the high-ranking Gods, have been participating more frequently in events, and I've heard that their involvement in Human Realm festivals has risen by about 30% compared to previous years......]","[I’m impressed. You seem to possess a broad perspective. Yes, as you said, the God Realm is indeed shifting toward greater involvement with the other realms. Now, regarding my situation: compared to the other Supreme Gods, God of Fate and God of Time and Space, I’ve had far fewer interactions with Humans, something I've considered to be a problem. However, as a Supreme God, I cannot expand my sphere of influence recklessly.]","At Life’s words, Eris nodded lightly in understanding. Despite her confusion at the sudden situation, she was quick-witted and had already begun organizing her thoughts in her head while listening.","(If Life-sama’s goal is to deepen relations with Humans, then perhaps I truly am the most suitable person in this venue to be approached. I don’t know to what extent Supreme Gods are bound by agreements or restrictions regarding their assigned nations, but if Life-sama’s purpose is to increase her interaction with the Humans of her assigned country, Archlesia Empire, and the target is someone with at least a certain level of status within the Empire...... then Emperor Chris would be excluded due to already being in contact with her. Commander Bard and Satania-sama are Demons, which leaves Amel-sama or myself as candidates. I’ve also heard that the Wingeds are devout followers of God of Life-sama and often invite high-ranking Gods to their ceremonies, so it’s possible Life-sama already has contact with them. If that’s the case, then my selection was a process of elimination...... Perhaps I’m being used as a foothold to arrange meetings with my father or other influential nobles...... If that’s the intent, this would make perfect sense.)","Having quickly assembled her thoughts, Eris concluded that her selection must have been a matter of process of elimination. Life’s true goal, she reasoned, was likely to reach out to higher-status individuals such as Marquis Hamilton and the other heads of the Four Great Noble Houses, and she had merely been chosen to facilitate introductions. Realizing this, Eris resolved to take this crucial role seriously and dedicate herself fully to supporting Life, however...... That resolve was shattered almost immediately.","[When I consulted Miyama-san on the matter, he recommended you. He spoke very highly of your knowledge, personality, judgment, and character...... If someone is held in such esteem by Miyama-san, I believe there could be no better person for me to build a relationship with, and so I’ve come to speak with you. If possible, I’d like to converse with you for a while, but would that be acceptable?]","[Y- Yes...... It is a tremendous honor. If I’m suitable, then I’d be glad to speak with you for as long as you like.]","It wasn’t about other nobles at all, Life had come specifically because of Kaito’s high opinion of her. The moment those words registered, Eris nearly blacked out, but she clung to consciousness, forcing a smile as she replied.","(......Why......? No, seriously, why am I being held in such high regard by Kaito-sama!? I mean, it’s an honor! It’s truly an honor!!! But the fact that Kaito-sama’s recommendation alone carries this much weight, it’s overwhelming...... P- Please...... show a little mercy......)","Feeling the intense trust Life placed in Kaito’s evaluation of her, Eris, unable to understand why she was held in such high esteem, quietly pressed a hand to her aching stomach.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Probably, from Eris's perspective, she thinks she's just acting normal...... but most of Kaito’s acquaintances have pretty strong personalities, so someone who's gentle and without quirks ends up being rated really highly just for that.]","? ? ? : [Or rather, Eris-san is fundamentally competent, so through her everyday conversations and gifts, she's been steadily boosting Kaito-san’s opinion of her...... At this point, she's been completely classified as \"someone he genuinely enjoys talking to\", so her favorability just keeps going up no matter what. If that were all, there wouldn’t be a problem but...... when Kaito-san’s favorability towards someone rises, everyone around him automatically starts rating that person higher too......]","Serious-senpai : [As is the case with Lilia and Kaori, it seems those with chronic stomachaches tend to be the ones Kaito holds in high regard.]"]},{"number":2311,"title":"Chapter 2311: After the Birthday Party 5","paragraphs":["Although the sudden conversation with Life gave Eris a stomachache, ironically enough, she is an extremely competent individual, and once the conversation began, things progressed quite smoothly.","To begin with, as the daughter of a marquis, Eris had been raised with a proper education, possessed a diligent personality, and placed great importance on information. As a result, she had a wide range of knowledge, and conversation was one of her strong suits.","[Come to think of it, you achieved quite an impressive result at the quiz competition, didn’t you? Even just speaking with you like this, I can sense the breadth of your knowledge, and it makes you easy to talk to. I myself am someone who doesn’t know many things, and while I don’t think ignorance is a sin or anything like that, I do feel that intellectual people are easier to speak with.]","[Those are kind words. As for the quiz competition, I was lucky in many ways, but I do make a conscious effort to gain various knowledge on a daily basis. Still, when it comes to things related to Kaito-sama, I often feel my own lack of ability. There are so many unpredictable situations that I find myself at a loss.]","[In regards to Miyama-san, I do think there are some aspects where you just can’t help it. To be honest, even when I first met him, while I did recognize him as someone important, being the one blessed by Shallow Vernal-sama, I never imagined he would become such a pivotal figure.]","Fortunately, Life had approached the conversation with a desire to interact, so she was relatively friendly in her manner, which in turn made it easier for Eris to keep the conversation going and engage in a calm and pleasant chat.","Life, for her part, had a very favorable impression of Eris, and felt that she truly was someone worthy of the high praise Kaito had given her. Their interaction could be described as going quite smoothly.","[......This has been a pleasant time, with some truly fascinating topics, but I suppose we can’t go on talking forever.]","[You’re right. I’ve noticed more and more people gradually heading home, so we probably shouldn’t remain here either.]","At Life’s words, Eris felt a small sense of relief inside. She understood that this was a signal to wrap up the conversation, and she was glad she had managed to get through it without incurring any displeasure.","[I realize this was all quite sudden and must’ve been a bit overwhelming for you, but if possible, I’d like to continue having interactions like this from time to time in the future. I myself have a lot to learn when it comes to interacting with other races......]","[Yes, of course. If I can be of help in any way, I’d be glad to cooperate. Speaking with Life-sama, I also found it to be a very valuable and educational experience. I’d be honored if more opportunities were to come.]","Though she had been quite nervous at first, Life turned out to be gentle and polite, and not the type to speak in roundabout ways or test others with subtle implications. Because of that, Eris found her a fairly easy person to converse with.","Of course, there was still the pressure brought by speaking with a Supreme God, but even so, Life was undoubtedly someone who made conversation enjoyable, and Eris responded to her words with sincere gratitude.","However, it was at this point that an event occurred which, in a way, could be considered Eris’ greatest miscalculation.","Life, having observed Fate and Chronois, had made up her mind to deepen her interactions with the Humans and was now acting on that decision. In other words, she had precedents to refer to. And when precedents exist, it is only natural, whether God or Human, to follow the actions of one’s predecessors.","Which means that, in continuing her interaction with Humans...... with Eris, it would be entirely reasonable for Life to model her behavior after the other two Supreme Gods.","So then, which of the two would Life choose as a reference? ......Fate, in this case, is an extremely special example. In her case, she deepened her relationship with Kaito and became his lover. As her affection for him grew, she also came to regard the people around him as important to him, and thus became interested in them as well.","In other words, she didn’t consciously set out to interact with Humans; her broadened perspective was a result of her romantic involvement with Kaito. Therefore, her situation doesn’t serve as a useful model for how to engage with Eris in this current context.","Naturally then, the one Life would turn to as a reference was Chronois. It was only logical that she would choose to imitate Chronois’ actions, especially since she too had deepened her relationship with a noblewoman, Lilia. In a sense, it was a perfectly reasonable course of action.","And what did Chronois do when she first met Lilia......?","[Eris, our conversation has been a truly meaningful experience.]","[Your words are far too generous.]","[Please take this as both a token of gratitude for that, and as a sign of my hopes for our future relationship. It’s a provisional one but...... I grant you the Blessing of Life.]","[ ! ? ! ? ! ? ]","As Life raised her hand, Eris’ body began to emit a faint glow———- it was clear that a Blessing had been bestowed upon her.","[Well then, I look forward to our next meeting.]","[Y- Yesh......]","Eris managed to reply somehow, but mentally, she was on the verge of collapse. Her knees were about to give out, and the shock of what had just happened completely overwhelmed her ability to think.","A Provisional Blessing from a Supreme God was simply too much. Technically, during the first Six Kings Festival, Life had already granted her Provisional Blessing to all participants under Shallow Vernal’s orders. However, that was solely due to Shallow Vernal’s will, and while certain physical enhancements like youthfulness had not persisted, the other effects of those Provisional Blessings had faded after a year.","Now, however, Eris had received a personal Provisional Blessing directly from Life herself. This was an extraordinary matter, proof that Eris, as an individual, had been highly esteemed by a Supreme God, and just like with Lilia, imagining how that might affect her reputation going forward was enough to make her feel like her stomach might literally start bleeding.","Even as Life departed, Eris remained in a daze. Then, a gentle hand patted her on the shoulder. When she turned around, she saw the face of Lilia, looking at her with an expression of deep, heartfelt sympathy.","[......Ahh, D- Duchess Lilia...... I- I...... why did something like this have to happen to me......]","[I understand how you feel...... truly, deeply, painfully so. But if I may say this, even if it sounds cruel...... from my own personal experience, this is just the beginning.]","[What...... What terrifying thing are you saying......? D- Don’t tell me...... you too, Duchess Lilia......?]","[F- Fufu...... I even feel a bit nostalgic now. If you ever need someone to talk to when things get tough, please don’t hesitate to reach out.]","Eris already felt like she was at her limit, but the way Lilia said this was just the beginning, with such earnest, unwavering eyes, left her pale and trembling in fear.","<Afterword>","Ultimate Stomachache Warrior : [The place you're standing right now...... I passed through it more than two years ago!!!]","※ Lilia’s encounters with the Gods included the God of Time and Space -> God of Creation -> God -> God of Life -> A full all-star lineup of high-ranking and low-ranking Gods held a rally in her garden. (All of this happened over roughly three months.)","Serious-senpai : [......So in the end, Lilia Albert really is the strongest......]"]},{"number":2312,"title":"Chapter 2312: After the Birthday Party 6","paragraphs":["Despite the stomachache so intense it felt as though it might bore a hole right through her, thanks to the Provisional Blessing of the Goddess of Life, her body was brimming with vitality, so much so that she hardly felt any fatigue from the party at all...... Still, she couldn’t help but think “So even a Blessing can’t touch psychological stomachaches” as she stepped through her personal transfer gate.","Thereupon, she was standing in front of a familiar residence, the estate of Hamilton Marquisdom. Glancing up at the sky, she saw the sun still high above.","(Although I spent a fair amount of time in that world, just as I was told beforehand, almost no time has passed here upon my return. The sheer power of the Gods never ceases to astonish me.)","She had arrived a day early for Kaito’s birthday party, but when she pulled out her watch to check the time, it was 10 in the morning on the day after she had left the Hamilton estate. The numbers made no sense when compared to how much time she had spent in the other world, but since this was the doing of Gods capable of creating worlds, a realm far beyond the bounds of common sense, Eris didn’t dwell on it and simply stepped inside.","[Welcome home, Milady.]","[Yes, I’ve just returned. Where's Father and Mother?]","[They’re waiting in the room at the back. Please, allow me to guide you.]","After a brief exchange with the maid who greeted her at the entrance, Eris followed her into the house, heading to the room where her parents were waiting. Eris had informed them in advance that she would be attending Kaito’s birthday party, and both of them had cleared their schedules today so they could promptly receive her report or discuss any concerns upon her return.","[Father, Mother, I’ve returned.]","[Ah, welcome back...... Good work guiding her here. You may leave now. From this point on, no one is to enter this room unless the matter is of the utmost importance.]","After lightly acknowledging Eris’ greeting, Marquis Hamilton dismissed the maid and activated a magic tool on the table to ensure their conversation would not be overheard.","Then, looking at Eris’s expression...... his own twisted into one of clear unease.","[......What kind of look is that, my daughter? It was as if you’ve braved countless life-or-death trials.]","[It doesn’t look like...... things went off without a hitch. We’d better brace ourselves for what we’re about to hear......]","Of course, both the Marquis and his wife had hoped that Eris would return having peacefully and uneventfully completed the party...... but judging from the look on her face, it was obvious she had something significant to report or discuss, which immediately made their expressions stiffen.","[I’m not sure where to begin...... so I’ll start with what I believe is most important. Though I’m still struggling to wrap my head around it myself...... I received the Provisional Blessing of the God of Life, Life-sama.]","[....................]","[....................]","An indescribable silence fell over the room. The Marquis and his wife were frozen in shock, their minds unable to catch up with the words Eris had just spoken.","Still, perhaps befitting his role as the current Prime Minister, the Marquis managed to recover from his confusion after a short pause and opened his mouth.","[......H- How did that happen? Did something happen like during the previous Six Kings Festival?]","[No, unlike the first Six Kings Festival, where the Blessing was granted to everyone, this one was given to me personally...... In fact, I was even granted permission to refer to Life-sama by name, and she expressed a desire to continue meeting with me periodically in the future.]","[......W- Wait a moment...... Why!? How could this happen......? What kind of situation could possibly lead to you speaking directly with the God of Life......?]","[Well, you see......]","The daughter who had gone off to attend Kaito’s birthday party had somehow returned with the Provisional Blessing of a Supreme God. Naturally, Marquis Hamilton couldn’t possibly remain calm.","Faced with her obviously bewildered parents, Eris began explaining the circumstances in as much detail and as carefully as she could.","[......I see...... Given those conditions, it would indeed make you the most suitable candidate......]","[Yes. I believe part of the reason is simply that there are very few Humans Kaito-sama is acquainted with residing within the Archlesia Empire. But beyond that...... for some reason, it seems Kaito-sama holds me in very high regard. And that high opinion of his seems to influence the first impressions others have of me far more than I could’ve imagined.]","[Does that mean Miyama Kaito-sama has such a keen eye for people? Well, considering he’s built such an extensive network of connections, and even the Gods place their trust in his judgment, it’s certainly a believable conclusion...... but, um...... are you absolutely sure that Miyama Kaito-sama hasn’t shown any indication of desiring you in that way?]","Though she accepted the significant weight of Kaito’s high opinion, Marchioness Hamilton still gently asked Eris for clarification.","[At the very least, from our conversations, I’ve never gotten that impression. He definitely holds me in high regard as a friend he finds easy to talk to, but I’ve never sensed any intent or feelings from him that go beyond that.]","[A mental compatibility then...... In any case, we ought to reconsider our position as well. At the very least, we need to acknowledge that Miyama Kaito-sama holds Eris in higher esteem than we had assumed. If we don’t, we risk making missteps in unexpected ways.]","It was undoubtedly a fortunate turn of events, but at the same time, also a deeply stressful one......Perhaps it was only natural that not just Eris, but both her parents as well, unconsciously placed a hand over their stomachs.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Master : [Full combo, don! One more hit for the heck of it, don!]","Serious-senpai : [Seriously, have mercy already...... Stop with the Eris -> Hamilton Marquis couple chain stomachache combo...... Poor souls.]"]},{"number":2313,"title":"Chapter 2313: After the Birthday Party 7","paragraphs":["The Hamilton couple was initially shocked upon seeing Eris return with a provisional blessing from Life, but as they calmed down and discussed the matter further, they came to see that the situation wasn’t necessarily a bad one.","[......Lately, too many benefits have been gathering around Eris personally rather than the marquisdom. I had been thinking it might be necessary to put her in charge of a few business ventures, both to give her some formal authority and to deter anyone from harboring strange ideas. But with the Blessing of God of Life-sama, the situation is different now.]","Just as Eris had been considering, Marquis Hamilton had also been thinking about how other nobles might grow jealous of her and turn against her, so he had planned to grant Eris a degree of authority to help shield her.","While this would make it a bit more difficult for her to continue interacting with Kaito as freely, it was something he believed necessary for her safety...... but now that she had received Life’s blessing, everything had changed.","Even though Blessings largely depend on the Gods' own discretion, for the Gods, a Blessing is a significant matter. Harming someone blessed by Life is tantamount to declaring war on her. Whether or not Life would actually intervene was another matter, but from the perspective of other nobles, they could no longer lay a hand on Eris.","Furthermore, unbeknownst to the Hamilton family...... Life was the most God-like in thinking among the Supreme Gods. Setting aside rare cases like the Six Kings Festival, when she gives a Blessing with her own volition as she did this time, she considers the recipient under her protection.","Harming Eris would be seen as hostility toward Life, and by extension, toward Shallow Vernal herself. If such a thing were to happen, Life would likely act immediately to purge the threat. In this sense, her Blessing was not only extraordinarily powerful as a form of backing, but also carried tangible deterrent power.","[There’s a lot to consider, but overall, it’s a huge advantage. As expected of Miyama Kaito-sama......]","[Yes, though...... my stomach is killing me......]","Putting aside the damage to their stomachs, it was clear that Eris had obtained exactly what she needed at this moment, making it a huge gain for her. Of course, even with that, her stomach still hurt terribly.","[By the way, Eris...... That's the end of it...... wasn't the case at all, right?]","[No, let’s move on to the next matter. I was able to exchange greetings with Satania-sama, the Chairman of the Lord Trading Company. It seems she holds me in high regard, likely because of Kaito-sama's evaluation of me as well...... Though it's more of a verbal promise, she has offered a proposal to do business with the Hamilton family.]","With a concerned look, the Marchioness asked, to which Eris nodded once before continuing. What followed was another staggering revelation, one that made even the corners of Marquis's mouth twitch.","[That is...... tremendous. A connection with the Lord Trading Company would be enormously beneficial to us, especially since they’ve already been supporting the reformist faction. Deepening ties with them will be incredibly useful going forward. Of course, coordinating things will be quite a challenge......]","[Indeed, but Satania-sama has left the terms of the proposal entirely in our hands. I believe if we reach out, she will almost certainly respond positively. Which is precisely why we must proceed carefully...... we already have business with Rasal-sama, after all......]","[We may be spreading ourselves too thin...... In this case, we need to be more cautious of not drawing resentment from other trading companies rather than from the nobles.]","[Yes. Although...... it’s a terrifying thing to say, somehow, uncannily...... I’ve also managed to gain connections at this party that could resolve that problem too.]","Doing business with the Lord Trading Company would mean dealing with large volumes, and there was also the mining-related venture that Rasal had proposed. From the outside, it might seem like the Hamilton family was aggressively expanding into multiple fields, and more trading companies would likely approach them hoping to piggyback on that momentum, but even for a marquisdom, there was a limit to how many business partners they could take on.","They would need to find ways to decline offers without earning ill will, but trading companies and merchants operated within a different network from the nobility, making negotiations much more delicate.","[......A connection that could resolve it?]","[Yes. Umm...... I was granted the honor of greeting the Underworld King, Kuromueina-sama... and she even permitted me to call her nickname, Kuromu-sama.]","[ [ ............... ] ]","Hearing Eris speak those words with an indescribable expression on her face, the Hamilton couple both looked up to the heavens in unison. Their daughter had only attended a birthday party, and yet she came back with the Blessing of the God of Life, a near-guaranteed business deal from one of the Five Great Trading Companies, and a personal acquaintance with one of the Six Kings. It was the kind of situation that made one want to mentally check out.","However, perhaps thanks once again to Kaito's absurd level of luck, this connection with Kuromueina was massive. Kuromueina stood at the top of several elite trading companies and could essentially be called the pinnacle of all merchants and trading companies on a global scale.","Because of her personality, she was often approached for support in rescuing failing businesses or mediating conflicts between companies, so there were countless trading companies that dared not go against her. Simply being connected to her came with immense benefits in the commercial sphere.","[......Just to be sure, the reason Underworld King-sama treated you so kindly is......?]","[......Apparently because Kaito-sama holds me in high regard, it seems Kuromu-sama had heard about me from him and was extremely friendly as a result.]","[This is truly on another level...... My years of experience don’t mean a thing anymore.]","No matter how mild-mannered Kuromueina was known to be, it was unthinkable for someone to form such a close relationship with her on a first meeting. Kuromueina herself was well aware of the influence she wielded and was normally very cautious, especially when dealing with nobles, typically keeping contact to a minimum...... And yet, the filter \"Kaito holds her in high regard\" easily swept all of that aside.","[......If possible, I’d love for you to tell me that’s the end of it...... We're done here, right?]","[......There’s still more.]","The benefits were immense, but seemingly in direct proportion, so too was the pain in their stomachs. The three members of the Hamilton family once again looked to the heavens, perfectly synchronized in their silent suffering.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Normally, you'd have to steadily build up goodwill from zero to start forming relationships, but if Kaito holds you in high regard, your initial friendship level starts at like 50 or 80, or something like that huh......]","? ? ? : [Giving exactly the connections you need alongside stomachaches...... that's just so typical of Kaito-san, isn’t it?]"]},{"number":2314,"title":"Chapter 2314: After the Birthday Party 8","paragraphs":["It was already an overwhelming amount of information, but when Eris said that it still wasn’t over, an indescribable expression showed in the Hamilton couple's faces.","[......That said, I started with what I felt were the most impactful matters, so regarding the rest, there’s little that would require any action from us.]","It was true that some events from the birthday party remained, but the matters that would require the Hamilton household to respond had already been covered. What remained were mostly things that would affect Eris personally to some degree.","[First, during a quiz competition held at the birthday party, I was fortunate enough to tie for third place, and I received a trophy created by Phantasmal King-sama.]","[I see...... That’s certainly not a problem. If you display the trophy in your room or in the mansion’s hallway, it might help improve Eris’ reputation when guests visit. But it’s not something with major consequences......]","[Aside from Her Majesty, Archlesia Emperor Chris-sama, there were few nobles among the party guests, so unless someone goes around bragging, it’s unlikely to stir up any strange rumors.]","Hearing Eris’ explanation, the Hamilton couple nodded in agreement.","There was little issue with Eris winning a trophy in a quiz competition. While it was necessary to report and share the information so they could respond if any nobles who had heard about it brought it up, beyond that, there was virtually no problem.","Eris had always been known for her intelligence and broad knowledge, so her achieving results in such a field wasn’t unnatural. Therefore, there was no need for the marquisdom to take any particular action.","[Next, a God named Electrone-sama, a World Creator different from the one the Hero Actors came from, attended the party, to which I exchanged brief greetings and conversation with. However, this wasn’t just with me, Electrone-sama seemed to address all the party attendees, so I don’t believe it will have any special impact.]","[A God from another world...... It’s astounding that Miyama Kaito-sama’s connections even extend beyond this world, but yes, it doesn’t seem like it will affect us at this stage...... And what sort of person was this Electrone-sama?]","[My impression was of a supremely gentle and broad-minded, magnificent being. At the very least, I don’t believe she would issue warnings to those who displease her, unlike that esteemed one...... Though it’s unclear whether she’ll ever return to this world again.]","For nobles, the concept of Gods from other worlds often brought to mind Eden, which invoked a certain fear, but based on Eris’ account, Electrone did not behave like Eden, which came as a small relief.","[Next, I was invited to Kaito-sama’s house.]","[That shouldn’t be a problem either. It still falls within the scope of your personal interaction with Miyama Kaito-sama. In fact, it’s a good thing that you’re able to build a friendly bond. That said, depending on what happens during the visit to Miyama Kaito’s home...... we may need to have another discussion afterward......]","[If at all possible, I really do hope you just return with nothing but stronger friendship......]","[......If I can help it, I hope for that outcome as well.]","There was nothing wrong with Eris visiting Kaito’s house——— They were friends, and visiting each other’s homes was natural. However, all three of them shared the same concern...... that Eris might come back with yet another source of stomachache. It was an anxiety none of them could completely shake off.","Still, it wasn’t as though there was anything they could do about it, so they could only keep their almost certainly futile wish that she return without issue close to their hearts.","[Next, I had a chance to speak with Symphonia Kingdom's Duchess Lilia, and I believe we built a reasonably good relationship. That said, our conversation mainly revolved around Kaito-sama and wasn’t about forming any sort of business relationship between households.]","[Duchess Albert now holds enough influence to be considered the foremost noble in the Symphonia Kingdom. Even for our Hamilton household, it would be good to foster a positive relationship with her in the future...... but that’s more of a long-term perspective. If your relationship with the Duchess leads to something between the households later, that’s fine, but don’t approach her with that intention in mind. Hidden motives like that tend to be seen through.]","[Yes. I’ll be very careful on that point.]","As for meeting Lilia, it was true that they had gotten along well...... But that was largely due to their shared understanding of the pain that is stomachache. Given that it was unclear whether Lilia herself sought to strengthen ties with the Hamilton household, it would not be wise for Eris to make any moves on her own.","[That concludes the main points. As for the minor details, I’ll compile them into a written report. Also, there was a commemorative gift given to all party attendees, and among those was this wine......]","[......Ah, the phantom wine that was said to have only been distributed to guests at Miyama Kaito-sama’s new house celebration...... This is quite something. I have a friend, a Count, who’s a wine enthusiast. Thanks to Her Majesty Chris’s kindness, he managed to taste a single glass, and he supposedly said that if he could get a whole bottle of this wine, he wouldn’t mind giving up his entire wine collection, which he’s spent years building.]","[That much huh...... In that case, maybe it’d be best if I entrusted the wine to you, Father.]","[Indeed. If we manage the rumors cleverly, we might be able to divert some of the attention currently focused on you onto me, the one who possesses the wine...... Well, let’s talk through all of this, including how we’ll respond moving forward...... I’m sure you’re tired, Eris, but bear with us.]","[Yes.]","In any case, Kaito’s influence was simply too immense. If they let their guard down, they were sure to find themselves once again suffering from unforeseen developments and stomachaches, so the three of them earnestly discussed how to proceed from here on.","That said, if Lilia had been present at that moment...... she likely would have offered a painfully accurate piece of advice drawn from firsthand experience: “Kaito-san is the kind of person who breaks through any plan by going in a completely unexpected direction.”","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [The struggles of the Stomachache Warriors continue huh...... Looks like that’s the end of the Eris-related matters for now. So, who’s next?]"]},{"number":2315,"title":"Chapter 2315: After the Birthday Party 9","paragraphs":["In the capital of Archlesia Empire, the largest and most important building is not the imperial castle...... but rather the temple of the God of Fertility, Elune.","Given that Archlesia Empire is not particularly blessed with favorable climate or land conditions, the presence of the God of Fertility, Elune, is considered of the utmost importance. Many people visit to offer prayers, and various ceremonies related to fertility are frequently held. As such, the temple is extremely large, one of the grandest among all temples in the Human Realm.","Deep within that very temple, in a room located in the area where Elune resides, she placed a cup of prepared tea on the table.","[Here you go.]","[Thank you. Your skills are as impressive as ever.]","[Cooking and such are my hobbies after all. That said, it’s rare for God of Life-sama to visit my temple.]","[Yes, I came to confirm a few things...... and I also have some questions I’d like to ask you.]","[Questions, you say?]","It was just after Kaito’s birthday party had ended. Before returning to the God Realm, Life had said she wanted to stop by Elune’s temple, and so the two of them were now seated together in one of its rooms.","[I’ve been trying to increase my interaction with Humans, following the example of God of Fate and the God of Time and Space...... Do you know of a noblewoman named Eris Dia Hamilton?]","[Yes, she’s the heir to the Hamilton Marquisdom, one of the Four Great Noble Houses. She’s a highly intelligent woman known for her talent, and lately she’s been rumored to be on close terms with Miyama-san, so I’ve heard her name often. As far as I know, she hasn’t been involved in any shady dealings behind the scenes, and she seems to be a person of fine character.]","[As expected, you’re well-informed.]","[Many people come to my temple to worship, and I also attend various events, so I naturally hear all sorts of rumors.]","Elune was someone Life greatly trusted. Were it not for the crucial role Elune played within Archlesia Empire, Life would have liked to make her a direct subordinate. Elune was an exceptional figure, highly knowledgeable even among the Gods about matters concerning the Human Realm.","[I spoke with her myself and judged her to be trustworthy. With Miyama-san’s recommendation backing her, I granted her a Provisional Blessing. That’s why I wanted to ask, if you have any insight into what she might desire moving forward, to help foster smoother relations, I’d like to hear it.]","[Let’s see...... Based on recent rumors, I’d say Eris is seeking a strong backing...... someone she can rely on. She’s been rumored to be in close contact with Miyama-san, and some even say she's favored by him...... Though the part about \"being favored\" is likely just gossip, their frequent interaction is true. However, compared to the scale of that relationship, Eris herself doesn’t possess overwhelming power. That could lead to people underestimating her or even envying her.]","[Now that you mention it, people did say the same about Miyama-san at first, that he was just some youngster favored by the Underworld King.]","[Yes, jealousy is unavoidable in such situations...... In Miyama-san’s case, he was initially dismissed as someone with mere connections, but as the Phantasmal King backed him, and then there was the matter with Earth God-sama, his web of connections kept expanding, now making him someone of immense authority. Even without the threat of Earth God-sama, no one underestimates him anymore.]","As she spoke of the envy and scorn that inevitably arises toward those who appear to rely only on connections rather than their own strength, Elune took a sip of the tea she had prepared for herself.","[So, the Provisional Blessing from God of Life-sama will be a benefit for Eris-san, and further interaction with you will also be a major advantage for her. I believe that alone should be more than sufficient.]","[I see. It sounds like a relationship similar to the one between God of Time and Space and Lilia Albert would be ideal. That’s helpful to know...... Ah, also, regarding my interactions with Eris, I intend to create a space where we can talk on a somewhat regular basis, but given my position, frequently visiting the Hamilton Marquisdom would cause quite a stir.]","[Ahhh, so you stopped by to confirm whether you could use my temple as the location for that interaction. Yes, I believe it’s better to meet here than to visit the marquisdom directly. I can prepare as many rooms as needed but...... if God of Life-sama will be using one yourself, perhaps I should make some special adjustments to the interior and such.]","Indeed, the main reason Life had visited Elune’s temple this time was to see if she could borrow a room for future interactions with Eris.","Sensing Life’s intentions, Elune nodded while noting that, since it would be a Supreme Goddess herself using the space, the room should be properly outfitted to suit that level of importance.","[I’ll leave that part to you. I hold your ability and taste in the highest regard. I’m sure you’ll prepare a room worthy of my interactions with Eris, one so perfect that I’ll be satisfied the moment I see it.]","[Eeeek! Why do you always put so much pressure on me...... No, I’ll do my best! I will, but can you please not get your hopes too high?]","[From the bottom of my heart, I look forward to it.]","[Eeeek......]","Though Elune understood this was a sign of Life’s deep trust in her, she still let out a helpless whimper in response to the merciless expectations placed upon her.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Elune might actually be a rare case of a stomachache character where Kaito isn’t the direct cause......]"]},{"number":2316,"title":"Chapter 2316: After the Birthday Party 10","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","Yesterday, while I was riding my scooter, I got stung in the neck by a skilled bee as it passed by, and the pain was so intense I was writhing in agony, so I took the day off.","(T/N: The Japanese use hachi for Hymenoptera in general, so the author could be stung by either a bee, a wasp, or a hornet, not sure which.)","After Kaito's birthday party came to an end, Kaori and Akane decided to chat a bit and moved together to Kaori's shop to talk about how the party went.","[Wow, that really was an incredible party. With the way time flows differently over there, it honestly felt like I just had a dream.]","[Yeah, Kaito sure is as tremendous as ever. That guy is living in a totally different dimension from us. Not even at the Festival of Heroes do you see a lineup like that...... But well, having that boat party in between really helped take the edge off.]","[Well~~ My stomach was still in knots though. But yeah, having a heads-up this time made a big difference.]","It was true that this birthday party had gathered a truly astounding cast of people. For the two of them, who could be considered “ordinary” attendees, it had been an overwhelming situation where no matter which direction they looked, they were surrounded by big names.","However, thanks to the boat party hosted earlier by Kaito, they already had an idea of who would be showing up, so they were mentally prepared and that helped a lot.","On top of that, this time even the servants from Lilia’s mansion, Kuromueina's family, subordinates of the War King and the World King who knew Kaito, had all gathered. Compared to the boat party, the presence of less “overwhelming” attendees helped soften the overall pressure somewhat.","[Oh yeah, Kaori, here’s the prize money from the hidden talent contest...... Half-half sound fair?]","[Oh right, we came in third place, didn’t we? I was really surprised when Akane-san suddenly said you wanted to join, but it turned out really well. Still, performing in front of that lineup was seriously nerve-wracking......]","[Well, at least we got our names out there. Might even bring in some new customers to your shop huh?]","[No, I already have more than enough amazing people dropping by...... Honestly, ever since I got to know Kaito-kun, my shop’s been visited by VIPs one after another. It’s kind of terrifying. Like, I’m seriously scared he might bring someone like Shallow Vernal-sama over someday.]","Accepting the envelope with the prize money that Akane handed over, Kaori gave a strained, awkward smile.","[But hey, whatever the case, extra income like this is always nice. Maybe I’ll treat myself to a nice new cooking uten...... sils......]","[Hm? What’s up?]","Though the future gave her stomach anxiety, Kaori had been genuinely excited at the thought of the bonus income. She opened the envelope to check inside, but immediately froze up like she’d turned to stone, then closed the envelope and rubbed her eyes.","As if she thought her exhaustion had caused her to hallucinate, and she needed to clear her vision for a second look......","[W- Well, I thought I was seeing things...... The amount in there seemed wrong......]","[Eh? I thought I put it in properly. Wasn’t it five platinum coins?]","[It was in there! That’s why I’m freaking out! Wait, you put five!? I saw something platinum-looking and shut it right away, but...... five!? That’s...... That’s 50 million yen......]","[Yeah, between the two of us it’s 1,000,000R...... so that’s 100 million yen total. If third place gets that much, second must be 300 million and first, what, 500 million? Man, talk about generous.]","[Wait, wait, wait! How are you so calm about this, Akane-san!? That’s five platinum coins!!!]","While Kaori was clearly shaken by the prize of five platinum coins per person, Akane remained perfectly composed.","[No, I mean, we're talking about a party with that kind of guest list, you know? Of course the prize money would be around that level.]","[I- I mean, y- yeah, I guess...... But still, it’s shocking. Just from doing a silly performance, I got way more than I’ve ever managed to save up. Who wouldn’t be surprised by that?]","[Yeah, fair point. It’s not often regular people get that kind of money after all.]","[......You know, Akane-san, I sometimes forget, but you’re actually pretty rich, aren’t you?]","[Well yeah, I’m the head of a mid-sized trading company. In Japanese terms, it’s kind of like being the CEO of a startup, so I’ve got a decent amount. But compared to Kaito, I’m practically invisible.]","In reality, Akane's trading company was a mid-tier business with significant clients, and her financial resources were considerable.","In particular, Akane was a master of Teleportation Magic. She often received high-paying requests from other companies to transport goods using her magic, so her personal wealth was nothing to scoff at.","[Honestly, I kind of thought I was the richest among the Otherworlders......]","[I’ve never really thought about it, but...... Kaito-kun’s that wealthy?]","[He’s definitely got at least a major corporation’s worth. And if you seriously calculated the value of all the stuff he casually tosses into his magic box and forgets about, his total wealth might literally be on the level of a nation. I heard he’s got dozens of Fruits of the World Tree in there......]","[He’s a monster...... That boy really is just on a whole different scale.]","[No kidding~~]","Once again confronted with just how absurd Kaito was, the two of them shared a strained laugh as they continued to chat about him for a while longer.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......In fact, I bet Kaito’s magic box is packed with an absolutely ridiculous amount of insane stuff.]"]},{"number":2317,"title":"Chapter 2317: After the Birthday Party 11","paragraphs":["A special space created in what could be called the rift between dimensions. This place, connected to multiple worlds, serves as the base of the fan club that Electrone belongs to.","Due to a twist of fate, Electrone had obtained the right to attend Kaito's birthday party and had gone to Trinia. After distributing the accessories entrusted to her by Kaito to the other World Creators, she returned to the fan club's base.","『This unit has returned.』","[Ahh, E- Electrone-san...... um......]","A petite girl, with several divine artifacts floating around her body, ran up to Electrone with an expectant expression.","This girl was also a World Creator belonging to the same fan club and was the one who had gifted Kaito a hand-knitted hat.","Although she herself didn't possess omniscient power, she had been told by other World Creators in the fan club about the item Kaito had entrusted to Electrone. As a result, she was fidgety and visibly restless.","『Outputting agreement...... <I totally get how you can't hold back your excitement. I'd feel the same if our roles were reversed...... So here, this is the handmade accessory entrusted to me by Kaito-sama!> ......You may accept it.』","[Ah, wow...... This is...... U- Um! Excuse me! Could someone help me preserve this in a way that it doesn't deteriorate......? I'm not capable of doing it myself.]","Though the girl wielded godlike power over the management of her own world thanks to the divine artifacts granted by Nebula, outside of that, she possessed little ability. Thus, she was unable to preserve Kaito's accessory, which did not originate from her world, and had to rely on other World Creators.","『You may rest easy. This unit already had its condition maintained.』","[Thank you so much! What should I do......? I want to display it, but I also want to wear it...... I'll also need to get a new outfit to match......]","『If you're happy with it, then this unit is glad. However, outputting a warning...... <Still, for now, it'd be best to step away for a bit. Things are about to get noisy. I'd recommend having a fellow World Creator you're close to keep yourself safe.> ......This is a warning based on what is about to happen.』","[Ah, right. Electrone-san, umm...... please do your best.]","Sensing something, the girl muttered quietly, gave a slight bow, then jogged off toward one of her close World Creator friends standing at a distance.","Once she had gone far enough, Electrone slowly extended her arms out.","『Now, outputting provocation...... <Thanks for waiting! Come at me, you foolish losers driven mad by jealousy! But right now, I'm in my ultimate state, fully charged with the preciousness of my oshi! Prepare to have the tables turned against you!!!> ......This unit is in perfect condition, body and soul.』","Not only had Electrone earned the right to give her present to Kaito, she had gone to meet him in person, attended the party, received permission to visit Trinia in the future, taken a commemorative photo with him, and even personally received a handmade accessory from him...... Of course, the rest of the fan club, made up of fellow die-hard fans, couldn't possibly not be consumed with jealousy.","Even so, the fact that they quietly watched until Electrone and the girl finished their exchange, and didn't direct any hostility toward the weak girl, showed that they were at least rational.","And Electrone, who boldly provoked that group, even seemed to carry a sense of composure. However, that composure...... vanished the moment a bell rang with a light chirin.","『......Outputting panic...... <W- Wait, no, hold on, something's wrong! This isn't right!! I mean, ∇∮◆£, you're part of a different fan club, right!? What's happening here is all within this fan club, and that provocation earlier was directed only at the members here, so ∇∮◆£ has nothing to do with what's happening here!!!> ......Please consider the proper order!』","[........................]","『......Outputting despair...... <Ugh, nope. This d*mn barbarian is hopeless, she absolutely got no intention of having a conversation. Dialogue is important, you know! Sometimes, understanding each other through discussion is...... Ah, you're already raising your fists. Ahh, this freaking gorilla...... Is she raising them slowly to give me time to set up defenses? If you've got that much rationality, how about we talk instead......? Ah, nope, not happening? Great. Seriously, please learn the concept of communication, barbarian. I'll defend with everything I've got but......> ———-!?』","Faced with ∇∮◆£, who was clearly radiating an intense aura of jealousy, Electrone desperately attempted to initiate a dialogue...... but tragically, ∇∮◆£ didn’t utter a single word in response and silently raised her fists.","Seeing this, Electrone wore an expression of resignation, and immediately deployed every bit of defensive power she had, but the very next moment, a brutal punch, one that shattered all of her defenses as if they were paper, smashed straight into her face.","<Afterword>","Unreasonable Berserk Gorilla : [......I’ll wait until you’re ready. Resist with everything you’ve got.]","Virtual Angel : [If you’ve got that much rationality left, I’d rather you just talk it out...... but no, this barbarian clearly has zero intention of listening......]","Unreasonable Berserk Gorilla : [I’ll hit you square in the face with a straight punch. You’d best focus your defenses there.]","Virtual Angel : [But the fact that I still couldn’t block it is exactly what makes it so unreasonable!]"]},{"number":2318,"title":"Chapter 2318: After the Birthday Party 12","paragraphs":["In a newly created space, separated by several dimensional walls from a previously festive and chaotic special dimension, ∇∮◆£ and Electrone were having a conversation.","[But really, Electrone, you’re so lucky with these kinds of things, like your luck with draws or fate or whatever. I totally thought I’d be the first to meet Kaito-sama, and yet you got to see him first in that way? I didn’t expect that at all.]","『......Outputting dissatisfaction...... <Before that, shouldn’t we talk about how you relentlessly punched this virtual angel in the face over and over again!?> ......Prioritizing face-punching is totally barbaric.』","[Yeah, I really am sorry about that.]","『Outputting emotion...... <When you apologize that straightforwardly, it kinda makes it hard to keep complaining...... You’re usually so kind, ∇∮◆£, so why do you suddenly flip into barbarian mode like that?> ......It’s similar to this unit’s emotion ON/OFF switch.』","[Maybe I just lack self-control...... Whatever the reason, it’s honestly embarrassing.]","At Electrone’s words, ∇∮◆£ lowered her head with an apologetic expression on her face. When her switch flips, she acts like a violent machine that won’t listen to a word, but usually she’s gentle and kind-hearted. Even now, she clearly felt genuine remorse over losing control due to jealousy.","『If I bring up the whole \"losing control due to heightened emotions\" thing, it’ll bounce back on me too, since I got overly worked up in front of my oshi, so I’ll refrain. Switching topic...... <So, how was it? You met with Nebula-sama, right?> ......That’s a situation even I deeply envy.』","[It was amazing. Nebula-sama is still Nebula-sama, no matter what form she takes. Just talking with her made me so happy...... And she noticed I was jealous of you and the others, so she let me join in on making Kaito-sama’s birthday present. After having tea together, we worked on it side by side, it was so blissful~~]","『......Outputting dissatisfaction...... <Huuuuuh!? You got to do something that enviable, and then turned around and beat me to a pulp like that!?> ......Utterly unreasonable.』","[Yeah...... once again, I’m truly sorry about that.]","『Outputting complex emotions...... <See, and now that you’re sincerely bowing your head again, I really can’t say anything more......> ......What a complicated feeling this is.』","When ∇∮◆£ mentioned making Kaito’s birthday gift with Nebula, Electrone looked like she wanted to say \"You got to do something super enviable too\", but in the end, because she’s also kindhearted deep down, once ∇∮◆£ admitted her faults and apologized, she found herself unable to continue complaining.","[But speaking of that, Electrone, you got official permission from Shallow Vernal to visit Trinia, right? That means you’ll be able to meet Nebula-sama soon too, which is honestly really enviable. I want that permission too...... but Shallow Vernal is scary, and there’s no way I could handle that kind of negotiation......]","『Outputting emotion...... <Well, yeah, I have to admit getting that right was an unexpected joy, something I never imagined would happen. Of course, I have to consider not causing trouble for Kaito-sama, so I’ll need to be careful with the schedule, but I’m really happy about it> ......A great boost for my oshikatsu. Continuing, outputting a hypothesis...... <As for whether you could get the same permission I did...... well, if it’s not under special circumstances like this time, it probably depends on whether Kaito-sama takes a liking to you or not? If he does, then I feel like Shallow Vernal would give permission too> ......Though this is just speculation.』","Though it wasn’t intentional and more of a lucky coincidence, Electrone had received Shallow Vernal’s permission to “continue visiting Trinia in the future”, and she had also arranged to visit Kaito again at some point. So depending on how things played out, she might actually get a chance to see Nebula again even before ∇∮◆£ meets Kaito.","[It’s pretty tough, isn’t it? I mean, of course I’d be happy if we got along, but trying to approach him with an ulterior motive of getting him to like me would be rude. So I plan to just be myself and see how things go......]","『Outputting honest opinion...... <Nah, I think ∇∮◆£ has a great personality, and as long as you don't go into barbarian mode, I’m sure you’ll get along with him just fine> ......Assuming that switch isn’t flipped, this unit recognizes Bipolar God as someone with an admirable character.』","[Ahaha, thanks. That really makes me happy to hear. Oh yeah, Nebula-sama gave me some of her own blended tea leaves as a souvenir. If you’d like, Electrone, want to have some with me? As an apology for punching you...... I’ve also got some sweets we made together.]","『That’s a very tempting offer. I’ll gratefully accept. Outputting joy...... <Nebula-sama’s tea! Oh wow, I’m so excited! I already knew with my Omniscience that she made her own tea blends and ceramics and such, so I’ve always wanted to try it!> ......My anticipation grows.』","Since ∇∮◆£ and Electrone were usually on good terms anyway, once their jealousy-fueled exchange ended, the two quickly returned to chatting cheerfully together, enjoying each other's company.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [By now, the readers who've followed the story this far have probably already figured it out. Kaito will unconsciously suggest something, Shiro will approve it...... and poor Lilia will be left with a gut punch to the stomach in the near future......]"]},{"number":2319,"title":"Chapter 2319: After the Birthday Party 13","paragraphs":["Regarding the castle where Kaito’s birthday party was held, guests weren’t required to leave immediately, they were welcome to use the lounge or other rest areas, and could leave whenever they wished.","Because of that, some guests who didn’t often get the chance to meet due to living far apart took the opportunity to chat in the lounge before heading home. Greene and Anne were among them, in similar circumstances, and wanting to talk things over, they too moved to the lounge rather than leaving right away.","[......Was it really fine not inviting the Yellow Pipe group?]","[They didn’t attend the last party on the ship, and for now, just us from Scarlet Blue and you from Black Muscat should be enough...... Also, they’re just too overbearing and annoying to deal with......]","Everyone who had even briefly spoken with Kaito before had been invited to the birthday party, not only Greene and Anne, but also the members of Scarlet Blue, Black Muscat, and the trio from Yellow Pipe.","[......Well, in any case, let’s just...... leave those four aside for now.]","[It can’t be helped. If we hadn’t attended the last ship party, we’d definitely be acting the same way......]","As Greene and Anne spoke, they glanced toward their respective teammates, who were either slumped lifelessly on the sofa or staring blankly up at the ceiling in a daze.","[......Arehh? That’s weird. No matter how long I wait, I’m not waking up from this dream...... Could this be the afterlife? Or maybe a world born from Greene-chan’s fantasies? I’ve always longed for high society, but this feels like something entirely different, literally another world......]","[Common sense...... Common sense doesn’t work here at all...... This is another world, right? Not just Trinia’s elites, but actual Gods from other worlds were here? That party Greene-san told us about, she wasn't exaggerating the whole time......?]","[Our union leader is actually being favored by such an esteemed person? I seriously thought she was just being shy and dodging the truth......]","[Well, if it’s this kind of scale, I guess it makes sense that something like a magic box would be handed out as a party game prize. I really regret brushing off Anne-san’s story now......]","Both the Scarlet Blue and Black Muscat members had heard stories from Greene and Anne about the previous ship party, but because the content had sounded so far-fetched, they were half in doubt...... Today’s party, however, proved everything to be true. Completely overwhelmed by an event unlike anything they’d ever experienced, they were left stunned.","[......Well, I suppose one good side effect is that the misunderstandings got cleared up.]","[I am a bit irritated by their weird trust that I’d definitely be exaggerating everything, but sadly, this is so far beyond my imagination there’s no way I could exaggerate it.]","After exchanging glances and seeing the speechless expressions of their team members, Greene and Anne decided to get to the main topic.","[So then, Anne-san...... what do you think about the souvenirs we received this time?]","[Errr, the instant food items are no problem. It’s a joy to get our hands on a product that’s been practically impossible to buy due to its popularity, and being able to easily eat freshly made meals during mining breaks is a big plus. As for the commemorative coin...... it’s quite valuable, isn’t it?]","[It is. After all, it was only given to those who attended this party, meaning there are only about 500 of them in existence. That gives it real collector’s value.]","Yes, the reason Greene and Anne were sitting together now was to discuss the souvenirs that had been handed out to every party guest.","Having someone in a similar situation to talk to was better for one’s mental state, so the two of them decided to go over the items together.","[And now the issue is...... this wine, right? I honestly don’t know much about wine, but what about you, Anne-san?]","[Fuuu...... I long to be part of high society, and since high society and wine are deeply entwined, I’ve been training myself daily in imagining a wine-savvy version of myself...... but alas, I’ve yet to step outside the realm of imagination, so I can’t say I know much either.]","[So basically, we’re in the same boat, we don’t know the value of this.]","[Not quite, but rest assured! Just in case something like this happened, I came prepared!]","With a certain air of confidence, Greene took out her magic box. It was a pale orange color, about the size of a handbag, and though compact in capacity, it was an expensive luxury item that Greene had paid a considerable sum to obtain, something she used daily and took great pride in.","From inside it, she pulled out a book and placed it on the table.","[This here is the latest wine information magazine. I figured there was a chance we’d need some wine knowledge at a party like this, so I bought it and brought it along...... but the lodging we were guided to the day before the party was so spectacular that I completely forgot about it until now.]","[......I understand how you feel. I had trouble falling asleep myself...... Well, anyway, we don’t know if it’s in there, but let’s take a look.]","While they could tell the wine was high-end, they needed to know how high-end it was, after all, that would determine how carefully they’d need to store it. And so, Greene and Anne began flipping through the latest wine magazine together.","[......Ah! Isn’t this it!? There’s only a photo of the empty bottle, but the design matches!]","[It really does. Let’s see...... \"An ultra-rare, top-tier wine sought after by wine enthusiasts around the world. Some claim it was crafted by God of Creator-sama herself, and it’s said only a few dozen bottles exist in the world. There have been no reports of it appearing on the market, but if it ever did, it would easily exceed 50 million R per bottle\"...... hiiieee......]","[F- Fifty...... mil......!?]","Even though the article accounted for rarity at the time it was written, it estimated that the wine would go for at least 5 billion yen, and reading that, all the blood drained from Greene and Anne’s faces.","It went without saying that the two of them were just ordinary people, and when faced with such an outrageously expensive item, they had no idea how to store it properly...... Of course, there was no answer to be found, and both of them unconsciously clutched their stomachs with pale faces.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Six people suffering from stomachaches in a single chapter...... I’m impressed. Well, I suppose it makes sense they were invited, they do have some connection, after all......]"]},{"number":2320,"title":"Chapter 2320: After the Birthday Party 14","paragraphs":["I left for the world where the birthday party was held in the morning, but by the time I got back, it was already past noon. I guess the food and drinks from the party can count as lunch?","Thinking about the time I actually spent over there, it feels like three days passed, but everyone involved can bend that sort of thing however they want, and most of my time was just spent receiving presents, so I decided not to worry about it.","After setting up the photo with the magnification feature that I received, I didn’t really have anything else to do, so I decided to spend the rest of the day relaxing.","I even took a nap during a break, so I’m not tired at all, but I don’t really feel like going out at this hour either. Maybe I’ll just read a book and take it easy...... Oh, right. That gift I got from Canalis-san lets me watch movies, doesn’t it?","If that’s the case, might as well take advantage of it and watch something. When I pulled out the device I got from Canalis-san and touched it, a sci-fi-looking monitor floated up in the air.","It even seems to come with a help feature, so I gave it a quick read. Apparently, it can project onto the air or onto a wall, and I can freely adjust the size and volume.","It even has a function where, if I set a specific area, the sound from the movie won’t leak outside of it. That’s incredibly thorough...... Ah, this movie’s one of the latest releases...... I can even watch movies that are still in theaters? Alright, I’ll go with this one.","The movie I watched for the first time in a while was really good, so good that I ended up watching two in a row without meaning to, and by the time I noticed, it was already evening. This projector? Or terminal? I’m not sure what I should call it, but it’s an amazing gift.","If I carry it around in my magic box, I can watch movies wherever I go, and it sounds like it’d be fun to watch with my lovers or my friends too.","With such thoughts in mind, I headed to Lilia-san’s dining room since it was about time for dinner. Basically, dinner here is eaten together with anyone who's available, including Lilia-san. Since today was the birthday party, everyone had probably cleared their schedules, so I had a feeling nearly everyone would be there, Aoi-chan, Hina-chan, and also my parents.","[Oya? Milord, how was the birthday party?]","[A lot happened, but I had lots of fun.]","[That’s wonderful to hear.]","While I was on my way to the dining room, I happened to run into Nebula, so we made some small talk. For Nebula, meals aren’t necessary, it’s more of a personal preference. She’ll sometimes have sweets with tea, but she almost never eats a full meal, so she usually doesn’t join for dinner.","[Milord, may I ask for a bit of your time after dinner?]","[Sure, no problem.]","[Then I’ll bring you my birthday present to your room at that time.]","[Ah, I see...... I’ll look forward to it.]","For a moment I tilted my head, wondering what she needed me for, but as soon as I heard her say that, it all clicked. Come to think of it, when she helped with the preparations in the morning, I vaguely remember her saying she’d give me her gift later.","Of course, I don’t mind making time at all, and now I’ve got something to look forward to after dinner. I don’t know what she’s prepared, but if it’s from Nebula, I’m sure it’ll be something great. I really am looking forward to it.","[By the way, how was it for you, Nebula? Your friend came over today, didn’t they?]","[I had a pleasant time as well. I’d already contacted her in advance with Canalis-san’s help, so everything went smoothly. The one who visited today was gentle and kind by nature, so I was able to relax and enjoy myself.]","[Hehh, she sounds like a nice person.]","[She is. Though she does have a bit of a tendency to get narrow-minded and jump to conclusions sometimes, she's sociable and has a wide range of interests, so I think she's someone Milord would get along well with.]","[If you say so, then I definitely want to meet her.]","[Apparently, the discussions with Shallow Vernal have already wrapped up, and she’ll be coming for a formal visit sometime soon. I believe you’ll get to meet her before long.]","Nebula has a sharp eye for people, so if she describes her as \"someone I'd get along with\", I’m sure we’d be a great match personality-wise. I’d definitely like to meet her.","From what she said, it sounds like she’ll be visiting sometime soon, so I’ll be looking forward to that moment.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Up until now, all the information we’ve gotten about that unreasonable Berserk Gorilla has been nothing but anxiety-inducing, and yet here comes the one thing that’s going to skyrocket Kaito’s initial favorability...... \"Nebula’s seal of approval\"...... Isn’t this basically a guaranteed flag that Bipolar God will be able to freely come to Trinia now?]"]},{"number":2321,"title":"Chapter 2321: After the Birthday Party 15","paragraphs":["Nebula had said she'd come to my room one hour after dinner, so I spent the time leisurely writing in my diary and relaxing. Then, just about exactly an hour later, there was a knock at the door.","I answered and opened the door to let Nebula in. At a glance, she seemed to be empty-handed, so the present was probably in her magic box.","[Well then, Milord, please take this seat.]","[Hm? I just need to sit down?]","[Yes. There's no need for suspense, so I'll say it up front: your birthday present from me is a specially blended tea and a single-serving... a No. 3 size cake!]","As she said that, Nebula took out the cake and placed it on the table. It was a palm-sized whole cake, lavishly decorated with fruits. On top, there were sugar figurines shaped like chibi Bell and Lynn, and a message plate to celebrate the birthday. It gave off a very stylish birthday cake vibe.","[Wow, amazing. This really feels like a birthday cake, so colorful and festive that just looking at it makes me happy.]","[I'm glad to hear you like it. That cake wasn’t just made by me, you know. The friend of mine who was visiting also helped out, so please consider it a gift from both of us.]","[That's really kind. When I see her again, I’ll make sure to thank her properly. And thank you too, Nebula.]","[Yes!]","Smiling at my thanks, Nebula placed a fork and other utensils in front of me, then used a pot she took from the magic box to prepare tea with elegant, fluid motions.","She placed the freshly brewed tea in front of me and gave me a sweet, charming smile.","[......A grand and splendid birthday party surrounded by many people is certainly wonderful. It's proof of how deeply you're loved by so many, and the desire to express those feelings in a big way is admirable. But I don't think that modest celebrations are any less meaningful in comparison. What matters most is the sentiment behind them.]","Nebula spoke gently as she inserted a single slender candle into the cake, and with a light flick of her finger, she lit it up.","Then, after a short pause, she looked straight into my eyes and said with a smile:","[......Once again, happy birthday, Milord! I offer my heartfelt blessings for this new year of your life to come...... May it be a joyful and fulfilling one for you.]","[......Thank you, Nebula.]","A small cake and a cup of tea, and a heartfelt blessing that needed no Sympathy Magic to be felt...... yeah, this really was modest. But, just as Nebula had said, the warm joy welling up in my chest now was no less than the happiness I’d felt during the big celebration earlier.","When I blew out the candle, Nebula clapped her small hands, and I felt a faint, tingling warmth in the back of my eyes.","[Thank you so much for this lovely celebration. Well then, I think I’ll go ahead and enjoy the tea and cake you prepared...... but since it’s a special occasion, how about joining me, Nebula?]","There was no problem with the portion size, and enough time had passed since dinner that I could eat it alone without issue. But I was feeling happy and wanted to share that with Nebula if possible.","Hearing my words, Nebula puffed out her chest with a proud and confident air, and opened her mouth to speak.","[I figured Milord would say that...... So I’ve prepared a portion for myself as well!]","With that declaration, Nebula took out a chair sized to fit her small frame, along with a cake and teacup about two sizes smaller than mine.","Apparently, she'd anticipated that I’d invite her to join me, and had made sure to prepare her own cake and tea ahead of time.","[Wow, everything’s perfectly prepared.]","[Of course! I am Absolute after all!!!]","[Ahaha, as expected of Nebula.]","When I reached out to pat Nebula’s head as she proudly puffed out her chest, she narrowed her eyes with a look of bliss. After giving her a few more pats, I turned back to the table and began eating the cake with her.","[......This is insanely good. The fruit tastes amazing, and the tea pairs perfectly with the cake.]","[The fruits in your cake were grown by me in a special space created by Canalis-san. The cake was made entirely by hand, without using any magic. As for the whipped cream, my friend who helped me worked really hard on it, so it turned out incredibly smooth and delicious.]","[Yeah, the texture really is fantastic. But more than that, I can feel how much care went into making everything, and just eating it fills me with happiness.]","[That’s because it’s packed with our heartfelt blessings for Milord!]","Nebula spoke cheerfully with a beaming smile, and I found myself smiling in return. In this peaceful and joyful atmosphere, delicious cake, fragrant tea, and Nebula’s adorable smile...... How should I say this...... I felt truly content and happy, more than words could express.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [As expected of the Absolute...... As a separate celebration from the wild birthday party, this feels like a perfect 100-point gift...... There’s no romantic vibe...... not at this point, but if things were ever to seriously start moving in that direction, I can sense some seriously dangerous potential.]"]},{"number":2322,"title":"Chapter 2322: Phantom Item Rankings 1","paragraphs":["One afternoon, I was leisurely reading the latest magazine. Although only some sections used photos for now, the number of such magazines was increasing, and it felt like they were getting more interesting because of it.","This particular magazine was running a feature on luxury goods...... a kind of theme that was popular even in the world I came from, and this time, it was titled “Rankings of Phantom Items the Average Citizen Can’t Even Lay Eyes On.”","Indeed, looking at these kinds of items is entertaining, and putting them in a ranked format really drives home how impressive they are. Let’s see, now......","“10th Place: Nifty's Teacup (Initial Lot A)”","......Wait a second, that’s something I definitely recognize. Eh? Seriously? I did hear that the early batches, which Nebula was directly involved in producing, were very popular, but I didn’t expect it to be featured as a “phantom item”...... Also, what’s with this “A” at the end? I don’t remember there being such a classification...... Let me read the description.","“A teacup from the earliest release of the high-end tea brand \"Nifty\", which has been featured in this magazine several times. Commonly referred to as the \"Initial Lot\", this series is extremely rare and highly sought after by nobles. On the current market, a set of four cups can go for over 50 white gold coins, making it an item of exceptional value.”","Fifty white gold coins!? I’m pretty sure when they were sold as a limited release in the store, they were going for 12 white gold coins. So the price has quadrupled...... I guess rarity has driven the value up?","“However, even among the rare initial lot, there exists an even more elusive item known as \"Type A\". This is an extremely unique product said to have been sold only in small quantities during Archlesia Empire's Founding Festival, not in Nifty’s regular stores. A distinguishing feature is the brand mark on the back: unlike the later versions which feature three mountains enclosed in a circle, the Type A mark lacks the circle. It’s said that fewer than 10 sets exist worldwide, making this an item truly worthy of being called a phantom item.”","O- Ohh...... Ah, I see now. Come to think of it, the ceramic wares sold at Archlesia Empire’s Founding Festival had temporary branding, so the design was just the three mountains without the circle.","When we created the tea brand, we later revised the logo a bit so it would be easier to print or stamp on things like bags. So, yeah, thinking about it, the ones sold at Archlesia's Founding Festival might really qualify as ultra-rare.","“9th Place: Midnight Diamond”","......Another one I know. Isn’t that the diamond Sela makes? ......Ahhh, but now that I think about it, Sieg-san isn’t a jeweler and doesn’t own a trading company or anything. Probably only someone like Alice, who comes to buy them directly, actually gets any. That definitely makes them rare.","“A gemstone that shows shifting colors within a nighttime-like hue depending on the angle. With its beautiful design that seems to capture the aurora of the night sky, it’s often whispered about among gemstone enthusiasts...... However, its origin is completely unknown, no one knows where it’s mined, and only an extremely small number are said to exist. The gemstone itself is as hard as orichalcum, making it incredibly difficult to process, so many gemstone lovers are curious about where these finely cut examples come from, but so far, no detailed information has ever come to light.”","Hmmm...... could it be that Alice is intentionally withholding information? If people found out that the Midnight Diamond was that expensive, then a flood of customers would likely swarm to Sieg-san, but she doesn’t really seem interested in making money that way...... In fact, even the money she’s received from Alice is more than she knows what to do with, she ends up sending most of it to Rei-san and Fia-san as an allowance. So maybe Alice is keeping the information hidden out of consideration for her.","It’s probably also part of a strategy to only release a tiny number of them into the market. By quietly distributing a few in places outside Symphonia Kingdom, people might assume they’re being mined over there instead......","Still, it’s kind of surprising how many of these items I’m familiar with have shown up in a row...... I guess I have more ties to these so-called “phantom items” than I thought.","“8th Place: Painting – Seven Planet Series”","......And there’s another one I know in 8th place.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [At this rate, I wouldn’t even be surprised if Kaito ends up knowing every single item from 1st to 10th...... Though, I do wonder what’ll be in 1st place. I can guess a few possibilities, like that wine K or something along those lines...... but if you asked me whether that would take the top spot, I’d probably say no.]"]},{"number":2323,"title":"Chapter 2323: Phantom Item Rankings 2","paragraphs":["As for the Seven Planet Series, I’d heard about it through people like Rosemary-san, so I was familiar with the information...... but its placement at 8th was a bit surprising. There are only seven of them in the world...... eight if you count the hidden one, so there are only eight in existence. Their rarity is off the charts, and even Rosemary-san said you couldn’t put a price on them, so I thought it wouldn’t be strange for them to rank higher...... Maybe the ranking isn’t just based on monetary value, but also public recognition.","The Seven Planet Series is more of a \"for those in the know\" kind of item. They might have prioritized items that the average person would feel are “phantom items” near the top of the list.","Thinking about it, if the top-ranked items make readers go “what even is that?”, the magazine might fail to build hype. In that sense, recognizability might also be one of the ranking criteria.","“7th place: Fruit of the World Tree”","Yeah, that one fits. The Fruit of the World Tree is especially well-known by name in the public sphere, but very few have seen the real thing, definitely making it a phantom item.","In terms of actual value, the Seven Planet Series might still be above it, but it really does seem like recognizability is a major factor here too.","“A legendary divine fruit that World King Lillywood Yggdrasil-sama will very rarely bestow upon her dependents and people close to her camp. Said to cure all ailments and even regenerate lost limbs, it’s highly sought after, but virtually never seen on the open market. In the past, it once appeared in an auction held during the Hero Festival, where it fetched a final bid of 560 white gold coins, allegedly won by the head of a major trading company who was suffering from a grave illness.”","Yeah...... I mean, it’s hard to argue with that. I can easily imagine wealthy people desperate for the Fruit of the World Tree. Something that can cure any disease or extend lifespan definitely fits the kind of item the rich would covet.","Same goes for, say, Life-san’s Provisional Blessing, which allows one to revert to their ideal age. I'm sure there are millionaires who would pay any amount to receive it.","“6th place: Shallow Grande”","Sixth place goes to Shallow Grande huh. Right, if I recall, this was the legendary wine that’s generally only distributed once per Festival of Heroes as part of a God Realm-sponsored event. Less than 100 bottles exist in the entire world. Thinking about it that way, its rank makes sense, honestly, even feels like it could’ve been higher based on name recognition alone.","“A supremely rare wine said to have been personally crafted by God of Creation Shallow Vernal-sama, offered as a prize in a God Realm-sponsored event during the Festival of Heroes, distributed only one bottle per festival. There were even wine lovers willing to sell off all their belongings just to taste it...... However, in recent years, due to its limited release during the White God Festival, its rarity has slightly diminished. That said, it’s still a phantom item far beyond the reach of the average person...... And if we’re talking about wine as a category, there exists an even higher-ranked one, so be sure to check out the rest of the list.”","Ah, that makes sense. Its rank dropped due to being sold, in limited quantities it may be, during the White God Festival. Before that, it would probably rank higher...... Still, this phrasing about a wine ranked even higher than Shallow Grande makes me think it’s referring to the one called “K”.","It was given out as a commemorative gift at my birthday party this year, but originally it was something Shiro-san quietly distributed to guests at the housewarming party. Even rarer than Shallow Grande, so there’s no doubt it’s super valuable...... Wouldn’t be surprised to see it in the top three.","“5th place: Sky Castle”","......Unn? Could this be referring to the Sky Castle located in Symphonia's Royal Capital?","“Constructed by the Gods and gifted to Duchess Lilia Albert, a noble of Symphonia Kingdom, it is now a symbol of the Royal Capital itself, an enigmatic castle that floats in the sky. While it’s quite difficult to secure a reservation, it is open to the public as a tourist attraction, meaning that among the items in this ranking, it may be the most accessible to the general public. That said, its value is immense, and it was a special gift granted only because Duchess Albert was the first person in Human history to receive a True Blessing from a Supreme God. It's no exaggeration to call it a phantom item, especially since it’s a structure that current technology and existing materials cannot replicate.”","I see...... So from the public’s perspective, that castle is considered a special present given to Lilia-san after she received her True Blessing...... Now that they mention it, the timeline does roughly match when she received Chronois-san’s True Blessing, so it makes sense in a way.","But this probably came about because Alice tweaked the details to avoid mentioning my name, just patched the info to keep things consistent. I have a feeling Lilia-san might be quietly suffering over it.","That said, it has already been two years since she received the Sky Castle, so Lilia-san seems more or less used to it by now......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I see....... So with Kaito's existence almost completely hidden from the general public, it makes Lilia look like some incredible historical figure who accomplished feats unprecedented in history...... Still the same old stomachache black hole.]"]},{"number":2324,"title":"Chapter 2324: Phantom Item Rankings 3","paragraphs":["I’ve now finished reading up to the 5th-ranked item on the Phantom Items Ranking, and so far, I’ve known all of them. It’s possible the rest of the ranking might be items I’m familiar with too.","“4th place: MK Royale”","Not only do I know this one, it’s one of our products...... I never expected it to beat out things like the Fruit of the World Tree or Shallow Grande and make it into the rankings. That’s a surprise.","“This is the highest-grade tea from the luxury tea brand Nifty, and only one person per month is granted the right to purchase it via lottery, making it an extremely rare tea. While the current ranking reflects its rarity at this moment in time, since even one person a month will be able to purchase it moving forward, its ranking will likely fall in the future.”","Ah, I see, they’re taking period of time into account as well...... Considering the likely timing of this magazine article’s release, it makes sense. Back then, MK Royale had just launched, and its rarity was indeed quite high.","If the supply stabilizes over time, I imagine it’ll settle somewhere below Shallow Grande in the rankings.","“Nifty’s store operates on a strict reservation-only system. That said, as long as you’re willing to wait your turn, anyone can visit. Though it’s a high-end shop, some of their commodities are affordable enough that ordinary citizens can buy them if they stretch a little. Making a purchase even once at a Nifty store will make you eligible for the monthly MK Royale lottery. Of course, since MK Royale is a top-tier product, it’s unlikely the average citizen could afford to buy it even if they win the purchase rights, but those rights can be declined or transferred, and there are many nobles vying for them. So if you do win, it might just be your ticket to a fortune. A magic code for Nifty’s reservation application is included at the end of this issue, so if you’re interested, give it a try.”","The \"magic code\" is sort of like a phone number. You can scan it using a Hummingbird magic tool, which lets you send a Hummingbird message to apply for a reservation.","Incidentally, For those who don’t own a Hummingbird, you can instead apply through the commercial union offices in the cities where Nifty’s stores are located.","“3rd place: Phantom Wine K”","And here it is, Wine K taking the third spot. Its placement higher than Shallow Grande was hinted at earlier, but making it into the top 3 huh......","“Right now, wine lovers all over the world are desperately searching for this rare wine. Like Shallow Grande, it is said to have been created with the involvement of God of Creation Shallow Vernal-sama. Its flavor far surpasses even that of Shallow Grande, and its silver hue, impossible to achieve through normal means, makes it unquestionably a miracle of the Gods. Only a few dozen bottles are believed to exist in the world, and even the empty containers fetch high prices as reference materials.”","In a sense, this item’s 3rd-place ranking may also be due to timing. At the recent birthday party, Wine K was distributed to the guests, so now there are several hundred bottles in existence. Compared to back then, its rarity has definitely decreased.","Still, there’s no denying it’s a precious wine personally crafted by Shiro-san......","“And curiously, the origin of this wine remains unknown. It is said to have been created with the involvement of God of Creation Shallow Vernal-sama and distributed to prestigious individuals such as the Rulers. Because of this, it’s believed to have been handed out during an appropriately prestigious occasion. However, at the time when rumors of this wine first began circulating, there were no notable major events, and so the exact circumstances of its distribution remain unclear. Additionally, the recipients included the Rulers, the Six Kings, and the Six Kings' Executives, individuals of such high standing that interviews were impossible. Even this magazine has been unable to uncover any further details.”","So it’s being considered a “mystery wine of unknown origin” because my involvement has been kept secret...... Well, yeah. No one’s going to imagine it was distributed at a housewarming party for my new place. That’d be unthinkable. Alice and the others have probably also helped with information control, so it makes sense that the details are staying vague.","Well, that’s honestly a relief. I’d rather not cause a stir or have personal details about me published in a magazine. I hope things stay this way.","Anyway, I do seem to know most of the items so far, and at this rate, I might be familiar with whatever’s in 2nd and 1st place too.","Now then, what could 2nd place be......?","“2nd place: Statue of the Winged Gun Rock Dragon”","..............................Ahh~~...... errr...... hold on a second. My heart’s not ready to process this reality just yet.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [What could possibly go through your mind when you’re casually reading a magazine and suddenly see one of your own cringey creations from the past listed as a phantom item......]"]},{"number":2325,"title":"Chapter 2325: Phantom Item Rankings 4","paragraphs":["At first, it was a sad creature born from an attempt to make a dog, but after various twists and turns, it ended up becoming a sacred relic of the Gun Rock Dragon that I apparently made myself.","Personally, it’s a bit of a dark chapter in my past, and after giving it to the Gun Rock Dragon as a gift and getting it out of my hands, I felt relieved...... only to now be seeing it again in a place like this.","I mean, how on earth did that statue get ranked number two!? When you really boil it down, it should only be worth as much as a statue made by an amateur. And yet, it’s ended up in the Phantom Item Ranking...... How?","\"Regarding this 2nd place statue, this article contains the most unclear information, with much of it being mere rumors. We did as much investigative reporting as possible, but there are still many unknowns, so please keep in mind that what you’re reading is based on rumor-level information. The story begins on the first day of the Six Kings Festival, an invitation-only event. While unverified, there is persistent talk that at the time, the Six Kings, the Supreme Gods, Human Realm's three rulers, and even God of Creation Shallow Vernal-sama, along with an Otherworld God, all fought over ownership of a single statue. And that statue is said to have been the very same Winged Gun Rock Dragon.\"","......A- Ahh, I see now. True, it was decided by a game of rock-paper-scissors, but legendary figures like Shiro-san and Makina-san were among those who bet on that statue.","While the general audience had been evacuated outside the venue, that rumor must have spread afterward and elevated the status of the statue to a phantom item huh?","\"The statue that the God of Creation Shallow Vernal-sama is said to have ultimately won ownership of is now strictly preserved in the Gun Rock Dragon’s settlement. How it ended up being passed from Shallow Vernal-sama to the Gun Rock Dragons remains unclear, but there are other strange aspects to this statue’s story. First of all, the identity of the creator is unknown. The statue was made by a challenger during a three-round match with the War King Megiddo-sama. There should have been many spectators at the venue that day...... yet no matter how much we investigated, we couldn’t uncover the details of that opponent. Some say it was a man, others say a woman. Some claim they were Human, while others say Demon. It is suspected that the challenger may have used Recognition Inhibition Magic or Information Concealment Magic.\"","O- Ohhh...... This might be thanks to Alice manipulating the information, but it seems there’s almost no data about me, which was a huge relief.","Even though there were a lot of spectators, the event was primarily attended only by invited guests and their pre-approved companions, so perhaps information control was relatively easy for Alice.","\"Furthermore, there’s yet another strange story that highlights the oddity of this statue. Though this is still at the level of rumor, those who have attempted to investigate the Gun Rock Dragon statue too deeply are said to receive warnings from the Phantasmal King faction. One theory posits that during the conflict over the statue, a kind of agreement or pact was made between the Supreme Gods and the Six Kings, and that this is being deliberately kept secret. As for whether this article received any warning from the Phantasmal King’s faction, or whether it underwent any censorship, that is left up to the reader’s imagination.\"","It's a rather complicated situation, but as a result of the information being concealed...... that statue, and by extension, I, the one who made it, have ended up being treated like some kind of taboo-level urban legend. It’s hard to describe exactly how that makes me feel.","That said, if it were revealed that I was the creator, things would just get even more troublesome, so honestly, I’m grateful the information has been so thoroughly hidden.","“Considering all this information, perhaps this statue ought to have taken the number one spot. However, due to the overwhelming lack of clarity and detail, we ultimately decided to place it at number two. Why did the Gods and the Six Kings clash over the statue? What were the circumstances that led to the God of Creation Shallow Vernal-sama obtaining it? And why is it now stored in the Gun Rock Dragon’s dwelling? Who is the mysterious challenger who created such a statue...... The questions are endless, but the story is filled with a certain romantic allure.”","Well, yeah. If we assume that all information about me at the Six Kings Festival has been perfectly hidden, then there’s no way anyone could reasonably guess why the statue is now in the possession of the Gun Rock Dragons.","It's like one of those “mystery begets mystery” stories...... Though in reality, I just fulfilled my promise to go on a date with Shiro-san, got the statue back, and then, on a whim, gave it as a gift to the Gun Rock Dragon who had won the Dragon Carnival. No trace of “romantic allure” to be found in that reason...... but, well, whatever......","Still, for that sad little creature to become a sacred relic of the Gun Rock Dragons, and now even be called an urban-legend-class phantom item...... Its rise in status is so absurd, I can’t help but look up at the sky in disbelief.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Ah, looks like Alice tweaked the other information related to the Six Kings Festival too, and completely hid anything about Kaito...... The fact that she did it without even telling him, yep, that’s her usual devoted self, alright.]"]},{"number":2326,"title":"Chapter 2326: Phantom Item Rankings 5","paragraphs":["Now then, thanks to that thing being in 2nd place, I ended up feeling like I wanted to brood a little, but let’s pull ourselves together and take a look at 1st place.","Just what could possibly be at the very top of the Phantom Items Ranking......?","\"1st Place: The Eternal Flower\"","O- Ohh...... I see. That’s the direction they went with it, huh. Now that they mention it, I can definitely see why. It’s the flower I obtained during the White God Festival and gave to Rosemary-san.","Come to think of it, Sky-san did say back then that it was “bestowed to only a select few”, so its rarity might indeed be quite something.","\"For many readers, it is probably still fresh in their memory, the first White God Festival ever to be spearheaded by the Gods themselves and held in the God Realm. Since it was a large-scale festival in a place that’s normally difficult even to enter, it’s said that over a billion people visited the festival grounds, making it a truly bustling event. And among all that, the most valuable prize of the festival was this Eternal Flower. These flowers were given by none other than the God of Creation Shallow Vernal-sama as prizes for a quiz about the Gods, held in the restricted-access middle layer of the God Realm, and only three blossoms in total were bestowed. They are special flowers that never wither.\"","In other words, excluding those in the Sanctuary, there are only three of these flowers in existence in the entire world...... If that’s the case, their rarity is indeed insane. And if it’s an item connected to Shiro-san herself, the level of buzz around it would be extraordinary, so I can understand why it took 1st place.","\"This Eternal Flower blooms only in the Sanctuary where the God of Creation Shallow Vernal-sama resides, a special place said to be inaccessible to anyone but the Supreme Gods. Naturally, very few have ever even seen the Eternal Flower, making it truly a phantom item, and it is impossible to attach any sort of monetary value to it. Due to its rarity, a special Information Concealment Magic was cast by the Gods on those who won the Eternal Flower in the quiz, and it is completely unknown who obtained the three blossoms.\"","Special Information Concealment Magic...... so that’s what they did...... Well, I suppose it makes sense, flowers from the Sanctuary would have unimaginable value, and since the prize was given out through a four-choice quiz that theoretically anyone could win, if an ordinary person got one and ended up being targeted for robbery or even murder, it would be a disaster, so I guess such a measure was necessary.","\"Through our magazine’s thorough investigation, we have discovered that, through circumstances we do not know of, one of the flowers is in the Rose Princess Rosemary-sama’s Garden of Myriad Flowers, and another is in the most secure vault of the Central Cathedral in Friendship City Hikari. However, the whereabouts of the third blossom remain unknown. Furthermore, since the Eternal Flower in the Central Cathedral is not on display, we speculate that it is being safeguarded out of fear of theft, and that it is therefore unlikely to be the personal property of the Cathedral’s priests or clerics.\"","I didn’t know about the one in the Central Cathedral. But indeed, if it had been obtained by a priest or someone similar, there’s a possibility they might display it...... Could it be possible that Olivia-san was the one who got it? She did attend the White God Festival, and she was in the middle layer, so there’s a chance she could have seen the quiz contest after her prayers and decided to participate.","Since it's Olivia-san, she'd probably be strong in topics related to the Gods, and for someone as devout as her, a flower from Shiro-san’s Sanctuary would absolutely be something she’d want. On top of that, if Olivia-san had obtained it, she strikes me as the type who wouldn’t boast about it or put it on display, but rather use it for her personal prayers, so their theory actually fits quite well.","\"As for the one owned by Rosemary-sama, the Garden of Myriad Flowers itself is such a legendary place that it is called the Phantom Garden, and it can be said that it is essentially impossible for ordinary people to visit. Therefore, seeing the Eternal Flower there would be extremely difficult. As for the last blossom, given that its whereabouts are still unknown at the time of writing this article, it is believed that it will not be publicly displayed in the future either, making it a flower truly worthy of being called a phantom item that ordinary people will never have the chance to see. That said, while they are different from the Eternal Flower, there are reports that three other types of flowers from the Sanctuary were specially displayed during the White God Festival. Therefore, there remains a possibility that they could be displayed again at future White God Festivals. Whether or not you can participate in the middle-layer events, which have a strict attendance limit, largely depends on luck, but if you’re interested, you might as well apply for the lottery to enter the middle layer at the next White God Festival.\"","Looking at the overall ranking, I can’t help but feel that, from a worldwide perspective, the God of Creation Shiro-san enjoys overwhelming popularity, and that any item connected to her is generally regarded as having incredible value.","The same goes for things like the Shallow Grande and K, and if the ranking’s scope had been broader, I think Glorious Tea might have also made the list.","Well, in any case, though I got unexpectedly stabbed by my own dark history partway through, it turned out to be quite an enjoyable ranking.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [If anything, the magazine’s investigative ability is amazing...... they actually managed to track down that one of them is in the Garden of Myriad Flowers.]","? ? ? : [Well, if you’re under the World King’s command and have a certain level of familiarity with Rosemary-san, you can enter the Garden of Myriad Flowers, and it’s not like Rosemary-san herself is hiding it. She’s one of the strongest people in the world and a master of Barrier Magic, so there’s practically no need to worry about theft.]","Serious-senpai : [I see. By the way, who got the last blossom? You’d know, right?]","? ? ? : [......I’m thinking I might eventually display it somewhere under a different name and charge admission.]","Serious-senpai : [It was with you!?]"]},{"number":2327,"title":"Chapter 2327: Phantom Item Rankings 6","paragraphs":["The \"Phantom Item Rankings\" was something I happened to see in a magazine, but I ended up enjoying the article quite a bit, and it got me thinking about something. I figured it might be a good time for a break and a cup of tea, and the timing felt just right.","As I thought that, I stood in front of the gate-shaped magic tool, something you could already call a divine artifact, in my room and lightly touched the gate. The destinations I had registered appeared in the air, so I selected the Sanctuary and stepped through the opened gate to move there.","[Fumu, and what connection do I have to this ranking?]","[Ah, no, that's not it. I came to see you because Shiro-san thought I’d finally try the black tea I got at the birthday party...... You know, since we promised to drink it together.]","[I see.]","Shiro-san-san tilted her head in curiosity when she greeted me, but she seemed to understand quickly and conjured up a table and chairs. I took the black tea plant I’d received for my birthday out from my magic box.","It was a mysterious kind of tea that, when harvested, would automatically dry and become tea leaves......","[By the way, is there anything I should be careful about when brewing this? I’m not exactly confident in my tea-making skills......]","[Then I’ll brew it. It was a gift, after all. I’d like you to enjoy it in its best form.]","[Thank you, that really helps.]","Access to the Sanctuary is tightly restricted, or rather, even if Shiro-san herself doesn’t mind that much, the Gods around her are extremely particular about it, so asking someone like Illness-san to come make the tea wouldn’t really be an option...... Although someone like Canalis-san, who’s roughly on equal footing with Shiro-san, might be able to come, but since Shiro-san is willing to brew the tea herself, there's absolutely no issue.","I could’ve also stored the brewed tea in a pot and kept it in my magic box, but I’d come to the Sanctuary on a whim without any preparations, so Shiro-san’s offer was a real lifesaver.","With a light wave of her finger, the tea leaves floated from my hand, and various tea-making tools appeared. In the blink of an eye, everything was ready.","[Now then, here you go.]","[Thank you very much.]","At a glance, the color looked no different from ordinary black tea. The aroma...... had a slightly refreshing quality? Not quite like herbal tea, but there was a certain cool, clean scent to it.","Thinking that, I took a sip right away......","[O- Ohh...... wow, this is amazing. It’s incredibly refreshing. Even though it’s a hot tea, it leaves an aftertaste like iced tea...... I think I really like this kind of flavor.]","How should I put it? It had an incredibly refreshing mouthfeel. It wasn’t like menthol or mint with that sharp coolness, but rather it was light on the palate and very pleasant.","The flavor was also excellent, and personally, I really liked it. It felt like the kind of tea I could drink endlessly, perfect for that first cup in the morning, or after a heavy-tasting meal. It would be absolutely ideal in either case.","[I’m glad you like it, Kaito-san. I created it with the idea of making something unlike any other tea. I also received various pieces of advice from Nebula, so it’s not purely my own work but......]","[But knowing Nebula’s personality, she probably didn’t give you all the answers, just some advice and guidance, right? Which means the one who thought through everything and actually created this is you, Shiro-san. That honestly makes me really happy.]","[Fufu, just hearing you say that makes it all worthwhile.]","Sure, Nebula's advice must’ve played a part, but more than anything, Shiro-san put a lot of thought into my tastes and preferences when she made this...... According to what I heard from Kuro, she had been testing and refining different versions of it for quite some time, so knowing she went to all that effort just for me made it all the more meaningful.","When I expressed those feelings honestly, Shiro-san smiled softly, and a gentle breeze brushed against my cheek, accompanied by a faint \"Doyaa~~\" echoing in my ears...... I see. So instead of using 3D text this time, she conveyed her smugness with sound. A new type of doya pattern, I'm impressed.","Well, if anything, that’s very much like Shiro-san...... Thinking that, I smiled and continued enjoying a pleasant teatime with Shiro-san.","[......Ahh, right. My main reason for coming was to have tea with Shiro-san, but while I’m here, though I'm iffy to call it an extra, I actually have a favor to ask, Shiro-san...... The truth is......]","[......I don’t mind. All of it?]","[Ah, no, just this section is fine for now. It’s pretty expansive enough after all.]","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Doya Wind...... Well, putting that aside, he's asking Shiro for a favor?]"]},{"number":2328,"title":"Chapter 2328: Phantom Item Rankings 7","paragraphs":["Using the Teleportation Magic Tool, I moved to the front of Yggfresis, Demon Realm. There, I held up my card-based permit, and an entrance appeared before me, to which I passed through.","What awaited beyond was the Garden of Myriad Flowers, where Rosemary-san lived. I had contacted her beforehand about the visit, so she was waiting near the entrance to greet me.","[Hello, Rosemary-san. Sorry for the sudden visit today.]","[Hello, Kaito-kun. Don’t worry about it. If it’s Kaito-kun, you’re welcome anytime.]","Since it had been more of a sudden whim, I’d only confirmed her schedule yesterday before deciding to visit today. Despite the abruptness, Rosemary-san welcomed me with a gentle smile.","As we walked toward Rosemary-san’s home, we engaged in a bit of light conversation.","[By the way, thank you for the birthday party, Rosemary-san.]","[Not at all. I was nervous with so many strangers, but I had a lot of fun. Still, Kaito-kun, after that extravagant ship party, now such an incredible birthday party too, you’ve been busy.]","[Yeah, the gap between the ship party and the birthday party wasn’t that long. Well, for the birthday one, I was the one being celebrated, so I didn’t do much prep myself...... but having two gatherings where top figures from around the world show up in such a short time, even I think it’s kind of insane.]","[Fufufu, it really is. Normally, you’d never get a group like that together. It just shows how popular you are, Kaito-kun. That’s pretty amazing, but I bet it’s also exhausting for you, being at the center of it all.]","Now that she mentioned it, there has been a lot happening lately, the ship party, the opening of the brand store, the birthday party......","But well, even if things were a bit chaotic, I honestly enjoyed all of it, so there was no problem.","While chatting about such things, we arrived at Rosemary-san’s home. After being prompted to take a seat, Rosemary-san began preparing tea and spoke up.","[By the way, what brings you here today, exactly? Not that you need a reason, if you came just to hang out, I’d be happy either way.]","[Ahh, actually, there’s something I wanted to show you...... Errr, you know about recorder magic tools, right?]","[Unn. They’re getting quite popular, and I’ve been seeing more photos in magazines and such. They’re amazing. It’s different from artwork, but being able to capture scenery with such accuracy is incredible. Art has its charm, and so do photos, neither is better than the other, but being able to see places you’ve never visited in such detail is a wonderful thing.]","Although Rosemary-san is extremely shy, she opens up quite a bit with those she trusts. She even gave her own thoughts on recorder magic tools.","Well, considering they’ve become such a global phenomenon as a groundbreaking technology, I figured she’d know about them. Still, I was relieved that the conversation would go smoothly.","[Yes, it’s those magic tools. I actually own the latest version, since I’m involved with making the Nifty booklets.]","[Ah, right, they do use photos in those. The articles are really interesting, I look forward to them every month.]","Strictly speaking, I keep up with the newest versions of the recorder magic tools because of a promise I made with Alyssa, but that doesn’t mean they’re exclusively hers, I use them regularly too. When I summon Alyssa with Αναμνήσεις, I let her use it first, but otherwise, I use it to take photos myself.","[I think the one making the booklet will be happy to hear that...... So, about the recorder magic tool, it can capture scenery very accurately.]","[Unn.]","[And, since you mentioned before that you wanted to see Sanctuary’s flower fields, I asked permission from Shiro-san and took some photos for you......]","[ ! ? ! ? ]","Yes, the reason I came today was to show Rosemary-san the photos of Sanctuary's flower fields that I had asked Shiro-san for permission to take.","When I saw that Eternal Flower had appeared in the rankings, I remembered how Rosemary-san had once said she wanted to see Sanctuary's flower fields. It would be difficult for her to actually visit, but I figured if I could show her photos, that might be enough.","Upon hearing my words, Rosemary-san whipped around with great energy, speaking to me with an excited tone.","[S- Sanctuary's flower fields!? I- I want to see them! Can I?!]","[Ah, yes. Not the entire Sanctuary, but I was allowed to photograph the flower fields in the area where Shiro-san usually has tea. I had them developed and brought them with me.]","[T- Thank you! Kaito-kun!!!]","[Eh? Wait, whoa!?]","Overcome with emotion, Rosemary-san suddenly jumped into my arms. I reflexively caught her, startled by the sudden move...... Whoa, her waist is so slim, her body so soft, and she smells like roses...... I could tell just how excited she was, but the surprise hit me so hard, my brain couldn’t quite catch up right away.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Huh? Why are you just using the title as-is and seamlessly diving into flirting!?]","? ? ? : [......Is seamlessly even the right word in this context?]","Serious-senpai : [Shut up!!!]"]},{"number":2329,"title":"Chapter 2329: Phantom Item Rankings 8","paragraphs":["It may have been a completely spur-of-the-moment idea born from the fact that the Eternal Flower ranked first in the Phantom Item Rankings, but taking photos of Sanctuary’s flower field seemed to have made Rosemary-san very happy. So much so, in fact, that in a burst of excitement she impulsively hugged me, an unexpected incident.","When something like that comes at you completely out of nowhere, it leaves a strong impression along with the surprise, so even after Rosemary-san came to her senses a moment later and hurriedly stepped away, I still somehow felt the lingering sensation of her soft body.","Well, I decided not to dwell on that too much and instead focused on looking at the photos of the Sanctuary’s flower field again.","[I’m so excited! Sanctuary’s flower field...... I’d only heard about it from Kaito-kun, and imagined it in my head, so I’m really happy I actually got to see it for myself.]","[I’m glad you’re happy. W- Well then, I’ll get the photos out.]","[Mm!]","......Isn’t she a bit close? Her face is right next to mine...... Errr, so this is...... not the kind of setup where I put the photos on the table and Rosemary-san picks them up, but rather, I’m holding the photos and she’s leaning in to see them directly from my hand?","Rosemary-san has this habit of her sense of personal space breaking down a bit with people she trusts, so right now she’s got one hand resting toward me and is peering down at my hands with a cheerful look.","She’s probably not even aware of it, but her face is so close it’s practically right beside mine, and her body is pressing lightly against my back. How should I say this...... I can tell exactly which parts of her are touching me, and that’s making me weirdly tense.","A- Anyway, let’s just hurry up and show the photos......","[T- This is Sanctuary’s flower field I’ve dreamed about...... Woooow, it’s so beautiful! And every flower here doesn’t exist in either the Human Realm or the Demon Realm, and they’re all so beautiful they almost seem to be shining!]","[Y- Yeah, that’s right. Um, Rosemary-san, your face is a bit......]","[Ah! This! This is the flower you told me about before, isn’t it, Kaito-kun?!]","[Ah, y- yes, that’s right.]","......It’s basically like she’s hugging me from behind now!? Our cheeks are so close they’re practically touching. Honestly, Rosemary-san is completely defenseless and her sense of distance is so out of whack with people she trusts that it’s worrying.","What’s more, she seems to be having this closeness unconsciously, as there have been a few times in the past when I’ve pointed it out, and she’d usually blush and hurriedly step away...... But right now, she seems so excited from seeing her long-admired Sanctuary’s flower field that she’s not really listening to what I’m saying.","And while she herself might not think so, Rosemary-san is incredibly beautiful. She has shining golden hair with soft, loose curls, stunning red eyes, and remarkably well-proportioned features. At first glance she gives off the impression of a noble, sharp-looking beauty, but she’s also shy and has this side of her that feels like a cute little animal, and often shows a gentle expression to those she trusts. That combination makes her come across as a beautiful and kind yet adorably charming older-sister type.","And of course, maybe because she’s a Rose Spirit, she smells wonderfully of roses, so when she’s this close, my heart can’t help but race.","[Kaito-kun, which flower do you like? For me...... From just a glance, I think I like this red one.]","[Ah, it’s gorgeous and beautiful. The shape is different, but it has a bit of a rose-like feel to it, so I like it quite a lot too.]","[I see, it makes me happy that you like the same one as me. I don’t know, it’s like sharing this happy feeling with you makes me feel a bit giddy. Just being able to look at Sanctuary’s flower field together with Kaito-kun, who I like so much, already makes me happy, but when we find little things we have in common, it feels like a small bonus that makes me even happier.]","She’s probably just completely caught up in the excitement and the wonder of the flower field, with almost no deeper meaning behind it, but hearing her say she likes me so naturally still takes me by surprise.","Or rather, so this is what Rosemary-san is like when her excitement peaks, even though her sense of personal space is already a bit broken on a normal day...... she’s pressing up against me even more than before, and now our cheeks are completely touching. Isn’t her guard way too low!?","I mean, I do get that it’s probably just because she’s extremely shy and only lets a very small number of people get this close, but guys can be pretty simple creatures. At this kind of distance, it’s dangerously easy to start misunderstanding and think that Rosemary-san might actually like me in that way.","Well, I’m pretty sure she does like me in the sense of the word......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [They’re flirting about three times more than I imagined!? And I’m pretty sure, no, without a doubt, that’s not just \"like\", that’s more \"love\" kind of feel!!!]","? ? ? : [It’s true that with people like Camellia-san or anyone she’s comfortable with, she tends to close the physical distance, but with Kaito-san in particular, there’s also their personality compatibility and the fact that she enjoys talking to him. She already had a good impression of him and was interested in him, and on top of that, there’s that massive Spirit Favorability Boost constantly stacking.....]","Serious-senpai : [Oh right, there was that hellish system where, if someone of the Spirit Race likes you, a favorability boost for the Spirits in their entirety applies...... Since he's been racking up favorability with other Spirits like Jutia, Rosemary’s favorability has been going up too......]"]},{"number":2330,"title":"Chapter 2330: Phantom Item Rankings 9","paragraphs":["Rosemary-san was thoroughly enjoying the photos of Sanctuary's flower fields, talking about all sorts of topics with far more enthusiasm than usual.","That was great, really great, but my attention kept drifting toward how unexpectedly close we were physically. I couldn’t really focus on the conversation, and in the end, all I could do was wait for her excitement to settle down a bit.","After a while, I felt like her mood had calmed from its peak, so I took the chance to speak.","[......Umm, Rosemary-san. I’m really happy that you’re delighted about it, but I feel like you’re a bit too close. Could you maybe move back just a little......?]","[Ah, s- sorry!? I got so caught up in the moment I didn’t even notice. Are you okay, Kaito-kun? You weren’t uncomfortable or anything, were you?]","[No, I’m fine. If you were so delighted that you'd be engrossed looking at them, then that makes me happy too.]","Rosemary-san hurriedly moved away, but this wasn’t the first time something like this had happened...... In situations like these, she would usually seem flustered or embarrassed, but she almost always asked if I was alright, never showing the slightest sign of concern about having been pressed up against me herself.","In fact, I got the impression that Rosemary-san didn’t mind being physically close to me at all, rather, she seemed to think that distance between us was just perfectly natural...... This girl, her guard is way too relaxed once she’s comfortable with someone. The barriers before reaching that stage are absurdly high, but once you’re past them, her level of trust is incredible.","[But you really do love flowers, don’t you, Rosemary-san?]","[Unnn. I guess it’s because I’m a Flower Spirit? Seeing flowers blooming beautifully and vibrantly just makes me feel so happy. I also love how each flower has a different mood or atmosphere. For example, the flowers in the Sanctuary flower fields have this mystical, almost noble air about them, though I’m not sure if that’s the right way to describe flowers.]","[Hehh, maybe it’s because they grow in the place where Shiro-san lives. Though according to Shiro-san, she just plants them on a whim without much thought.]","[Fumu fumu. Have there been any new flowers recently?]","[Apparently about three kinds. Ah, these flowers in this part of the photo are ones she just added recently. The rest are in another area entirely.]","[Come to think of it, the Sanctuary has a lot of flowers outside of these flower fields too, right? I’d love to hear more about that...... Ah, s- sorry! I haven’t even served you tea yet...... Just a moment.]","Speaking of which, she had leapt onto me in the middle of preparing tea. Rosemary-san quickly moved away and promptly prepared some black tea, setting it in front of me.","[Thank you. By the way, Rosemary-san, about these photos of Sanctuary's flower fields...... would you like them?]","[Eh? I- I can have them? These are incredibly valuable, you know!?]","[Yes. I can see them directly, after all, and I got permission for these photos. Well, to be honest, Shiro-san probably doesn’t care in the slightest, but I figured the ones who might care would be the Gods.]","[U- Unn, that makes sense. After all, no one except the Supreme Gods can enter the Sanctuary. I’m sure there are plenty of Gods who are like me, wanting to see the place but never can.]","Since they were precious photos of Sanctuary's flower fields, I’d planned to give them to her if she wanted them. Still, the Sanctuary was an extremely special place, so I made sure to get confirmation beforehand for anyone who might take issue with it.","[And so, I also checked with Chronois-san, Fate-san, and Life-san, and they said that as long as you don't show them to anyone else, it’s fine to give them away. So if it’s just for you to look at personally, Rosemary-san, there shouldn’t be any problem.]","By the way, when I asked each of them, Chronois-san said \"The photos themselves belong to Miyama, and the right to decide what to do with them is yours. However, I wouldn't guarantee that others won’t come pressing the recipient to let them see, so you should impose them a restriction against showing them to others\". Indeed, if people knew Rosemary-san had photos of the Sanctuary, many would want to visit her to see them, and with how averse of strangers Rosemary-san was, that would only trouble her, so that restriction was essential.","Fate-san’s response was more along the lines of \"Eh, Kai-chan can just do whatever you want, right?\", and Life-san said \"If Shallow Vernal-sama has granted permission, then I have nothing to say...... but to avoid confusion, I believe a restriction should be attached.\"","After I explained all this to Rosemary-san, she smiled happily.","[Thank you. Of course, I’m really happy to get photos of Sanctuary's flower fields, but even more than that, I’m so happy you thought everything through for my sake, Kaito-kun.]","The smile she gave me as she said that radiated such genuine happiness that it was almost dazzling.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Eh? Wait, is it just me, or does it feel like the Rosemary route has already started? It’s like the romance progress is speeding along......]","Makina : [No, if that were the case, the title would change to a special one, right? So I think this is just the usual pace.]","Serious-senpai : [If this is the usual pace, that’s downright terrifying!]"]},{"number":2331,"title":"Chapter 2331: Intermission: Preparing for the Promised Tea Party","paragraphs":["In one of the rooms of Hamilton Marquisdom in Archlesia Empire, a room whose frequency of use had recently increased for important discussions, were Eris and the Hamilton Marquis couple, with a large number of documents placed on the table.","[We’ve narrowed the candidates down to some extent, but once you include the investigation materials and such, it’s enormous.]","[Ahh, but we absolutely cannot afford any oversight in this matter. The Hamilton Marquisdom has mobilized all its resources to thoroughly go over the information. Given that, this amount of material is unavoidable.]","Marquis Hamilton gave a grave nod, taking one sheet from the stack of documents on the desk. Listed there were the names of every noble in Archlesia Empire, not only the heads of houses, but also heirs, other children, and even those only recently born, as many names as could be recorded, with several of them marked.","[......Then, let’s carry out the final selection of the young ladies and gentlemen from noble houses to be invited to the tea party planned for Kaito-sama.]","[I’d be more at ease if we could choose purely based on character, but we also have to thoroughly check their backgrounds since we don’t know who might be backing them.]","[Given the horizontal and vertical connections in noble society, there will inevitably be requests that are hard to refuse. We should examine even the small possibilities.]","At those words, the Hamilton Marquis couple also wore serious expressions as they scrutinized the documents. Yes, what they were now doing was the final selection of guests to be invited to the tea party promised to Kaito some time ago.","Enough days had passed since the initial promise that they wanted to move to the stage of sending invitations, but given the situation, the participants had to be chosen carefully.","From the start, they had decided to exclude heads of noble houses, planning to invite only a small number of heirs and heiresses, but because of Kaito’s tremendous influence, there was a need to counter nobles who would try various means to take advantage of it.","[Father, what shall we do about attendants?]","[......We can’t exactly refuse them, but if we allow them just as we usually do, some will surely take advantage of it.]","In the context of a noble’s tea party, an “attendant” essentially means a bodyguard. Rather than waiting outside in a carriage or the like, this refers to a bodyguard who waits inside the tea party venue, and is described as an “a person who accompanies the attendee”.","The reason is simple: calling them a “guard” would cause friction and give the impression that one does not trust the noble who issued the invitation or the security of the venue, so the term “attendant” is used instead.","[If we prohibit attendants, there will be nobles who complain, asking what we would do if something happened. It’s absurd, especially when they’re not even the ones invited to the tea party......]","[Well, noble society is built on mutual checks and balances. There are those tiresome people who only think of making trouble, but such checks are also part of what keeps the balance. In any case, we should take precautions against any points that could become unnecessary weaknesses.]","If attendants were allowed without any restrictions, as in an ordinary tea party, there would be the possibility of nobles being brought along as “attendants”.","While in most cases the attendant would indeed be a bodyguard, there is no explicit rule that they must be a bodyguard, which means this loophole could be exploited.","[......Would it be best to limit attendants to non-nobles?]","[I suppose so. It would be unusual, but that way, it wouldn’t look like we were banning guards outright. Some will still complain, but it will be easier to answer them.]","[Even if it’s a misunderstanding, there is a perception that Kaito-sama dislikes nobles, so those who receive the invitation might be more willing to accept it.]","It was decided to add the line proposed by the Marchioness Hamilton, that attendants be limited to non-nobles, to the invitations, and the discussion then moved on to what could be called the main topic: choosing whom to invite.","[......When inviting young ladies, we should exclude those who might harbor ulterior motives. Would it be ideal to choose those who are already engaged?]","[However, in that case, wouldn’t there be a possibility of trouble if Kaito-sama were to take an interest in one of the young ladies?]","[Hmmm...... Given Kaito-sama’s personality, I think it’s extremely unlikely he would desire a noble lady as a mistress.]","[I see. In that regard, Eris, who has direct dealings with Kaito-sama, would understand his thinking better, so please disregard my previous statement.]","After confirming that Marchioness Hamilton nodded in agreement at Eris’s words, Marquis Hamilton also spoke.","[Are there any promising young men?]","[Well...... among those close in age to Kaito-sama, many have already inherited their titles or hold positions at the Imperial Castle, and aside from that, there are hardly any who have ties to the Hamilton Marquisdom and whom I can judge to be without character issues. Father, do you have any candidates?]","[No. If we exclude heads of noble houses as well as those who are not heads but hold some position as nobles, there are indeed few candidates. There are some who seem to have no character problems, but they belong to different factions...... Even if this is, in the end, a tea party hosted by you personally, Eris, inviting them would be difficult...... Depending on the situation, it could be taken as trying to entice them to switch factions with a tea party with Miyama Kaito as bait.]","[I see...... In that case, it seems we really will be focusing on young ladies.]","This tea party was, at least in name, unrelated to noble connections, a tea party Eris would hold with friends she had personal ties to...... so there were restrictions on whom she could invite.","Within those limits, she had to choose people who would likely get along with Kaito and had no personality issues, while also preparing for interference from other nobles, making the task quite difficult.","Just like that, for a while, the three members of the Hamilton Marquisdom continued their serious discussion, deciding on the guests for the tea party.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [Now, just a pinch of a body blow to the stomach......]","Serious-senpai : [Oi oi oi oi oi oi oi oi oi oi oi oi, we’re talking about a young lady who got beaten to a pulp at the birthday party and then took a stomachache right after the party, yeah? And now you want to go for another follow-up punch to the stomach? Isn’t she just way too pitiful?]","Stomachache Devil : [All that’s happening is the episode where she invites someone to the tea party she had promised long ago. She just has to invite and treat her guests normally.]","Serious-senpai : [Nah nah nah nah nah nah nah nah nah nah nah nah nah, just treat her normally, you say...... You’ve got a visible landmine, no, a visible napalm bomb called \"attendant\" sitting right there. Plus, Eris has been taking stomachaches nonstop since her introduction. She’s way too pitiful, she deserves some mercy, right? And it’s not just this matter, there’s still the event where she’s going to visit Kaito’s home in the future. The stomachache Eris is going to go through from here on is unimaginable!!!]","Stomachache Devil : [If her stomach is pitiful, why so punchable?]","Serious-senpai : [That’s why I like you.]"]},{"number":2332,"title":"Chapter 2332: The Promised Tea Party 1","paragraphs":["As usual, I received the letters that Anima had neatly sorted and brought to me, and among them was one from Eris-san. It was in a rather sturdy, high-quality envelope, and when I opened it, it turned out to be an invitation.","Ahhh, this must be for the tea party she mentioned back when we first met, when I told her I’d like to attend one someday, and she said she’d arrange an opportunity for me eventually......","Along with the invitation, there was a letter containing details about the tea party, so I read through it...... Errr, the location is the Hamilton Marquisdom’s villa, and it seems the tea party will mainly consist of young nobles who are not heads of their households or high-ranking officials.","Her leaving out the heads of the noble families, I guess this is her being considerate toward me? Eris-san is amazing when it comes to that sort of thoughtfulness, so I imagine she’s also made various other arrangements so that a tea party novice like me won’t have any trouble.","While reading, I came across a line that caught my attention.","\"Additionally, only one attendant is permitted, and for this tea party, nobles will not be recognized as attendants. Please bring a non-noble attendant.\"","Attendant? Do noble tea parties normally allow people to bring attendants? Ahh, maybe it’s for cases where someone brings their betrothed. Nobles being engaged to someone isn’t unusual, and the hosting noble might not necessarily know both parties, so that kind of consideration could be necessary.","Since it says nobles are excluded this time, I guess normally nobles are allowed......","Or maybe this is another kindness on Eris-san’s part, since I’m inexperienced with tea parties and won’t know anyone besides her, she might have made it so I can bring along someone I’m familiar with.","In that case, maybe I should also bring someone along...... it would also feel safer...... But nobles are out huh...... If nobles were allowed, the best choice would be to have Lilia-san come with me but......","Lilia-san is well-versed in noble tea parties, and she said she got to know Eris-san at the previous party, so she’d be ideal...... but with nobles banned, that’s not an option.","[Hmmm......]","[Kaito-kun! I came to visit~~]","[Oh, Kuro, welcome. You came at noon today, that’s unusual.]","[Unn. The development of the new instant products has finally settled down, so I have a lot more free time lately. Arehh? Kaito-kun, is that an invitation?]","Kuro, who had come to visit, tilted her head when she saw the fancy envelope in my hand. Come to think of it, it’s kind of similar to the one I got from Seditch Magic Tool Company for the barbecue invitation. I guess there’s a certain standard format for invitation envelopes.","[Yeah, it’s an invitation from Eris-san for a tea party. I’ve been wanting to attend one for a while...... And it seems I can bring one attendant, but perhaps out of consideration towards me, nobles aren’t allowed, so Lilia-san’s not an option. I’m trying to figure out who I should bring instead.]","[Hehh, then how about I go with you?]","[Eh? You, Kuro?]","[Unn. I met Eris-chan at your birthday party before, and we got along pretty well.]","[Ahh, I see...... In that case, I guess I’d like to ask you to come with me.]","It seemed that Kuro had met Eris-san at the party and at least knew her by face. In that case, from Eris-san’s perspective, bringing Kuro, someone she was already acquainted with, would be easier than having to deal with a complete stranger, and for me, having Kuro along would be reassuring as well.","[Unn, leave it to me. I know the World Coordinates for Hamilton Marquisdom’s estate, so I can just use Teleportation Magic to take us there.]","[By the way, Kuro, have you ever been to a noble tea party before?]","[Hmmm...... not really. I do get invited to parties sometimes, but tea parties? Almost never. The only ones I’ve attended would be the ones Lillywood hosts after the Harmonic Symphony. I do have tea with Chris sometimes, but I wouldn't really call that a tea party.]","[Hehh, so this might be kind of a fresh experience for you too.]","[Yeah. But I’m fairly familiar with a lot of nobles because of business connections, so there might be a few people I know there. Well, either way, if I’m with Kaito-kun, it’ll be fun, so I’m already looking forward to it.]","I smiled back at Kuro, who was grinning cheerfully. In the end, having my girlfriend Kuro attend the tea party with me was something I truly appreciated, and I had a feeling we’d enjoy ourselves, so I was already starting to look forward to it.","<Afterword>","~ ~ This Chapter's Summary ~ ~","Baby Castella Demon : [So, it’s going to be a body-blow after all...... When do we depart? I’ll come along too.]","Stomachache Devil : [Stomachache Culprit, leading one to the Stomachache Hospital.]"]},{"number":2333,"title":"Chapter 2333: The Promised Tea Party 2","paragraphs":["In the room of Eris, the heir to Hamilton Marquisdom, she sat quietly in a chair, deep in thought. Invitations had already been sent to the selected noble youths, including Kaito, and it could be said that the die had been cast.","Even so, Kaito was far too formidable an individual to approach without caution, and Eris genuinely wanted to prepare as much as possible.","(......As I thought, the main concern should be the matter of his attendant. First, I need to consider whether Kaito-sama knows the significance of an attendant at a noble tea party...... Honestly, this is my own oversight. If I had casually brought it up during our past conversations, mentioning that attendants at such events are mainly meant to be guards, then I wouldn’t have to worry about this now. But of course, I can’t go so far as to insert an explanation of “what an attendant means” into the invitation. Doing so would surely give some people the excuse to gleefully accuse me of treating Kaito-sama as ignorant or being discourteous. And even setting that aside, it would simply be rude.)","Eris was intelligent enough to consider the possibility that Kaito might not fully understand the meaning of “attendant” in the context of a noble tea party. However, if there was also the possibility that he had learned it from someone like Lilia, then assuming he didn’t know and explaining it outright would be disrespectful. She regretted not having subtly confirmed it in earlier conversations.","(Well, it’s too late for that now, so I should prepare for both possibilities. If Kaito-sama does know the meaning, then there’s likely no problem. In that case, the most likely attendants would be Anima-sama, his Head Retainer; Illness-sama, a capable maid and one I heard was also his lover; and Sieglinde-sama, who serves as Duchess Lilia’s guard and should be well-versed in noble functions...... These three would be strong candidates.)","Since this was Kaito’s first noble tea party, Eris predicted that he would most likely choose either someone knowledgeable about noble culture or someone he relied on emotionally.","(And the real issue is the scenario where he doesn’t know the meaning of an attendant...... Ideally, I would have liked to make an exception, allowing only Kaito-sama to bring a noble. In that case, he would almost certainly choose Duchess Lilia, which would put my mind at ease. However, if she were to attend a tea party, one specifically excluding heads of noble houses and those with official posts, it could be taken as favoritism toward the Albert Duchy. Even if it’s a tea party I am personally hosting, it is still connected to the Hamilton Marquisdom. As the leader of a faction, the Hamiltondom must avoid creating a situation where it looks like we are blatantly favoring nobles from another country, as that could damage the faction’s standing.)","Personally, Eris would have been grateful if Lilia could attend as Kaito’s attendant, but from the standpoint of the Hamiltondom’s position as one of the Four Great Nobles, even without that intention, it could easily be seen as prioritizing foreign nobles over those within her faction.","Since she had already decided to exclude heads of noble houses and those with official posts, inviting Lilia was impossible. Thus, the “no nobles allowed” note had been necessary.","(......Still, even if Kaito-sama doesn’t know the meaning of an attendant, I think there’s a high chance it will work out fine. If I put myself in his position, this tea party, aside from me, would be full of strangers. Given the choice, he would surely want to bring someone along. And the selection criteria for that person would naturally lean toward someone knowledgeable about noble culture and tea parties. However, with nobles excluded, he might not immediately think of anyone suitable. In that case, Kaito-sama would likely seek someone’s advice...... And the person he would turn to would, of course, be well-versed in noble society, have attended many tea parties, and be easy to consult with as his lover...... Duchess Lilia. If so, he should also learn the meaning of an attendant from her.)","Eris’ assumption was not exactly wrong. If Kuromueina hadn’t happened to visit at that timing, Kaito would likely have been left wondering who to take as his attendant, gone to consult Lilia, and in doing so would have learned that an attendant was essentially meant to serve as a guard.","(Thinking along those lines, the possibility of him bringing someone truly extraordinary as an attendant is extremely low...... However, I’ve dealt with Kaito-sama many times before. I understand that letting my guard down here would be a mistake...... Yes, I should consider even Phantasmal King-sama coming with him as a possibility. Still, if it were Phantasmal King-sama, since they aren't widely recognized, I could probably just ask them to refrain from revealing their identity......)","With a sharp, focused expression, Eris tried to account for the worst-case scenario. However, she could never have foreseen the string of coincidences that had occurred, at the exact moment the invitation arrived, Kuromueina had just happened to drop by for a visit, and, unusually for her busy schedule, had some free time.","As a result...... Kaito chose his attendant without consulting Lilia at all, and that attendant, though she had attended many parties, had never once been to a noble tea party, and thus knew nothing of what “attendant” meant...... That this person turned out to be Kuromueina was something even Eris could never have imagined.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Eris is doing her best. She’s really doing her best, but...... the problem is her opponent. No matter how much she prepares or anticipates, he’s the kind of person who somehow manages to slip through everything, right on the mark......]"]},{"number":2334,"title":"Chapter 2334: The Promised Tea Party 3","paragraphs":["On the day of the tea party to which Kaito had been invited, Eris was in her room at Hamilton Marquisdom, wearing a serious expression as she carried out her final checks. Although the tea party itself would begin in the afternoon, as the host she had naturally been busy from early on, thoroughly confirming every detail.","(Tea, sweets...... no problems there. While I can’t say it’s absolutely perfect, based on what I saw when visiting Nifty’s shop and when Kaito-sama came shopping at my store, I’ve gathered items I believe will suit his tastes. Given his personality, he likely doesn’t care for excessive decorations, so I’ve kept the adornments simple. The weather is clear, so holding it on the terrace with a garden view as planned will be fine. The custom-made Barrier magic tools are in place, and the anti-teleportation barrier is the finest our house can provide...... There are no issues with countermeasures against spying or eavesdropping, and I’ve re-investigated the backgrounds of everyone who will be entering the venue, including the servants......)","In any case, Kaito attending a noble’s tea party was a major event within noble society. Unless one was Alice, it would be impossible to completely conceal the information, and many nobles had already heard about it.","Naturally, there had been many letters expressing a desire to participate as well, but Eris had firmly refused them, carefully selecting only a few young men after a strict screening process.","[Eris-sama, pardon me. Cornelia Sharon-sama has arrived.]","[Understood. Please show her to my room.]","Before long, guided by a maid, a woman entered Eris’ private chambers. She had a refined and composed demeanor, wearing a clearly high-quality dress. Her distinctive features were soft, dark gray semi-long hair and pale green eyes. She was Cornelia Sharon, the young lady of the Sharon County, a noble of the Archlesia Empire.","[Good day to you, Eris-sama. I am truly grateful for the honor of being invited to such a wonderful gathering today.]","[Good day to you as well, Cornelia-sama. I apologize for calling you at such an early hour.]","[Not at all, in fact, I had hoped to speak with you once before the tea party if possible, so I was thankful for the invitation.]","Speaking with gentle smiles, the two were close enough to be considered childhood friends. Sharon County was also an influential noble house within Hamilton Marquisdom’s faction, so the two houses had many dealings with each other and could be said to be on close terms.","[......Still, that is quite a fine dress and accessories you’re wearing. You’ve gone for a deliberately subdued design, but the quality is exquisite.]","[......Yes, well...... my parents got a bit carried away. Since this is not a ball or evening party, they avoided anything too extravagant and instead focused entirely on the quality of the materials. When I think about how many evening gowns could be made from just the fabric of this one dress, I do get a bit of a headache, but I can’t exactly fault my father and mother for their feelings.]","Sharon County was strong in trade related to magic tools, and among the nobles of the Archlesia Empire, they were wealthy enough to be counted among the upper ranks. This time, for the tea party their daughter Cornelia is attending, they had prepared clothes and accessories that incorporated the latest trends from the Hydra Kingdom, using expensive materials without restraint.","At a glance, they gave the impression of calm and refined attire, but to those who knew what to look for, their high cost would be obvious.","[Well, of course, they don’t mean anything as vulgar as having me use my femininity as a weapon to ingratiate myself. It’s just, embarrassing as it is to admit, I imagine they're hoping for me to be at least somewhat liked by that gentleman at this gathering. Lately, the Hamilton Marquisdom, especially Eris-sama, has been drawing an extraordinary amount of attention, and I suppose part of them does feel envy towards your rapid rise.]","[That’s true. From the outside, the benefits our Hamilton Marquisdom and I have gained in such a short period are indeed remarkable, and I can understand feeling envy. Does Cornelia-sama feel that way as well?]","[......Of course, there’s some envy, but more than that, I’d say I feel wariness and astonishment...... I’ve known Eris-sama for a fair amount of time, and I believe I understand the general direction of your thinking. If it were Eris-sama or the Hamilton Marquisdom, I would expect that when rumors among the nobility grew too large, you would deliberately hold back your momentum, considering the overall balance, but from the way Eris-sama’s fame is only rising and rising without pause...... it seems less like it's not that you’re choosing not to hold back, and more like...... even Eris-sama and the Hamilton Marquisdom are unable to hold it back......]","[......Yes.]","[......Umm, Eris-sama? I know I’m the one who brought up the topic, but why are you smiling at me with that look......? It’s as if you’ve overcome countless trials...... Eh? W- Was it really that much......?]","[....................................Yes.]","Though it should have been a beautiful smile, an air of melancholy, as if she bore an immense sorrow behind her, drifted about Eris. Seeing this, Cornelia had an indescribable expression on her face, feeling a growing unease that this tea party might turn out to be far more outrageous than she had imagined.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Looks like someone’s about to get dragged into Kaito’s fetish for striking noble ladies in the stomach again...... I see, a noble house strong in magic tools, huh...... I see...... They’re top-tier, sure, but...... will their stomach be okay?]"]},{"number":2335,"title":"Chapter 2335: The Promised Tea Party 4","paragraphs":["Originally, the reason Eris summoned Cornelia earlier than the tea party time was because, as someone of the same faction and close acquaintance, she wanted to warn her about dealing with Kaito and, at the same time, ask her to provide as much support as possible.","And Cornelia, having lived in noble society and experienced plenty of probing and intrigue, had sensed something unsettling from Eris’s expression.","[......From observing your reactions, Eris-sama, I can tell, but my own impression of Miyama Kaito-sama was that, while his circle of acquaintances is indeed extraordinary, he himself was more like an ordinary Otherworlder, similar to the past Hero Actors...... No, of course, given how many connections he has built, I did think his character must be excellent and his communication skills high...... but should I revise this perception?]","[Yes, that was my understanding as well, in the past, that is. But after spending some time with Kaito-sama, I realized that his truly overwhelming qualities are his ability to draw opportunities to himself, and his almost absurd level of mental resilience. It’s as though fate itself loves him, as at just the most precise, opportune moment, he draws opportunities to himself. In a wide city, by coincidence, he happens to meet the exact person with whom the encounter would be mutually beneficial. Without aiming for it at all, he forges bonds that turn out advantageous for both sides. Kaito-sama himself acts perfectly normally, and yet the effect he has on those around him is immense.]","[To be blessed with opportunity is certainly enviable for anyone involved in business...... but if it is enough to make Eris-sama speak with such dread, then it must be on a completely different level.]","In truth, Kaito was loved not only by fate but also by the very world itself, and beyond that, thanks to his connection with Nebula, he had received overwhelming blessings from countless supernatural beings. As a result, in matters involving fate, chances, or luck, Kaito could be said to be virtually unbeatable. Coupled with his Sympathy Magic and his keen eye for people, even beings like the Supreme Gods and the Six Kings gave serious weight to Kaito’s intuition.","[To give an analogy...... yes, it is like the wingbeat of a giant dragon. Kaito-sama is the immense dragon, and we are but small birds...... or perhaps insects. Kaito-sama merely intends to flap his wings normally, but the gale stirred by those vast wings blows us away. That is how tremendous the influence he exerts on his surroundings is.]","[I- I see...... and since these are not deliberate, calculated actions on his part, it would be very difficult for us to predict them...... And as for this \"mental resilience\" you mentioned?]","[Kaito-sama is bizarrely tough in spirit, he does not consider socializing to be a burden in the least. Imagine this, if you will: Cornelia-sama, suppose you attend a party. The attendees are all acquaintances, people you know fairly well. But there are nearly a hundred of them, and you must greet each one. How fatigued would you become?]","[Greeting a hundred people huh...... Well, if I could take breaks, that would be one thing. But even among familiar faces, exchanging that many greetings, once I pass the halfway mark, I wouldn’t be able to hide my mental exhaustion. By the end, I doubt I’d even be capable of proper conversation......]","Even if one skipped idle chatter, kept greetings and small exchanges brief, and limited each to 3 minutes, it would still take about 5 hours. Even Cornelia, well-accustomed to noble parties, would prefer not to imagine such a scenario.","[......At Kaito-sama’s birthday party the other day, he received gifts continuously from over 450 people, one after another, without a single break. He even managed to hold a reasonable conversation with each of them...... and yet he showed no sign of fatigue whatsoever. Thinking back on it, I cannot recall ever seeing Kaito-sama visibly weary, mentally or otherwise.]","[......Wait a moment, I need to revise my expectations there. I had come here prepared as though meeting an Otherworlder akin to the past Hero Actors...... but I think I must brace myself as though I am facing a God.]","[Yes, that would be best. I, too, have taken all kinds of precautions, carefully considered every possibility, and prepared thoroughly...... and still, I can find no sense of reassurance. In any case, approach this with the resolve it deserves.]","[Now I’m getting nervous. Very much so......]","With Eris speaking with such a convincing expression, Cornelia too felt an indescribable unease as she nodded.","Eris was certainly intelligent, and she had prepared with solid knowledge and many scenarios in mind. But if one were to point out what she still lacked, it would be experience with Kaito-related matters...... the so-called Subject K.","If, by chance, the one present here had been Lilia, the person in this world with the most overwhelming amount of experience weathering countless Subject Ks, she would no doubt have offered precise advice with a detached, enlightened gaze.","\"No, unfortunately, planning or countermeasures against Kaito-san are meaningless. The more you try, the more he slips through everything, as if on purpose, and brings stomachaches from completely unexpected directions...... The best approach when dealing with Kaito-san is to give up from the start, accept everything, and focus on how to care for the stomachaches afterward.\"","That is what Lilia would have said, with eyes that had already abandoned all resistance. But sadly, while Eris had indeed suffered her share of stomachaches from Kaito, she had not yet reached Lilia’s realm of resignation and enlightenment. At this point, all she could do was tremble with a vague and inescapable sense of dread.","<Afterword>","Eris-chan : [I have to think through Kaito-sama’s thought process, analyze the situations, take every precaution possible, and prepare for unforeseen circumstances...... B- But will that really be enough to handle everything?]","Lilia-chan : [......Countermeasures don’t mean anything against Kaito-san. He won’t restrain himself either, so preventing it is impossible. The stomachaches will come, they will definitely come. The best thing you can do is give up, and focus on making sure the damage to your stomach doesn’t linger afterward.]","Serious-senpai: [I see, you can certainly feel the difference in experience. So this is the dignity of the Strongest Stomachache Warrior......]"]},{"number":2336,"title":"Chapter 2336: The Promised Tea Party 5","paragraphs":["At last, as the time for the tea party drew near, Eris performed one final check of her appearance and composure before settling herself down to quietly wait.","She had already received word from Kaito that he would be arriving at the Hamilton Marquisdom via Teleportation Magic, so Eris had provided him with the world coordinates of the gate that led to the Hamilton family’s villa. She had also shown the gatekeepers his portrait and instructed them to report immediately upon his arrival.","(Since this time it was decided that only young nobles from the Hamilton Marquisdom’s faction would attend, there should be no chance of Kaito-sama accidentally encountering anyone else at the gate. I’ve already told them to come earlier, and all of them have already arrived, so there’s no problem there. In the end, I couldn’t find any suitable young lords, so the guests are all young ladies...... but given Kaito-sama’s position and influence, there’s no need for him to look for a mistress at a tea party. No strange rumors will arise, so that should also be fine. The only real concern is regarding his attendant, but...... it should be fine...... it has to be fine.)","As she tried to reassure herself with such thoughts, the magic tool on the table chimed. This was linked to the magic tool carried by the gatekeepers, and its ringing meant Kaito had arrived. Eris immediately touched the teleportation magic tool she had prepared in advance.","Although the distance from the room to the gate wasn’t all that far, the best way to avoid keeping Kaito waiting even a little was to use teleportation magic. Since she had already registered with the barrier beforehand, she wasn’t affected by the teleportation-blocking magic tool, and in an instant, she was able to transfer directly in front of the gate.","And then, the moment she teleported, Eris immediately spotted Kaito’s figure. Turning toward him with a smile on her face, she opened her mouth to speak.","[My apologies for keeping you waiting, Kaito-sama. Welcome......]","But her words faltered when her eyes caught the figure standing at Kaito’s side...... none other than Kuromueina. Eris froze, looking at Kuromueina, then at Kaito, then back again.","Eris Dia Hamilton, the woman praised as a prodigy, had just executed a perfect double take.","(......Kuromu-sama is here...... Eh? Why? Whyyyyy!?)","The shock nearly wiped her mind blank, sending her thoughts into a storm of confusion. Yet the faint shred of reason left reminded her she was still mid-greeting, and so her lips somehow continued moving despite her turmoil.","[M- My apologies. Once again, welcome and thank you for coming.]","[Hello, Eris-san. Thank you for inviting me. You said I could bring an attendant, so I came together with Kuro.]","[Hello, Eris-chan. It’s been since the last party, hasn’t it? I’m happy to see you again.]","[W- W- Welcome, Kuromu-sama. It is also an honor for me to see you again.]","Though shaken, Eris still managed to maintain proper etiquette, a feat worthy of praise. Yet as she looked upon Kuromueina’s bright smile, her mind whirled with frantic confusion.","(A- A- Attendant, her!? W- Why Kuromu-sama......!? And judging by this, not only Kaito-sama but also Kuromu-sama don’t know what \"attendant\" means in the context of a noble’s tea party. They must have taken it literally...... b- but why? I mean, Kuromu-sama has turned down countless invitations in the past, never attending noble tea parties, only occasionally showing face at imperial castle gatherings out of courtesy. And since she doesn’t even know what \"attendant\" is, this is definitely her first time participating...... abababa...... This has become a bit, well, it’s making things way too big, far too far beyond anything I could have imagined......!)","If Underworld King Kuromueina attended a noble tea party for the first time, it would undoubtedly elevate the host’s reputation sky-high. Eris, whose name was already more widespread than she would have liked, could only feel her stomach cry out in protest at the implications of such a development.","Even so, perhaps due to her inherent mental toughness, Eris, though wracked by turmoil and a stabbing pain in her stomach, swiftly moved one hand behind her back and sent hand signals to the maid standing behind her.","Those signals were instructions to add another seat to the tea party. Anticipating the possibility that Kaito might bring someone along without knowing the implications of an \"attendant\", Eris had already made preparations so additional seats could be readied at a moment’s notice, along with a set of discreet hand signs to convey such orders.","[Sorry for showing up so suddenly. But since it’s a tea party hosted by Eris-chan, I’m looking forward to it.]","[I- I’m honored to hear that.]","Of course, Kaito’s high regard for her played a part, but it was also due to Eris’ own sincere and kind nature that Kuromueina held her in high esteem.","That in itself was an honor. But even so, Eris’ stomach continued to ache unbearably as she forced herself to keep her smile steady, leading Kaito and Kuromueina toward the terrace that served as the venue for the tea party.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [At this point, it feels like her stomach’s been punched so hard I’m not even sure she can drink tea or eat sweets anymore......]"]},{"number":2337,"title":"Chapter 2337: The Promised Tea Party 6","paragraphs":["On the terrace of Hamilton Marquisdom’s villa, the venue for the tea party, all the participants except for Kaito had already gathered, each engaged in their own conversations.","They had been instructed by Eris, via the invitations, to arrive earlier than Kaito, so naturally they had come ahead of time. Still, instead of sitting in the seats prepared for them, they stood and chatted casually.","That was simply because, given Kaito would be the last to arrive, it would feel too awkward if everyone were already seated waiting. So, to make things easier, they pretended as though they had only just arrived and remained standing.","[Of course, considering who we are meeting, it’s only natural to feel nervous.]","[According to Eris-sama, in terms of temperament, he is similar to the past Hero Actors, essentially an ordinary person. So we should not apply noble customs or unspoken rules when interacting with him. Well...... I’ve never actually spoken to a Hero Actor myself, but still.]","[Isn’t that the case for almost everyone? Even by age, at most someone might have seen two Festivals of Heroes......]","Gathered here today were eight noble young ladies...... For a noble tea party, that was a somewhat small number, but since this was Kaito’s very first tea party, they had deliberately kept the group limited.","From Cornelia onward, the young ladies gathered had all been carefully chosen, with personality being the highest priority. They were mindful of the fact that Kaito was inexperienced in such gatherings and were determined to act accordingly.","[Still, the reactions around us have been quite intense. You could feel the desire for us to somehow gain Miyama-sama’s favor, it was a lot of pressure even when I was leaving home.]","[Considering the influence he holds, it can’t be helped. My fiancé even said something utterly ridiculous, like \"If it comes to it, I’d gladly dissolve our engagement, so be sure to introduce me if that happens.\" Honestly, I felt like ending our engagement on the spot.]","[Wanting to form a friendly relationship is one thing, but wishing for you to be taken away is just disgraceful. Of course, I would never approach Miyama Kaito-sama with such disrespectful ulterior motives, but this only makes me recognize again how great his influence truly is.]","As is the case with Cornelia, it seemed that the families of the young ladies, as well as the nobles who have connections with them, had sent them off with the hope that they might somehow win Kaito’s favor.","Considering the rapid rise of Albert Duchy and Hamilton Marquisdom, such feelings were understandable to a certain degree. Still, as to be expected of the people Eris had carefully chosen, none of the young ladies gathered here seemed to harbor any intent of currying favor through charms or seduction.","Watching them, Cornelia recalled her earlier conversation with Eris.","(Eris-sama seemed anxious, but so far there’s no sign of trouble. All the nobles here are reformists, firmly within the Hamilton faction, and Eris-sama, on behalf of the Hamilton Marquisdom, has thoroughly investigated their backgrounds. Even from my own perspective, every young lady here is sociable, free of elitism, and exemplary in character...... At the very least, I can’t imagine any of them angering Miyama Kaito-sama.)","This time, the selection was based on character. Many were second or third daughters rather than heirs...... or even further down the line, but they had been chosen because of their virtues. At the very least, none of them were the type to cause Kaito trouble.","(In that case, it seems nothing will go wrong. It’s important to consider all possibilities, but being too tense won’t help either. I should approach this calmly, without overthinking it.)","Just as Cornelia finished gathering her thoughts, several maids appeared in a somewhat flustered manner and began adding an extra seat to the table.","That alone would not have been an issue. Everyone had been informed beforehand that Kaito might misunderstand the meaning of \"attendant\", and instead of bringing a guard, he might bring an ordinary companion. In that case, an additional seat would simply be prepared to accommodate them.","However, the behavior of the maids was unusual. They weren’t just adding a seat, they were rechecking the entire table arrangement, radiating the kind of nervous tension that suggested even the smallest mistake would be unacceptable.","Sensing that abnormal atmosphere, the young ladies gathered all turned their eyes toward the table, where one of the maids looked over them before speaking.","[......Ladies, please remain calm as I say this. As Miyama Kaito-sama’s attendant...... Her Majesty, Underworld King-sama will be attending this tea party as well.]","[ [ [ [ [ [ [ [ ! ? ] ] ] ] ] ] ] ]","It was the very definition of a shockwave. The noble ladies were visibly stunned by the maid’s words.","[U- U- U- Underworld King-sama!?]","[P- Please wait, Underworld King-sama has never once attended a noble tea party before......]","[S- She’s coming right away!? I- I need time to prepare myself......]","[I’m not ready! I’ve never steeled myself for the idea of meeting one of the Six Kings and sitting at the same table!]","Thus, a bombshell of monumental scale had been dropped. Though no one raised their voices too loudly, their agitation was unmistakable...... and of course, it was only natural. Kaito’s fame and influence were already significant, and even his participation alone made this tea party a major event.","But they had been prepared for that. Eris had informed them in advance of Kaito’s character through letters, and they had steeled themselves for meeting him, imagining scenarios and bracing themselves up until today.","......But none of them had anticipated, nor prepared themselves for, the addition of what was essentially the pinnacle of the Demon Realm.","And so, though there was nothing they could do about it now, until Kaito and his party actually arrived, the young ladies struggled to keep their voices low, but the atmosphere itself was sheer chaos, the very picture of pandemonium.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [At last, it has escalated, no longer just hitting one at a time, but unleashing an AOE body blow straight to the gut, taking out several at once. These poor nameless young ladies...... they showed up only to get their stomachs smashed right from the start......]"]},{"number":2338,"title":"Chapter 2338: The Promised Tea Party 7","paragraphs":["Eris-san said she would personally guide us to the tea party venue, so Kuro and I followed her while chatting along the way.","[Speaking of which, Eris-san, about this tea party, how many people are attending?]","[This time, since it will be Kaito-sama’s first time attending, I just want you to get a feel for the atmosphere. Excluding us, there will be 8 participants. Ideally, I would have also invited some young men closer to Kaito-sama's age, but I couldn’t find anyone suitable, so it ended up being 8 noble young ladies......]","[Ah, that’s fine. In fact, thank you for being so thoughtful. So, if it’s 8 noble young ladies, does that mean with attendants included, there will be around 16 people?]","Eris spoke with an apologetic tone, but I understood that this world had a much higher ratio of women, and being the only man in a group of women wasn’t unusual for me, so I had no problem with it.","What caught my attention, though, was that Eris said \"8 participants excluding us\" yet then clarified \"8 noble young ladies\", which made me wonder, did that not include their attendants? I recalled attendants weren’t supposed to be nobles.","[Ah, no. At a noble’s tea party, attendants are usually bodyguards. Some feel uneasy if their guard isn’t nearby, but if they wrote \"bodyguard\" directly, it could be seen as mistrusting the host’s security. That’s why they phrase it as \"attendant\".]","[Eh? R- Really!?]","[That said, it’s just that bodyguards are the most common. It’s also possible, like in Kaito-sama's case, to bring another noble as one's attendant, so Kaito-sama and Kuromu-sama haven’t done anything wrong. Please don’t worry. The host always prepares extra seating to account for such cases.]","So attendant = guard was kind of an unspoken rule...... I had no idea. It wasn’t that you couldn’t bring a normal attendant, but still, that was a surprising revelation.","[I see. I had no idea either.]","[It’s a noble custom, or rather a convention. If you aren’t a noble, you rarely get the chance to learn about these things, so it can’t be helped. Tea party attendants are just one example, there are many other customs as well. Many of them don’t even have any deep meaning, just things that continue simply because they always have...... I shouldn’t say this as a noble myself, but many are just troublesome.]","Seeing Eris-san give a wry smile as she said that, I suddenly recalled how I’d once gotten confused over the decorative wording in the letters Chris-san sent me.","Thinking about it, that too was just one of the many aristocratic customs. And realizing there must be a whole lot of such things...... I couldn’t help but feel that being a noble really does seem troublesome.","[Still, this was a little unexpected. Well, Kaito-sama is an Otherworlder, and Kuromu-sama has no prior record of attending tea parties, so it’s not strange that you didn’t know the nuance of attendants. But I thought Phantasmal King-sama might have explained it to you in advance......]","[......Ah, well, Alice......]","[......Shalltear would warn Kaito-kun if it were something that might harm him. But if it’s just something that makes us or Eris-chan fluster, she prefers to sit back and watch for fun.]","Right. If not knowing the correct meaning of \"attendant\" would have put me at a disadvantage, Alice would have told me beforehand. But since bringing Kuro wasn’t completely wrong, and Eris-san had prepared enough flexibility, she probably just found it amusing to watch us learn it the hard way.","Well, when it comes to things involving Lilia-san, she does seem to sympathize and occasionally help out, even if it doesn’t affect me directly......","While I was thinking about this, Alice’s voice came from behind me, though she didn’t reveal herself.","[......No, it’s not like I’ve done nothing, you know. For instance, in this case, I kindly gave a word of warning to a couple of noble families who were plotting something.]","[Wha...... P- Phantasmal King-sama!? That’s......]","[Ahh, don’t blame yourself, Eris-san. You couldn’t have noticed anyway. Those families had very little connection with you, and since I gave them a warning before they even acted, there weren’t any outward signs to see.]","Hearing Alice’s words, Eris looked visibly shocked. As the host, she must have been surprised to learn that some noble families had been scheming behind the scenes.","[No, really, it wasn’t anything big. More like petty or small-time mischief. One was trying to pressure the viscount’s third daughter, who was scheduled to attend the tea party, into casually introducing them to Kaito-san. The other was scheming to sneak one of their merchants in as someone’s companion, since nobles are forbidden from taking other nobles as companions...... It wasn’t anything so serious as a crime, so I just gave them a gentle warning...... Well, they did end up sobbing and rubbing their foreheads against the ground in apology though......]","[......What the heck did you do to them......]","From what I just heard, it really didn’t sound like anything that could be called a major plot...... Basically, one group tried to get a participant to put in a good word about them to me, and another thought about passing off a merchant as someone’s companion. They hadn’t even acted on it yet, it was still just at the planning stage.","Still, if they ended up crying and apologizing like that, did Alice threaten them that badly?","[No, I really did just give a gentle warning. And honestly, it was such a minor prank-level thing that even if they had gone through with it, Eris-san could have easily dealt with it. It wasn’t something that would have harmed Kaito-san in any way either, so even if they had, I’d have let them off with just a scolding....... Well, if there’s one thing of note about how it went down...... I had Eden-san, who seemed bored, \"silently stand by in the background\" while that was happening.]","[You’re a devil......]","Of course they’d break down crying and grovel on the floor! Eden-san already left countless nobles traumatized, and while people like me who know about Makina's relationship with Alice might see it differently, to an ordinary noble with no knowledge of Eden-san’s ties to the Phantasmal King, it would just look like Eden-san got angry and came to deliver a warning, right!? And on top of that, having her silently waiting in the background is just way too terrifying.","W- What the heck...... Just imagining the scene feels like a vision of hell. Against my better judgment, I actually felt a tiny bit of sympathy for those nobles who tried to pull something sneaky.","<Afterword>","Alice-chan : [It’s really just no different from a petty little prank, so I’ll forgive them. Even if it had actually been carried out, I’d forgive it with a big heart...... But I wonder, would this guy in the back forgive them?]","Serious-senpai : [Ain't that a scene from hell there?]","Makina : [......No, just so there’s no misunderstanding here, I have zero interest in the power struggle between these lumps of flesh, and I’m not angry, okay? If my beloved child had actually been harmed, I’d deal with it, but in this case, that didn’t happen. I only stood in the back because Alice told me to.]","Serious-senpai : [Ah...... I see......]","Makina : [Besides, I only came along because Alice said \"Let’s go eat together\", and then asked me to appear as Eden, so I thought that was a little strange......]","Serious-senpai : [Coz this guy doesn’t use omniscience on Alice, so she keeps getting tricked occasionally......]","Makina : [I kind of feel like I’m being used as a convenient intimidation tool, which I’m not happy about......]","Alice-chan : [No, not at all! I had no intention of using you to threaten anyone. It was really such a small matter, so I just took care of it while going out to eat. I had Makina stand in the back...... well, you know, I just wanted my best friend close by.]","Makina : [T- Then I can’t complain~~ Yeah, I get wanting your best friend nearby~~ If that’s the case, I have no objection at all. Sorry for misunderstanding things weirdly.]","Serious-senpai : [The heck, oi!?]"]},{"number":2339,"title":"Chapter 2339: The Promised Tea Party 8","paragraphs":["While chatting as we walked, I suddenly remembered something and called out to Eris-san.","[Come to think of it, Eris-san, errr...... I brought a little gift of sorts. Would it be alright if I gave it to you now?]","[Eh? A gift?]","[Yes. Since you were kind enough to invite me, I thought I should bring something, so I consulted Canalis-san. She prepared one of the new products that Nifty plans to handle, so I brought that along.]","[Hyiiih...... T- Thank you so much for the courtesy. B- But, um...... would this perhaps be one of the rather expensive items?]","[No, not at all. Apparently, it was made with the concept of being affordable and easy to buy. Canalis-san said bringing something too expensive might embarrass the host, so she picked something in the lower price range but still flashy in appearance...... here it is.]","Nifty is a tea specialty shop with a luxury focus, but it seems they’re also planning to expand with items that are more affordable. What I brought was one of those.","Incidentally, Nebula and Illness-san had nothing to do with this one. It was a product planned and created by Canalis-san herself.","[What a very lovely and charming box. Pardon me for asking, but what exactly is inside?]","[It’s an assortment of unusually shaped sugar cubes. Nothing with any special effects or unique production method, just a design-focused item that takes popular monsters as motifs, making them colorful and cute. Errr, there are three jars like this, the see-through kind.]","The sugar cube set Canalis-san prepared didn’t have any special gimmicks like the crafted sugar Nebula made. It was simply sugar molded into the shapes and colors of popular monsters, with cute, fanciful designs.","Things like Funny Rabbits and Petite Devis were so well-made you could recognize them at a glance. Sieg-san, who likes animals, and Luna-san, who loves cute things, praised them highly.","[These are remarkably detailed designs.]","[They really are. The craftsmanship is quite intricate, and I can see them becoming popular...... but this must take a lot of effort to make, right? Wouldn’t that make them rather expensive? You’re planning to sell this as a low-priced item?]","[Canalis-san said \"With godly power, I made a tool that molds them as long as you put sugar in. So basically, the cost is zero.\"]","[That person...... having such a working in business, she’s honestly on a completely unfair level......]","Canalis-san, who can ignore costs and such entirely, was, from Kuro’s perspective, a cheat-like existence. He gave a wry smile with a hint of exasperation.","Still, Canalis-san is only responsible for Nifty. She doesn’t handle negotiations with other trading companies, or deals with the shops and merchants Anima works with. She has the good sense to refrain from interfering in those areas with her omnipotence, so there’s essentially no problem.","As for Nifty, it seems Canalis-san has free rein within the scope of permission granted by Shiro-san......","[Well, in any case, thank you very much for the lovely gift.]","[I’m glad you liked it. I actually brought extras, thinking it might be nice if I had a chance to give some to the other participants as well...... but would it be better not to do that?]","[No, that falls under my discretion as the host. To avoid causing trouble, I did tell the other participants not to bring gifts for Kaito-sama to the tea party. But if Kaito-sama wishes to hand things out yourself, there’s no problem. I believe everyone would be delighted.]","[In that case, would it be alright if I gave them out towards the end of the tea party?]","[Yes, that would be perfectly fine.]","Since I had Eris-san’s permission, I decided I’d hand out the sugar cubes to the participants later. There were supposed to be 8 people, so the amount I brought should be enough.","Well, actually, Canalis-san said \"If it turns out not to be enough, just call out in some random direction and I’ll deliver more instantly with Godly Shipping, so you don't have to worry\", so even if we ran out, it really wouldn’t be a problem.","[Ah, I can see it now. Is it over there? ......Oya?]","[Yes, that terrace is today’s venue.]","[I see...... Unn?]","[......Please don’t mind it. It’s understandable that things turned out that way......]","Circling around what seemed to be the detached mansion, we stepped into what looked like a courtyard. There I could see a gathering of people, marking the location of the tea party.","But something felt off...... or at least caught my attention. There was no doubt that the ones gathered were noble ladies, the other participants. But...... they were all standing in an incredibly neat and orderly formation, waiting...... Why would they...... ah, right! It’s because Kuro is here......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Well yeah, even if it’s within the scope Shiro allowed, being a God who can basically make anything and mass-produce it at will is a total foul play in the business world...... It's only because she wields her Godly power solely on the walking extraterritoriality Kaito's tea brand———- which he treats more of a hobby———- that it hasn't become a problem......]"]},{"number":2340,"title":"Chapter 2340: The Promised Tea Time 9","paragraphs":["The sight of young ladies in dresses standing neatly upright in a row was, in a sense, rather strange, but it couldn’t be helped under the circumstances.","If only Kaito had been coming, things would not have been so complicated. Through a letter, Eris had already informed them of Kaito’s character beforehand and given advice on the proper attitude to take when interacting with him.","Had Kaito come alone, they could have acted as though they had only just gathered, chatting casually in small groups so as not to make him feel that everyone had been waiting on him.","But with Kuromueina accompanying him, the situation was entirely different. Certainly, Kaito himself was an extraordinary individual, the World's Singularity that possesses immense influence, overwhelming connections, and words that carried great weight. Yet if one were to speak strictly in terms of social standing, he was still an Otherworlder immigrant, essentially closer to an ordinary citizen.","In contrast, Kuromueina was one of the Six Kings, the very pinnacle of the Demon Realm, holding a position that was practically representative of it. While she was reputed to be gentle, much like the World King Lillywood, no one present had ever spoken with her directly, and none knew how they ought to behave in her presence. Moreover, the announcement of her participation had come so suddenly that there had been little time to prepare.","Thus, when striving at least not to offend, lining up in orderly fashion to await them was inevitable.","[Ladies, I believe the maids have already informed you beforehand, but in addition to Miyama Kaito-sama, who was originally scheduled to attend, Kuromueina-sama will also be joining our tea party today. Under normal circumstances, it would be ideal for everyone to introduce themselves, but having each of you stand and speak in turn would take too much time. For now, let us take our seats. Please, this way......]","As expected of Eris, by the time they had arrived, she had already regained a measure of composure and, as hostess, firmly took command of the gathering.","Foreseeing that a line of noble ladies giving introductions one after another would only create awkwardness for Kaito and Kuromueina, she instead guided them all to their seats first.","With Eris clearly assuming her role as host, the young ladies felt relieved and moved to the large table where seats had been prepared.","[Kaito-sama, Kuro-sama, please, these seats are for you.]","[Thank you very much.]","[Thanks. Then, if you’ll excuse me.]","With natural grace, Eris guided Kaito and Kuromueina to sit side by side, then seated herself beside Kaito.","(There was some debate over the seating order, but sitting next to Kaito-sama should be the best choice. It goes without saying that Kaito-sama and Kuro-sama must sit together. That left me with two options: either take the seat next to Kaito-sama or the one next to Kuro-sama. If I considered only the other ladies’ feelings, perhaps it would have been better to seat Kuro-sama between Kaito-sama and me. But since this is Kaito-sama’s first time attending a tea party, he is likely feeling uneasy. Supporting him takes priority...... so I believe the seat beside him is the optimal choice.)","Incidentally, Eris’ decision had been the correct one. Makina, who had been secretly watching to make sure none of the nobles acted disrespectfully toward Kaito, saw that Eris prioritized Kaito over Kuromueina and nodded approvingly, thinking \"She understands the basics\". In doing so, Makina raised her evaluation of Eris, though Eris herself did not have any knowledge about this.","[Once again, thank you all for attending the tea party I am hosting today. I believe that while you are all familiar with Kaito-sama and Kuro-sama by name, many of you are likely seeing them in person for the first time. Therefore, with your permission, I would like to begin with each of the young ladies giving a brief self-introduction. Would that be acceptable?]","[Yes, I’d actually appreciate it if we could start with introductions.]","[Same here. I recognize a few faces, but I haven’t spoken with anyone directly. I’d be glad if you could tell me your names.]","Eris’ suggestion that the gathered young ladies introduce themselves before the tea party truly began was met with smiling approval from both Kaito and Kuromueina.","Had Kaito been the only guest, the flow might have been one of polite individual greetings and introductions. But with Kuromueina also in attendance, such an approach would have taken far too much time. Thus, Eris chose to have each noble lady introduce herself briefly in turn, keeping things concise. For the ladies too, who were unsure how best to interact with Kuromueina, this was a welcome proposal. With no objections raised, the tea party began with the young ladies’ introductions.","<Afterword>","Makina : [Un, unn. Prioritizing my beloved child above all else, of course, that’s something that should be the most basic of basics. But to make that choice without being swayed by the lofty title of Kuromueina, one of the Six Kings? Not bad at all. She seems like a noble who really understands the fundamentals, and that puts me at ease.]","Serious-senpai : [Eris is once again being highly praised behind her back in a way that’s only going to give her stomachaches later...... No, she really is outstanding, no doubt about that...... but somehow, I can’t help feeling sorry for her.]"]},{"number":2341,"title":"Chapter 2341: The Promised Tea Party 10","paragraphs":["At Eris’s suggestion, the young ladies would introduce themselves in turn, and naturally, the order followed the rank of their families...... in other words, according to the nobility’s hierarchy.","This time, since the tea party had been organized with personality in mind, not everyone present was from a high-ranking family, but among the 8 young ladies gathered, the one with the highest standing was the daughter of a Count, Cornelia. Thus, it fell to Cornelia to begin the introductions.","To make things clear for Kaito and Kuromeina, Cornelia stood up from her seat, quickly running her thoughts as she prepared herself.","(This is an important role. As the first, my self-introduction will likely set the standard for the others to follow, failure is not an option. I must remember that what’s needed is not a formal greeting but a self-introduction. Noble etiquette can be set aside, conveying things as simply as possible is key. But how much should I say about myself...... Too much could be unpleasant, but too little and I’ll leave no impression on Miyama Kaito-sama and Kuromeina-sama. The goal should be just enough for them to remember my face and name, without becoming tedious......)","Having experienced noble society as the daughter of a Count, and being competent enough that Eris had chosen her for this role, Cornelia quickly gathered her thoughts, smiled, and gave a light bow.","[Then, if I may have the honor of going first...... I am Cornelia Sharon, eldest daughter of Sharon County. Since I have an elder brother, I am neither the heir nor the successor. I am still young at 18, but I often assist with the trading company our house manages, and thus have some knowledge in that field. I would be delighted if today’s encounter proves to be a good one for us all. Please, treat me kindly.]","Her introduction was short and concise, while also including her age and her family’s business...... Cornelia herself felt she had done well for something so impromptu, and it seemed a good reference for the others as well...... Yet inwardly, she was shaken.","(J- Just now, Miyama Kaito-sama made a slightly puzzled expression...... He returned to normal right away, but d- did I displease him somehow? Was it a mistake to bring up my family’s affairs? No, wait. That expression appeared right at the very start of my self-introduction...... W- What mistake did I make......?)","Yes, though Cornelia outwardly maintained composure, her nerves were in turmoil because the moment she began speaking, Kaito had shown a fleeting confused look on his face.","Kaito’s emotions were quick to show, and the doubtful, questioning expression had unsettled her.","......But in truth, Kaito’s look had nothing to do with any problem in Cornelia’s introduction. The reality was simply that Cornelia had, during Archlesia Empire's Founding Festival, once visited Kaito’s stall to buy ceramics after receiving information from Eris. They had hardly spoken, and she had worn a light disguise, but still, they had met once before.","Because of that, when Cornelia began her greeting, Kaito had simply thought \"Huh? I feel like I’ve seen her somewhere before?\". A moment later, he concluded \"Maybe I caught sight of her when I visited Chris-san’s place or something\", and returned his expression to normal. He hadn’t felt any doubt or dissatisfaction about Cornelia’s introduction at all, but Cornelia had no way of knowing this, so to her, waiting for Kaito’s response felt like a prisoner awaiting the execution of her sentence.","[Ah, you’re the child from the Sharon Trading Company, right? I don’t think we’ve spoken directly before, but I’m pretty sure I’ve seen you a few times.]","[Y- Yes, I have had the opportunity to see Kuromeina-sama on occasions relating to our trading company, so it is an honor to finally speak like this.]","Just then, Kuromeina smiled and addressed Cornelia, which turned out to be her salvation. Seeing that exchange, Kaito decided to clear up the sense of familiarity he felt, and when their short conversation came to a pause, he spoke up.","[Is it alright if I call you Cornelia-san?]","[Of course.]","[Errr, Cornelia-san...... haven’t we met somewhere before? No, I don’t mean this as a pickup line or anything, it’s just that I feel like I’ve seen you before......]","[A- Ahh, that might have been at Archlesia Empire's Founding Festival. I purchased some ceramics at your shop, Miyama Kaito-sama. At the time I was wearing a hat, so perhaps the impression was a little different from now......]","[Ohh, that explains it! No wonder you looked familiar...... thank you, that clears it up. Ah, and it’s fine if you just call me by name.]","[Then, I’ll address you as Kaito-sama. The ceramics I purchased back then were truly wonderful, and I still treasure it dearly.]","Seeing Kaito’s smile once his question had been answered, Cornelia felt an immense wave of relief wash over her.","(T- T- T- Thank goodness...... I really thought I might have offended him somehow......)","Relieved, Cornelia didn’t realize it. No, she couldn’t possibly have realized it...... Just now, Cornelia had carried out the act of “praising Nebula’s work” toward Kaito.","By doing so, she had effectively obtained an express ticket straight to stomachache,the kind that came from Kaito’s favorability shooting up drastically...... But at this moment, she still had no idea.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [The most effective way to raise Kaito’s initial favorability is to praise either his pets or Nebula...... but if his favorability goes up because of that, then it opens up a direct route to a body-blow to the stomach...... What kind of outrageous trap is this!?]"]},{"number":2342,"title":"Chapter 2342: The Promised Tea Party 11","paragraphs":["At the core of the matter, the young ladies already knew to some extent what kind of person Kaito was from Eris, and they were aware that he was gentle-hearted. As for the irregular participant, Kuromueina, she too was famous for her mild and kind nature. In fact, during the tea party she wore a gentle smile, answering each young lady’s self-introduction with a few warm words. Combined with Cornelia setting the tone with her introduction at the start, the sequence of introductions went smoothly.","Six of them had already finished introducing themselves, leaving only two...... and since the order was based on family rank, it was inevitable that the very last person would be the one with the lowest standing among the nobles gathered at this tea party...... the fourth daughter of Baron Ritch, Lady Marie Ritch.","(......I’m so terribly nervous. I still don’t understand why I was invited here...... Our family is barely above commoners with just a bit of land, and I’m the fourth daughter...... I’ve studied etiquette, yes, but this is my very first formal tea party...... I’ve only ever greeted Lady Eris-sama once before...... I’m not even someone who deserves to be spoken to by people of such rank...... No, I know it isn’t a mistake, I confirmed the invitation many times, but still......)","Marie was born into a Barony with a modestly long history, though their domain was very small. She was undoubtedly a noblewoman, but as the fourth daughter of a poor baron, she had never lived a lifestyle befitting nobility. Simply being on the terrace of the marquis’ estate already made her feel as though she had stepped into a world far above her own.","That said, there were others of comparatively lower standing, such as the third daughter of a Viscount, but that family, despite its Viscount title, was quite wealthy. Unlike the Ritch family, who carried the name of nobility without the means, their resources were on an entirely different level.","In fact, the dress Marie wore today had been borrowed from her elder sister. While the other young ladies, following Eris’ advice, had deliberately chosen elegant but restrained gowns suited to the tea party, Marie’s outfit stood out for its clearly inferior quality.","(W- Why was someone like me, from such a powerless family, invited to a tea party where even the renowned Miyama Kaito-sama would attend, and together with the U- U- U- Underworld King herself?! Father, Mother...... Marie might very well lose her head today for some terrible lapse in decorum!)","Incidentally, the true reason Marie had been invited was her kind personality and the fact that...... having not lived in a particularly aristocratic manner, her values were closer to those of ordinary citizens. With Kaito’s nature in mind, Eris had thought it best to include someone with such a perspective.","Even so, the sense of being out of place was overwhelming. Feeling that way, Marie rose when her turn came, and gave a respectful bow.","[I am the fourth daughter of the Ritch Barony, my name is Marie Ritch. Honestly, our family’s standing as nobles is very low, we’re practically half farmers. This is my first time attending such a splendid tea party, and I must admit I am quite nervous. I may fall short in many ways, but I ask for your kind regards.]","[Pleased to meet you.]","[Likewise. By the way, since you said your family is half farmers, do you grow any crops yourselves?]","Kaito and Kuromueina both responded to Marie’s greeting with warm smiles, and then Kuromueina followed up, curious about Marie’s mention of farming.","[Ah, yes. Our family runs a ripple orchard of fairly decent size.]","[Really? Ripple is actually my favorite fruit, out of all fruits, it’s the one I like best.]","[Is that so? Then, if it pleases you, Miyama Kaito-sama, I’d be happy to send you some.]","[Eh? Really? If that’s the case, I’ll gladly buy them properly.]","[No, no. Since I’ve been given the honor of meeting you like this, please allow me to offer them as a gift, in commemoration. I can guarantee their taste.]","[In that case, I’ll gratefully accept your kindness.]","For Marie, it was truly just a small, casual exchange. The Ritch Barony owned a large ripple orchard passed down for generations, and every year they harvested more than enough to have a surplus. Since Kaito said he liked ripples, she thought she would simply give him some. It was really no more than that.","And yet, this became the turning point for Marie Ritch, the fourth daughter of the so-called \"poor Barony\". What seemed like a trivial gift would later bring her household tremendous wealth, while earning her great merit...... and countless bouts of stomachaches along the way.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Another victim of stomachaches has appeared...... What move would’ve even been the right one here?]","? ? ? : [It’s a tough call, but perhaps just having him buy them normally would’ve been best. By offering them as a gift instead, it basically guaranteed that later on Kaito-san would deliver a \"return gift\", which, of course, means a straight body-blow to the stomach......]","Serious-senpai : [Is our protagonist some kind of minefield aimed at people’s stomachs or something?]"]},{"number":2343,"title":"Chapter 2343: The Promised Tea Party 12","paragraphs":["With Marie-san’s greeting, the simple self-introductions of the eight young ladies came to an end. Everyone seemed like a good person, but the ones who left the best impression on me personally were Cornelia-san and Marie-san.","Cornelia-san seemed to have a high opinion of Nebula’s ceramics, so there’s no doubt she has a wonderful eye for fine things. She might even shop at Nifty, so it would be fun to talk about that sort of thing with her.","As for Marie-san, just as she herself said that this was her first tea party, I could sense a slight nervousness from her...... but that, along with her overall atmosphere, made her feel the most approachable and familiar.","Cornelia-san had soft, dark gray hair, pale green eyes, and a somewhat tall, model-like elegance to her. Marie-san, on the other hand, had semi-short pink-brown hair with a reddish-purple tint, blue eyes, and a petite, cute charm. Those two stood out to me so much that I remember them clearly; I’ll probably recognize them right away even if I ran into them on the street later.","[Well then, now that the simple introductions are over, I shall prepare the tea.]","At that moment, Eris-san spoke, and as if responding to her, the maids quickly began arranging tea and sweets on the large table.","The atmosphere was like an afternoon tea, elegant and stylish, but...... there were baby castellas as well. Come to think of it, during one of my chats with Eris-san, I mentioned that baby castella was the sweet I ate the most, so maybe she prepared them with that in mind.","Kuro also nodded with satisfaction, so it seemed like the lineup of sweets had no issues.","Back when I visited Lilia-san’s house, I didn’t fully understand it yet, but...... while Kuro’s diet is usually just a matter of taste with no real likes or dislikes, there’s one thing she clearly dislikes: \"sweets that look hard to eat\".","Come to think of it, at Lilia-san’s mansion, when the tea sweets were served, Kuro, who rarely shows such reactions, quite plainly gave off the feeling that they weren’t to her taste.","At the time, I thought she just didn’t like overly extravagant, appearance-focused sweets, but as I got to know Kuro better, I realized it was more complex than that.","She doesn’t dislike luxurious or flashy sweets per se; she eats those happily enough.","What she dislikes are the kinds of sweets that sacrifice ease of eating for the sake of appearance. In Kuro’s food guide, such sweets always get low evaluations.","On the other hand, if there’s clear thought put into making them easier to eat, even if they look gorgeous, she praises them highly. For example, Nifty’s decorated baby castella, which Kuro really liked, had a very flashy and luxurious appearance. But since each piece was skewered and the plate itself was cleverly arranged to make them easy to eat, Kuro had no complaints at all, in fact, he praised them highly.","In short, as long as it’s clear that the sweet was made with the act of eating in mind, it’s fine by her, but sweets that ignore that consideration, she dislikes.","Well, since baby castella is her ideal sweet, the farther something strays from that, the lower her evaluation drops, but the only time she shows clear dislike is when it looks difficult to eat.","Looking at today’s tea party sweets with that in mind, they were all refined and stylish, but also simple, bite-sized, and easy to eat.","[Nice, all these sweets look delicious. And I’m glad to see baby castellas too. I wonder, are baby castellas a standard at noble tea parties as well?]","[......E- Errr......]","Hey, Kuro, don’t go dropping hellish questions like that. Eris-san was clearly troubled, probably because the answer is that they’re not completely unheard of, but they’re also not exactly a staple.","But how could anyone tell the Baby Castella Demon that truth straight to her face? Lying is also out of the question. Watching Eris-san struggle between those two impossible options, I decided to step in and rescue her.","[But, baby castellas are usually pretty sweet, so if you pair them with tea they might come off a bit heavy. That’s probably why they’re not that common at tea parties, right?]","[......Kaito-kun, baby castellas hold infinite potential, so they can pair with any drink.]","[But not everyone studies baby castellas the way you do, Kuro. That means preparing baby castellas that go well with tea would be a lot of work, wouldn’t it?]","[Hah!? T- That’s true......! N- Now that you mention it, you’re absolutely right!? I’ve been pursuing the infinite possibilities of baby castellas day after day, but I completely overlooked the fact that not everyone is as well-versed in baby castellas as you or I, Kaito-kun! Maybe, as I thought, I really do need to spread the results of my pursuit of baby castella potential more widely!!!]","[......Y- Yeah, maybe so......]","Please don’t just lump me in as a baby castella expert too...... Well, at least the hellish question directed at Eris-san had been deflected, but at the cost of triggering \"baby castella mode\". If I don’t calm her down before the tea is ready, there’s a real risk this entire tea party will turn into an endless lecture about baby castellas.","<Afterword>","~ ~ Chronicles of the Stomachache Warriors 1~ ~","<Lilia Albert>","Stomachache Power: ★★★★★★★★★★","Draw Power: ★★★★★★★★★★","Endurance: ★★★★★★★★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★★★★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★★★★★★★★★★","Author’s Malice: ★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★","The first and strongest of all Stomachache Warriors, with both Stomachache Power and Draw Power at overwhelming levels. She is also the greatest victim of Kaito, having suffered countless body-blows. Compared to the other warriors, the trials she’s endured and the sheer amount of stomach medicine she’s had to consume are on a completely different scale, placing her at an absolute pinnacle.","She has become so firmly established as the stomachache character that whenever the author gathers powerful figures together, the default routine is basically “Let’s give Lilia a stomachache”. Because of this, her suffering shows no sign of slowing down.","At the beginning, her endurance was a little low, like when she fainted outright when she first met Shiro...... But after being hit with far too many stomachache-inducing situations, she’s been toughened up to the point where fainting is no longer even an option.","Even individuals at the pinnacle of the world and eccentric Gods can’t help but sympathize with her, which speaks volumes———- truly, in every sense, she deserves to be called the strongest of the Stomachache Warriors.","All the kinds of stomachaches suffered by every other warrior? She’s basically experienced them all already. On top of that, she still has a mountain of stomachache flags piled up ahead of her...... Indeed, Lilia Albert is the strongest (Stomachache Warrior, that is)......"]},{"number":2344,"title":"Chapter 2344: The Promised Tea Party 13","paragraphs":["I had imagined all sorts of things about what a noble tea party might be like, but when it actually began, it turned out they weren’t doing anything particularly special. The impression I got was that it was basically just chatting while drinking tea.","Of course, normally I suppose there would be the sort of scheming unique to nobles, smiling as they talk while secretly probing each other’s thoughts or trying to keep the other in check, but this time, it really just felt like casual conversation.","[It’s quite a beautiful garden. The flowers are so colorful, but there are many I don’t recall seeing before.]","[The flowers in this villa’s garden are a little unusual. We use a special Barrier Magic to adjust things like air pressure, so we’re able to gather flowers that only bloom in high mountain regions.]","[Hehh~~ so does that include stuff like Sky Flowers then?]","[Ahh, no, cultivating Sky Flowers together with other plants is far too difficult. So they aren’t among these.]","Since she said the flowers were gathered from high mountain regions, I thought maybe Sky Flowers, which is the true body of Ariel-san, might be here, but apparently not...... As Eris-san answered me, Kuro added a little explanation.","[Sky Flowers only bloom around the summits of mountains that exceed 5,000 meters in elevation. It also has to do with the concentration of mana. They’re not the rarest thing in existence, but they are fairly uncommon. In the Demon Realm, they often grow in the southern mountains where Magnawell lives.]","[Hehh, now that you mention it, I do remember there being a lot of tall mountains where Magnawell-san lives.]","[Who knows, there might even be a few growing on Magnawell’s back. He meets the height requirements after all......]","Come to think of it, Magnawell-san’s body height alone is over 6,000 meters...... When I think of it that way, it really drives home how absurd his size is.","[Kaito-sama, do you often travel to the Demon Realm?]","[I do go often since I have many acquaintances there, but I wouldn’t say I travel around everywhere. At least, I have been to all the places where the Six Kings live.]","Cornelia-san asked me, and I thought a little before answering. It’s true that I often go to the Demon Realm, but not to tour sightseeing spots or travel widely. It’s usually to meet with the people I know, so the places I visit are rather limited.","Honestly, the place I’ve been to the most might actually be the Land of Death.","[What about the others, ever been to the Demon Realm?]","[I was fortunate enough to be invited to the first Six Kings Festival, so I participated then, but other than that, I’ve had very few opportunities to go.]","[I’m the same as Eris-sama, I’ve attended the Six Kings Festival once. Also, since my family’s company deals in magic tools, I’ve gone to Kuromu Lake a number of times.]","Eris-san and Cornelia-san answered my question, but one word in their replies caught my attention.","[......Kuromu Lake?]","[It’s the name of a town near my home.]","[Oh, so that town is called Kuromu Lake? Sounds like it was named after Kuro.]","[Seems so. At some point, everyone just started calling it that.]","Kuro answered my question with a slightly embarrassed smile.","So the town near Kuro’s castle, where her baby birds and their families live, is called Kuromu Lake...... Come to think of it, I’ve been there many times, but I don’t recall ever hearing its name.","You’d think I would have seen it on a signboard or something, but now that I think about it, I usually head straight for Kuro’s castle and don’t spend much time in the town itself...... Maybe only when I went around with Sieg-san. I should take my time to look around properly next time.","[I’ve never been there myself. Even if my family were invited to some event, as the fourth daughter, I’d almost certainly never be the one to attend.]","[Fumu, I don’t know much about noble customs, so I'm sorry if this is a silly question, but when it comes to those sorts of invitations, parties and events, does that usually mean the eldest son or daughter goes?]","[There isn’t a strict rule, but generally the heir would attend. Since social gatherings are also about building connections, it’s best for the successor to be present. That said, sometimes someone other than the heir is brought along under the pretext of seeking a marriage arrangement. Wealthier families can afford to bring several children at once. In my family’s case, though, we’re a small-time household with little money and too many children, so there’s simply no room for me, the fourth daughter, to attend such parties. I was only brought along a few times, just so I could gain a bit of experience in social settings.]","[I see, being a noble sounds pretty tough in its own way.]","Marie-san, who had said this tea party was her first, also seemed not to have attended many parties at all. Indeed, being the fourth daughter meant she had at least three older sisters, and probably brothers too. It makes sense they couldn’t possibly bring every child to every event......","On top of that, there must be all sorts of delicate power balances among the nobility that complicate things further. It’s definitely not simple.","......Ah, but if it’s a party I’m the one hosting, then there’s no problem inviting her. Just like with the ship party before...... maybe it would be nice to host another one at some point.","<Afterword>","~ ~ Chronicles of the Stomachache Warriors 2~ ~","<Chronois>","Stomachache Power: ★★★★","Draw Power: ★★","Endurance: ★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★","Bust Desparity: ★★★★★★★★★★","The Stomachache Handler of the Divine Realm. The Flat Warrior tormented by her (big-breasted) boss and (big-breasted ×2) colleagues...... or at least she was, but the main source of her troubles, Fate, has improved her behavior thanks to Kaito’s influence, so Chronois’ opportunities for stomachaches have decreased overall.","However, if she does end up suffering, the cause is almost always Shiro, meaning that when the stomachache hits, it’s a heavy blow...... Incidentally, Lilia is usually dragged into it every time.","<Lillywood Yggdrasil>","Stomachache Power: ★★","Draw Power: ★★","Endurance: ★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★","Rate of Causing Stomachaches: ★★★★","The Stomachache Handler of the Demon Realm. The main sources of her suffering used to be Isis or Megiddo, but since Isis has grown greatly on a mental level, the one who mostly gives her headaches now is Megiddo.","Normally gentle and kindhearted, she tends to snap at Megiddo, showing just how much trouble she constantly causes her.","That said, as one of the Six Kings and a powerful authority herself, she can also be the one to cause stomachaches, making her a double-edged figure.","In the end, as long as Megiddo stays quiet, she rarely suffers, so her stomachache power is on the lower side...... Still, when things do involve Megiddo, Lilia usually gets dragged in as well."]},{"number":2345,"title":"Chapter 2345: The Promised Tea Party 14","paragraphs":["As time passed, everyone gradually grew accustomed to one another, and the conversations began to flow more naturally than at the start. It had been the same when she first visited Lilia’s home, since Kuro was inherently sociable and kind, even those who at first seemed intimidated by her title as one of the Six Kings began to open up once they got to know her.","[So, by the way, Kuromueina-sama......]","[Ahh, you can just call me Kuromu. So, what’s the matter, Cornelia-chan?]","[Well then, Kuromu-sama...... this may not be the most fitting topic for a tea party, but since I have the chance to meet you, I wanted to offer my thanks...... Thanks to Kuromu-sama, and by extension the Seditch Magic Tools Trading Company, publishing educational materials for magic tool technicians, the Sharon Trading Company is now able to introduce a trainee-apprenticeship program.]","[Ohh, that’s wonderful. I had really hoped others would take it up, so hearing you’re actually implementing it makes me happy.]","What Cornelia-san brought up was the trainee–apprenticeship system that my parents had also made use of. I had thought it was an initiative exclusive to the Seditch Company, but it turned out Kuro had been sharing the educational curricula with other companies as well.","[So the system Mom and Dad used, that was made public?]","[Unn. Our original goal was to increase the number of human magic tool technicians after all. At first we just tried it out in our company, but once we saw there weren’t any problems, we shared it with others. Instead of having the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company monopolize all the technicians, I wanted as many companies as possible to adopt it and help grow the number of Human technicians. That way competition would arise, people would sharpen their skills against one another, and the overall technology of magic tools across the human world would advance.]","[I think it’s truly a wonderful initiative. In truth, when it comes to crafting magic tools, the Human Realm is far behind the Demon Realm, and highly skilled Human technicians are extremely rare. To have educational methods and teaching materials made available is a huge boon. The Sharon Trading Company doesn’t have the capital that Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company does, but we plan to recruit a small number of apprentices in the near future.]","[Unn, unn. I’m really looking forward to seeing those kids grow and the number of technicians increase.]","Kuro really wished for the development of magic tool technology. She even opened up some patents free of charge, and since many different companies were making recording and projection magic tools, she must have been providing technical support too.","You could feel the authority of the parent of magic tools in her attitude.","[Speaking of which, I heard from them they’re doing fairly well, but how are Mom and Dad, really?]","[Akari-chan and Kazuya-kun are amazing. Especially with recording and projection magic tools, since those are based on the technology from your world, they need to be reproduced through magic formulas. But because those two know exactly what the finished product should look like, they’ve been a huge help. There’s even talk that, once they gain a bit more experience, they could each lead their own teams.]","When I asked Mom and Dad, they just humbly said things like \"We’re working comfortably in an ultra-white environment\", but judging from Kuro’s words, they seemed to be doing very well. Hearing that kind of news made me really happy.","[Cornelia-sama’s Sharon Trading Company is already a major firm among those based in the Human Realm, since you also deal in teleportation magic tools. Seeing your number of technicians grow is something I look forward to as well.]","[Fumu fumu, among magic tools, the most expensive and difficult to handle are teleportation magic tools, right?]","[That’s correct. The formulas themselves are complex, and the magic crystals required must be of the highest quality, making teleportation magic tools absolutely top-class among magic tools. Even among the nobility, many Barony and Viscouncy don’t own one.]","Eris-sn gave me a clear explanation in response to my question. Indeed, teleportation magic tools were ultra-high-class items, worth billions to tens of billions in yen. Even for nobles, it was not something easily affordable.","[Our household doesn’t own a teleportation magic tool either. So just getting to the Capital is quite a struggle.]","[Yeah, having one or not makes a huge difference. By the way, Marie-san, how did you get here today?]","[Embarrassing as it is to admit, there’s no large city within the Ritch Barony’s territory that has a Teleportation Gate, and we don’t have the financial means to hire someone capable of Teleportation Magic, so normally, we take a carriage to a city that does have a Teleportation Gate, use the gate to reach the Capital, and then pay to rent a carriage again to travel from there. This time, however, Lady Eris-sama, kindly sent a carriage to the Capital’s Teleportation Gate to pick me up, so I came with that.]","Now that she said it, it made perfect sense. Teleportation Gates only existed in fairly large cities. If you didn’t own a teleportation magic tool, you had no choice but to travel to such a city first, then use the gate to reach the capital, and then continue on again from there.","Considering the costs and demand, teleportation services would only be run in big cities where they could expect enough customers. For people living out in the provinces without their own teleportation magic tools, travel really must have been quite a difficult ordeal.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [You sure are courteously stacking stomachache flags there, Marie...... If you hand over that kind of info, the Stomachache Devil will come and smack you with goodwill......]","~ ~ Chronicles of the Stomachache Warriors 3~ ~","<Ryze Ria Symphonia>","Stomachache Power: ★ (including buffer)","Draw Power: ★ (including buffer)","Endurance: ★★★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★","Screen Time: ★★★★★","As the current King of the Symphonia Kingdom, where Kaito originally should have resided, he should be prone to all sorts of stomachaches, and the foundations for it are solid. However...... Most of the stomachache cases in Symphonia Kingdom are funneled into Lilia’s stomach, who acts as a buffer, meaning Ryze rarely becomes the direct sufferer of stomachaches.","While the sheer draw of the Strongest Stomachache Warrior can be overwhelming, Ryze’s actual Stomachache Power is among the weakest in the roster. Eating meals at the expense of your beloved sister’s stomach, does it taste good?","<Chris Dia Archlesia>","Stomachache Power: ★★★★★","Draw Power: ★★★★","Endurance: ★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★★★★","Future Risk: ★★★★★★★","The current Emperor of Archlesia Empire, she might be the one among the three rulers who has taken the most direct bodyblows from Kaito. During Archlesia Empire's Founding Festival, she suffered an impressive number of stomachache incidents, making her Stomachache Power quite notable. Naturally, Lilia was caught up in it as well.","At first, she had a somewhat scheming and dark aura, but after showing her hopelessness in romance and mellowing out, it could be said she started taking stomach hits.","Additionally, the Stomachache Devil has recently extended his reach towards Archlesia nobility, so future stomachache developments are a cause for concern.","<Laguna Dia Hydra>","Stomachache Power: ★★★","Draw Power: ★★★★★★","Endurance: ★★★★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★","Chance of Abdication: ★","The current King of Hydra Kingdom, she’s been facing a lot of troubles recently due to the actions of the problem child (lost child) and ultra-problem child (chivalrous thief) in the Hero Party.","She did encounter a massive stomachache incident when Shiro made her attack during the Founding Festival, bringing with her a stomachache of incredible magnitude, but it happened in a parallel world, and Laguna did not inherit the memory. In a sense, she avoided the worst stomachache case. Lilia, however, did inherit the memory and suffered the parallel-world body blow.","Laguna has a fairly level-headed personality, so she’s primed to be manipulated by Subject Ks...... but she also has enough cunning to dodge effectively. While she may experience minor stomachaches, the big ones are likely avoided. In that sense, she has high Draw Power but low actual Stomachache Power."]},{"number":2346,"title":"Chapter 2346: The Promised Tea Party 15","paragraphs":["At the point where the conversation had warmed up and was flowing smoothly, Eris-san gave me a sidelong glance before lightly touching the jar of sugar cubes placed on the table.","It was probably her way of asking if now would be a good time to hand out the sugar cubes we had discussed earlier as souvenirs.","The gesture was subtle enough that no one else would notice, but clear enough for me, who was in on the plan, to understand. That kind of consideration was just like Eris-san.","Catching her intent, I gave a small nod. She nodded back and then spoke.","[Everyone, may I have a moment of your time? In relation to today’s tea party, Kaito-sama has kindly prepared a gift for everyone, so I was thinking this would be a good time to distribute it now. For those who do not own a personal magic box, or if you are unsure whether your box has enough space, our household will provide disposable magic boxes, so please let us know.]","[Ah, in that case, may I have one? I do own a magic box, but its capacity is nearly full......]","Right, it really would be inconvenient to carry things back without a magic box. I had assumed all nobles would own one, but now that I thought about it, there could be those who didn’t, or those whose boxes weren’t particularly large...... In fact, I overheard Marie-san asking Eris-san for a disposable magic box.","[As for the gift, it’s a new product from our tea brand, Nifty: sugar cubes shaped like cute monsters and animals. They probably aren’t suitable for formal occasions, but for personal enjoyment, I think they’ll be delightful......]","[That sounds wonderful. I already use Nifty’s products regularly, so the thought of trying a new one ahead of release is exciting.]","[Ah, Cornelia-san, you’re already a regular customer? Thank you so much.]","Apparently, Cornelia-san often shopped at Nifty. Hearing that here made me genuinely happy.","[Nifty is the talk of the social circles, after all. I’m sure there are many others besides myself who use it.]","[Yes, we’ve also purchased from them several times.]","[That said, the demand is so overwhelming, and the shops are booked in advance, so I’ve only managed to get a few items.]","[Ah, w- well, I haven’t actually gone shopping myself...... but at a noble household we're connected with, I did get to enjoy the tea once.]","It seemed several of them had purchased from Nifty, though with the current reservation system, few had visited multiple times.","Cornelia is a countess, so she likely has plenty of connections, and it seems she also owns a large trading company. It’s possible she had been buying from Nifty even back when we were selling on consignment.","On the other hand, people like Marie-san, who lived far from the Capital where the shop was located, had difficulty getting hold of the products.","Ahh, maybe I could give them order terminals like I’ve handed out to other acquaintances...... We’d already exchanged introductions and had proper conversations, so I considered them friends now. Ahh, but...... I only had two spares in my magic box, not eight.","Hmmm...... could God Express handle this? Maybe I should give it a try. After excusing myself with a quick \"Pardon me for a moment\", I called out into the air.","[......Canalis-san, could you deliver enough terminals for everyone?]","[Yes, this is God Express, renowned for our instant delivery. Tahaa~~ For your convenience, I’ve even frozen time in the area around you for the handoff. Here you are, the order terminals you requested, all wrapped as gifts.]","As expected of God Express. Not only was the delivery instantaneous, but the items were thoughtfully packaged as well...... Truly, Canalis-san was as capable as ever.","[Thank you, as always, for everything. I’ll make sure to give you a proper thank-you another time.]","[Tahaa~~ For me, just catching a single glimpse of Kaito-sama’s ultra-fabulous smile feels like more than enough of a reward, but since my motto is to snatch up anything I can get with a big hyahhaa, I’ll look forward to it. ......That said, I do claim myself a very low-maintenance woman, so if Kaito-sama would simply have tea with me, I’d cry tears of joy.]","Her face was as expressionless as ever, but her voice carried more energy than usual, so she seemed genuinely happy. After thanking her once more and receiving the terminals, Canalis-san gave a bow and vanished. At the same time, the time stop was released, so I turned back to address everyone.","[It seems many of you already shop at Nifty, so along with the souvenirs, I’ll also hand out these order-only terminals I usually give to acquaintances. With these, you can place orders without having to go to the shop in person.]","[Y- Y- Y- Yes. Thank you very much, I’m honored...... I- I never expected to receive one of the terminals I’d heard rumors about, said to be given only to Kaito-sama’s friends, so I’m rather surprised.]","Just like Cornelia-san, the other young ladies were also visibly shaken...... which meant, could these terminals actually be quite famous among nobles? Since they allow ordering without the reservation waitlist, and Nifty is already popular among nobles, it might have been natural for them to have become the stuff of rumors.","<Afterword>","~ ~ Chronicles of the Stomachache Warriors 4~ ~","<Mizuhara Kaori>","Stomachache Power: ★★★★★★★★","Draw Power: ★★★★★★★★","Endurance: ★★★★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★★★★★★","Romance Flags: ★★★★★★★","A Stomachache Warrior with high Stomachache Power, making her dashing debut in the Afterstory as an Otherworlder. Unlike the Stomachache Warriors before her, she holds the position of an ordinary citizen, and because her range of “stomachache targets” even includes Lilia herself, her Stomachache Power is considerable.","On the other hand, since her social standing is not high, she wouldn’t normally participate in gatherings of high-ranking individuals unless Kaito is involved. In fact, the number of influential figures she has interacted with isn’t that many. Conversely, you could say that about 90% of the stomachache situations Kaori faces aren't just indirectly, but directly involve Kaito himself.","While she certainly suffers a hefty share of stomachache incidents, they are unusual in that they rarely spill over onto Lilia. You might even call her a Stomachache Warrior gentle on Lilia’s stomach.","And because she isn’t a noble or the like, she doesn’t gain benefits from forming connections with influential people like Lilia does. Instead, perhaps as compensation, romance elements often get tangled up whenever she’s caught in a stomachache incident, leading to stomachache flags and romance flags progressing side by side.","<Mikumo Akane>","Stomachache Power: ★★★★★★","Draw Power: ★★★","Endurance: ★★★★★★★★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★★★","Sharpness of Tsukkomis: ★★★★★★★★","She’s quite a rare character who openly calls out the absurdity of Kaito’s social circle head-on. Though not to the same extent as Kaori, she still gets dragged into stomachache incidents because of Kaito’s influence.","That said, while her stomach does hurt, she also has the shrewdness and quick adaptability to see such situations as opportunities to build connections and profit from them. Because of this, depictions of her actually suffering stomachaches are relatively few...... and more often than not, during those stomachache cases, she’s the one fiercely snapping back at Kaito. In that sense, she’s truly a valuable asset.","However, since she isn’t a person in power, many of her headaches and stomachaches come from maid-related matters. With Frau as her close aide being a maid, she ends up with a lot of maid-related trouble. And since Lilia often gets dragged into maid-related affairs as well, she’s actually harsher on Lilia’s stomach than Kaori ever is."]},{"number":2347,"title":"Chapter 2347: The Promised Tea Party 16","paragraphs":["For Kaito, handing over Nifty’s exclusive purchase terminals wasn’t some special gesture, he had given them to other acquaintances in the same way, so to him it was a completely ordinary act.","But for the 8 young ladies who received them, it was an earth-shattering event. To start with, in the noble society and the social world, Nifty’s name was extremely well known. Right now, there’s even a waiting list, making their products difficult to obtain. That alone made it a kind of status symbol.","(T- This is that magic tool I heard rumors about, the one said to be given only to Kaito-sama’s friends, granting them priority purchasing rights...... Eh? A- Arehh? That means I’ve been acknowledged as Kaito-sama’s friend......? T- That’s a tremendous matter in itself...... How am I supposed to explain this to my parents......)","It was common knowledge among the nobility that Kaito gave his friends a special order-use magic tool that included priority purchasing rights. Possessing such a terminal was essentially the same as being regarded by everyone as Kaito’s friend.","Of course, the young ladies gathered here, Cornelia foremost among them, were all sincere people, so none of them considered deliberately exploiting this.","Still...... the position of being Kaito’s friend was far too powerful. Especially since Kaito currently had very little contact with nobles, the attention it would draw was bound to be enormous. That much was easy to imagine, having seen the precedent that is Eris.","(N- No, the benefits this brings are enormous. Of course, I would never think of using Kaito-sama’s name for my own gain, but simply being seen as his friend will greatly raise my own recognition, which in turn would be highly advantageous in running our trading company. But...... there’s also the risk that others might see me as a mistress candidate of Kaito-sama...... If I handle this wrong, it could become a huge problem. I should consult Eris-sama later.)","The benefits were indeed great, but considering how things might develop, it was no wonder that some of them unconsciously pressed a hand to their stomachs.","Cornelia, however, was still among the more fortunate. She had already been using Nifty, and by obtaining an order terminal, she gained the great advantage of being able to continue purchasing Nifty’s products stably.","But not everyone was in such a position. For example...... Marie, the fourth daughter of the impoverished Ritch Barony.","(......Eh? Arehh? What am I supposed to do here......? The Ritch Barony doesn’t even have the finances to make regular purchases of Nifty’s products...... N- No, wait, since this is meant for me personally, I don’t have to buy them as goods for the household. I only need to buy them for myself...... C- Can I even manage that with my personal funds......?)","Nifty was a luxury tea brand, and all of its products were aimed at nobles and the wealthy, making them very expensive.","Of course, Marie was still technically a noble, which gave her more wealth than commoners, but while she could manage a purchase once or twice, she absolutely did not have the spare funds to keep buying luxury goods regularly.","(But if I receive this and then fail to place orders, people will definitely say things like “Are you trying to throw away Miyama Kaito-sama’s kindness?”, so I have to buy something...... But if I only buy small amounts, people will criticize me for being stingy. I need to buy to some extent at least...... F- For now, I should discuss this with Father and Mother.)","Marie concluded this was not something she should decide on her own and resolved to consult her parents once she returned home.","Of course, Marie had no way of knowing at this point that thanks to the “Kaito Effect”, vast wealth would soon flow into the Ritch Barony, leaving them more than able to afford monthly purchases with ease.","(That’s another problem, but...... wouldn't this end up making me more well-known than my older brothers and sisters? N- No, surely I’m overthinking it. I’m the fourth daughter, not an heir or anything, so I practically have no involvement in high society, and I almost never get invited to parties, so it should be fine...... it should be fine...... probably...... But then why does my stomach feel so uneasy, this restless, indescribable sense of dread......)","At this point, nothing had actually happened...... yes, at this point, that is...... But perhaps by some instinct, like a premonition, she had already sensed the looming crisis pressing upon her stomach.","With that vague, unsettling feeling gnawing at her chest, Marie unconsciously placed her hand against her abdomen, gently stroking it.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Marie really is carefully and diligently piling up stomachache flags......]","~ ~ Chronicles of the Stomachache Warriors 5~ ~","<Greene>","Stomachache Power: ★★★","Draw Power: ★★★","Endurance: ★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★★","Longing for High Society: ★★★★★★★★★","Originally just a throwaway character in the Flying Board arc, but before anyone knew it, she had a name, and made a striking stomachache debut at the ship party as an ordinary citizen.","She had a strong yearning for high society and did hope to make acquaintances with the wealthy...... but certainly never imagined becoming entangled with the World's Singularity. ......How did it come to this?","If she continues to involve herself in high society, she’ll inevitably be exposed to even more stomachaches, making her a promising future Stomachache Warrior.","<Rimegithe Lenoria Githurd Armetes Anne>","Stomachache Power: ★★★★","Draw Power: ★★★","Endurance: ★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★★","Affection for Kaito: ★★★★★★★","An ordinary citizen Stomachache Warrior who appeared at the same time as Greene. Her main stomachache incident was also the ship party, but since she’s a complete commoner, the damage to her stomach was far greater. Compared to Greene, she has a quieter, more reserved personality, which makes her come across as more pitiable.","That said, for both Anne and Greene, their stomachaches so far have been nothing more than body blows from being overwhelmed at the grand-scale parties. They’ve yet to be introduced to the pinnacles of the world, meaning their potential for future stomachaches is limitless.","Thanks to Kaito introducing her to Tre, her working conditions improved drastically. Because of this, she holds an extremely favorable view of him, saying she received “a debt so great she could never repay it in a lifetime”. As such, she seems very likely to raise romance flags soon, a rare heroine of a different skin color type."]},{"number":2348,"title":"Chapter 2348: The Promised Tea Party 17","paragraphs":["Nifty’s order terminal was the kind of item that might leave someone of low noble standing and limited wealth, like Marie, unsure how to handle it, but of course, there were those for whom that wasn’t an issue.","Cornelia, eldest daughter of the Sharon County, one of the most powerful and wealthy noble families in Archlesia Empire, was such a person. Even among the surrounding nobility, she was not someone to be easily targeted, any attempt to interfere with her directly carried considerable risk. At most, a few whispered slanders born of jealousy might circulate, but nothing truly problematic.","Cornelia frequently purchased high-grade tea leaves, including Nifty’s, and since her personal fortune was also considerable, there was absolutely no problem. In fact, she found it rather welcome that she could purchase without having to wait on reservations.","[Kaito-sama, I have a question...... When ordering through this magic tool, would it still be valid if someone else operated it?]","[Ah, no. That terminal is designed so that only the person it was given to can use it. If anyone else touches it, it won’t respond. So for placing orders, Cornelia-san, you’ll need to operate it yourself.]","[I see, I understand. Thank you for your explanation.]","At the words spoken as if they were the most natural thing in the world, Cornelia smiled, gave her thanks, and then cast a glance at the box that presumably contained the ordering terminal.","(......It’s not like the magic box, where you have to register the user, it’s simply unusable by anyone except the recipient? Eh? But it’s still inside the box, isn’t it? And there’s no difference in appearance between my box and the others...... Besides, this is the first time I’ve even met Kaito-sama today, so how exactly was the user restriction set? No, more importantly, this small magic tool somehow allows not only people at my home but even those far away, like Lady Marie, to place orders...... This isn’t just high-grade, it’s an unbelievably advanced magical tool. And yet he’s giving them away for free?)","It was the kind of doubt born precisely because her family owned a magic tools company. She had, of course, heard rumors in high society about order-related magic tools, but now that she held one herself, questions naturally arose.","Just then, another young lady addressed Kaito with a question.","[Miyama Kaito-sama, is it correct to understand that this magic tool only allows us to purchase items that are currently available?]","[Ahh, no, actually, when new products are released, the information updates automatically. There’s a simple instruction sheet in the box, so if you check that, you’ll understand how to operate it.]","Hearing that, Cornelia once again looked down at the box in her hands.","(......I see, so when new products are released, the information is added automatically...... Remote updates...... Technically speaking, that isn’t impossible, but to fit a magic crystal engraved with such a technique into something this small...... S- Still, the fact remains that Eris-sama and Kaito-sama’s other friends are already using them, so...... T- This is truly beyond all normal standards......)","Few knew that Canalis was an Omniscient and Omnipotent God. Within the Archlesia Empire, at least, Chris had warned the more ill-behaved nobles that Eden’s equal was running the shop, so they’d better not meddle, but since all the families gathered at this tea party were above such concerns, no warnings had been issued. Unaware of this, Cornelia, being well-versed in magic tools due to her family’s business, trembled at the sheer strangeness of the unknown technology, never imagining that the ordering terminal was essentially God-made.","(Well, I already knew beforehand that Kaito-sama was far beyond the bounds of our common sense. There’s no point in dwelling too deeply on this.)","Though surprised, she concluded there was little use in worrying, given that Kaito himself was the World's Singularity, far outside the world’s norms. With that, she stored the gifted item into her magic box and returned to casual conversation at the tea party.","After everyone finished receiving their souvenirs from Kaito, the mood once again settled into pleasant chatter. Watching the harmonious scene, Cornelia felt a small sense of relief in her heart.","(When Kuromueina-sama appeared, my blood nearly ran cold, but she was indeed as merciful and gentle as the rumors said, and I think I managed to converse with Kaito-sama without issue. Eris-sama’s prior warnings had made me brace myself, but at this rate, it seems the tea party will end peacefully.)","That was a fatal lapse in caution...... Precisely because her acquaintance with Kaito was still shallow, Cornelia let her guard slip.","And amidst the pleasant chatter, she casually brought up a certain topic.","[Come to think of it, Kaito-sama, I’ve heard you keep a Behemoth and a White Dragon as pets...... Actually, I also keep several monsters, and I look after them myself.]","[Eh? Oh, really!? I’d love to hear more about that!]","Unwittingly, Cornelia had just played a most dangerous card. In one sense, it was the perfect move...... this was one of the very best topics for swiftly raising Kaito’s favorability. And yet...... that very increase in Kaito’s favorability was, at the same time, the seed of tremendous stomachaches to come.","In this moment, unknown to both of them, the scythe of the Grim Reaper was quietly and gently pressed against Cornelia’s stomach.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Just when I thought Marie was steadily stacking up her stomachache flags, Cornelia went and stomped on a one-hit-K.O.-class stomachache flag......]","~ ~ Chronicles of the Stomachache Warriors 6~ ~","<Eris Dia Hamilton>","Stomachache Power: ★★★★★★★★★","Draw Power: ★★★★★★★★","Endurance: ★★★★★★★★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★★★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★★★★★★★","Combo Potential: ★★★★★★★★★","A rising supernova of the stomachache world. Though she first appeared during Archlesia Empire’s Founding Festival, she only officially became a named character after the ship party, during the establishment of Nifty’s shop. Despite such a short time since her entry, she has already been subjected to a storm of consecutive stomachaches, making her a highly promising contender.","While her stomach constantly suffers, her high endurance allows her to either keep up appearances or recover after suffering, precisely why she is repeatedly exposed to stomachache situations.","A combo-type Stomachache Warrior, one who (gets) overwhelmed with a rapid succession of strikes in a short span of time.","<Cornelia Sharon> (Stats Provisional)","Stomachache Power: ★★★★★★★","Draw Power: ★★★★","Endurance: ★★★★★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★★★","Weight of a Single Blow: ★★★★★★★","Because the strongest Stomachache Warrior, Lilia, is far too overwhelming, even the supernova Eris found it difficult to oppose her alone. Thus, within the Archlesia Empire, the course was set to rally three stomachache noble ladies.","Still only newly introduced, her evaluation is partly based on potential. Unlike Eris, Cornelia is the “one-hit kill (getting one-hit killed)” type of Stomachache Warrior———- she tends to let her guard down and then deliver, or rather suffer, a devastating strike all at once.","<Marie Ritch> (Stats Provisional)","Stomachache Power: ★★★★★★","Draw Power: ★★★★★★","Endurance: ★★★★","Pitifulness: ★★★★★★★★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★★★★","Stockpiled Stomachache Flags: ★★★★★","One of the newly debuted Stomachache Warriors. Having only just appeared, she hasn’t yet suffered direct stomachache damage, but she’s steadily piling up stomachache flags.","Unaware, she keeps stockpiling those flags, only to later have them all explode at once. A “charge (and then get smacked)” type of Stomachache Warrior. Much is expected of her future performance."]},{"number":2349,"title":"Chapter 2349: The Promised Tea Party 18","paragraphs":["Once, the wise emperor Chris Dia Archlesia learned a lesson at the Six Kings Festival. That lesson was: “Bringing up the topic of pets with Kaito is dangerous.”","Not that it would be wrong in terms of raising Kaito’s favorability. Kaito adored his pets, Bellfried and Lindwurm. Although he wasn’t particularly fond of luxury, the one thing he would spare no expense on was anything related to his pets.","If you were already close to Kaito, bringing up pets would definitely liven the conversation and be effective. But at this point, when they had only just met, bringing up pets, and worse, being recognized as a fellow pet owner was...... from a stomachache-inducing perspective, extremely dangerous.","Yet sadly, no one present noticed this. Kuromueina probably only thought of it as a topic that would excite Kaito. The only possible exception was Eris, but the one time she had brought up pets with Kaito had been at his birthday party, and since that was during the present exchange, the talk had been short, leaving her no chance to notice.","[Nobles often keep high-ranking monsters as a form of status, so in our Sharon County, we also keep several. Perhaps because I grew up around them from childhood, I came to enjoy caring for monsters, and now I even keep a few of my own. The ones I raise personally are all small species, but among those kept by our Sharon household, there are also large species. Well, the large ones aren’t cared for by me but by specialized servants......]","[Hehh, I see. By small species, you mean things like Funny Rabbits or Petite Devis, right?]","[Yes, exactly. In fact, I keep a Petite Devi myself.]","[Petite Devis are adorable, aren't they? I once saw one at a monster interaction event, they were so friendly and cute...... Ahh, but Petite Devis have somewhat unusual fur, don’t they? Isn’t grooming them difficult?]","[Indeed, their fluffy coat is part of their charm, and grooming them requires care. Our Petite Devis dislikes stiff brushes, so I use soft ones to brush it.]","Though she answered calmly, Cornelia was inwardly rather shaken. She could clearly feel the difference in Kaito’s reaction——— he was more talkative, his excitement visibly rising.","The flow of conversation was clearly unlike before, and though Cornelia grew slightly flustered, she kept her expression steady and continued speaking.","[Ah~~ so there really are individual differences. With Bell’s brushes, I basically buy any I come across and try them, but she definitely has preferences. I heard monster fur contains faint traces of magic power, so depending on the brush’s material, they might feel discomfort?]","[Yes, that’s what I heard too. Especially brushes made from monster materials, they seem to divide preferences very sharply.]","[By the way, Cornelia, do you have any brush recommendations?]","[As for me...... or rather, for the monsters raised in the Sharon household, we generally use specially made, custom brushes.]","[......Custom-made brushes...... Sorry, but could you tell me more about them in detail?]","[Eh? Ah, yes.]","His gaze was piercing. Even Cornelia, with all her experience in the social world, felt a little pressured by the sheer enthusiasm in his eyes, eyes that plainly said he desperately wanted to know about those custom brushes.","[There was once a trading company that tried a project where, by submitting a few strands of a monster’s fur, they would make a custom brush tailored to that monster. That’s where I get them. It’s true that these custom brushes are of the highest quality, superior to any sold on the market, but the difference isn’t dramatic enough to be obvious. Meanwhile, their prices are literally on a completely different level compared to ordinary brushes...... To put it simply, there was no demand. Since they’re entirely custom-made, they’re extremely expensive, and unless someone has a deep obsession with monsters, they wouldn’t even notice the difference......]","The difference was just enough for those with discerning eyes to notice, but when asked whether they would pay dozens to hundreds of times more for a custom-made brush, not many were willing to buy.","Since it was a true high-grade product that required immense effort, costs, and equipment investment to produce, yet demand was underwhelming, that trading company ended up suffering major losses.","[The one who provided the recovery funds for that company was our Sharon Trading Company...... Since the equipment and staff had already been prepared, they downsized operations and now only take orders through referrals. They still produce custom-made brushes that way, and that’s what I’ve been using.]","[......Um, could I use that service too?]","[Yes, of course. If you’d like, I can introduce you.]","[Thank you so much! Errr, when would be a convenient day for you to guide me there, Cornelia-san?]","[Eh? Well, let’s see...... the 23rd of this month should be open......]","[Then, if you don’t mind, I’d love to go on that day!]","[Ah, yes. Leave it to me......]","Here, a difference in perception arose between Kaito and Cornelia. When she mentioned an \"introduction\", Cornelia meant writing a letter of referral. Kaito, however, understood it as \"being taken to the trading company in person\".","If Cornelia had clarified that she meant a written letter of introduction, there would have been no issue...... But because she had relaxed her guard a little earlier, she now answered without thinking too deeply, caught off-guard by Kaito’s overwhelming enthusiasm and eagerness.","(......Huh? Eh? Arehh? Isn’t this turning into me personally guiding Kaito-sama there......? Eh? Are we...... going out together, just the two of us? N- No, I don’t particularly object to that, but Kaito-sama has only just met me, someone whose true intentions he can’t possibly know yet, shouldn’t he feel reluctant going out with such a person......? But he doesn’t seem bothered at all...... Eh? I- In fact, why is this atmosphere so positive...... huh?)","Since Kaito’s first impression of Cornelia was good, and now he even saw her as a kindred spirit after bonding over pet talk, his favorability toward her was high. He showed not the slightest sign of aversion to the idea of going out together.","On the contrary, Cornelia, thrown into confusion by Kaito’s unexpectedly high level of favorability, could only smile through her fluster, while Eris, watching from the side...... had an expression that was hard to describe.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [The Wondrous Stomachache Carnival has been set...... may Cornelia rest in peace.]","~ ~ Chronicles of the Stomachache Warriors : Extra~ ~","<Miyama Kaito>","Stomachache Power: ★★★★★★★★★★","Draw Power: ★★★★★★★★★★","Endurance: ★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★","Pitifulness: ★","Stomach Medicine Consumption: ★","Ability to Inflict Stomachache: ★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★★","The root of many stomachaches, and himself carrying quite a few stomachache flags. He’s oddly popular with dangerous perverts, and since he knows basically everyone who makes Lilia or Eris clutch their stomachs, not to mention the likes of Makina, Phantasmal King's perverted subordinates, and countless other stomachache-inducing cases, both his Stomachache Power and Draw Power...... should be extremely high but...... in his case, his mental fortitude is absurdly strong, so his Endurance is off the charts, meaning none of it is actually a problem.","Every once in a while, he’ll claim he’s feeling mentally tired, but in reality, he’s not tired at all, remaining completely unfazed.","Even though he’s saddled with flags that should, under normal circumstances, annihilate his stomach, like Eden appearing 5 times a week, briefly it may be, Makina constantly chatting with him in his dreams, random perverts or a muscle-brained gorilla showing up now and then, and Gods from other worlds dropping by in turn...... his mind is ridiculously tough, and his adaptability is incredible, so he treats it all like nothing.","If anything, lately he’s gotten so used to it that even when Makina runs wild, spreading madness at a level that would drive an ordinary person insane, pouring out grotesquely long and abnormal monologues, he just lets it wash over him with a carefree air, thinking “If it weren’t for this side of her, Makina-san would actually be a really approachable, nice person.”. That’s how much of a monster he is."]},{"number":2350,"title":"Chapter 2350: The Promised Tea Party 19","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","I don't have much time, so today's chapter is a bit short.","I’m really glad I decided to join this tea party. Who would’ve thought there were custom brushes made specifically for each individual? That was a blind spot for me.","Bell’s coat is my pride and joy, I wash and shampoo her every day without fail, and brush her thoroughly, so I’ve always considered it to be soft, fluffy, and with the best texture, but the thought that it could be made even better makes my heart race.","I had been getting Alice to make special-order shampoos, but as for brushes, while I’d collected the highest-quality ones available, it never occurred to me to commission a custom-made brush.","......Maybe I could have one made for Lynn’s scales, too? The one I’m using now is good, but if something even better could be made, I’d love to have it. I should bring a few of Lynn’s scales and ask if it’s possible.","[I already knew that Kaito-sama cherishes his pets, but it seems you’re quite particular about it too.]","[Bell-chan’s coat is amazing. I remember it wasn’t just shiny like a professional groomer’s work, but the magic power in the fur was also incredibly beautiful. Do you even special-order the shampoo?]","Following Eris-san’s murmured remark, Kuro asked while recalling Bell’s fur. As expected of Kuro, she really understands. Of course, Bell’s fur being perfect is only natural, but noticing that the shampoo is special-order too shows her sharp eye.","[I asked Alice to make it. It’s a fairly recent thing, but we realized that if you process and add just a small amount of Fruit of the World Tree, the luster of the coat improves dramatically, so I had her tune it for me.]","[ ! ? ]","[Hehh, if Shalltear’s making it, then it must be flawless. Their food too, you have Shalltear prepare that, right?]","[Unn. I give Lynn one Fruit of the World Tree every day, but I figured she’d get bored of eating it raw, so I have it processed and mixed in. For Bell, I mix Magnawell-san's powdered scales into her food, which is also tricky to prepare, so I leave it to Alice.]","[ ! ? ! ? ! ? ]","As expected, Fruits of the World Tree hold strong life force, or rather, natural magic power, making them a perfect match for monsters like Bell and Lynn, so they’re extremely useful. I did receive quite a lot from Lillywood-san, but lately, Nebula has been able to produce as many Fruits of the World Tree as needed, so I’ve been using those instead.","According to Nebula, her fruits are specially adjusted for Bell and Lynn respectively, so these days I mainly use those. Incidentally, it was also Nebula who told me that mixing processed Fruit of the World Tree into shampoo enhances the sheen of the coat.","[Since Sela also wants to eat Fruits of the World Tree, Sieg-san also asks Alice to make her food too...... In Sela’s case, it seems she thinks of Lynn like an older sister, so she’s imitating Lynn, I guess?]","[Ahh~~ well, they’re both dragons, and Lynn-chan is older than Sera-chan, so that makes sense~~. Stories about close, sister-like relationships are heartwarming. Back then, Zwei also liked to imitate Ein a lot.]","These days, Sieg-san also asks Alice to specially make food, but instead of paying with money, it’s done through a kind of barter, exchanging them with Sela’s Midnight Diamonds.","She seems to have more money than she knows what to do with, sending most of it to Rei-san and Fia-san, so having food made directly must be convenient for Sieg-san as well.","[T- T- T- That’s such remarkable dedication.]","[Y- Yes. You can really feel Kaito-sama’s love for his pets.]","[......Just how much more luxurious is the life of Miyama Kaito’s pets compared to mine......]","Still, talking about pets naturally gets me excited. Since this is a tea party, it would be a bit much to stick to just one topic, so it’s probably time to change the subject.","Either way, I’m really glad I was able to attend this tea party. I’m truly grateful to Eris-san.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [He really spares no expense when it comes to his pets, and Kuro, being the richest in the world, talks about it casually, but the young ladies listening to these outrageous stories must be getting stomachaches...... Also, I’m pretty sure Marie is losing to Bell and Lynn in terms of standard of living.]"]},{"number":2351,"title":"Chapter 2351: The Promised Tea Party 20","paragraphs":["The tea party hosted by Eris went smoothly, though seeds of stomachache had indeed been sown here and there, if one focused solely on the event itself, aside from Kuromueina’s unexpected appearance, nothing irregular occurred.","Kaito, too, was happily chatting with the young ladies. Given that he already had many connections and was highly skilled in communication, he seemed to fit in quite well.","(......I can’t afford to lower my guard just yet, but for now, I’m relieved things are going smoothly. No, this tea party is hosted by me, held at the Hamilton Marquisdom’s villa, and the participants were carefully selected, so unexpected incidents shouldn’t occur...... That should be the case, but with Kaito-sama involved, the unease that lingers is frightening.)","In truth, Eris had prepared for all sorts of contingencies up until today, and she wasn’t careless. Kuromueina’s attendance as Kaito’s attendant was unforeseen, but thanks to her preparations, even that posed no issue.","Nothing further should happen, and yet that sticky feeling of unease wouldn’t go away.","[But tea parties are actually pretty fun. I kind of had this image that they’d be more like nobles probing each other’s intentions.]","[It’s not that such things don’t happen at all. But in this case, all the participants are from the Hamilton Marquisdom’s faction...... Simply put, they’re nobles who already share a fairly close relationship with the Hamiltons. That removes the need for probing and posturing, which is a big factor. If the scale were larger, however, then yes, it could become something like what Kaito-sama imagines.]","[Hehh. The only other tea party I’ve been to, aside from this one, was the afterparty for the Harmonic Symphony. That one had lots of tables set up, and people broke into small groups to enjoy themselves. Are large-scale tea parties like that too?]","[Yes, that’s exactly the right image. It’s a bit lighter in atmosphere than a formal party.]","Smiling at Kaito’s words as she replied, Eris allowed herself the tiniest bit of relief. The tea party was already nearing its end. She wasn’t letting her guard down, but it was hard to imagine anything happening at this point.","Even if an additional guest were to arrive, most of the tea and sweets had already been consumed, and the response would simply be \"Please come again another time\".","Considering Kaito’s personality, even if an acquaintance suddenly arrived near the end, he wouldn’t insist on extending the tea party. He’d persuade them instead.","Therefore, no more participants would be added. Kaito had already given parting gifts to each young lady, so there wouldn’t be any surprising development like him producing something extraordinary at this stage. Even Kuromueina was calmly enjoying herself without causing a stir.","Yes, there should be nothing to worry about. There should be no stomachache-inducing developments left......","[But since I’ve gotten a feel for what a tea party is like, maybe it’d be fun to host one myself. After all, I do have a tea brand......]","What words could describe the sensation in that moment? It was as though her back had frozen over. A tea party hosted by Kaito...... remembering the ship party and birthday party, it was easy to imagine the scale would far exceed common sense, but compared to such parties, a tea party should be smaller in scale.","And since it would be held at Kaito’s residence, it wouldn’t be possible to gather every acquaintance of his the way they had for his birthday party or the ship party.","[I- I- I- Indeed. I think it’s a fine idea, but if it’s at Kaito-sama’s mansion, perhaps it would be best to set a limit on the number of guests.]","[I suppose so. I can’t invite everyone I know, and besides, there are surely people who don’t even like tea...... Since today’s tea party was so enjoyable, I think a scale similar to this, or perhaps a bit larger, would be ideal. That way, it wouldn’t take too much preparation either, and I could put it together quickly.]","Yes, since it would be impossible to invite everyone, narrowing down the guest list to a certain number was inevitable. If one envisioned a gathering only slightly larger in scale than this tea party, then at most there would be room for about 20 participants...... Suppose he were to invite the God of Creation, the Supreme Gods, the Six Kings, the three rulers of the Human Realm, and the Founder...... just those top figures across all realms would already make 14. That would leave only a handful of slots, and anyone chosen to fill them would inevitably find themselves surrounded by the most powerful beings of every world, a situation sure to annihilate one’s stomach.","From her original standing, it would be unthinkable for Eris, a mere marquis’ daughter, to be selected for one of those precious few places. However...... if the very reason Kaito thought of hosting his own tea party was today’s event, and if he felt gratitude toward Eris for arranging it......","[Well, I’ll think it over carefully, but if I do host one, I’ll definitely invite you, Eris-san.]","[Y- Yesh......! I- It's an honor......]","For Kaito, his words were simply an expression of thanks, as since Eris had arranged such an enjoyable tea party, he wanted to repay her by entertaining her in return.","But for Eris, it was like receiving a death sentence to her stomach, and a strained smile inadvertently crept onto her face.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Just when I thought the newly introduced Stomachache Warriors were busy stacking up flags, in the very end, Eris got hit with a death sentence of a body-blow.]"]},{"number":2352,"title":"Chapter 2352: The Promised Tea Party 21","paragraphs":["The tea party that Kaito attended ended safely...... well, somehow safely...... aside from the participants’ stomachs, it concluded without incident. After seeing off all the guests, Eris gave instructions to the maids to clean up, then returned to her own room and finally let out a sigh of relief.","(F- For now, I managed to get through it. Of course, there are still worries about the future, but at least the tea party is over, and it seems Kaito-sama was satisfied, so that’s good. Still, with Kuromu-sama having participated as well, people might now assume that, on top of being close with a Supreme God, I’m also on good terms with one of the Six Kings. Considering the future, I’ll need to think carefully about this.)","First and foremost, Eris herself had become the center of attention in high society, which was already a fundamental problem. News of this tea party would undoubtedly spread quickly.","Even if they claimed to be from the same faction, there were 16 outsiders including the companions, the servants involved in preparing the tea party, and the servants who had seen Kaito and Kuromueina being guided....... Eris understood all too well that she can’t keep people from talking.","(Negotiations with the Death King camp were already moving forward, and I also have ties with one of the Seven Princesses. I’ve never directly met or spoken with Death King-sama or World King-sama, but given Duchess Lilia’s precedent, it’s entirely possible people will assume I’ve met the Six Kings as well.)","Up until now, the only two of the Six Kings Eris had personally spoken with were Kuromueina and Alice. As for Alice, there was no need to worry about rumors. If Alice wished, she could control gossip among the nobility however she liked, so Eris’ speculations on that front were meaningless.","(The real question is whether people will view these ties as mine personally, or as belonging to the Hamilton Marquisdom as a whole. In truth, it all stems from Kaito-sama and my personal connection with him, but the story of Kuromu-sama visiting the Hamilton household will certainly spread. And since dealings with the Death King camp will be carried out through the Hamilton household...... There's no doubt those seeking favor will increase. That said, countermeasures on that front will primarily be handled by Father, so I’ll likely need to arrange another discussion with Father and Mother.)","Since meeting Kaito, Eris reflected, the number of family councils had increased drastically. With that thought, her mind shifted toward the future...... toward what lay ahead.","(Without a doubt, Kaito-sama’s tea party will become a major issue...... Just imagining it already makes my stomach hurt. But if I attend without any preparation, who knows what might happen. And then there’s the matter of my promise to visit Kaito-sama’s home...... That’s already been decided for next month, so I should think of it separately from the tea party.)","During the previous party, Eris had accepted Kaito’s invitation to visit his home. After further discussion, they set a schedule, and it was decided she would visit next month.","She would be the first foreign noble to visit Kaito’s residence. Thinking about what might happen...... and about her stomach, which was already beginning to ache a little, she could only hope and pray that nothing would go wrong.","After returning home to the Sharon County estate from the tea party, Cornelia immediately headed for her father’s office. Inside, Count Sharon was working through a stack of documents, but he warmly welcomed his daughter when she arrived.","[Oh, welcome back, Cornelia. How was the tea party hosted by Hamilton Marquisdom...... ah, no, rather, the one hosted by Lady Eris?]","[I’ve just returned. Yes, as expected of Eris-sama, it was a splendid tea party...... but, um, there’s something I must report to you immediately......]","[......Is this about that esteemed person?]","[Yes.]","At Cornelia’s words, Count Sharon’s gentle expression hardened into one of seriousness. With a small wave of his hand, a prearranged signal, the aides and servants present in the office quietly excused themselves, leaving only Cornelia and her father inside.","[......First, let me confirm. There’s no denying that forming a connection with Miyama Kaito-sama would be highly advantageous for our house. However, the risks of overreaching and earning his displeasure are far too great in comparison. You understood that well and acted accordingly...... I can trust that, yes?]","[Yes. I didn’t try to push our name upon Kaito-sama, nor did I recklessly try to close the distance, and certainly, I didn’t attempt anything underhanded like using my feminine charms to curry favor.]","[I see. And...... what happened?]","[......The Underworld King, Kuromueina-sama, attended the tea party.]","[........................]","Upon hearing his daughter’s report, Count Sharon slowly raised his gaze toward the heavens. The only thought swirling through his mind was a single question...... \"Why did things turn out like that?\"","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [So, the time has come for the stomachache flag set at the tea party...... for the landmines scattered around to detonate......]"]},{"number":2353,"title":"Chapter 2353: The Promised Tea Party 22","paragraphs":["Even a man like Count Sharon, who possessed immense wealth within Archlesia Empire and had the standing of a prominent merchant, could never have predicted that Kuromueina would suddenly show up at a tea party his daughter attended. Thus, even after hearing a certain amount of explanation, his mind was still somewhat confused.","[......I understand that Underworld King-sama attended as Miyama Kaito-sama’s attendant, but I still find it hard to believe. No, it’s not that I think you are lying, but I simply cannot wrap my mind around it yet.]","[I understand how you feel, Father. I couldn’t quite accept the reality myself for a while either......]","[F- For now, I believe the Underworld King-sama is a gentle person, so there should be no problem...... but there was no rudeness that occurred, I hope?]","Kuromueina was the richest person in the world and the owner of countless major trading companies, a figure who could rightly be called the pinnacle of the economic world. Most top companies in various fields were under Kuromueina’s control, and though she had no desire to dominate personally, she possessed overwhelming power enough to rule the entire economy if she wished.","The Sharon family was a noble house with both power and wealth, owning one of the top five magic tool trading companies in the Human Realm, yet Kuromueina existed on a completely different plane. With the wealth and authority she commanded, she could easily bring the Sharon Trading Company to ruin, so it was no wonder that Count Sharon asked his questions with unease.","Count Sharon had met and spoken with Kuromueina several times regarding business matters and knew that just as the rumors say, she had a gentle and benevolent nature, but given the stature of the person in question, he still wanted to make sure.","[Yes, just as I had heard from rumors and from Father, she was cheerful and kind. At first, I was a little intimidated, but by the middle of the tea party, I and the other attendees were able to converse with her calmly.]","[I see, that’s good. It must have been difficult to deal with such an unexpected situation. However, eventually you would have had the chance to meet Underworld King-sama in your role at the Sharon Trading Company, so having made your introduction in advance is an advantage......]","[Umm, Father......]","[......Unn?]","[It’s not over yet.]","[.................]","Naturally, Count Sharon, as a noble who had dealt with many other nobles, had experience in deceit and strategy, so it was easy for him to read something from Cornelia’s expression.","It also didn’t take long for him to understand that the shocking content of Kuromueina’s story was still only the prelude.","[......What is this ominous feeling? Is there something more problematic than the Underworld King-sama matter......?]","[Yes...... Although it is unrelated to that matter, first there is this. It's that magic tool that allows direct orders to Nifty, which has been given to Kaito-sama’s friends. All the young ladies who participated received one as well.]","[Ahh, the magical tool I’ve heard about...... Is it really this small? If all the functions I’ve heard about can work at this size, the magic formulas engraved in it must be quite advanced. Well, since Miyama Kaito-sama is on good terms with Underworld King-sama and likely has many connections to the Seditch Magical Tool Trading Company, I wouldn't say it's impossible......]","After prefacing that it was unrelated to the main matter, Count Sharon looked at the magic tool with evident interest. He had often heard about it in rumors, but this was his first time seeing the actual item.","That said, for the Sharon family, Nifty’s products weren’t prohibitively expensive; rather, the ease of placing orders was welcome, so there was no issue.","No, the problem lay in the conversation that would follow.","[Now, for the main matter. It concerns the Victor Trading Company......]","[The Victor Trading Company? That small firm dealing in monster-related goods?]","[Yes. Miyama Kaito-sama has taken a strong interest in their custom brushes for monsters......]","[Unn? That shouldn’t be a problem. You can simply introduce him. They would be pleased as well.]","[Well, um, that is...... I would be the one to guide Kaito-sama......]","[..............................Huh? W- Wait...... g- guide? You mean you would personally accompany Miyama Kaito-sama for the introduction, rather than writing an introduction letter? W- Why would it come to that......?]","Even Count Sharon found himself completely at a loss. Indeed, regarding the tea party, he had hoped that his daughter, Cornelia, might leave a favorable impression on Kaito and build a friendly relationship, which would be very helpful for the Sharon family.","But arranging a meeting that felt almost like a date on a first encounter was several steps beyond what Count Sharon-sama had anticipated.","[No, in this case, it is partly my fault. Initially, as Father-sama suggested, I assumed I would write an introduction letter and offered to introduce him if Kaito-sama wanted to...... but it seems Kaito-sama interpreted that as meaning I would personally guide him...... In hindsight, I didn’t consider that Kaito-sama might be unfamiliar with the concept of introduction letters.]","[I- I see, so that’s how it is...... Indeed, given his influence and the breadth of his social connections, it’s easy to misunderstand, but if we consider Miyama Kaito-sama’s perspective as that of an Otherworlder, it makes sense that he would be unfamiliar with introduction letters......]","[Yes, I failed to anticipate that and my explanation was insufficient.]","[Well, it can’t be helped. It would be rude to correct it afterward...... So, when is it?]","[The 23rd of this month.]","[Only six days from now!?]","[Umm, Kaito-sama is extremely enthusiastic, and it just happened to fall on a day when my schedule was free......]","Seeing Cornelia’s expression, which was a mix of resignation and something else, Count Sharon looked up at the ceiling once more. Surely, by now, she and Marquis Hamilton would be having a lively conversation.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [His daughter went to a tea party and came back having made a promise to go out in six days with the World's Singularity...... In a way, this blow might be even heavier than what was dealt to Marquis Hamilton...... So this is the one-hit-kill type......]"]},{"number":2354,"title":"Chapter 2354: The Promised Tea Party 23","paragraphs":["A small territory on the frontier of Archlesia Empire...... peaceful, without any notable tourist spots, and although some effort was put into cultivating fruit, it was only enough to ship to slightly larger neighboring cities, not enough to call it a specialty product.","Into this poor barony, with few residents and even less tax revenue, returned Marie, who had attended the tea party. As usual, there was no teleportation gate within the territory, so she had returned by carriage from the nearest city that had one, and it was already late enough to be considered night by the time she got home.","The Ritch Barony had only the bare minimum of servants, so of course, no one came to greet her. Marie said a few words of thanks to the carriage driver, stepped down, and moved toward the mansion, opening the front door to go inside.","At that very moment, she encountered the eldest daughter of the Ritch Barony passing by the entrance.","[Ara, Marie. Welcome back.]","[I’m back, Onee-sama. Thank you for lending me your dress today.]","[Don’t mention it...... but, were you alright? It’s the best dress I have, but I was worried it might pale in comparison at a marquis’ tea party.]","[It’s true the other young ladies’ dresses were amazing...... but the fact that the Ritch Barony are a poor noble family is well known, so I don’t think it was a problem.]","Although the heir of the barony was the eldest son, the eldest daughter also attended social events compared to Marie, and possessed dresses sufficient to maintain the minimum decorum of a noble lady. Marie had borrowed one of these dresses to attend the tea party.","[Was it really that amazing?]","[It really was. It might have even been more luxurious than my brother’s wedding, and as expected, I felt nervous since I was the lowest-ranked among the young ladies who gathered. In terms of rank, there was also the third daughter of the Viola Viscounty...... but their financial power is completely different from ours. Honestly, I still wonder why I was invited...... I’ve only ever greeted Lady Eris-sama once...... I was impressed she even remembered me.]","[Hmmm...... I’ve only greeted Eris-sama once as well, so I’m in the same boat as you...... She’s someone on a completely different level, even if we're in the same faction. Still, it is indeed strange for the fourth daughter, Marie, to be invited. Hmmm...... maybe because you have no fiancé, and just convenient as a potential mistress?]","[If that’s the criterion, it definitely isn’t me. There are plenty of other beautiful noble ladies...... Well, I do take care of my appearance as a noble lady, but high-ranking noble daughters just have a completely different aura.]","Hearing her eldest sister speak jokingly, Marie let out a wry smile. She was indeed cute, but not an exceptional beauty, there were many noble daughters with superior appearances. In her own view, she was at best above average, and she was certain she hadn’t been chosen for her looks.","[Well, the plans of the great nobles often have depths we can’t even begin to imagine, so there’s no use thinking too hard about it. More importantly, Father and Mother were eager to hear about it too, so once you change, come to the dining hall.]","[Understood. There really is so much to report...... some of it is beyond what I can decide on my own, so I’ve been wanting to consult with them as soon as possible......]","[......Was it really that amazing?]","[......I still feel like I’m dreaming.]","After answering her eldest sister with an indescribable expression on her face, Marie moved to her room. On the way, she called one of the servants to help her change.","Normally, she would dress herself in her usual clothes, but since she was wearing her sister’s dress, a piece that could be considered the most expensive in the Ritch Barony’ household, she had the servant assist her and entrusted the dress to them.","[Oh, and regarding the ripples I can operate with my authority...... for now, please prepare to send one wooden crate. If possible, please pick out those with the highest quality.]","[Understood.]","Before she could forget, Marie gave instructions to prepare the ripples she had promised to gift to Kaito. One wooden crate might be a bit much, she thought, but Kaito owned a large-capacity magic box, and above all, it’s better to give more than less, so she decided to send a generous amount.","In a sense, it was both a masterstroke and a potentially disastrous move.","Indeed, giving more is better than giving less, and it also shows generosity. The ripples from the Ritch Barony were only distributed to nearby cities and wasn’t famous, but its quality was extremely high. It was the sort of product that could do well in a ripple exhibition.","Marie had no idea what would happen if she gave Kaito such a large amount.","She never even dreamed that he would like the ripples so much that, seeing how much there was...... he would decide to \"share it with acquaintances\".","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [She's really charged an enormous amount———– if it all detonated at once, the flags are so firmly set that there wouldn't be a trace of her stomach left.]"]},{"number":2355,"title":"Chapter 2355: The Promised Tea Party 24","paragraphs":["The Ritch Barony...... to put it simply, they were a poor noble household with many children. Including Marie, the Baron and Baroness had three sons and five daughters, ten people in all when everyone gathered. And now...... every single member of this large family had stopped eating and were holding their heads in distress.","The reason, of course, was the story Marie had brought back from the tea party she attended. At first, the atmosphere was cheerful, like they were listening to a pleasant tale from a trip. But as Marie’s story went on, the faces of the Baron’s family grew steadily darker, until at last they were holding their heads in despair.","[......Errr, to summarize...... being invited to a marquis’ tea party is already a huge matter, but not only that, it was one Underworld King-sama herself attended, where you are allowed to introduce yourself...... and on top of that, Miyama Kaito-sama acknowledged you as a friend and even gifted you a magic tool for placing exclusive orders with Nifty, which could be considered proof of that friendship......?]","[Yes, that’s correct.]","[......We were never taught how to deal with a situation like this.]","Baron Ritch forced a strained smile as he asked for confirmation, hoping it was just a mistake...... But when Marie affirmed his words, the Baron buried his head in his hands once more.","[To think...... even I have never spoken directly with one of the Six Kings. What on earth should we do......? And since this was at the Hamilton Marquisdom’ tea party, the entire Archlesia Empire’s nobility will probably know by tomorrow...... T- This is a disaster......]","[Well, in that regard, my husband and I only attend the capital’s parties about three times a year...... If things go as usual, the next one will be the celebration for Emperor Chris-sama’s birthday, so we still have some time.]","The Ritch Barony stood at the very bottom ranks of nobility...... so low that some might even forget such a house existed. And yet tomorrow, they would be at the center of noble society’s gossip.","Naturally, neither the Baron nor his wife had any confidence in handling such a situation well. Still, as the Baroness pointed out, their poverty meant they rarely attended social gatherings in the first place, so there was at least some breathing room.","[......Just how many times more expensive is Nifty’s tea compared to what we use now?]","[Would it even be measured in times? Couldn’t it be dozens of times more......?]","At the second daughter’s murmur, the eldest son replied with a complicated expression. Just as Marie had worried during the tea party, regularly buying Nifty’s products in amounts sufficient to avoid criticism from other noble houses was far beyond the Ritch Barony’s means.","[In that regard, it seems they do have lower-priced products, like the sugar cubes I received this time...... So I was thinking we could somehow manage with those, at least enough to keep appearances...... or so I hope. Ah, and since Miyama Kaito-sama mentioned he liked ripples, I was planning to give him a crate, but would that be alright?]","Though Marie was also troubled by the financial burden, she thought they might manage by purchasing only the cheaper options in modest amounts, just enough to preserve appearances.","And as for gifting ripples to Kaito, she decided to confirm it with her family just in case.","[Ah, that’s no problem. We have plenty of ripples left over.]","[......Expanding sales channels costs money too. The world really is harsh.]","The Ritch Barony owned a large ripple plantation, and aside from taxes, sales of ripples were their primary source of income. However, their shipments only reached nearby towns, and expanding their distribution across the entire Archlesia Empire would require significant resources. Compared to the businesses of other noble families, their earnings were little more than a drop in the bucket. What’s more, because their plantation was large but their outlets were few, their ripples tended to pile up in surplus every year, so giving away a crate posed no issue at all.","[Still, since we’re sending it to none other than Miyama Kaito-sama, we should really send something of good quality, and as fresh as possible. Hmmm...... it’ll cost a bit, but let’s use the teleportation service.]","[Indeed. With the teleportation service, including preparations, it should reach Miyama Kaito-sama by the day after tomorrow. That might be best.]","Marie agreed with the Baron’s words. The teleportation service, as the name suggested, used Teleportation Magic to deliver packages. While more expensive than carriage or flying dragons, it allowed goods to reach Symphonia's Royal Capital in a short time, even from the remote corners of the Archlesia Empire.","[We have confidence in our ripples’ flavor. I do hope he’ll take a liking to it.]","[Hahaha, if he does, sales might even go up.]","The Baroness spoke half in jest, and the Baron cheerfully played along with a laugh.","At this point, it was only a joke...... just the sort of \"wouldn’t that be nice\" talk...... yes, at this point, that is......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [T- These guys...... they’ve gone and hastened their stomach’s death on their own...... I thought Cornelia would be the first to get her gut punched, but they just went and booked themselves an express delivery straight to stomachache hell......]"]},{"number":2356,"title":"Chapter 2356: The Promised Tea Party 25","paragraphs":["It happened just as I’d finished lunch and was relaxing. Illness-san came by my room.","[Kaito-samaaa, a package has arrived for youuu. Since it’s quite laaaaarge, I’ve had it placed in front of the warehouse out baaaaack.]","[A package?]","Normally, any mail or deliveries for me are handled by Anima, but today she was out meeting with a shop she invested in, so Illness-san had come to let me know instead.","[Yeeeees. It’s a package frooooom the Baron Ritch household of the Alcrecia Empiiiiiire. A large wooden crate filled with ripplesss.]","[Ah, ohh, from Marie-san’s family...... Eh? It’s here already!?]","Marie-san had indeed said during the tea party that she’d send me some ripples produced at the Ritch Barony, but I never imagined it would arrive only two days later.","Did she really rush to send it?","[She did say she’d send some ripples, but I’m surprised it arrived in just two days. Errr, it’s in the backyard, right? I’ll go check...... wait, was the box really that big?]","[It was a wooden crate of the kiiiiiind used by merchants for stock, a commercial-size craaaaate. If the contents are all ripplessssss, then these ripple craaaaates...... there are about 10 crates of theeeeem, which likely contains around 30 ripple fruuuuuuits.]","[That’s a huge amount.]","So basically, errr, they sent it in something like a shipping container...... around 300 fruits. That’s insane.","When I went with Illness-san to the backyard warehouse...... sure enough, there were wooden crates the size of a container sitting there.","If it was full of ripples, then having hundreds inside wouldn’t be strange at all.","The letter from Marie-san that arrived with the crate read: \"Since I wasn’t sure how many servants lived at Miyama Kaito-sama’s estate, I’ve sent you a commercial-sized box\". She went on to explain that since they had relatively few buyers compared to their harvest, ripples often went to waste, so she hoped I’d accept them without hesitation.","Ahh, I see. Marie-san doesn’t know that my home only has a few servants, so she assumed it was like a high-ranking noble’s mansion such as Lilia-san’s, and sent enough to handle heavy consumption without issue.","[The ripples look delicious, but the sheer amount is amazing.]","[Indeeeeed. If you keep them in a magic boooooox, they won’t deterioraaaaate, but even so, consuming this much will be difficuuuuuult. Perhaps you could distribute them to your acquaintances, Kaito-samaaa?]","[Good idea. Yeah, with this much, I’ll set aside one crate for us to eat at home, and share the rest to those I know.]","Just as Illness-san said, even though storing them in a magic box would prevent them from deteriorating, it would still be tough to consume all of these at my place alone, so I decided to share them with my acquaintances.","[Will you be having some right awaaaaay?]","[Yes. Since we’ve got them, I’d like to try one.]","[Theeeeen, I’ll cut it and bring it to your room with some tea that goes well with rippleeeees.]","[Thank you.]","I handed Illness-san one crate of ripple that we planned to eat at home, stored the rest in my magic box, and returned to my room.","Soon after, Illness-san arrived with the sliced ripple and tea, so I decided to try some right away.","I suggested she join me, and she readily agreed, so it became our afternoon snack time together.","[Ah, it’s sweet and delicious.]","[Yeeees. This is an even better quality ripple than expecteeeeed. Even in Symphonia Kingdooooom, which grows a lot of fruit, you rarely see ripples of this qualityyyyy.]","The ripple from the Ritch Barony was far more delicious than I had anticipated. How should I say this...... In appearance, it looked like a normal ripple, but its sweetness struck immediately, clearly a variety with stronger natural sugar.","That said, it wasn’t cloying; it had the refreshing sweetness typical of ripple, and it paired wonderfully with the tea.","[Making it into jam might also be deliciouuuuus.]","[That sounds good. I’d like to try spreading it on bread.]","[I’ll prepare some for you sooooon.]","[Looking forward to it. Anyhow, this tastes quite different from the ripples sold around here. I guess it’s the variety?]","[This rippleeeee is a variety relatively common in Archlesia Empiiiiire. However, to bring out such rich sweetneeeeeess, the growing conditions and cultivation methods must be carefully manaaaaaged. Ritch Barony seems to have a very fine estate for thaaaaat.]","Indeed, it had that sense of a high-quality ripple crafted with care. With a taste like this, it wouldn’t be surprising if it became hugely popular, but according to Marie-san’s letter, it’s only sold in nearby towns. In that case, it’s probably consumed mostly around Ritch Barony and might not be circulating in the Capital or elsewhere.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [The Stomachache Carnival begins!]","Serious-senpai : [Mercy...... Couldn't you have any mercy......?]"]},{"number":2357,"title":"Chapter 2357: The Promised Tea Party 26","paragraphs":["Deciding to share the large number of ripples that Marie-san had sent, I immediately went to a certain place that same day.","[Heh~~ so that’s why you brought them.]","[Yes...... By the way, what about Cento-san and Cien-san?]","[They’re both kids who enjoy pottery and glasswork, so it seems they’ve gathered to work on their creations. Maybe seeing Nebula-chan’s work before inspired them to create?]","[I see.]","I had come to Tre-san’s room in Kuro’s castle, but since Cento-san and Cien-san weren’t there, I asked about them. Both were in the castle, but apparently engaged in their own hobbies.","[Well, anyway, here’s the ripples I’m sharing.]","[Thanks~~ They look delicious. Hmmm, but why did you think of coming to me first?]","[Ah~~ I was planning to distribute them to various acquaintances, and the first person who came to mind was Tre-san.]","In reality, there were others who received hummingbirds before Tre-san, but I planned to check their schedules and deliver it another day.","It’s considerate to confirm their availability, rather than just showing up unannounced. Tre-san...... well, if she’s free, I figured it’d be fine to hand it over for now.....","[Staaaaare~~]","[W- What is it?]","[Hmmm...... feels suspicious...... Kaito should have lots of acquaintances, so why did you think of me first?]","Tre-san gave me a sharp look...... a- as expected of her, she has quite the keen intuition.","[Ahh...... well, maybe it’s because our closeness, like our affection meters, went up?]","[Hehh~~ hoh~~ hmmm~~.]","[Quite the doubtful look you got there.]","[Hmmm, I wonder if it’s really because that afexion meter went up...... Or maybe it’s because, in Kaito’s mind, I fall into the category of “someone you can handle a little roughly”...... that part is what I’m curious about.]","[......Tre-san! Shall we eat the ripples!?]","[You’re trying to dodge it!? That’s basically an admission there!]","N- No, of course, it’s not a lie that Tre-san was the first person I thought of. But, well, it’s also true that I’ve categorized Tre-san...... fairly close to how I treat Alice in my mind.","In other words, she’s someone I can interact with comfortably, so my favorability towards her has definitely increased......","[Good grief, Kaito, you don’t seem to show enough respect or admiration toward me.]","[......Respect or admiration toward Tre-san?]","[Stop making that face like you’ve never heard those words before. Don’t you think it’s rude to this Onee-chan?]","[If Tre-san doesn’t categorize me in a similar way, then I apologize.]","[......Shall we eat the ripples!?]","[......Let’s eat.]","Being able to exchange jokes like this, knowing full well that both of us are just teasing, makes talking with Tre-san really fun.","Tre-san picked up one of the ripples I had given her and took out what looked like a fruit knife from her magic box, beginning to peel it.","[......You can peel it huh.]","[Of course I can...... Eh? Did you think I was such a useless person that I couldn’t even peel a ripple?]","[...................]","[I wish you’d deny that without smiling silently......]","While we were having that exchange, Tre-san finished peeling a ripple, cut it into bite-sized pieces, and placed them on a small plate.","[Now then, can this satisfy the palate of the ripple critic that I am?]","[Alright, then please give your review in a critic-like manner.]","[Sure~~ Then, I’ll dig in right away~~]","Tre-san took a bite of the ripple, quietly closed her eyes, and chewed. As always, she looked like a tall, cool-type woman, so it suited her perfectly.","After a moment, she opened her eyes wide, extended one hand toward me, and gave a thumbs-up.","[......Sweet and delicious!~!]","It was an extremely strong, simple-is-best kind of review.","[......Seems like you might need to take down the \"critic\" claim there.]","[It's no good huh~~ too bad. That aside, it really is a delicious ripple.]","[Yes, I like it too. I’d like to give something back to Marie-san, who sent so many of them......]","[A return gift? Ah~~ but Kaito, you just met that Marie girl, right? So you wouldn’t really know what she wants......]","I wanted to send some kind of thank-you gift to Marie-san, who had sent so many ripples, but as Tre-san said, I’d only just met her, so it was hard to figure out what would make her happy.","[......Ah, speaking of which, she mentioned it’s inconvenient to move around because there aren’t any nearby Teleportation Gates in her place, right?]","[Oh, in that case, how about a teleportation magic tool? It’d be really useful.]","[Ah, indeed. With a teleportation magic tool, she could go straight to a registered location, and even for other places, if she registers a city with a Teleportation Gate, moving around would be much easier.]","[Unn, unn...... Ah, I’ve got it!!!]","[Unn?]","[Fufufu...... I have a brilliant idea!]","......I wonder why? For some reason, when Tre-san says that, I can’t help but feel slightly worried.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I see, I see, someone who’s good at punching your stomach out of kindness...... and Tre, who’s adored by the richest person in the world, possesses a rare ability that earns her tons of money, and as we’ve even seen hints of it in Cento and Cien’s past arc, a money sense comparable to that of a noble lady...... the two of them are now thinking of a return gift...... while the reasonable Cento and Cien are absent...... It’s over for you, Marie.]"]},{"number":2358,"title":"Chapter 2358: The Promised Tea Party 27","paragraphs":["For now, regarding the return gift, I decided to hear Tre-san’s opinion, who seemed unnecessarily confident.","[Still, even if it’s something the other person wants, a teleportation magic tool is way too expensive to give as a return gift, right?]","[Indeed, that would be far too much as a return gift for ripples.]","Just as Tre-san said, no matter how many ripples she sent, in the end, they're still just ripples...... Even if each piece is about 200 yen, and there were 300 of them, that’s only around 60,000 yen.","Of course, considering she sent that much just because she heard it was my favorite at the tea party, it’s a significant amount and sum, but compared to a teleportation magic tool, the price is literally in a completely different range.","[Exactly! That’s why I make it myself at a low cost!]","[Oh? Making a teleportation magic tool yourself...... That sounds pretty difficult, doesn’t it? And even if you make it yourself, can it really be that cheap?]","[Don’t worry, first, look at this...... Hmm, ei!]","With that, Tre-san pulled out a rather large chunk of crystal.","[A crystal...... no, wait, could this be a magic crystal?]","Because it was transparent, I initially thought it was just normal crystal, but on closer inspection, I thought I could faintly see a greenish tint.","[Yep. This is a magic crystal with less than 1% purity, too weak in magic power to be used in regular magic tools. They're instead used as a material for magic paper.]","[Magic paper? That’s the stuff used for disposable magic formulas like in random boxes, right? Isn’t that usually made from scraps left over when processing magic crystals?]","[Exactly, but even as scraps, if you only use high-purity magic crystals, the cost gets high, and any extra magic power is wasted. So we crush low-purity magic crystals like this, which have no other use, into powder and mix it in...... well, basically, it’s just for bulking.]","[I see......]","Indeed, if you only need enough magic power for one magic formula, anything beyond that is wasted, so mixing in low-purity magic crystal powder would make it cheaper to produce.","[......So, what about this magic crystal?]","[Right. Take this, along with this set of metal materials...... all together, 500 R.]","[Huh? You mean I’m buying that from you, Tre-san?]","[Unn.]","[Understood. Here’s 500 R...... actually, that’s cheap. For something this size, only 500 R?]","[It really only has use as bulking for magic paper. If you want it for decoration or something, a normal crystal is fine, and processing a magic crystal requires specialized skills, so it’s not worth the effort to process such a low-purity magic crystal.]","I see, there aren’t many uses, and even for decorative purposes, it requires skill and effort, so using normal crystal is better. Given that, the price of 50,000 yen for this size including other materials makes sense.","[Well, anyway, this magic crystal and materials are now yours, Kaito. And...... Hmph!]","[Whoa......]","When Tre-san touched the magic crystal, the color spread through it as if paint were mixing in transparent water, turning the entire crystal green, gradually deepening in shade.","After a while, the entire magic crystal turned black...... now over 90% purity.","[All right, preparation is complete.]","[Ahh, so now we can make the magic item. That would certainly keep costs down...... but isn’t the magic formula for teleportation magic difficult to inscribe?]","[That part’s fine. I just called the others and told them through hummingbird to come to my room, so they should be arriving soon.]","[Unn? Who?]","Just then, there was a knock at the door, and when Tre-san gestured for them to enter, Funf-san and Sechs-san came in.","[Tre-neesan, you needed me...... Arehh? Kaito’s here too. Welcome.]","[Hello, Funf-san, Sechs-san.]","[Well, well, Miyama-dono. Hello...... it’s been since the birthday party.]","After exchanging brief greetings with Funf-san and Sechs-san, Tre-san placed the plate with the cut ripple in front of them.","[Thanks for coming, you two! First, here, this is the ripple Kaito brought to share! Go ahead, eat up!]","[Eh? Unn...... oh, this is a really tasty ripple.]","[Indeed, it has quite the exquisite flavor.]","Watching Funf-san and Sechs-san eat the ripple, a deep smile spread across Tre-san’s face.","[......You ate it, right?]","[ [ . . . . . . ] ]","At Tre-san’s quiet words, Funf-san and Sechs-san froze mid-motion.","[......W- We did eat it...... Eh? This? Tre-neesan, is this some kind of trap?]","[Calling it trap makes it sound bad~~ It’s not like that. I just thought, since you two ate the ripple Kaito shared, you might as well help with making a teleportation magic tool~~ See, Kaito and I prepared the materials here, so we want to use these to make a teleportation magic tool.]","[A- Ahhh, I see...... so, I’d handle the processing, base, and decorations.]","[And I would inscribe the magic formula on the magic crystal. That’s an easy task. With a magic crystal of this size, even the latest magic formulas can be engraved.]","At first hesitant, the two nodded in understanding after Tre-san’s explanation and willingly agreed to assist with the creation of the teleportation magic tool.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [No, even if you cut production costs, it doesn’t change the burden on the recipient’s stomach though!? And since Tre’s abilities have to remain a secret, in the end, it’ll just be like Kaito buying an enormous, high-purity magic crystal and sending it as a return gift, right!?]","? ? ? : [Do you understand now? I’m sure it wasn’t intentional, but from Tre-san’s explanation, Funf-san and Sechs-san don’t know that the ripple originally came from Marie-san, nor that the teleportation magic tool is meant as a return gift...... In this state, Funf-san and Sechs-san are interpreting it as Kaito wanting a teleportation magic tool for use at home, something not for his personal use but by other people like his servants. With their normal common sense, they’re in no position to say anything to stop it.]","Serious-senpai : [The whole course of this thing...... it’s like they’re trying to give Marie a stomachache on purpose...... you could have just told them yourself......]","? ? ? : [No, I...... Alice-chan finds situations like this funny, and as long as it doesn’t cause any harm, she just watches and laughs.]"]},{"number":2359,"title":"Chapter 2359: The Promised Tea Party 28","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","Thank you for waiting. The Volume 10 of YuuShou's manga adaptation will be released on September 24. Pre-orders have already started on Amazon and other sites, so I hope for your support.","The official URL and related information are posted in the Activity Report.","Thank you as always, and sorry to keep you waiting! Here is the release date and cover reveal for Volume 9 of the manga adaptation!","The release date will be September 24! Here is the official site from KADOKAWA:","[I Was Caught up in a Hero Summoning, but That World Is at Peace – Manga Adaptation (KADOKAWA official site)]","And here’s the cover!","It features the very cool Alice-chan. Alice sure is an all-rounder, she can handle serious scenes, comedy, and even romance.","I had already shared some with Tre-san, and thanks to the cooperation of Funf-san and Sechs-san, the teleportation magic tool was quickly completed. Since I had come all the way to Kuro’s castle, I figured that if there were any other acquaintances available, I might as well give them some too.","[Hawawawa, this ripple is super delicious!]","[Yeah, it really is tasty. I like it too.]","[Yes! This is a ripple from the western part of the Archlesia Empire, isn’t it? It’s a different variety from Raz’s ripple, but this kind is also very delicious!]","Checking with the hummingbird, I saw that Raz-san had some free time, so I went to the farm and shared some ripples with her. She was really happy and reacted in such an adorable way that it warmed my heart as well.","[Raz-san, your ripples have that refreshing sweetness with perfect balance, right? That one’s really delicious too. But still, that’s amazing, you can tell where a ripple comes from just by tasting it?]","[Raz really loves fruits, so Raz can usually tell~~ There are lots of different varieties of ripples~~ There are red ones like Raz’s ripple and this one, and even green ones that stay green even when ripe~~]","[I see. You sure know a lot, Raz-san.]","[Ehehe, I just happened to know about it~~ But this ripple is really, really delicious. Raz loves it too!]","[I got it from a lady named Marie of the Ritch Barony in Archlesia Empire, but according to her letter, they don’t really sell it much elsewhere, so they end up with a surplus.]","[Ahh~~ that’s rough. Raz understands how that feels very well. Before Kaitokun-san introduced Raz to Kaori-san, there was too much rice piling up, and Raz didn’t know what to do.]","Come to think of it, that was true. Before I introduced Kaori-san, Raz-san had been troubled because she had too much rice. But since Kaori-san runs a diner, even though it’s a personal business...... her consumption of rice as an establishment was on a completely different scale. After the introduction, Raz-san had been overjoyed, saying she was able to \"sell a lot of rice\".","[If you don’t mind, if Raz-san knows anyone who also likes ripples, could you tell them? If sales go up, I’m sure Marie-san will be happy too.]","[Yes! Raz has lots of friends, so Raz’ll tell them too!]","[Thank you very much.]","Well, it might just be a small push, but if it helps raise sales even a little, it’s worth it. I decided that I would casually introduce the Ritch Barony’s farm to acquaintances whenever I shared some.","While we were talking like that, a bright, familiar voice called out.","[Raz-sama~~! I came to visit...... Aya!? Kaitokun-san is here too!]","[Ah, it’s Tir! Welcome!]","[Hello, Tir-san. What a coincidence.]","The one who showed up was Tir-san, and as always, she seemed close with Raz-san, probably often playing together. After a light greeting, the conversation turned to what we had been doing, so I mentioned that I had brought some ripples as a gift to share.","[If you’d like, Tir-san, please have some too.]","[Thank you! Tir really likes ripples, so Tir is very happy.]","[Tir~~ there are some already cut up over here, so you should try them~~]","[Okay, I’ll dig in! !? Hawawawa, this ripple is super delicious!]","Her reaction was almost identical to Raz-san’s, and honestly, it was adorable. The way Raz-san and Tir-san acted and reacted together was just so cute that simply watching them was very soothing.","[Marie-san, from the Ritch Barony in Archlesia Empire, is a friend of Kaitokun-san’s. It seems she’s having a hard time with sales, so Tir, if you don’t mind, could you also introduce her ripples to your friends too?]","[Yes! Tir also has lots of friends, so I’ll make sure to introduce Marie-san’s ripples properly!]","Hearing Raz-san’s words, Tir-san gladly promised to help spread the word as well. Like Raz-san, Tir-san seemed sociable with many friends, so I thought this might really turn out well, and continued happily chatting with the two of them.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [Heeeeere's the second one!]","Serious-senpai : [Oi, cut that out, that’s the kind of thing that goes on for five rounds straight, isn’t it......?]","? ? ? : [Raz-san (super popular, tons of friends), Tir-san (super popular, tons of friends)...... No doubt they’re gonna be selling hot. Well, anyway, more importantly, the cover of the manga adaptation’s Volume 10...... What in the world, there’s a transcendental beauty gracing the cover. This is one of those times where you have no choice but to bulk-buy!]","Serious-senpai : [......I just witnessed some shameless self-promotion. But well, since this cover has a serious vibe, I personally rate it pretty highly.]"]},{"number":2360,"title":"Chapter 2360: The Promised Tea Party 29","paragraphs":["The day after Kaito visited Kuromueina’s castle, a certain guest arrived at Razelia’s farm.","[Ah, Nia-san and Mina-san! Welcome!]","[Hello, Razelia-dono.]","[Thank you for having us.]","The ones visiting Razelia were Satania and her aide, the minotaur Minagard, and Razelia welcomed them both with a smile.","Sociable as she was, Razelia’s circle of acquaintances was broad. She was on familiar terms with nearly all of the Six Kings' executives and got along well with them.","[Razelia-dono, thank you for mediating with the Fairies the other day. It’s only a small token of gratitude, but we’ve brought some sweets.]","[Waa~~ thank you! If anything comes up again, please let me know. Raz has loooots of Fairy friends, so if Raz can help, Raz’ll always lend a hand!]","This time, Satania’s visit was to express her thanks. She had previously needed specialty goods from the Fairies for her trading company’s supply line, and since Razelia was well-connected among the Fairies, she had asked her to act as a mediator.","At Satania’s signal, Minagard handed over a neatly wrapped package to Razelia, who received it with a cheerful smile.","They passed a little time in lighthearted conversation, until Razelia suddenly spoke as if something had occurred to her.","[Oh, that’s right! Nia-san, yesterday Kaitokun-san shared some ripples with me, would you like to try some too?]","[From Miyama Kaito-sama?]","[Yes! Kaitokun-san received these ripples from a noble friend in the Archlesia Empire, and it’s really delicious! Kaitokun-san said he liked them very much.]","[Ripples that Miyama Kaito-sama himself praised...... and from the Archlesia Empire, no less? I’m very interested. Then, if you’ll allow me to try one...... I see, this is indeed a ripple of quite high quality.]","When she heard that Kaito had taken a liking to it, Satania’s eyes clearly lit up, and after taking a bite of the ripple handed to her by Razelia, she nodded in satisfaction.","[......You say they're from the Archlesia Empire, but where exactly?]","[He said they're from Marie-san of the Ritch Barony, who’s apparently a friend of Kaitokun-san! But, um, even though they're really delicious ripples...... errr...... mmm...... it sounds like Marie-san’s family isn’t very good at business, so they’ve been troubled by having too much ripples left over.]","[The Ritch Barony, is it? I see...... Certainly, that region’s distribution flow is rather poor. There’s no transfer gate, and the nearest trade city is quite far from the Barony’s lands. In terms of shipping, there are many inconveniences. It’s quite possible that even high-quality goods could end up buried and overlooked.]","[Yes. Kaitokun-san was worried too. He asked Raz to introduce ripples from the Ritch Barony to Raz’s friends.]","Hearing Razelia’s words, Satania touched her chin, her expression thoughtful. Since Kaito’s name had been mentioned, there was no way she would respond carelessly.","(......If the revered Miyama Kaito-sama is troubled, then it is unthinkable for one who has sworn loyalty to him to remain still. Financially supporting the Ritch Baron household would be simple, but matters of distribution are not something solvable by money alone. The ripples themselves are of very high quality, and if tied into western distribution channels and improved further, it could yield long-term profits...... Perhaps it would be best to simply purchase land in that area and establish one...... a \"transfer gate\", that is...... If it involves Miyama Kaito-sama’s friend, I could also secure Gluttony’s cooperation. That would allow the gate to be constructed with very little investment...... Yes, I’ll try bringing this up with Gluttony.)","The Lord Trading Company, which Satania headed, was so massive it was counted among the Five Great Trading Companies, its financial power far beyond comparison with most nobles.","Even constructing a transfer gate wouldn’t be such a great expense, and with the help of Gluttony, an expert in Space-Time Magic, the construction cost could be dramatically reduced.","Moreover, Gluttony, like Satania, held deep loyalty to Kaito. Since this involved Kaito’s friend, there was no doubt she would readily agree to cooperate. Considering both the investment and return, it was a venture that promised considerable profit.","[......Razelia-dono, you’ve given me some very useful information. I will also take some steps, as a trading company, to support Miyama Kaito-sama’s friend.]","[Ohh! If Nia-san’s going to help, that’s really reassuring!]","Satania smiled at the chance to be of service to Kaito while Razelia was just innocently delighted...... Meanwhile, the members of the Ritch Barony, completely unaware of these events, were about to be swept up in a great tide of change.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [And heeeeere's the third one!]","Serious-senpai : [Stop that, pleaseee!? At least break it up into stages and divide it!!! If you cram it all in at once, would there even be a trace left of her stomach!?]"]},{"number":2361,"title":"Chapter 2361: The Promised Tea Party 30","paragraphs":["Before me stretched a breathtaking sight: a field of Blue Crystal Flowers blooming in full glory, with snowy plains and mountains in the distance. The white and blue contrast blended together in a way that was simply magnificent.","[It's amazing. A Blue Crystal Flower field this large is overwhelming, and having this terrace where you can see it all at once is really wonderful too.]","[......Unn...... Everyone...... worked hard for it.]","I had come to visit Isis-san to share some ripples, and since the terrace she had once mentioned, built to overlook the Blue Crystal Flower fields, was now complete, I was invited to enjoy tea there together with her and the Death King's subordinates.","It seemed she hoped to someday hold tea parties here, so this gathering was also something of a trial run.","[By the way, have you decided on a group name, like those of the other Six Kings’ factions?]","[Yes! With Iris as our Head, we decided on the name \"Six Stars\". Since the other Six Kings’ Executives also have numbers in their titles, it matched nicely. Well, I’m not really strong enough to call myself an Executive yet, but I joined as one of the initial members.]","[I see. But I’m sure you’ll soon be strong enough that no one could beat you, Eul.]","[Ehehe, thank you so much!]","I gave Eul’s head a light pat in response to her lively answer, and she narrowed her eyes happily while wagging her tail. Just then, Iris-san and Polaris-san brought over tea, fruit-based sweets, and some Ripple I had brought along as a gift, neatly cut and arranged on the large table.","[......Iris...... Polaris...... Thank you...... Since everything is ready...... let’s begin.]","At Isis-san’s words, the tea party started. They began by trying the ripples I’d brought, cut into bite-sized pieces with toothpicks stuck in them for easy eating.","[......Delicious...... A really wonderful ripple.]","[Indeed. The flavor seems well-suited for use in sweets and desserts.]","Isis-san clearly enjoyed it, smiling softly, while Iris-san also looked impressed. Since Iris-san had a hobby in cooking, perhaps she was already thinking about desserts she could make using ripples.","[Ohh, so this is a ripple. It’s my first time trying it. The texture feels kinda nice.]","[Spica, you’ve never had Ripple before? Well, it’s my first time too...... though for some reason, I feel like I might’ve eaten it before? Hmmm, maybe in those hazy memories I had before mutating into Mystic Silver?]","It seemed both Spica-san and Eul were tasting ripples for the first time, their curious expressions showing genuine interest.","[Good gracious, how fascinating. Even among ripples, the flavors can vary so much depending on the type......]","[Yes, quite so. Its taste is very different from the Black-Blood Fake Ripple I once had.]","[No, that one's a poisonous fruit resembling ripples, growing by feeding on corpses...... it’s not a ripple at all......]","Polaris-san and Rasal-san also gave it favorable reviews...... though I couldn’t help but overhear something about a rather questionable \"fruit\" that definitely didn’t sound edible. I decided to pretend I hadn’t heard it. Most likely, I’d never eat it anyway.","Overall, everyone seemed pleased with it, but among them, the one radiating the strongest joy was Sirius-san.","[......Magnificent!]","[Did it suit your taste, Sirius-san?]","[Yes, this ripple is truly wonderful. Insectoid Demons generally have a fondness for fruits, and I’m no exception...... I especially enjoy sweet fruits. This ripple perfectly matches my tastes.]","Perhaps it was rude to compare, but it reminded me of how rhinoceros beetles loved sweet fruits. Either way, it was clear that this ripple hit right at the center of Sirius-san’s preferences, both as a member of her species and on a personal level.","[......If Sirius likes it that much...... and since Iris also wants to try using them in cooking...... perhaps we should buy some in bulk?]","[That would be great. Marie-san did mention they had difficulty selling their ripples......]","Seeing Sirius-san so visibly delighted by the taste, Isis-san chuckled and suggested buying ripples directly from the Ritch Barony.","Considering sales had been struggling, having another buyer would surely be a welcome thing for Marie-san as well.","[......Then, Rasal...... sorry...... but could I ask you again?]","[In that case, I will soon visit the Ritch Barony and secure a contract.]","[......Unn...... please do...... since she’s Kaito’s friend...... give them slightly better terms.]","[Understood. I will propose a contract with terms somewhat favorable to the Barony.]","At Isis-san’s words, Rasal, the one among the Death King’s subordinates who handled trade, gave her consent. Still, if she just suddenly showed up, Marie-san would surely be startled, so I figured I’d better send a hummingbird or a letter ahead of time to let her know.","[Oi, Alice. Why did you suddenly appear and start pouring wine into a glass?]","[Well, I was simply marveling at how you can so precisely provide both profit and stomachaches at the same time, fascination and delight, you see.]","[......What on earth are you talking about?]","Apparently, Alice had appeared beside Iris-san, pouring wine into a glass while exchanging words with her, but since their voices were low and I was seated a fair distance away, I couldn’t quite make out the full details.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [And heeeeere's the fourth one!]","Serious-senpai : [Please stop already! Just from the charge so far, the Ritch Barony’s stomach-life is already at zero!!! And hey, why are you drinking wine over there!?]","? ? ? : [Well, it’s just amusing...... Besides, aside from the whole stomachache thing from the sudden developments, everything happening is actually in Ritch Barony’s and Marie-san’s favor, so there’s no real reason to stop it...... and, well...... it’s just so entertaining to watch......]"]},{"number":2362,"title":"Chapter 2362: The Promised Tea Party 31","paragraphs":["After visiting Isis-san, I headed over to the God Realm. The reason was to share some ripples with Fate-san and Shiro-san.","At first glance, going from the Demon Realm to the God Realm sounds like traveling an incredible distance, but with my teleportation magic tool, it’s quick and not a problem.","For now, I only plan to share the ripples with Shiro-san and Fate-san. The other Gods I know don’t really eat much, and I don’t get the impression they enjoy food for its own sake. Chronois-san, for instance, does drink alcohol, but hardly eats. Life-san, apparently, hardly eats or drinks at all.","Shea-san does eat and drink, but since she dislikes sweets, bringing her sweet ripples would be more like harassment. As for Sky-san, Gaia-san, and Marine-san, I don’t really know their eating habits, so I’ve left them out this time.","Fate-san will eat if I bring them to her, so that’s no problem. Shiro-san, though, most likely, well, she definitely has no interest in the ripples itself. If she wanted to, she could make as much as she liked anyway......","But if I left her out in this kind of situation, she’d sulk, so I plan to bring her at least one.","(I do not sulk. It is simply a rightful protest against unfairness.)","R- Right...... Well, I’ll make sure to bring some, so please don’t protest.","Speaking of which, this isn’t related, but I’ve been thinking about hosting a tea party someday. Would you come, Shiro-san? I’ll be inviting some others too but......","(I have no interest in the tea party itself. However, the prospect of it being a tea party hosted by Kaito-san is very appealing, so I’ll attend.)","Well, we already have tea together pretty often, so that makes sense. Anyway, understood. When I actually hold it, I’ll send you an invitation.","As I was having this exchange with Shiro-san, Fate-san’s temple came into view. Waiting outside to greet me was Fate-san herself...... and also Life-san.","[Oh, Kai-chan, welcome.]","[Hello, Fate-san. Life-san too, I see you’re also here to visit.]","[Hello, Miyama-san. Yes, I had just come to ask God of Fate about the proper mindset when dealing with Humans. But perhaps I should return later.]","It seemed Life-san had only just arrived, dropping by unexpectedly, and from her attitude, if Fate-san and I had already arranged to meet, she didn’t intend to intrude.","[Kai-chan brought me some of his stuff to share, you know.]","[......Share?]","[Yes. I recently got to know a lady named Marie-san of the Ritch Barony from the Archlesia Empire, and she gave me a lot of ripples, so I’m sharing some of it.]","Hearing my words, Life-san placed her hand thoughtfully on her chin, looking intrigued.","[The Ritch Barony...... if I recall, they are nobles with lands in the western part of Archlesia Empire. So one of their members is friends with you, Miyama-san?]","[Yes, though we only met recently. The ripples she gave me were really delicious, I like them a lot. I hadn't thought of sharing with Life-san since I heard you hardly eat or drink but...... if you’d like, would you care for some ripples as well?]","[Thank you very much. Then, if only as a reference, may I try one?]","[Of course. Here you go.]","Since we’d met anyway, I offered Life-san a ripple. She accepted it and gave me a polite bow.","[My heartfelt thanks...... Well then, if I stay too long, God of Fate might get mad, so I’ll excuse myself here...... The Ritch Barony huh...... perhaps I should confirm with God of Fertility...... Miyama-san seems to hold them in high regard...... so depending on the situation......]","After smiling and offering her thanks, Life-san muttered something under her breath and took her leave.","[Kai-chaaaan, what about mine?]","[I figured you’d find eating ripple as it is a hassle, Fate-san...... so I had Illness-san bake it into an apple, well, ripple pound cake. Let’s eat it together.]","[Ooh, nice! Okay then, let’s have some tea together~~]","I was certain Fate-san would consider peeling or cutting fruit too much trouble, so I had Illness-san turn it into a dessert instead.","I planned to spend about an hour leisurely with Fate-san, and then head over to Shiro-san afterwards.","(If you’re worried about time, shall I activate the Super WIN System?)","No, I don’t think using the Parallel World Utilization System just for tea is necessary...... I still have plenty of time today, and nowhere else to go, so it’s fine.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [Aaaaand the fifth one!]","Serious-senpai : [Y- You're a devil...... This is gonna be that, right? First the teleportation magic tool, then promotion, then teleport gates, then new business partners, and just when she thought it was over...... now this...... Isn’t this gonna lead to something blessing-related......? Like going to talk to Elune and strengthening the Blessing of Fertility or something......?]"]},{"number":2363,"title":"Chapter 2363: The Promised Tea Party 32","paragraphs":["In the God Realm, at the Temple of Life, the God of Fertility, Elune, had arrived after being urgently summoned.","[Thank you for coming, God of Fertility. I’m sorry for calling you here on such short notice.]","[Eh? No, God of Life-sama always tends to be abrupt with these things......]","[Is that a problem?]","[Hyiih!? N- Nothing at all!]","Elune, who had almost dug her own grave with that slip, hurriedly shook her head. Life looked at her with some suspicion but decided to move on to the more pressing matter.","Placing the ripples she had received as a gift from Kaito on the desk, Life began to ask Elune.","[Do you know of the noble family called Ritch Barony?]","[Ritch Barony...... ah, yes, a Barony that holds lands on the western frontier. It’s an old family, but their territory has no particular strengths, and they’re poor at business as well. It’s said their influence and wealth as nobles rank among the lowest in Archlesia Empire.]","[I see...... well, the young lady of that house, Marie Ritch, told me herself that she is friends with Miyama-san.]","[Friends? That’s the first I’ve heard of it...... Miyama-san doesn’t have much to do with the Empire’s nobility to begin with...... ah, but come to think of it, I heard that Eris-san of Hamilton Marquisdom recently hosted a tea party and invited Miyama-san. They may have met there. The Ritch Barony should be part of the Hamilton faction after all.]","As Elune was responsible for Archlesia Empire, she was well-informed about its internal affairs. Thus, she was aware of Eris hosting a tea party where Kaito was invited, and surmised that might have been when he met Marie.","[Miyama-san seemed to value the ripples produced by the Ritch Barony very highly.]","[Ah, yes. The ripples from Ritch Barony are indeed well-regarded. They only distribute it to nearby cities, so it isn’t famous, but it’s like a hidden gem. Still...... Miyama-san huh......]","For most matters, Elune possessed a fairly ordinary sense. However, with a God's way of thinking, as Life's subordinate, her way of thinking is close to that of Life's.","In other words, as someone who received Shallow Vernal's Blessing, Kaito must always be given top priority, a principle that guided her actions.","After listening to Life’s words, Elune thought for a moment, then spoke.","[......Shall we strengthen the Divine Protection upon Ritch Barony?]","[Indeed so. It would help prevent a situation where Miyama-san might be unable to obtain the ripples he values. Of course, if I were to perform the Divine Protection myself, it would cause too much of a stir......]","[Indeed. The Divine Protection I’ve spread over the whole Empire emphasizes coverage over potency. So for the Barony, I can grant a separate, stronger Divine Protection. That should greatly increase ripple harvests, and may even improve their quality further.]","[Then let’s proceed with that.]","[Understood. If we wish to strengthen it further, Divine Protection from God of Harvest, God of Trees, or even God of Time and Space-sama's subordinate, God of Agriculture, might also be effective.]","[Yes, that may be useful if needed...... But for now, let’s see how things go with your Divine Protection alone. Speak with Marie Ritch of the Ritch Barony, and once she’s informed, reinforce your Divine Protection.]","[As you command.]","And so, without anyone present to retort, a nearly unheard-of decision was made: to strengthen a Divine Protection specifically over one small territory.","Six days after the tea party hosted by Eris, in the mansion of the Ritch Barony, on the western frontier of Archlesia Empire, Marie, dressed in clothing modest for a noble, was humming to herself as she brewed tea.","Though she was a noble lady, Marie was the fourth daughter of a poor Barony, and had neither a personal maid nor servants. The Baron and his wife, the heir and eldest son, as well as the eldest daughter who managed the orchards, each had maids who doubled as guards, but for the other children like Marie, the family could not afford such luxuries.","Thus, in the Ritch Barony, it was common sense that even as nobles, \"they do for themself what they can do themself\". Marie, too, brewed her own tea.","She prepared it, dropped in one of the adorable animal-shaped sugar cubes Kaito had given her as a souvenir, and smiled happily.","(When it looks so cute, it really lifts your mood. What a lovely sugar cube, just what one would expect of a gift from Miyama Kaito-sama.)","With such pleasant thoughts, Marie was enjoying a tranquil moment...... until a maid, pale and frantic, burst into her room......","[Lady Marie!? S- S- S- Something s- serious has happened!!!]","[W- What is it, all of a sudden...... a natural disaster? No, in such cases, Elder Sister should———–]","[No, not that. I- I don’t even know how to explain this...... F- First, a return gift has arrived from Miyama Kaito-sama.]","[A return gift? A- Ahh, for the ripples...... oh dear, I’ve troubled him again. How embarrassing.]","Though confused at the uncharacteristic panic of the usually composed maid, Marie assumed it was nothing serious. But that notion was shattered to pieces by the maid’s next words.","[And also, a letter has arrived from Satania Darklord-sama, President of the Lord Trading Company, and from the Death King's Executive Rasal Marfik-sama, each requesting to meet with Master and Lady Marie. In addition, a letter from the Temple of Goddess of Fertility-sama has asked that Master and Lady Marie visit the temple on a convenient day!!!]","[.....................]","In that instant, all thoughts left Marie. The cup in her hand slipped, shattered on the floor, and left a spreading stain...... but neither she nor the maid had the presence of mind to react.","So this is what it truly means for your mind to go blank? She understood the words, yet couldn’t comprehend them. A dull, sluggish haze filled her head, and on top of it came a stabbing pain...... as though her stomach had shriveled to half its size.","[.....................................................Why?]","That single word was all she could squeeze out...... And tragically, there was no one to give her an answer.","For Marie Ritch, the fourth daughter of the Ritch Barony...... thus began the upheaval, the rise, and the stomachaches.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [Impact, now!]","Serious-senpai : [The power of that charged shot is way too much...... What did Marie even do to deserve this!? She only sent ripples out of goodwill, and now this...... This is just too cruel......]","? ? ? : [It’s nothing more than the perfectly natural cycle of goodwill being returned with goodwill. If I had to point out one thing, it’s simply that the goodwill being returned isn’t just on the level of a hundredfold repayment, it’s far, far beyond that.]"]},{"number":2364,"title":"Chapter 2364: The Promised Tea Party 33","paragraphs":["Of course, though both Eris Dia Hamilton and Marie Ritch are noble ladies, they are vastly different. Natural talent plays a role, but even more significant are their positions and authority.","As the heiress of a Marquisdom, Eris has undergone strict education since childhood, experiencing society and various settings, and possesses authority befitting her status.","For instance, if Eris were placed in the same situation Marie faces now, she would, of course, feel the strain on her stomach, but even then, she could make many decisions by her own judgment. At the very least, she could determine an initial course of action and response.","By contrast, Marie is the fourth daughter of a poor Barony. While she has received enough education to avoid disgrace as a noble lady, she is neither heir nor successor to the family’s enterprises, and therefore holds no authority to decide family policy.","[......N- No, no no no, impossible! This is far beyond what I can decide. E- Errr, please contact Father and Mother right away, and also Elder Brother and Elder Sister, and have them return immediately. If you say it concerns Miyama Kaito-sama, they should understand.]","Unless her parents, the heir Eldest Son, or at the very least the Eldest Daughter with some authority in the barony were present, she could not deal with the Lord Trading Chamber matter, the Death King faction’s matter, or the summons from the Temple of Fertility.","What’s worse, her parents were summoned by Marquis Hamilton to the capital along with the other tea party attendees’ parents, the eldest son was at another noble family’s party, and the eldest daughter had gone to a nearby city for agricultural trade.","Desperate to consult someone yet finding no one available, Marie, feeling her stomach twist in pain, ordered her maid to get in touch immediately.","[......F- For now, until someone returns...... let’s first check the return gifts. If there’s also a letter from Miyama Kaito-sama, it might explain the reason behind all this.]","[Do you think this is the influence of that esteemed person?]","[It has to be. I mean, otherwise, there’s no reason I’d be called by name like this......]","Not only Baron Ritch but all three parties who had reached out specifically named Marie alongside him, and the only explanation for such a thing could be Kaito’s involvement.","Pressing her aching stomach, Marie left the room with her maid to begin checking the return gifts.","In the main residence of the Hamilton Marquisdom in the Capital of Archlesia Empire, within its conference chamber, the head of the household, Marquis Hamilton was gathered with his heir Eris, Count Sharon, Baron Ritch, and the parents of the young ladies who had attended the tea party Eris hosted a few days prior.","The agenda was to discuss precautions for future dealings with Kaito. However, just as the meeting was about to begin, a maid entered.","[Pardon me. To Baron Ritch and his wife, an urgent message has arrived by hummingbird, addressed to your retainer. Lady Marie Ritch requests that you return home immediately, as a matter concerning Miyama Kaito-sama has arisen which she cannot resolve herself.]","[A- An urgent message...... N- No, but, we’re about to begin the meeting......]","Though Baron Ritch replied hesitantly, his expression showed clear unease. He and his wife were the lowest ranked among those present, and being summoned here by Marquis Hamilton, it was unthinkable to abandon the meeting and leave.","Yet, contrary to his reluctance, Marquis Hamilton spoke gravely.","[You must return at once. If you delay, things could become unrecoverable...... I’ll arrange for a mage who can cast Teleportation. Go home immediately by Teleportation Magic.]","[Eh? L- Lord Marquis!?]","Instead of simply granting permission to leave, the marquis was even providing them with a mage capable of Teleportation, making Baron Ritch stunned. Meanwhile, Eris, who seemed to have prepared in advance, received several small bottles from the maid and handed them to the Baron couple.","[Baron, Baroness, please take these.]","[T- This is......?]","[Something I was taught by Duchess Lilia Albert of Symphonia Kingdom. A very effective stomach medicine...... I’m sure you’ll need it. Please also give one to Lady Marie, and use them as directed.]","[......Y- Yes...... eh?]","It was an utterly bizarre thing, to be given stomach medicine as a gift. The Baron and his wife weren’t the only ones unsettled; the other nobles also stirred in unease. Yet both Marquis Hamilton and Eris were completely serious, leaving no room to object.","[......From the wine cellar, prepare a few bottles of wine for Baron Ritch and his wife to take with them...... Baron Ritch.]","[Y- Yes!? What is it, Milord......]","[Drowning in alcohol is foolish. But at times, there are circumstances where one must briefly avert one’s eyes, lest the heart break. Use it not for escape, but to collect yourself...... so that you may once again face forward.]","[......U- Uh...... Lord Marquis, Lady Eris, w- why are you looking at us like that...... W- What in the world are we about to go through......?]","This reception was exceedingly strange, yet both the Marquis and Eris wore earnest expressions, their eyes filled with genuine concern for the Ritch couple. This only magnified their dread.","[......Please, steel your hearts.]","[We shall reconvene regarding today’s discussion another time...... I wish you fortitude.]","The gazes cast upon them were like those sent to men marching off to die. Cold sweat ran down Baron and Baroness Ritch’s backs. For some reason, the words they soon heard, \"The Teleportation Magic is ready\", rang in their ears like the pronouncement of their execution.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I see...... Considering all the stomachaches Eris and the Marquis have endured up until now, their reaction is only natural. But for Baron Ritch, who hasn’t yet experienced many stomachaches, it must feel like a bizarre situation......]"]},{"number":2365,"title":"Chapter 2365: The Promised Tea Party 34","paragraphs":["For the time being, since it was about checking the return gift addressed to her, Marie came with a maid to the room near the mansion’s entrance where delivered parcels and such were kept.","[......That’s quite a large box. And this one...... has a sealing magic formula placed on it?]","[Yes. I believe the key to unsealing it is written in the letter. Since this letter is addressed personally to Lady Marie, we have not checked its contents.]","As for the parcels and letters delivered to Ritch Barony, those addressed to the household itself were generally checked by the maids and servants before reporting. The letters from the Lord Trading Company, from Rasal, and from Elune had been addressed to the household, so their contents were confirmed and then conveyed to Marie. But when it came to letters addressed to an individual, the maids could not simply open them on their own; instead, after checking for dangerous spells and the like, they would bring them to Marie herself for confirmation.","[For now, let’s read the letter.]","Along with the box containing the return gift was a personal letter to Marie from Kaito. Since it likely had something to do with the current situation, Marie opened it with a tense expression.","The beginning contained simple greetings, gratitude for sending ripples, and mention of sharing it with friends.","[It is delightful that Miyama Kaito-sama enjoyed our ripples. Now then, from here it seems to be about the return gift. Errr...... \"I remembered Marie-san once said you struggled with travel, so I purchased the materials and, with the help of a friend, had a teleportation magic tool crafted to send you as thanks\"...... Eh?]","[......A teleportation...... magic tool?]","Unable to believe what was written in the letter, Marie lifted her face from the paper in stunned silence and turned to the waiting maid. The maid too wore an expression of disbelief, and together, almost at the same time, the two of them looked toward the box that likely contained the gift.","[......U- Umm...... Teleportation magic tools...... even the cheapest ones, how much do they cost?]","[Even an outdated secondhand model...... would exceed 10 white gold coins, I believe......]","[Wait. Please wait...... This is so shocking I can’t process it...... Because, well, the difference in value compared to the ripples I sent...... it’s just far too......]","[H- He did say he purchased the materials and had it made himself, so the cost was probably reduced somewhat...... A- And if it truly is something as expensive as a teleportation magic tool, then sending it in a sealed box would make perfect sense.]","Teleportation magic tools were, without comparison, among the most expensive of all magic tools. Only high-ranking nobles could usually afford to own one.","Well, even the Ritch Barony could afford a secondhand outdated teleportation magic tool, but because the performance of that magic tool would just be poor and the magic crystals degraded with age, they would not last long. To pay several to dozens of white gold coins for such a thing would be too much of a waste, and so they had never bought one.","[I- I’m starting to feel frightened...... but first, let’s finish reading the letter. Errr...... ah, from here it talks about the letters that arrived at our house.]","Deciding to continue reading the letter first, she found that it went on to say one of Isis’ subordinates had taken a great liking to Ritch Barony’s ripples and, as part of the Death King’s camp, wanted to purchase a certain amount in bulk. It mentioned that Rasal, who handled such transactions, would likely be visiting the Barony soon, and asked for her cooperation.","[I see, so that’s why Rasal Marfik-sama of the Death King’s camp will be coming. In that case, Father should attend as well as Elder Sister...... Errr...... Well...... there’s nothing written here about the Lord Trading Company or the Goddess of Fertility. H- Hmmm, well, at least we managed to learn something.]","The reason for Rasal’s visit was explained in Kaito’s letter, but there was not a single word about the Lord Trading Company or about Elune, leaving Marie with a bewildered look. Still, since one of the three mysteries was now clarified before her parents’ return, she felt just a little relieved.","[......Ah, here is the pass for releasing the magic formula. Please go ahead.]","[Understood. I doubt it’s trapped or cursed, but just in case, Lady Marie, please step back a little.]","The maid, having received the letter from Marie, confirmed that she had stepped far enough away before touching the box and undoing the sealing magic formula. After giving Marie a reassuring nod, she opened the box.","[Ababababa, h- hyiiiiih...... ahyiiih......]","[Lady Marie! Please, stay calm!]","[N- No, no no no...... I can’t...... I just can’t......]","When the teleportation magic tool emerged from the box, Marie’s strength left her body; she collapsed onto the floor, letting out a strangled scream with a stiff expression.","It was only natural. Both Marie and the maid had assumed that even if it was a teleportation tool, it would be a cheap, outdated, low-performance model. But what lay before them was a magnificent piece made with a massive black magic crystal.","[Please...... Please tell me my eyes are playing tricks on me. That...... That looks like a black magic crystal to me.]","[......Lady Marie, I understand your feelings, and my own hands won’t stop trembling either...... but umm...... there’s no mistake. It is a top-grade crystal, with purity over 90%.]","Marie and the maid exchanged glances once again, their faces pale. She could almost feel her stomach screaming inside her, yet there was nothing she could do. All she could do was stare blankly at the teleportation magic tool.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Is that alright? At this rate, Marie’s stomach is going to be destroyed before Baron and Baroness Ritch even get back......]"]},{"number":2366,"title":"Chapter 2366: The Promised Tea Party 35","paragraphs":["Slumped where she had collapsed, Marie stared at the teleportation magic tool with eyes full of despair.","[......Um...... how much would you estimate this is worth?]","[There can be variation depending on the spell formula...... Ahh, there’s a manual here. Fumu...... I see...... Lady Marie, I believe this uses a nearly up-to-date magic formula. It’s probably the type that can readily transfer between the Human Realm and the Demon Realm.]","[H- Hyiiih......]","[No matter how you estimate it, I’d say it’s on the order of several hundred white gold coins......]","[Awawawawawa...... T- That’s easily worth more than our estate!?]","Hearing the maid’s words, Marie trembled and turned deathly pale. To be frank, it was an ultra-luxury item she’d never seen before, and just hearing the estimated price drained the color from her face.","[T- T- T- This is the return gift? No, no, no!? I mean, a ripple costs about 2R each! The ripples I sent were at most 6 or 7 copper coins...... and the return gift is several hundred white gold coins...... I- It’s just so expensive, I’m terrified. U- Umm, you’re not my personal maid or anything, but please......]","[Yes, rest assured. Until Master returns, I will guard Lady Marie and the teleportation magic tool. That said, an item of this class is so prohibitively valuable that almost no one would try to steal it, and even those who might would likely avoid it because the risk is too great......]","A teleportation magic tool more valuable than the Ritch Barony’s manor...... It couldn’t just be left here, so for now, it would be stored in Marie’s magic box, but possessing something so high-end terrified her.","It wasn’t that someone was targeting her or that burglars would break into the Ritch Barony, she was simply uneasy because it was so extravagantly expensive.","[......Um, Lady Marie. Is there a possibility that that esteemed one desires you...... as a woman, and sent such a luxurious gift as an indirect gesture?]","[Definitely not. It’s not just that Miyama Kaito-sama isn’t the sort to buy a woman with money...... but fundamentally, I’m not worth this much. Not out of self-deprecation, but objectively, the fourth daughter of a poor Barony wouldn’t command several hundred white gold coins. Even if I were an unparalleled beauty, it wouldn’t be possible. If anything, I'm someone the Ritch Barony finds somewhat difficult to handle.]","The Ritch Barony didn’t have much power as a noble house. They didn’t have the means to provide suitable positions or marriage matches for all their children.","In practice, the Eldest Son, who is the heir, and the Eldest Daughter, entrusted with managing the estate...... and perhaps the Second Son and Second Daughter as their assistants, can be provided for by the Barony, but beyond that, most must find work on their own.","As for Marie, she was studying accounting and aiming for a national certification; if she could pass the difficult exam, she might get into the estate’s accounting department, but it’s a narrow gate and quite difficult.","[If I don’t get the national certification, I’ll probably take an office job at some trading company...... Either way, it’s likely I’ll end up with a status similar to a commoner. We have few connections, so marriage prospects are unlikely...... The Ritch Barony is poor but not destitute, so they wouldn’t arrange marriage or an affair for money, but even if that were the case, I’d only be worth one white gold coin at best, two would be an exceptionally high price. This teleportation magic tool is completely out of proportion.]","[I see...... then why not become a maid in the future?]","[Being a maid is harder than getting the national accounting certification...... Besides, I can’t use magic, so it’s impossible for me.]","In this world, a maid is considered an elite profession, someone who possesses knowledge, skill, and combat ability at the highest level. There is a vast difference between an ordinary servant and a maid, only those who pass the strict examinations of the World Maid Association are permitted to call themselves maids.","Naturally, they are highly paid. The Ritch Barony employs a fair number of ordinary servants, but due to the high wages, they can only afford to hire five maids.","[......Then that means this really is a return gift for the ripples, isn’t it? Truly astounding.]","[......My stomach honestly feels like it’s twisting into knots. He said he bought the materials and had it made himself, but the magic crystal itself is already unbelievably expensive, isn’t it?]","[A crystal of this size, with over 90% purity, is not just costly but also nearly impossible to obtain without strong connections in the magic crystal trade. Processing something of this size requires top-class craftsmanship as well. Among magic tool trading companies, only the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company would likely be able to handle stock of this class with ease.]","[Well, Miyama Kaito-sama is Kuromueina-sama’s lover. His ties with the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company would be quite strong...... Um, just to confirm...... would it be unacceptable...... to claim this as Barony property instead?]","[He presented it to you, Lady Marie, did he not? In that case, for the Barony to take possession of it would come across as an insult to him......]","[I thought so...... but now my assets have surpassed Elder Brother’s and Elder Sister’s...... I really...... really feel sick to my stomach.]","If asked who the rightful owner of this teleportation magic tool was, the answer was obvious: since Kaito gifted it to Marie, for anyone else to claim it would risk being seen as an affront to him.","That meant the teleportation magic tool could only belong to Marie, and the Baron and his wife would surely conclude the same. Marie's mind understood this...... but her stomach rejected it entirely, sending sharp, stabbing pain as if to voice its protest.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Maids are the chosen elite...... W- Well, leaving that aside, for the sake of easy calculation: if we value the teleportation magic tool Kaito gifted at around 300 white gold coins, and the ripples Marie gave at about 6 copper coins...... that works out to a 50,000-fold return gift...... No wonder her stomach is screaming. And it should be about time for the Baron and his wife to return, right?]"]},{"number":2367,"title":"Chapter 2367: The Promised Tea Party 36","paragraphs":["In one of the rooms of the Ritch Barony’s mansion, larger than the others and more suited for discussions, the Baron and his wife, who had returned swiftly via Teleportation Magic, were left speechless after hearing Marie’s report.","This was truly what it meant to be at a loss for words. The dumbfounded Baron Ritch froze in shock, and it took him quite some time to reboot.","[......The Lord Trading Company, one of the Death King's Executives, Goddess of Fertility-sama...... and on top of that, a state-of-the-art teleportation magic tool as a return gift for the ripples...... N- No good. I’m getting dizzy......]","[......Me too. Honestly, I just want to pretend I never heard this and go lie down in the bedroom.]","The Baron muttered with a pale face, and his wife, pressing her head as if in pain, forced out her words. What was truly terrifying was that everyone who wanted to talk with them was, from the perspective of the Ritch family, overwhelmingly superior in rank.","The Lord Trading Company, one of the Five Major Trading Companies, possessing immense wealth and terrifying influence within Archlesia Empire. An Executive under the command of Death King Isis, one of the Six Kings. And the Goddess seated in the Temple of Fertility, one of the most crucial institutions to the Empire itself...... By rights, Baron Ritch, whose rank was so low he was practically at the bottom of the nobility, should never have any connection with such people.","[U- U- U- Umm, Father...... t- this means I myself also have to participate...... right?]","[Since you were directly named, Marie, you’ll have no choice but to attend. Given how overwhelmingly superior their positions are, it would be best for only the two of us, myself and you, as specified, to meet with them. The only one whose purpose is clear is Rasal Marfik-sama of the Death King’s camp huh......]","[Yes. That was written in Miyama Kaito-sama’s letter. They want to purchase a certain number of ripples in bulk, so I don’t think that will be a problem...... as long as we don’t commit any blunders...... um, but, I’ve only had the bare minimum of education, so I- I’m not very confident......]","[Don’t worry, Marie...... I’m the same. These aren’t people a poor Baron from the frontier should be talking to. I have no idea what I’m supposed to do either.]","For now, it had been specified that only the Baron and Marie would attend, and only they would respond to the talks. Naturally, the other parties were far too high-ranked to refuse, so not meeting was never an option.","Still, the fact that most of the intentions behind the meetings were completely unknown filled them with an indescribable unease.","[......Just what business could the Lord Trading Company have......? All our domain really has are ripples.]","[And what’s more, it isn’t just a subordinate who’s coming, but Satania Darklord-sama herself, isn’t it? Since my name was specified, I assume it’s connected to Miyama Kaito-sama, but I can’t think of any reason at all......]","There was no way the Ritch Barony could have imagined that, after hearing about the ripples from Razelia, Satania would be coming to propose a land sale contract for the construction of a teleportation gate in their Barony. All they could do was tilt their heads in confusion.","[The Goddess of Fertility wrote that we could come by on whatever day is convenient for us, so we could even visit as soon as tomorrow.]","[Indeed. We don’t know her purpose either, but we can’t keep her waiting. We’ll need to go as soon as possible. As for Rasal Marfik-sama and Satania Darklord-sama, I’ll write replies to their letters and arrange the dates. Most likely, we’ll need to set the earliest possible schedule, so Marie, prepare yourself for that.]","[Y- Yes, I understand.]","There were still many circumstances they're puzzled about, but now that Baron Ritch himself, the one who held decision-making authority in the household, had joined the discussion, the immediate plans began to take shape.","Both the Baroness and Marie were already suffering stomachaches and had quickly taken the medicine Eris had given them, but at least, they thought the course of action was now decided...... until the very next moment, when a flustered maid came rushing into the room.","[Forgive me for interrupting your discussion! There’s something urgent that I need you to confirm......]","[W- What happened?]","[Please look at this magazine. It’s my personal copy, but it’s a fairly popular publication. I bought the newest issue today, and when I was reading it, I found this page......]","[ [ [ ! ? ! ? ] ] ]","The maid placed the magazine on the table and opened to a page. The eyes of the Baron, his wife, and Marie widened in shock as they looked.","\"Hot Topic! The Rapidly Rising Fame of Ritch Barony’s ripples\"","Marie and the others stared at the headline as if it were something unbelievable. And of course, that was natural. The ripples of the Ritch Barony were indeed of good quality, but they were only distributed to nearby cities and were by no means famous.","At best, they might have been called a \"hidden gem\", but not anything exceptionally outstanding. There were plenty of ripples of equal or even superior quality produced elsewhere.","At the very least...... it should not have been the kind of product that warranted being written about in an article like this.","\"Right now, what’s rapidly spreading in popularity, particularly in the Demon Realm, is the Ritch Barony’s ripples. The reason is unclear, but we’ve learned that the owner of the Fairy Grand Farm, authorities of the Seditch Magic Tools Company, and even Executives under the Six Kings such as one of the Seven Princesses, the Fairy Princess Tirtania-sama have all been talking about their ripples. The rumors are still fresh and no detailed information has been obtained yet, so further developments will be worth watching. According to hearsay, a person named Marie seems to be involved in this matter, but we are still in the process of gathering information.\"","Reading the article, written in a slightly gossipy tone, the faces of the Baron, his wife, and Marie turned pale as sheets. Yes, what they didn’t know was that after Kaito had casually asked Razelia and Tirtania \"If you don’t mind, could you recommend them to your acquaintances?\", both had gone out of their way to introduce the ripples to others...... which was now leading to the stirrings of a small boom.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [Trap Card, activate! Pursuit!!!]","Serious-senpai : [Don't you...... have a heart?]"]},{"number":2368,"title":"Chapter 2368: The Promised Tea Party 37","paragraphs":["After waking up, finishing breakfast, and relaxing a bit back in my room, a thought suddenly came to me. Probably today or tomorrow, the return gift, a teleportation magic tool, would arrive at Marie-san’s place.","Hmmm, it’s definitely going to surprise her...... I really feel like I’ve done something bad to Marie-san.","When I first heard Tre-san’s proposal, I thought it was great if we could make a teleportation magic tool at a low cost and send it as a return gift. But once the tool was finished, packaged with a sealing magic formula, and I sat down to write the accompanying letter, it finally hit me...... I couldn’t really write about Tre-san’s ability in the letter......","Tre-san’s ability is treated as top secret even within the Seditch Magic Tool Company, and I was asked not to tell even Cento-san or Cien-san. Tre-san herself never uses her ability or talks about it anywhere except in front of the family or me.","......Well, if it’s just me or the family, she uses it for all kinds of silly things...... Like the other time, after finishing the teleportation magic tool, she declared \"With my ability, I can make ripples even sweeter!\" and probably fiddled with the sugar content. She ended up making ripples so sweet it was overwhelming, then collapsed muttering \"It’s too sweet, I feel sick!?\", but that was only because it was in front of someone who already knew her ability.","And since I couldn’t mention Tre-san’s ability in the letter...... The teleportation magic tool, which should have looked like it was worth around 1000R, about the same as the ripples we had been sent...... was in reality crafted with an extremely expensive magic crystal of over 90% purity.","The value gap was far too great compared to the original ripples, so it was obvious that Marie-san would be shocked...... But by the time I realized it, the tool was already complete, sealed, and packaged. After putting in so much effort together with Tre-san, Funf-san, and Sechs-san, there was no way I could suddenly say \"Never mind, let’s prepare something else instead\". so I decided to send it as it was.","If Marie-san ended up feeling burdened or apologetic by it, I thought I could just ask her to share more ripples with me again another time. That was my reasoning...... but still, maybe I really should have prepared something else?","[......No, isn’t it fine? You’d just end up not knowing what to do with it if you kept it yourself anyway, Kaito-san.]","[Yeah, well, that’s true, but...... also, why the heck did you suddenly show up out of nowhere, drinking wine over there......?]","Just as Alice, who suddenly appeared and began sipping from a wine glass, said, honestly, I don’t need another teleportation magic tool. I already have a special one, and other than what I have, Anima carries one in her magic box, and we also have two more stored in the warehouse for anyone else to use when needed...... Counting mine, that makes four teleportation magic tools, and in my room there’s even that special teleportation gate that lets me return home just by picturing it. ......So really, I don’t need any more teleportation magic tools; they’d just go unused.","On top of that, Illness-san and Caraway can use Teleportation Magic themselves, so the two stored in the warehouse hardly ever get used anyway.","[Besides, even if you had prepared something else, you’d just end up pulling some new source of stomachache from somewhere unexpected, so it’s meaningless. ......Oh, and by the way, this isn’t wine, it’s grape juice. Want some, Kaito-san?]","[Ah, if it’s juice, then sure, I’ll have some.]","Since I had plans this afternoon with Cornelia-san to visit a trading company that makes special brushes for monsters, I didn’t feel like drinking anything alcoholic beforehand, even if my Blessing could nullify it, but grape juice is fine.","As Alice prepared a wine glass for me while listening to my words, she gave a wry smile and said:","[Well, it’s not like having a teleportation magic tool is ever a bad thing, so there’s no need to worry. And if something like pressure or harassment ends up falling on Marie-san or the Ritch Barony because of that overly expensive item, we’ll handle it on our end, so it’s fine.]","[In that case...... yeah, true enough. Then sorry, but if it does look like it’ll turn into some sort of noble-related mess, lend them a hand.]","[Yes, yes, understood. Anyway, this Subject K is one of the easier ones to handle, so Alice-chan’s just gonna take it easy.]","[......And the ones that are harder to handle?]","[Recently, it's that one regarding Kaito-san casually drawing in World Creators from other worlds one after another. I mean, we're talking about individuals whose specs are straight-up monster level......]","[I see......]","Well, indeed. When compared to World Creators among whom Omniscient and Omnipotent types are a dime a dozen, handling the squabbles and negotiations between nobles might be nothing more than child’s play for Alice.","<Afterword>","? ? ? : [In the first place, if anything related to Kaito-san could be handled with predictions or countermeasures, Lilia-san and Eris-san wouldn’t have gone through all that. Whenever you try to prepare something, he drags in something weird from completely out of left field and still lands a body blow, so honestly it’s easier for Alice-chan when he moves within a predictable range. She even has the leeway to enjoy herself.]","Serious-senpai : [No, stop enjoying yourself there...... Still, if I were to summarize this whole matter......]","~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~","Stomachache Devil : [Alright, I’ve already beaten up Marie to some extent, and the meeting stuff isn’t scheduled yet, so let’s go beat up Cornelia.]","~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~","Serious-senpai : [......Merciless.]<az887e> Follow current novᴇls on NovᴇlFire(.)nᴇt</az887e>"]},{"number":2369,"title":"Chapter 2369: The Promised Tea Party 38","paragraphs":["I take a sip of the grape juice I got from Alice, and it has a refreshingly crisp flavor, really delicious.","[This grape juice is pretty good.]","[By the way, this grape juice was made from grapes grown by the Ritch Barony. Well, it’s not like they sell it as grape juice or anything, so I was the one who turned the grapes into juice.]","[Eh? Really? So, Marie-san's place grows not just ripples but grapes too......]","[Not to the extent that Raz-san’s place does, but they do grow several types of fruit. Ripples are the main one though...... The Ritch Barony’s territory has good soil and climate. It’s quite suitable for cultivating fruit.]","When I ate their ripple before, I thought the same thing, but the fruit from Marie-san’s orchards is really tasty. Of course, it’s not like it’s on the level of \"the best in the world\" or anything like that, but I can tell it’s high-quality, carefully grown, and made with great effort.","[Their ripples were really good too, no doubt about its quality, right?]","[Yes, if they take them out in a produce fair, they might even win an award. But the problem is distribution. The territory is surrounded by high mountains and monster habitats, so to get to the nearest large trading city, you have to make quite a detour......]","[Fumu, in that case, wouldn’t flying dragon flight be useful? Or is it that unlike in Symphonia Kingdom, Archlesia Empire doesn’t really have flying dragon flight?]","[No, Archlesia Empire has flying dragon flight as well. It’s just that Ritch Barony’s territory falls under a no-fly zone for flying dragon flights.]","As she answered my question lightly, Alice pulled out something like a whiteboard from nowhere and sketched a map freehand.<az44e1> Thɪs chapter is updated by N0v3l.Fiɾe.net</az44e1>","In the center, she wrote \"Ritch Barony\" and drew several red circles around it.","[Flying dragon flights, as the name suggests, uses Dragons. Mary-san’s place is a special case, since she has a contract with Magnawell and borrows his subordinates, but otherwise, they use Dragons that aren’t classified as Demons. Since they fly through the skies, the biggest concern is naturally flying monsters.]","[Ah, right. If they got attacked midair, with passengers and cargo, they couldn’t just fight recklessly......]","[Exactly. That said, Dragons are generally high-ranking monsters, so most other monsters run away rather than attack...... with the exception of Wyverns. Wyverns are among the strongest monsters in the Human Realm, and with their low intelligence and violent temperament, if flying dragon flight happens to fly near their habitat, they’ll attack. That makes them the number one threat flying dragon flight contractors have to watch out for.]","Hearing that, I remembered something Alice had said earlier about \"there being a lot of high mountains nearby\". Wyverns live in high mountains...... in other words, there are wyvern habitats close to the Ritch Barony.","[Looks like you’ve realized it, but yes, that’s correct. There are several mountains near Baron Ritch’s lands where Wyverns live. That said, they’re still quite far from towns, so it’s not like towns or villages are ever attacked, but flying dragon flight companies designate a no-fly zone within a certain radius of Wyvern habitats, so flying dragon flights can’t reach the Ritch Barony’s territory.]","[I see. And on top of that, without a teleportation gate, it must be tough to ship out fruit and such......]","[Right. I’m sure you’ve seen teleportation gates a few times yourself, Kaito-san, but they’re massive facilities, and of course, building one costs an outrageous amount of money. So, if there isn’t much profit to be made, no trading company is going to pay that kind of money to build one.]","It’s a bit like train stations, I suppose. Since those who build them aren’t doing charity work, if they can’t expect profits from passengers and usage, no teleportation gate gets built. As a result, the area remains inconvenient, no more people settle there, and it becomes a kind of vicious cycle huh......","[I see, sounds like Marie-san's got it rough.]","[Yes, well...... that problem will be resolved soon enough. And besides, what’s rough for Marie-san probably isn’t that particular issue......]","[Unn?]","[Oh, nothing. Just thinking how tasty this grape juice is.]","Alice tilted her wineglass with a cheerful smile. I cocked my head at her words, but since I couldn’t quite put my vague doubts into words, I decided not to press further and just kept on with lighthearted small talk.","<Afterword>","Wyvern-senpai : [It’s been a while since I got some screentime, yahoo!]","Serious-senpai : [No, that's not screentime, you were just mentioned in conversation...... and every time you come up, you’re treated as either meat or a nuisance......]","Wyvern-senpai : [I leave the spotlight to Big Sis, so I’m fine with appearing in the shadows too. Besides, there was talk about ordering a special brush for Dragons, and if that leads to Big Sis getting more screentime, that’d be great.]","Serious-senpai : [......Ah...... T- That’s true, isn’t it...... Kaito's got an absurd number of Dragon acquaintances...... If they manage to make a special brush for Dragons, and Kaito takes a liking to it...... then it looks like Cornelia’s stomach really will be destroyed.]"]},{"number":2370,"title":"Chapter 2370: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 1","paragraphs":["Cornelia-san is going to take me to a shop that handles brushes exclusively for monsters, and as I had planned, I intend to ask if they can also make one for Dragons.","[So that’s the plan, Lynn, could you give me a few of your scales?]<az48ce> Follow current novels on nοvelfire.net</az48ce>","[Kyuu!]","After nodding at my words, Lynn turned her head as if to check her own body, then peeled off a few scales that were about to shed and placed them in my hand.","I put them into the small vial I had prepared, and the preparations were complete.","[Good, good. With this, I think they’ll also be able to make a brush for you, Lynn. I’m looking forward to it.]","[Kyui!]","The basic process shouldn’t be much different from making Bell’s brush, so I don’t think it’ll be a problem. Well, in the worst case that the trading company doesn’t handle it, I could always ask Alice for help.","As I was thinking that, I suddenly heard a small cry.","[Kuu......]","[Unn? Sela? What’s the matter?]","When I turned, Sela, who was normally quiet and rarely cried out, was looking up at me. When I asked what was the matter, she pulled a scale from her own body and moved as if to offer it to me.","[......Ah, I see...... You’re right. You’d want a brush exclusively for you too, huh, Sela.]","[................]","It really would be unfair if only Lynn had an exclusive brush and Sela didn’t. Especially since Sela looks up to Lynn like an older sister, of course she’d want to be included.","Smiling at her adorable insistence, I accepted a few of Sela’s scales as well and placed them into another vial, just as I had done with Lynn’s. It’s not like having them would be a problem anyway. I’ll buy a brush for Sela too, and give it as a present to Sieg-san.","While Kaito was leisurely spending time with his pets and waiting for the promised hour...... in a room of the Sharon County in Archlesia Empire, Cornelia was staring seriously into a mirror.","(This time, it’s not a party or a tea gathering, but I still need to pay proper attention to my appearance...... Flaunting extravagance or luxury would be a poor choice, so I should go with a calm design that doesn’t stand out too much among the common people, yet if seen by those with discerning eyes, still holds enough value to befit a noble’s daughter...... That would be best.)","As the young lady of the Sharon family, which also has a merchant background, Cornelia had experienced many social settings from a young age. In particular, she kept track of all the latest fashion trends in the Hydra Kingdom and could say with confidence that she had a fair amount of knowledge in clothing.","But since the one she would be meeting was Kaito...... she felt she needed to be even more careful than usual with her attire.","(The most ideal choice would be to match the atmosphere of Kaito-sama’s clothing...... but if our styles are too similar, mine will inevitably pale in comparison...... At the tea party, Kaito-sama wore something that, while seemingly simple at first glance, was in truth a work of art. His jacket was most likely made from the threads of a Crown Spider from the Demon Realm. Not only is acquiring enough of that rare and dangerous material to make clothing impressive, but the craftsmanship required to create that garment must have been nothing short of extraordinary. Considering Kaito-sama’s wealth is in another league entirely, just how much did that outfit cost......?)","Cornelia, knowledgeable in clothing, recognized that Kaito’s outfit had been made from first-rate materials using top-class skill, and she marveled at the vast difference in his wealth.","She wasn’t exactly wrong. In truth, Kaito usually bought all his clothing from Alice, and the full set he had worn to the tea party had cost him only 500R.","For a commoner, it would be considered somewhat expensive, but in terms of actual monetary value, Cornelia’s own outfit had been much more costly.","Still, regardless of price, Alice, utterly smitten with Kaito, would never compromise when it came to making clothes for him, personally gathering only the finest materials and ensuring everything was of the highest quality.","(Without a doubt, Kaito-sama must be someone with very strong preferences regarding clothing...... If I wear something careless, I’ll only be laughed at. I’ve already narrowed down my options, but I need to reconsider them carefully and choose again.)","This, however, was a great misunderstanding. Kaito was actually quite indifferent towards clothing, usually just giving Alice a rough idea of what he wanted and leaving the rest entirely up to her.","But thanks to Alice’s excellent sense for fashion and her ability to incorporate the latest trends flawlessly, to someone like Cornelia, Kaito appeared incredibly stylish.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......The subtitle changed. Which means there’s plenty of time (chapter limit) to spare...... Cornelia’s stomach is done for.]"]},{"number":2371,"title":"Chapter 2371: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 2","paragraphs":["This time, Cornelia was guiding Kaito not to the Sharon Trading Company of Sharon County, but to the Victor Trading Company. That said, since they wielded considerable authority, including financial backing, it could practically be considered a subsidiary of the Sharon Trading Company.","However, while the headquarters of the Sharon County and the Sharon Trading Company were in the capital of the Archlesia Empire, Victor Trading Company was located in a different city, one Kaito had never visited.","Therefore, the plan was to first meet in the capital and then, using a teleportation magic tool, proceed to the Victor Trading Company.","Cornelia had arrived an hour early at one of the capital’s teleportation gates where she was to meet Kaito and waited quietly inside a carriage parked in a space reserved for nobles.<azdebf> The source of this content ɪs novel※fire.net</azdebf>","Since Cornelia, as a countess’s daughter, would attract attention if she waited for Kaito in a crowded teleportation gate, a servant was stationed there to escort him to the carriage upon his arrival.","After receiving notice of Kaito’s arrival, Cornelia would step out of the carriage to greet him and then travel via Teleportation Magic. Until then, she quietly organized her thoughts.","(I’ve already sent thorough notice to the Victor Trading Company and prepared everything else as well. Since Kaito-sama is coming alone this time, aside from the Phantasmal King, who I hear is always at Kaito-sama’s side, there shouldn’t be any situation like the previous tea party.)","There was no scenario this time in which Kaito would suddenly bring along an extraordinary companion, and preparations, including those for the following schedule, had been fully made.","Unlike Marie and the Ritch Barony, Sharon County was a noble household with considerable wealth and multiple teleportation magic tools, so travel posed no problem.","(......However, regarding rumors, they are unavoidable. Since we are meeting in the capital, there will be those who speculate or twist the nature of my relationship with Kaito-sama. Well, those who merely whisper behind our backs are no problem. But recently, as is the case with Eris-sama’s situation, there will likely be rumors that Kaito-sama is close to a noble lady of the Archlesia Empire. Anyone who speaks ill of Kaito or tries to set a honey trap will disappear without us having to intervene...... The real concern is how to handle other noble ladies at future social gatherings who might ask how to get close to Kaito-sama.)","In any case, in noble society, the status of being friends with Kaito carries tremendous influence. Especially now, with Lady Eris and the Hamilton Marquisdom gaining enormous profits recently...... there will likely be those hoping to become second or third beneficiaries.","Of course, anyone trying to directly promote themselves to Kaito would be taking too high a risk, so no one would attempt that, but questions directed at those currently recognized as close to Kaito...... could certainly occur.","(This is something that will likely need to be handled in coordination with Lady Eris. Everything should be fully prepared...... I hope this \"flap of the great dragon’s wings\" passes without incident.)","Preparations and expectations were indeed thorough, but what still weighed on her mind was the story Eris had previously told about Kaito’s influence...... Called \"the flap of the great dragon’s wings\", it referred to how Kaito could unintentionally exert enormous influence over those around him.","At this point, Cornelia simply lacked enough information. After all, she had only just met Kaito. Her experience was nothing compared to Eris, who had endured countless stomachaches; she either trusted that her preparations were sufficient...... or felt some unnameable anxiety and used the sense of readiness to bolster herself.","However, when it came to dealing with Kaito, \"being fully prepared\"...... could almost be considered a prelude to an \"unexpected event\", yet Cornelia lacked the experience to think in such terms.","Nidzveld was walking through the fortress that she, one of the Four Great Demon Dragons of the Southern Demon Realm, called home, when one of her subordinates happened to pass by and spoke up.","[Arehh? Big Sis, you heading out?]","[Unn? Ah, yeah. I have plans with Eingana. We’re going to listen to a performance by an orchestra that Eingana recommended. Apparently...... they’re currently performing in a commercial city of the Archlesia Empire, so I intend to go there and watch.]","[Hehh, an orchestra...... I don’t really get it, since I get restless if I sit still listening to music and can’t make it through, but I hope it’s a good performance. Oh, by the way, if you’re going anyway, why not invite Big Bro too?]","[My comrade? That is tempting, true, but suddenly inviting him might trouble him. I’ll save that for another occasion.]","[I see. Ah, sorry for holding you up. Have a good day, Big Sis.]","[Yeah.]","With a faint smile in response to her subordinate’s words, Nidzveld set off toward the Human Realm...... Yes, \"the very city Kaito and Cornelia were planning to go to\"......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Exactly. You mustn’t let your guard down just because it's not around at first. That guy’s the type who’ll casually pull something off like \"happening to run into you in the middle of the city\"......]"]},{"number":2372,"title":"Chapter 2372: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 3","paragraphs":["Cornelia waited in the carriage for a while, and about 10 minutes before the scheduled meeting time, one of the two servants she had stationed at the teleportation gate returned and informed her that Kaito had arrived.","Hearing this, Cornelia stepped out of the carriage and gracefully bowed to Kaito, who was being guided by the other servant.","[Kaito-sama, welcome. Thank you for back at the tea party the other day.]","[Hello, Cornelia-san. No, thank you, not just for the tea party, but also for taking the trouble to guide me today.]","[Please, don’t mention it. Even if indirectly, it is delightful that a business associated with our family has caught Kaito-sama's attention.]","As she exchanged light greetings and looked at Kaito, Cornelia felt a surge of astonishment internally.","(W- What amazing clothing...... Such an extremely simple design, yet it seems to have been crafted by an artisan of incredible skill...... Even I, who have some confidence in judging garments, cannot tell what materials were used. I’m certain the fabric is extraordinary, but I have no idea what it could be...... As expected of Kaito-sama. I thought I wore decent clothes myself, but this is on an entirely different level.)","For reference, the outfit Kaito was currently wearing was a full set given to him by Alice on his birthday. Since it was also Kaito’s birthday, Alice had put considerable effort into making it.","The clothes were made with theoretically top-quality materials created by Makina, materials that would otherwise be impossible, and though at first glance, it looked like an ordinary outfit, anyone with a keen eye, like Cornelia, would be completely overwhelmed by it.","[Cornelia-san, your outfit has great taste. It’s calm and elegant, yet the design feels refined. It really suits you.]","[Thank you. This outfit was made using the traditional methods of the Empire while incorporating trends from the Hydra Kingdom. But even more than my outfit, Kaito-sama’s clothes are truly extraordinary. Simple, yet every detail reflects careful thought.]","[I received it as a gift, but I like it myself.]","As she lightly thanked him for the compliment and praised his outfit in return, Cornelia noted that such exchanges were common in high society. It was customary, when praised, to compliment the other person’s attire, so this interaction was familiar to her...... but Kaito’s words struck her with renewed astonishment.","(......A gift? Judging by appearances, this must have cost multiple white gold coins...... Depending on the materials, it could easily be tens of coins...... As expected, Kaito-sama is astonishing. I must redouble my focus......)","Reaffirming Kaito’s remarkable nature, Cornelia braced herself even more. At that moment, Kaito, as if remembering something, appeared holding a magic box.","[Oh, right. Since you’re guiding me today, I brought a little gift as thanks.]","[A gift? Oh, I’m sorry if it caused you any trouble.]","[Errr, I heard Cornelia-san has pets, so this is a shampoo I habitually use for my monsters. I was thinking you might have some large-sized monsters, so I brought a bit extra...... Is it okay to give it to you here?]","[Yes, I also have a magic box, so that’s fine.]","[Then, I’ll take it out now.]","Hearing Cornelia’s words, Kaito took out a large wooden box, and Cornelia touched it, placing it into her magic box.","Although she maintained a composed expression as she accepted it, Cornelia’s mind was far from calm.","(The shampoo Kaito-sama habitually uses for pets? C- Could it be the one he mentioned at the tea party, with a small amount of Fruits of the World Tree added? I thought it would be rude not to accept it, but the value of this thing is just too incredible...... n- no, calm down. It’s not necessarily the one made with Fruits of the World Tree. Kaito-sama is very particular about pets, so it’s not strange for him to use several different kinds of shampoo.)","The value of a shampoo containing Fruits of the World Tree was, without question, extraordinary. Considering that it was made directly by Alice, it could even be said that Kaito was the only person in the world to possess it.","[......U- Umm, Kaito-sama. This shampoo, could it be the one you mentioned at the tea party before?]","[No, that would have been fine too, but I heard that one with a small amount of Fruits of the World Tree can be unsuitable for some monsters, so this is a different one. I usually use about three types of shampoo, and this is one of them. Since compatibility with materials may vary depending on the monster, I also prepared a note with the ingredients, please use it on the ones it’s safe for.]","[Thank you for your thoughtfulness. Indeed, the Fruit of the World Tree contains strong healing properties and Nature Magic, so there would certainly be monsters that are sensitive to it...... Hyiih!]","[Cornelia-san?]","[A- Ahh, no, it’s nothing.]","Cornelia gave a quick glance at the note she received from Kaito and let out a small squeak. For on it were listed a huge number of rare materials, even she would have difficulty acquiring some of them.","(Magic Flowers' extract, Sky Flowers' extract, the oil of a Peerage-ranking High Treant, honey of Vask Hornets...... and all the other ingredients are extremely rare...... Awawawa, this isn’t a gift one gives as a simple thank-you, it’s definitely not something you give just for an introduction, Kaito-sama!)","Of course, Cornelia’s inner cry did not reach Kaito.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Can he really secure enough of such rare materials to use that shampoo regularly......?]","? ? ? : [No, Kaito-san does have Gods in Trinia who can produce unlimited amounts of any material that exists...... and well, all the shampoos Kaito-san buys, I...... no, Alice-chan prepares them.]","Serious-senpai : [......How does she do that?]","? ? ? : [Well, once she makes one, she can just copy the rest with Factory Gear...... It’s not useful in combat, but Makina’s Heart Tool is surprisingly convenient......]"]},{"number":2373,"title":"Chapter 2373: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 4","paragraphs":["After handing the shampoo to Cornelia-san, we decided to head once again to the town where the trading company we were aiming for was located. Since I had never been to that town before, we would be traveling using Cornelia-san’s teleportation magic tool.","This time, however, I was leaving the guiding to Cornelia-san, so the plan was to meet near the teleportation gate and head to the destination from there. Still, even for a city I’d never visited, it was easy to go there now if I wanted.","That’s because the teleportation gate in my room had been updated multiple times by Shiro-san, and was now at version 3.0...... Even without knowing the world coordinates, it had a tablet-like touch interface that lets me search for a location on the map and specify it. Thanks to that, I could reach almost anywhere.","[Well then, let’s head to the trade city right away. You may choose between directly teleporting to the front of the Victor Trading Company, or teleporting a little distance away and taking a carriage into town while enjoying the scenery. Which would you prefer?]","[Ah, in that case... since it’s my first time visiting this area, I’d like to see what the place looks like, so let’s take the carriage.]","I didn’t know how long the application for brush-making would take, but it probably wouldn’t be hours and hours. It might be nice to do a bit of sightseeing afterward before going home.","[I’ve arranged for a carriage and a maid who will serve as both guard and driver to wait at the teleportation point. Now then, I’ll be touching your body for a moment.]","[Yes.]","......Hearing about a maid serving as both guard and driver no longer struck me as strange. Well, in this world, if she’s a maid, being able to drive a carriage is only natural. That was the only thought that came to mind, which made me realize how much I’d already been influenced by this world’s common sense.","When we traveled using the teleportation magic tool, a large carriage stood before us, and a maid was waiting there, bowing as she saw us..... but she was a familiar face.","[......Arehh? Is that you, Anne-san?]","[My, I’m honored that you remembered my name.]","[Oh? Kaito-sama, you know her?]","[Ah, no, it’s not like we’ve spoken directly before, but when I went to watch the Maid Olympia, she fought against a maid I knew. That left an impression.]","Yes, the maid waiting for us turned out to be none other than Anne-san, Lunamaria-san’s first opponent in the Maid Olympia. A completely unexpected reunion.","[I see. I also once attended the Maid Olympia as a spectator. The one two tournaments ago...]","[Oh, but despite its scale, there were hardly any ordinary visitors, right?]","[Ah, w- well...... the Maid Olympia is something of a sanctuary for maids, so it’s rare for non-maids to watch. Admission to the spectator seats is also prioritized for those with maid qualifications...... and, well, it has a rather unique atmosphere. When I attended, the contents and themes were all wonderfully arranged, but...... being surrounded almost entirely by maids made it hard to fit in. So I didn’t watch the last one.]","[......I get what you mean. No matter where you look, it's nothing but maids. It really feels like you’ve wandered into some strange otherworld.]","Before I realized it, Cornelia-san and I exchanged eye contact and shook hands. It was like our bond had deepened, we’d found something only those who had endured the same hardship could truly understand.","No, really, the matches themselves were fun to watch, but that overwhelming sight of maids filling the entire venue was so bizarre, the sense of being an outsider was unbearable.","[......Still, I’m a bit surprised. From the Maid Olympia introduction, I thought you were Alexandra-san’s disciple, so I assumed you worked at the imperial castle.]","[Yes, just as you had guessed, until three years ago, I did serve as a maid in the castle. But after marrying, I was now employed by the Sharon County.]","[Her husband serves as my father’s, Count Sharon’s, assistant, so she came to us through that connection. She now serves as our head maid.]","Well, considering she competed in the main tournament of the Maid Olympia, and if I recall correctly she was introduced as having placed sixth in the previous tournament, she must be a highly capable maid. RäNȏbƐs","Although, in this world, being a “capable maid” could mean being well-versed in a very peculiar worldview, so one has to be careful about referring someone like that...... but honestly, the only one I know who’s extremely skilled yet never once brings up the Maid World or Maid Power is Illness-san.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [A totally unexpected reappearance, but...... with it being almost certain they’ll run into Nidzveld afterward, it just looks like another Stomachache Warrior has been added...... strange, isn’t it......]"]},{"number":2374,"title":"Chapter 2374: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 5","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","Today is the release date of the manga adaptation’s Volume 10! Please check the official URL and other details in the Activity Report.","I get into the carriage with Anne-san as the coachman and start moving. Maybe because this city is a trade city where all sorts of businesses are thriving, the roads feel quite wide. It might be because they transport big cargo, but either way, the view is wide and the scenery from the carriage is nice.","[There are quite a lot of shops huh.]","[Yes. It’s not as bustling as a major trading city that serves as a logistics hub, but several merchant associations have their headquarters in this city, and festivals and events are also held frequently.]","[Hehh, so if a lot of trading companies have their headquarters here, that means there are advantages to putting them here, right?]","[There are several factors. The biggest factor is that before my father’s time, the head of the Sharon County wanted to build this city up through commerce and reduced or exempted many trade-related taxes. That attracted many trading companies and led to this city’s development.]","[I see, I’ve heard the Sharon County also owns a big trading company, so your family must have been strong in business for generations.]","[There was also luck in being the very first to start doing that. Nowadays, similar tax reductions are done in various regions, so it’s not like the tax rate here is uniquely low anymore.]","Indeed, I think things like that are like a head start, being the first to do it gives an advantage. If you succeed in gathering trading companies first, this trade city becomes convenient for trade with other trading companies, giving value beyond just the tax rate and leading to prosperity.","But still, being the very first to try something like that and succeed is amazing, and that’s probably why the Sharon County became such a wealthy noble house in Archlesia Empire.","[......Unn? What’s that big building?]","[That is a concert hall. It’s a relatively new building, constructed a few years ago because the current city representative is focusing on music-related things. The city has always been strong in commerce but was somewhat lacking in tourism, so they probably wanted something that would create buzz in that area. It’s one of the largest concert halls in the country, built with a considerable budget.]","[Hehh, so bands play there?]","[Yes...... please wait a moment.]","Cornelia-san gives me a quick word of excuse, opens the small window inside the carriage...... the one that allows speaking with Anne-san on the driver’s seat, checks something with her, and then turns back to me.","[......Thank you for waiting. It seems that today, a group called the Allegra Symphony is scheduled to perform. They are a new band and not very well-known yet, but they are very skilled and rumored to become a popular band later.]","[I see, I’m kind of interested. Well, there are concert halls in Symphonia Kingdom too, but they’re almost all in the Northern District, so I haven’t gone much. I’ve been to see plays a few times, but I haven’t gone to listen to a band much.]<azff0e> The source of this content ɪs noᴠelfire.net</azff0e>","[I see. Then, since this is a good opportunity, I think it would be nice to go and watch. They are a skilled band, but not so popular yet that the hall sells out, so I think you could still buy tickets on the day.]","Honestly, I am a bit interested in a band performance. I imagine it would be something like an orchestra, and listening to it in a concert hall sounds amazing, so I do want to hear it.","But since I don’t have much experience with places like that, I feel a bit hesitant.","[That sounds nice. But since I have almost no experience watching that kind of performance, I feel a little uneasy about going alone...... if it’s convenient for Cornelia-san, would you like to go together after the introductions?]","[......O- Of course, if it’s an invitation from Kaito-sama, I’d be delighted...... I also have no plans after guiding you, so there’s no problem but...... um, will that be okay? I mean...... just the two of us......]","[Yes. If Cornelia-san's fine with it, then I’d very much like to go together with you.]","Cornelia-san clearly seems knowledgeable about things like concert performances, so having her come along with me feels reassuring. If I were to go alone, I’d probably just end up getting more nervous about it being my first time in a place like that, but with Cornelia-san there, I feel like I could relax and enjoy it.","[......There’s no...... hidden meaning to this, right? Considering what Eris-sama said...... this isn’t that kind of invitation......]","[......Cornelia-san?]","[Ah, no, I’m sorry. I was just lost in some personal thoughts...... We’ll be arriving at Victor Company soon.]","Cornelia-san had been muttering something in a small voice, but when I called out to her, she responded a bit flustered. Her reaction felt a bit strange, but since we were almost at our destination, I didn’t press her about it and instead turned my gaze back to the window.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Indeed, from Cornelia’s point of view it might have felt like \"Arehh? Wait, am I being hit on right now?\" but no, that’s not it...... That devil just came to make sure the future where your stomach gets punched by one of the Four Great Demon Dragons is set in stone......]"]},{"number":2375,"title":"Chapter 2375: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 6","paragraphs":["The Victor Company headquarters that Cornelia and Kaito arrived at wasn’t exactly grand or imposing, but rather like a local government office, organized with all necessary functions in place, spotless down to every corner, and a beautiful building designed with practicality in mind.","There were corners decorated with paintings of various monsters, as well as spaces selling what seemed to be monster-related goods, making it obvious at a glance that this was the headquarters of a company dealing with monsters.","Naturally, since it was known that Kaito and Cornelia would be visiting today, the company president himself came out to welcome them and personally guided the two to the reception room.","[Once again, welcome to our Victor Company...... Since today’s discussion concerns special brushes for monsters, please note that our resident monster scholar will also be present.]","[Thank you...... I take it this would be the monster scholar?]","[Yes, the creation of specialized brushes involves professional work such as magic power appraisal.]","[I see.]","The president’s expression as he answered Kaito’s question clearly showed tension. Well, that was only natural. After all, for Victor Company, this guest was none other than the eldest daughter of the Sharon County, which oversaw the Sharon Company, a business far above Victor in standing. When the one being guided was such a person, and they had received repeated orders beforehand to “absolutely avoid any discourtesy”, of course he would be nervous.","Though the president of Victor Company was not a noble, the goods related to keeping monsters as pets, something only wealthy nobles could generally afford, meant he had frequent dealings with nobles, and he had already heard rumors of Kaito. Most of those stories sounded dubious and hard to believe, but the fact that Cornelia was clearly treating Kaito as a superior, even going so far as to issue strict orders in advance to show no disrespect, meant that he must be of higher standing than Cornelia herself, the eldest daughter of the Sharon County.","[This time, I understand the consultation is about a brush for Miyama Kaito-sama’s pets, is that correct?]","[Yes...... ah, by the way, can you also make brushes for dragon scales?]","[Of course. While only certain dragon species can be kept as pets, they are extremely popular among nobles, so we can also craft special brushes for scales and horns.]","[I see, that’s reassuring. Well then...... I’d like brushes made for a Special Individual-variant Behemoth, for a White Dragon, and for a Special Individual-variant Rainbow Dragon. Here are the hairs and scales I brought.]","[ [ [ ! ? ] ] ]","At Kaito’s words, the president, the monster scholar, and even Cornelia all showed expressions of shock. For the president and the scholar, it was the sheer level of the monsters Kaito had named...... For Cornelia, it was that last pet he mentioned...... Rainbow Dragon.","(......A Special Individual-variant Rainbow Dragon? Kaito-sama’s pets should just be the Special Individual-variant Behemoth and the White Dragon...... Wasn’t the Special Individual-variant Rainbow Dragon Sieglinde-sama’s pet? No, wait...... Kaito-sama and Sieglinde-sama are lovers, so it’s possible he’s making the request on her behalf......)","For a moment, Cornelia was taken aback by the unexpected words, but she quickly recalled Sieglinde’s identity and organized her thoughts. In front of her, Kaito placed the bottles containing hair and scales on the table.","[T- Then, if I may, I’ll begin the inspection...... P- Please excuse me.]","Looking nervous, the monster scholar put on a special magic tool, one in the shape of a pair of glasses, and first picked up Bellfreed’s hair.","[......This is an incredible amount of magic power. If this much is contained in just the hair, then the body itself must hold several times more than an adult Behemoth...... So this is how different a Special Individual huh. Ahh, my apologies...... yes, there’s more than enough magic power contained within. I believe there will be no problem in creating an exclusive brush.]","Though astonished by Bellfreed’s hair brimming with such overwhelming magic power, he then picked up the bottle containing Lindwurm’s scales and peered inside...... tilting his head in puzzlement.","[......White Dragon? These are White Dragon scales? Strange. They don’t match the traits of either a normal White Dragon or a Special Individual-variant....... They feel like scales I’ve never seen before.]","[Ah, errr, I think Lynn...... my White Dragon has undergone a special evolution due to her diet.]","[I see, that does happen. There are indeed cases in which long-term consumption of food infused with magic power causes mutation. However, those examples mostly involve weaker monsters that are easily influenced by the small amount of magic power in such food...... To induce a variant evolution in a monster on the level of a White Dragon, the food in question would need to be infused with truly extraordinary magic power. May I ask, just for reference, what kind of food it was?] ꞦáꞐỘ₿È§","[Errr, I’ve been feeding her one Fruit of the World Tree a day.]","[................]","Hearing Kaito’s words, the monster scholar froze with the expression of someone who had just heard something incomprehensible. The company president already looked as though he might faint with foam at his lips.","Of course, their reactions were understandable. The Fruit of the World Tree was an incomparably rare treasure, so much so that many wealthy individuals spent years, even decades, striving to obtain a single one. Beyond its staggering value, it wasn’t even something one could acquire with money; obtaining one was an almost impossible feat.","So to be told they were being fed to a pet, one per day, left them utterly dumbfounded. The monster scholar glanced nervously at Cornelia, who solemnly nodded.","Seeing that response, he understood that Kaito’s words were neither joke nor exaggeration. Trembling, yet forcing himself to speak, he managed:","[..................A- Ahhh...... I- I see....... If it’s a food infused with the magic power of a Fruit of the World Tree....... t- then such a mutation is certainly understandable.]","It felt as though all the common sense he had cultivated as a monster scholar had been shattered to pieces, but he reminded himself that his role was simply to determine whether there was enough magic power present to craft the brushes. As for everything else, he decided not to think too deeply about it.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Somehow, some nameless mob just got punched in the stomach out of nowhere......]","<White World Dragon Lindwurm>","A special dragon that has mutated and evolved to the point of being considered an entirely new type, after being fed Fruits of the World Tree every single day by her overly doting owner. Even while Kaito was away in his original world, he entrusted Siegfried with large amounts of Fruits of the World Tree to keep feeding her, allowing Lindwurm to absorb immense amounts of that magic power. She can use a Healing Breath, and her base magic power reserves are overwhelmingly vast.","On top of that, since recently she has also been eating Fruits of Nebula’s World Tree, she has gained the ability to use a buff-type Breath as well, making her something like a healer/buffer dragon.","In truth, her magic reserves have already reached the level where she can use Humanization Nagic. However, while Fafnir did advise that she should consume food rich in magic power, he never imagined she was being fed Fruits of the World Tree every single day. He expected her magic to increase over perhaps 10 years or so after the Six Kings Festival, before checking in on her again. As such, Lindwurm is still happily devouring fruits and continuing to grow. At this rate, her magic power reserves may soon reach the level where she could be officially recognized as a Demon."]},{"number":2376,"title":"Chapter 2376: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 7","paragraphs":["At the Victor Trading Company, I showed the president and the monster scholar some of Bell’s fur and Lynn and Sela’s scales, but I think I ended up surprising them quite a bit.","Well, it’s only natural they’d be surprised upon hearing about them eating Fruits of the World Tree. Still, lying in response to a specialist’s questions might cause trouble later for the brush-making process, so I simply answered everything honestly.","As for the Fruit of the World Tree, Sela eats it as well...... though in her case it’s mostly because she wants to imitate Lynn. Also, since Sela has quite a small appetite, she doesn’t eat a whole fruit each day, just a little bit at a time.<az0734> Follow current novᴇls on novel{f}ire.net</az0734>","Sela, or rather, Rainbow Dragons in general, can absorb magic power from the air through her wings and convert it into nourishment. So it has nothing to do with being a Special Individual; they’re just naturally light eaters. Even a fully grown Rainbow Dragon apparently eats no more than two or three nuts a day.","Sela is no exception, and eating a whole Fruit of the World Tree is basically impossible for her. Instead, she drinks something like a smoothie made by refining juice made from the Fruit of the World Tree.","She would prefer to eat a whole fruit like Lynn does, but whenever I give her one, she gets full after just a couple of bites, so in the end, smoothies really are the most suitable food for her.","[E- Each one is truly a marvelous monster. I am deeply impressed. There should be no problem with the crafting, so we’ll have you select the material, length, and shape of the brush. We’ve prepared a catalog here, so please take a look.]","[Oh, so I can choose things like the material and hardness of the brush?]","[Yes, we’re prepared to replicate your requests as faithfully as possible. That said, deciding on combinations can be tricky, so if you can give us even a vague idea of what you’d like, we can make suggestions.]","[I see...... in that case, I’ll take one of every possible combination.]","[Wha!?]","Of course, I could imagine what sort of brushes would suit Bell, Lynn, and Sela, but sometimes you only discover something unexpectedly good by actually trying them out. If possible, I really did want to try them all.","[A- All varieties...... you mean every possible combination......?]","[Yes. Ah, wait, could it be that there’s not enough fur or scales?]","[Oh, no, not at all. The fur and scales you’ve provided are simply for us to read each monster’s magic power wavelength. Once those wavelengths are recorded into our specialized magic tools, you may take the materials back with you, and there are no limits on the number of brushes we can craft. However...... our brushes are luxury products aimed at relatively affluent customers. The price of each is rather considerable, and if you request every possible combination, even for just one creature, the cost would exceed 10 white gold coins......]","[I see......]","[Yes, so if you could perhaps consider it in light of your budget......]","[Then for Bell...... For my Behemoth, I’d like brushes for both her fur and her horns. For my White Dragon, brushes for her scales, horns, and also fur since she has some around the tail. And for the Rainbow Dragon, brushes for both scales and horns...... with every variety and every combination, one of each, please.]","[......V- Very well. As you wish.]","The president of the company nodded, still stunned by my request. Well, considering that one full set per creature was estimated at around 10 white gold coins, the order I just placed came to 70 white gold coins in total...... that’s about 700 million yen. It’s no wonder he was shocked, but when it comes to Bell and Lynn, I have no intention of holding back on spending, so it’s not a problem at all.","If anything, I need to spend more aggressively, because money is piling up faster than I can possibly use it. Anima is brilliant, raking in fortunes through countless successful investments and ventures, and lately Nifty’s sales have been staggering as well. Even though I entrust most of my wealth to Anima, my personal funds just keep growing.","Nifty in particular is insane. Despite being a luxury brand, under Canalis-san’s management it’s practically running at pure profit, which is absurd.","Even after paying wages to the staff she created, with Shiro-san’s permission, the margins are enormous.","And although I pay Canalis-san a salary befitting her role as Nifty’s representative and the manager of all three shops, she just hands almost all of it back to me, saying “Well then, please accept this as rent......”, so over 90 percent of her wages return to me anyway.","She insists “As long as I have a little money for snacks or the occasional bite while out, I’m fine.” If it were just modesty, I could persuade her to keep more, but the truth is...... she really doesn’t need money.","After all, Canalis-san can create whatever she needs at will. What use does an Omnipotent and Omniscient Canalis-san have for money?","Because of her strict sense of propriety, she does prefer to pay with earned money, not conjured money, when shopping at stalls or stores outside, but aside from that, she truly has no need for it. So, under the pretense of “rent”, most of her salary flows back to me...... Nifty’s profits are downright terrifying.","On top of that, I personally don’t have expensive hobbies.... I don’t collect pricey art or jewels. I prefer homestyle meals over extravagant gourmet dining...... Honestly, I probably spend the most on pet-related items. In that sense as well, this payment isn’t a problem in the slightest.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Hmm, but you know...... the thing is, it’s going to take some time before these brushes actually spread through Kaito, and they can’t even be made right away. Sure, it’s confirmed that we’ll meet Nidzveld and Eingana after this, but maybe Cornelia’s stomachaches will turn out to be relatively minor this time?]","? ? ? : [That’s true! If Serious-senpai says so, then maybe that’s how it’ll be (+1 flag). Aside from those two who are already confirmed, there’s no way we’d run into anyone else, right? (+1 flag) After all, this isn’t even the capital of the Archlesia Empire, just some trade city, so there’s no way we’d meet anyone of even higher status here, right? (+1 flag) And besides, Nidzveld-san and Eingana-san are relatively reasonable people, so it’s not like anything outrageous could happen, right? (+1 flag) Given that Cornelia-san’s supposed to be the type of character who gets one-hit-KO’d with stomachaches, just two of the Six Kings’ executives doesn’t really pack that much punch, so there shouldn’t be a problem, right? (+1 flag)]","Serious-senpai : [......Somehow, I feel like something’s going to happen.]"]},{"number":2377,"title":"Chapter 2377: Intermission: The (Stomach’s) Creeping Doom","paragraphs":["At the time when Kaito was at the Victor Trading Company hearing about their special brushes, two figures were walking side by side through the commercial city.","[Fumu, as I thought, everything here feels fresh and new, and all of it so fascinating. Ever since I obtained this clone body, I’ve taken quite a liking to sightseeing.]","[Well, with your size, up until now you couldn’t exactly stroll into a city so carelessly. Of course everything you see now would seem novel to you.]","[Indeed. In the past, it was impossible for me to even take on this size. I thought that was fine enough, but now that I have this clone body and can experience various things, I feel as though I wasted a great deal of time before...... Though, even if I had been interested in cities and entertainment earlier, without this clone body, it wouldn’t have been possible anyway.]","[No point worrying about the past. Now that you’ve got that clone body and can move around, just enjoy it. Nidzveld and Eingana went out of their way to invite you to a concert, no need to overthink things.]","[Yes, that’s true.]","On one side was a calm, silver-haired gentleman with a dignified air, and on the other, a small girl with curled horns radiating an overwhelming pressure and presence...... the clone body of Magnawell, and Megiddo in human form.","The reason the two of them were in the city was simple: Nidzveld and Eingana had invited Magnawell, who had recently obtained a clone body and was enjoying things he couldn’t before, to a concert. By coincidence, Megiddo had been drinking with Magnawell at the time and came along as well.","Since there was still time before their band’s performance, the group had split into pairs, Nidzveld and Eingana together, Magnawell and Megiddo together, to enjoy a leisurely stroll through the city.","[......Still, Megiddo, why do you take on the form of such a small girl?]","[Ahh, that’s because Kaito likes this look. Makes sense if you think of Kuromueina or Shalltear, this figure probably fits his tastes. So lately, when I take on a human form, it’s often this one, so that if Kaito feels like embracing me, it’ll be easy. Funny thing is, I never thought of myself that way, but maybe I really am the type to go out of my way for someone I’m in love with!]","[Is that truly what you’d call devotion? Well, I don’t understand much about romance...... but at least make sure you don’t get scolded again by Kuromueina or Shalltear.]","[Mm, feels a bit roundabout though...... I’m already head over heels for Kaito, and it’s not like he dislikes me. Wouldn’t it just be faster if we had a physical relationship......? But fine, taking our time can be fun too. Anyway, Magnawell, where are you headed? I’ve been to this city a few times, so if there’s somewhere you want to go, I can guide you.]","[Unn? Is that so? I thought you disliked the Archlesia Empire......]","As Magnawell saw it, Megiddo tended to dislike Archlesia Empire’s noble-oriented doctrines, so it was hard to imagine Megiddo visiting a town of the Archlesia Empire very often.","[Nah, it’s not like I hate everything about it. If anything, I quite like the current Emperor. She’s been doing reforms, trying to change the country, and that kind of drive is admirable. The one before her was trash...... If Kuromueina hadn’t told me not to, I would’ve killed him outright.]","[The previous Emperor? I don’t recall him much...... I only remember thinking he was a small-time figure.]","[The ones that annoy me most aren’t the ones who do spectacular crimes or line their pockets blatantly, but the types who do everything half-ass and sneak around earning petty side money. If one of them showed up in my sight outside the Festival of Heroes, I was thinking of leaving them half-dead. Anyway, I actually like this city. The past Count Sharon implemented some bold policies...... It isn’t unusual now, but back then it was revolutionary and impressive, his willingness to take risks was good. Well, Sharon County’s been stable lately, so they don’t gamble much anymore.]","[If their stability comes from not gambling, then that’s fine, isn’t it?]","[......Well, that’s true.]","Megiddo gave a wry smile and nodded at Magnawell’s words. Megiddo liked people who took on challenges, and respected those who succeeded because of them, so Sharon County seemed to leave a fairly good impression to her.","[So, where to now?]","[Fumu, I want coffee. I’ve been getting into it lately, the taste varies by shop, so it’s quite interesting.]","[Coffee huh. I know a few good places. I’ll show you around.]","[Ho ho, then I shall look forward to it.]","The two members of the Six Kings walked through the city laughing cheerfully...... no one at that time could have known that their presence would give Cornelia such an excruciating stomachache. ṙAŊo͍bƐš","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Ahh...... yeah, it’s over, Cornelia...... She's about to encounter two of the Six Kings and two Six King Executives all at once...... T- This is the overwhelming power of a one-hit-kill type huh......]"]},{"number":2378,"title":"Chapter 2378: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 8","paragraphs":["The application for a custom brush at the Victor Trading Company was completed without issue. Of course, ordering doesn’t mean the brush will be ready immediately, it will be shipped at a later date.","Yes, that’s the proper way of things usually are. Recently, though, with Canalis-san being so absurdly capable that she can prepare things instantly upon request, my sense of what’s normal has gotten a little dulled. But naturally, it takes time, so I’ll just enjoy waiting for it.","[How should I say this...... We finished faster than I imagined.]","[Yes. Normally, considering the material or combination for the brush would take time, but since you went with ordering all types, that step was skipped. In a way, it was inevitable......]","[I guess so. That part usually takes the longest, doesn’t it?]","That was exactly right, normally, the most time-consuming part is choosing the shape or material of the brush while working within a budget.","But I forcefully cut through that, ordering every possible combination, so it was only natural that the order was finished quickly.","[Well, anyway, just like we talked about on the way here, let’s go listen to the Allegra Symphony perform...... ah, but there’s the matter of the concert times, right?]","[Yes, I had Anne look into the performance times and available seats...... Let’s see, how is it?]","[Yes, Lady Cornelia. Here’s a summary of today’s schedule. The next available one is at this time. As for seats, the top-tier ones are already full, but the others still have openings, so I think tickets can be purchased without issue.]","O- Ohhh, impressive preparation. While I was handling the order at the Victor Trading Company with Cornelia-san, it seems she’d already instructed Anne-san to gather details about the concert times and seat availability, so the information we needed was provided right away.","As I was thinking that, Alice suddenly appeared before me.","[Kaito-san, want to buy tickets? I’ve got two adjacent top-tier seats here, and one seat just behind them that’s perfect for a bodyguard......]","[......Hmmm. Sure, better seats are always preferable, so I’ve no problem buying them...... but that look on your face, you’re scheming something, aren’t you?]","[My, whatever do you mean? Oh, and don’t worry about resale or anything shady like that. I own the rights to that concert hall, so I just secured them using that authority.]","Alice waved the three tickets in her hand with a playful grin, the kind she always wears when she’s up to mischief.","That said, the seats themselves are undeniably good, and the arrangement seems ideal too. But still, I can’t shake the feeling she’s scheming something......","[......Cornelia-san, what do you think? No doubt they’re good seats, but I’m pretty sure she’s scheming something.]","[Well...... given that we’re talking about Phantasmal King-sama, a person of such insight and strategy, it’s only natural that even a single action of hers would carry multiple intentions......]","[No, it’s not that sort of thing. This feels more like the kind of mischief she has when she finds something amusing...... though I can’t really figure out what exactly.]<az83cb> Fresh chapters posted on novelfire.net</az83cb>","[If they’re seats recommended by Phantasmal King-sama, then I don’t think there can be a mistake. And in terms of respecting her wishes as well, those seats seem best...... They are top-tier seats, after all, so they should be excellent for enjoying the performance.]","I knew Alice well enough to be certain she’s somehow finding something amusing...... but what, exactly, she found amusing in sitting in specific seats at a concert hall and listening to a band, I couldn’t begin to guess. She wouldn’t do anything I’d truly hate, but the whole thing still felt suspicious.","Cornelia-san, on the other hand, wasn’t familiar with Alice’s mischief, so she seemed to be viewing the situation as though the Phantasmal King had some lofty scheme in mind...... and looked inclined to agree to the purchase.","[...Well, alright then, Alice. I’ll buy those seats.]","[Yes yes, thank you for the purchase~~ Regular price is fine.]","Just as Cornelia-san had said, they really were good seats, so though still doubtful, I purchased the tickets. Once she finished taking my payment, Alice gave a soft smile, then clapped Cornelia-san lightly on the shoulder.","[......Honestly, I find you a bit pitiful, so I’ll tweak things on the information side and cover for you.]","[......P- Phantasmal King-sama......? W- Why are you looking at me with such pity......? Am I going to suffer some kind of tragic fate in those seats?]","[No, no. If it’s Kaito-san we’re talking about, things will probably happen regardless of the seats, or even before you get to them, really. So in that sense, the seats don’t really matter...... Anyway, good luck!]","[P- Phantasmal King-sama? Phantasmal King-sama!!!]","After giving a firm thumbs-up, Alice vanished. Cornelia-san, face gone pale, called out to her, but she never reappeared.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......So, seats close to the Megiddo and Magnawell?]","? ? ? : [More like right next to them. Well, honestly, ticket or not, they’ll probably end up running into them in front of the theater anyway...... so in the sense of sitting near acquaintances you “happen” to bump into, this is actually a good cover. If Gorilla-san or Kaito-san are around, they might even force their way into nearby seats too......]","Serious-senpai : [Yeah, true. Even if you don’t do anything, running into them is a given. And in the end, if the outcome just guarantees a bit of backup, then for Cornelia it’s actually a plus......]"]},{"number":2379,"title":"Chapter 2379: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 9","paragraphs":["Leaving the Victor Trading Company, Cornelia walked alongside Kaito towards the concert hall. If they were to arrive in a carriage, they would inevitably attract a fair amount of attention, something Kaito likely wouldn’t appreciate. Besides, walking allowed them to take in the sights of the city, making it something of a sightseeing stroll as well.","Fortunately, the concert hall wasn’t far from the Victor Trading Company’s headquarters, so even on foot it wouldn’t take much time. As for escorts, Anne was following at a slight distance, which was more than sufficient, and in any case, Alice was always at Kaito’s side, so strictly speaking, additional escorts weren’t even necessary.","[We still have plenty of time, but not enough to go sightseeing anywhere else.]","[Indeed. We don’t have the time to go shopping at stores far from the concert hall, but there are cafés and such nearby. Spending the time there until the performance begins might be a good idea.]","[That’s true. Then, once we get to the concert hall, let’s look for a café and take a break.]","As they chatted idly and lightly discussed their plans, Cornelia’s thoughts turned toward the unease rising within her.","(......Phantasmal King-sama’s behavior, the suspicion Kaito-sama sensed...... Does that mean something will happen with the seating at the concert hall? For example, it wouldn’t be impossible to run into other nobles. Allegra Symphony is gaining attention as a promising band among music lovers, and it wouldn’t be surprising if nobles came to hear their performance. If that happens, seeing the two of us visiting the concert hall together could very well look like we’re on a date.)","What came to mind immediately was the possibility of nobles who knew Cornelia being seated nearby, leading them to make unwarranted assumptions about her relationship with Kaito.","(Still, the impact wouldn’t be that great...... I don’t have a fiancé, so I wouldn’t be accused of infidelity. Unlike Lady Eris, though I am the eldest daughter, I’m not a legitimate child nor the heir. At most, rumors might spread that the Sharon County was trying to strengthen ties with Kaito-sama by offering me as a mistress, but that would only be idle speculation. Thanks to Lady Eris’s tea party, it’s already known that Kaito-sama has some level of interaction with the noble ladies of the Archlesia Empire, so handling it wouldn’t be too difficult.)","Even if other nobles were to think she was on a date with Kaito, the effect on Cornelia would be minimal. Such gossip was common in high society, and with just a little inquiry, anyone could learn that at this point Cornelia and Kaito had only known each other for a few days. So even if people made a fuss, there would be limits.","Moreover, since Cornelia was neither a legitimate child nor an heir, if the rumors were to grow louder, she could simply refrain from attending parties and evening gatherings for a while until the gossip died down, preventing it from becoming a serious problem.","(Another possibility is that someone acquainted with Kaito-sama might just happen to be there...... but is that really possible? This isn’t the capital, and it’s Kaito-sama’s first time visiting this trade city. Out of the multiple performances being held each day, at this particular time, and within the short distance from the Victor Trading Company to the concert hall seats, an accidental encounter seems almost impossible...... unless it’s the flap of a great dragon’s wings......)","Normally, such a thing would be too improbable to consider, but recalling the tale Eris had told about the flap of a great dragon’s wings, where one might, by chance, encounter someone beneficial in the city, Cornelia felt her unease swell all the more.","Before long, they arrived in front of the concert hall, and as they looked around for a café, Cornelia discreetly checked her surroundings.","(......It doesn’t seem like anyone particularly famous is here. Was I just overthinking it?)","At the very least, within visible range, there were no notable figures, nor was there any commotion suggesting someone had spotted one.","(If Recognition Inhibition Magic were being used, I wouldn’t be able to detect it...... but if I start considering even that possibility, I’d have to doubt everyone except people I personally know. Best not to dwell on it.)","Concluding for now that everything seemed fine, she shifted her attention back to her conversation with Kaito.","[Ahh, Cornelia-san. That place looks like a café.]","[It does. Then, shall we go there?]","Finding a café near the concert hall, Kaito and Cornelia entered and, guided by a staff member, took their seats.","[It’s not packed, but I guess since the performance is near, there are quite a lot of people here.]","[Indeed. It seems many people come early and spend time nearby until the performance begins. We’re doing the same, after all.]","[True...... hmm, what should I get......]","Exchanging light words as they glanced at the menu, Cornelia allowed herself to relax a little. At least until they moved to their seats in the concert hall, it seemed nothing would happen. Yet it was precisely in that moment of carelessness that the stomachache struck mercilessly.","[Guess we’ll wait here until it’s time for us to meet up......]","[Yes. I think moving to the meeting place 15 minutes beforehand should be fine.]","[Right. Still, this up-and-coming band sounds enjoy...... hm?]","[......Unn?]","Just then, as a pair who had just entered the café made their way inside chatting, they noticed something, and almost at the same time, Kaito and Cornelia turned toward the familiar voices.","[Oh! If it isn't my comrade!]","[Frea-san and Eingana-san? What a coincidence!]","Yes, the ones who had appeared in the café were Nidzveld and Eingana. Upon spotting Kaito, Nidzveld broke into a delighted smile.","Meanwhile, in stark contrast, Cornelia, sitting at the same table as Kaito, felt herself turning pale.<azbf29> The latest_epɪ_sodes are on_the novèlfire.net</azbf29>","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Letting your guard down in front of Kaito...... That's a guaranteed stomachache flag......]"]},{"number":2380,"title":"Chapter 2380: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 10","paragraphs":["At the café they had stopped by, when Nidzveld and Eingana appeared and began approaching Kaito, Cornelia gazed off into the distance, her mind racing.","(......I’ve already heard of the great dragon’s wings. I’ve heard them, yes, but...... no one ever said I’d actually encounter beings who could truly be called great dragons. T- There’s no mistaking it, these are Nidzveld-sama and Eingana-sama of the Four Great Demon Dragons...... w- what am I supposed to do here......?)","It was obvious that as nothing more than the eldest daughter of a County, Cornelia stood on a completely different level compared to Nidzveld and Eingana, who were Six Kings Executives. Naturally, since Cornelia’s position was lower, she could not carelessly greet or speak to them first.","After all, the Dragon King Magnawell had once, after a peace treaty, bestowed upon humanity the means to command flying dragons...... the origin of what is now called flying dragon flight, bringing a massive revolution to human commerce. Even today, he was revered by countless merchants as if he were the God of Trade, and for the Sharon County, who managed a large trading house, he was an exceedingly important figure.","To incur the displeasure of the Dragon King’s camp was tantamount to commercial suicide, and with two of that camp’s Executives present, it was inevitable that she would tense up.<az5f3e> Get full chapters from novelꞁire.net</az5f3e>","Yet tragically, she could not move on her own; here, she could only wait for Kaito and the others to act.","[What a coincidence, running into you here.]","[Umu. To think even my comrade came to this city, what a delightful chance encounter...... hm? My apologies, I did not realize there was company with you. If we’re intruding, sorry about that.]","[P- Please, don’t give it a thought.]","With a smile, Nidzveld approached and, noticing Cornelia hidden behind Kaito, offered a brief apology.","Since it was directed at her, Cornelia stiffened with nervous posture and returned a simple reply.","[......I don’t recall seeing you at the birthday party. Miyama Kaito-san, who is this lady?]","Seeing the exchange between Nidzveld and Cornelia, Eingana, curious about the woman he had never seen before, asked Kaito, and in that instant Cornelia’s tension reached its peak.","(......K- Kaito-sama...... I beg you. Please, please have mercy...... In this situation, there are several possible ways you might answer. But please, just introduce me simply as “a friend I’m out with”. If you say it like that, then at least...... please......)","Cornelia now stood at what could only be called a decisive moment. Yet it was one where she herself had no choice; everything rested on Kaito’s words.","If Kaito simply stated she was a friend, Cornelia could give Nidzveld and Eingana a small bow, then quietly remain in the sidelines so as not to interrupt their conversation.","But depending on Kaito’s response, the situation could change drastically. Though Cornelia desperately wished for a safe and uneventful outcome, as with all previous victims of stomachache incidents, her prayers would not be answered.","[Ahh, since meeting here must be some kind of fate, “let me introduce you”. This is my friend, she’s the daughter of a Count, Cornelia-san.]","And so Cornelia’s wish went unheard, as Kaito explicitly introduced her. This was, in truth, extremely significant. In effect, Kaito had indirectly guaranteed her standing and granted Cornelia permission to greet Nidzveld and Eingana.","What’s more, as if to gild the lily, he had deliberately added “daughter of a count”, which was practically an invitation for her to state her household name as well...... of course, Kaito hadn’t thought that deeply about it.","[I offer my greetings to the great Sky Dragon-sama and Sea Dragon-sama. I am Cornelia Sharon, eldest daughter of the Sharon County of the Archlesia Empire.]","[Fumu. Since you are a friend of my comrade, I cannot treat you discourteously. I am Freabell Nidzveld, one of the Four Great Demon Dragons, the Dragon King’s Executives. I would like you to call me by the name Nidzveld, bestowed upon me by Magnawell-sama. I look forward to your company, Cornelia-domo.]","[Then I as well...... I am Aquaria Eingana, also one of the Four Great Demon Dragons, the Dragon King’s Executives. As with Nidzveld, please call me Eingana. I hope today’s meeting will lead to a good exchange.]","[I- It would be an honor.]","Truthfully, Cornelia was trembling. Of course, she had heard some things from Eris beforehand...... but this? For two of the Six Kings’ Executives, upon first meeting, to return such courteous introductions, and even go so far as to imply future association, this was an astoundingly favorable reception.","(I- I had heard from Eris-sama, but...... i- is it really to this extent? Just being introduced as Kaito-sama’s friend...... and already...... w- what incredible influence......)","In reality, being a “friend of Kaito” puts one in an immensely trustworthy position. Partly it was because Kaito had a keen eye for judging people, but more than that, being his friend was almost a guarantee of character.","The reason was simple: anyone with a troublesome personality or who tried to exploit their connection to Kaito...... would have been swiftly dealt with by Alice or others. Therefore, the fact that someone could maintain a friendship with Kaito was itself proof they were at least decent and reasonably trustworthy.","Still, even while receiving such preferential treatment, welcomed warmly by two of the Four Great Demon Dragons...... Cornelia, sitting in a café with plenty of people around, was acutely aware of the pain in her stomach.","......Little did she know that ahead still awaited a fateful encounter with not just one, but two of the Six Kings themselves......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Ah, I see. If someone’s a villain or greedy bastard, Alice or a certain crazy God would take them out right away...... so just being Kaito’s friend by itself is proof they’re a good person......]"]},{"number":2381,"title":"Chapter 2381: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 11","paragraphs":["<Author’s Notes>","I will be on a business trip, so there won't be a chapter tomorrow.","It was a chance encounter, but since it was such a rare opportunity, Frea-san and Eingana-san ended up joining our table. Cornelia-san and I shifted our seats to sit side by side, while Frea-san and Eingana-san sat across from us.","Since the other party consisted of the Six Kings’ Executives, Cornelia-san seemed quite tense, so I resolved to properly support her in the conversation.","As I was thinking that, Frea-san looked at Cornelia-san with a somewhat nostalgic expression and murmured:","[......Even so, Cornelia Sharon huh....... That’s a nostalgic name.]","[Eh? Frea-san, you know Cornelia-san?]","[No, not her. Several hundred years ago, the head of the Sharon County bore the same name. This is just my guess, but Cornelia-dono’s name may have been taken from hers.]","[You are correct. My name was given in honor of the sixth head of House Sharon, Cornelia Sharon, who is regarded as the family’s restorer.]","[I thought as much. She was a magnificent woman, overflowing with ambition.]","Apparently, a past head of the Sharon household shared the same name as Cornelia-san. Certainly, it’s not unusual to name someone after a distinguished ancestor, and given that, the way she was named wasn’t strange at all.","Still, the fact that Frea-san clearly remembered the name meant she must have been quite the figure. As if sensing my doubt, Cornelia-san turned toward me and explained:","[To explain for Kaito-sama, the sixth head was a person with an exceptionally strong merchant’s spirit, and it would be fair to say she laid the foundation for what House Sharon is today. The special system in this trade city that I mentioned on the way here, that too was established by her.]","[I see, so she was an incredible person?]","[Yes. At the time, the Sharon household was a declining Viscounty, but she elevated it to a Count’s rank. Among all the heads of the family, she is arguably the most famous.]","The innovative policies I had heard about on the way here were apparently her doing as well. It seemed she was a remarkable person who had achieved enough merit to raise the house from viscount to count.","Perhaps she had even been the one to establish the Sharon Trading Company.","[A person overflowing with passion and ambition. Despite being the head of a noble household, she personally traveled throughout the Demon Realm, establishing all kinds of business deals. She was someone I personally found admirable. Even Megiddo-sama was fond of her, to the point of saying “Among the Archlesia Empire’s nobles, she is the one I like best.”]","[Megiddo-san really doesn’t like nobles all that much, huh? Though they seemed to be very fond of Lilia-san......]","[Yes, the sort of backroom scheming nobles do is one of the things Megiddo-sama hates most. They may not have liked her as much as he does Lilia-dono, but it is certain that they held her in high regard.]","Megiddo-san dislikes underhanded scheming done behind the scenes, and when it comes to nobles, she generally doesn’t think highly of them. But that doesn’t mean she hates all nobles.","She likes Lilia-san so much that she even said if she weren’t the head of a noble household, she would have wanted her as a subordinate. And when I mentioned Eris-san briefly before, she commented that “the Hamilton Marquisdom is one of the better ones among Archlesia Empire’s nobles”, which suggested she held a certain degree of respect for them as well.","Well, as long as the head is skilled in martial arts, or has the enthusiasm to take on new challenges, she seems to approve of them. Since both Frea-san and Megiddo-san liked that sixth head of the Sharon household, she must have been a passionate and ambitious woman.","[Then, if Megiddo-san were to meet Cornelia-san, they might notice, just like Frea-san did, that they share the same name.]","[Hyiih...... U- Umm, would that be alright? My personality is quite different from the sixth head’s......]","[If you are a friend of my comrade, you shouldn't be in any problem.]","[As long as you are a friend of Miyama Kaito-san, I don’t think there’s any need to worry.]","Cornelia-san looked uneasy, fearing that if Megiddo-san saw someone with the same name as a person she respected, she might think her existence was somehow tarnishing that name, but both Frea-san and Eingana-san immediately reassured her in unison that it was no issue.","[Errr...... is that so?]","[Umu. When it comes to someone like the aforementioned Cornelia Sharon or Lilia-dono, compared to them, Megiddo-sama’s fondness for my comrade is on a whole different level. So long as you are a friend of my comrade, there is absolutely no problem. After all, Megiddo-sama is always in high spirits when my comrade is around.]","[In fact, not long ago when I spoke with Megiddo-sama, they even showed interest in Lady Eris Dia Hamilton, whom Miyama Kaito-san holds in high regard. They said they would like to speak with her sometime.]","[......Truly, Kaito-sama’s influence is overwhelming.]","So, for Megiddo-san, if someone is my friend, then even if they’re a noble, there’s no issue at all...... meaning if there were ever an opportunity, it wouldn’t be a problem to introduce her to someone like Eris-san. Not that I have any actual plans to do that......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Did you catch that? Just like that, a stomachache flag got set up for Eris......]"]},{"number":2382,"title":"Chapter 2382: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 12","paragraphs":["Nidzveld and Eingana’s conversation with Kaito and Cornelia, perhaps inevitably, shifted to the Allegra Symphony, which was set to perform at the concert hall.","Since the café was practically next to the concert hall, it was easy to tell that both groups shared the same destination, and so the conversation naturally moved in that direction.","[So then, Frea-san and Eingana-san also came to listen to the Allegra Symphony perform?]","[Umu. Well, in my case, my knowledge of music is still quite shallow, so it was really Eingana who invited me along.]","[Thanks to Nidzveld taking an interest in music recently, I’ve been able to invite her to events like this, which makes me really happy. It may be different from the rock she prefers, but the Allegra Symphony is an excellent band with both talent and potential.]","Watching Kaito and the others exchange words calmly, Cornelia began to gather her thoughts with a clearer head.<sfivu> Thᴇ link to the origɪn of this information rᴇsts ɪn NoveIFire.net</sfivu>","(It’s truly fortunate that Kaito-sama is the one conversing with Nidzveld-sama and Eingana-sama. If it were Eris-sama, she could gather information on the Six Kings’ Executives and carry on such discussions with ease...... but I don’t have that kind of knowledge. I worry I might not be able to keep up with the topics. Still, this current discussion about music is a blessing.)","Cornelia did not possess as wide a breadth of knowledge as Eris, but in the fields of art and music...... subjects pertaining to the fine arts, she was quite well-versed.","And while her initial impression score was higher thanks to being Kaito’s friend, she herself wasn’t being directly addressed much in the conversation for now, which allowed her to secretly breathe a sigh of relief.","Of course, the one who often shattered such hopes of “let things stay peaceful like this......” was none other than Kaito.","[Still, I must say, for Miyama Kaito-san and your companion to come hear the Allegra Symphony, it’s quite remarkable. They are not yet what you’d call a famous band, but you have a keen eye.]","[Ahh no, in my case, this is my first time visiting this city, so Cornelia-san has been teaching me all sorts of things. About the Allegra Symphony too, she told me they’re a new orchestra that isn’t very popular yet, but has great potential to grow in the future. Cornelia-san seems pretty knowledgeable about music and bands in general, not just the popular ones, doesn’t she?]","[......Hohh, so in Miyama Kaito-san’s eyes, she is a woman of keen intellect?]","[I do think she’s intelligent, of course, but I especially get the impression that she’s deeply knowledgeable in music and related fields. Her explanations were really easy to understand too.]","[......I see.]","Hearing Kaito’s words, Eingana turned her gaze toward Cornelia, with a look that clearly showed interest.","(Kaito-sama? Kaito-sama!!! I truly think your sincerity, never boasting of others’ achievements as if they were your own, is wonderful, and that your keen insight in recognizing my area of expertise despite us not being all that close yet is amazing! It is, it really is!! But sometimes, lies...... or at least holding back a little, hiding things just a bit, can actually save someone! Mainly my poor stomach, or my mental well-being......)","Unlike before, when she was merely “Kaito’s friend”, Eingana now seemed interested in Cornelia as an individual. Feeling that gaze, Cornelia straightened her back while screaming inwardly.","[Cornelia-san, right?]","[Y- Yes!]","[Do you often spend time listening to music?]","[Yes, I personally enjoy this field very much, and as for the Allegra Symphony, I first learned of them at the Arts Festival during the Wind Month.]","[Ahh, the festival held in a western trade city. I’ve attended it several times myself. Speaking of Arts Festivals, not only in the Archlesia Empire but also in the Hydra Kingdom......]","Eingana’s tone remained gentle, and she seemed to genuinely enjoy expanding the topic into a discussion of hobbies. However, from Cornelia’s perspective, Eingana was an overwhelmingly superior existence. Given that they were practically meeting for the first time, Cornelia had to tread carefully, answering with great focus to avoid saying anything careless that might offend her.","This time, in particular, since she had introduced herself with her family name, it might not be taken as just “Cornelia’s personal view”. That possibility made her all the more desperate, even as she maintained a smile on the surface.","(......Kaito-sama, i- if possible, some backup please...... I don’t know much about Eingana-sama, so I can’t tell what might offend her. It’s terrifying. A- And...... no, it looks hopeless. You’re happily talking with Nidzveld-sama now......)","Ideally, Cornelia would have wanted Kaito to step in occasionally and help carry the conversation, but Kaito basically was not particularly familiar with this world’s musical culture. And in a situation that looked very much like Eingana and Cornelia were enjoying a conversation about a shared interest...... the natural choice was for him not to intrude.","Of course, thanks to Sympathy Magic, he was aware of how nervous Cornelia is. If she truly became overwhelmed, or if she got stuck and couldn’t continue, he would surely step in to help...... But precisely because of that, until it reached such a point, the likelihood of Kaito joining in was low, meaning Cornelia’s ordeal seemed destined to continue for some time yet.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Ahh, so when it comes to general knowledge and such, Eris is superior, and that difference shows in situations like this...... Come to think of it, when she ran into Rasal, she seemed able to talk about necromancy with at least a veneer of knowledge. Her range of knowledge really does seem broad.]","? ? ? : [And Eris-san is also mentally tough, or rather, she has the strength to recover quickly and respond calmly. Looking at it overall, Eris-san comes out on top.]"]},{"number":2383,"title":"Chapter 2383: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 13","paragraphs":["While Eingana-san and Cornelia-san were excitedly talking about music, I was conversing with Frea-san. Well, since we were at the same table, I could still hear Eingana-san and Cornelia-san’s discussion, and since Cornelia-san seemed a little tense, I thought I might step in and support her if needed, but for now, she seemed fine, so I focused on talking with Frea-san.","[Speaking of which, my comrade, what brings you to this city? Sightseeing?]","[Ahh, no. Through Cornelia-san’s introduction, I visited a company called the Victor Trading Company, which deals in monster-related goods, and I placed an order for special pet brushes.]","[Hou? Special brushes? Something like that exists?]","[Yes. Apparently, they’re custom-made to match each creature’s magic power wavelength. I haven’t received the finished product yet, so I haven’t used one, but from what I heard, they sound really good. Oh, and it seems they can also make brushes for dragon scales, so I ordered one of those too.]","[ ! ? ]","Cornelia-san, who was sitting next to me, suddenly snapped her head toward me with a frightened expression on her face.","[Eh? Cornelia-san? Is something the matter?]","[Ah, n- no, my apologies. It’s just that the company you mentioned is one I have connections with, so I was curious......]","[Ah, I see......]","Victor Trading Company was essentially under the umbrella of the Sharon Trading Company, so if it came up, of course, she’d be concerned...... Eingana-san also looked intrigued, and it felt like she had temporarily set aside the music talk to listen in on our conversation.","[......That is quite an interesting topic. I too use brushes when tending to my scales, but the idea of preparing one attuned to one's magic power wavelengths had never occurred to me. Still, it certainly seems more effective...... My comrade, would it be possible for me to place an order as well?]","[I think so. From what I heard, they accept orders normally, so as long as you have enough scales to record your magic power wavelength, it should be possible...... Ahh, but......]","[Unn? Something concerns you?]","Well, speaking of concerns, Cornelia-san beside me had gone pale, which was also worrying, but for now, I decided to answer Frea-san first.","It wasn’t much of a concern, really, but something came to mind when I saw Frea-san show interest in the special brush.","[Ahh, no, it’s not a big concern. It’s just that, since my Lynn and Sieg-san’s Sela are still children and small, I was wondering...... for someone as large as Frea-san, the brush would have to be enormous. I just wondered if they could even make one that size......]","[......H- Hou......]","If they could handle Bell’s size, maybe it would be fine, but even though Frea-san was considered small among Dragons, compared to ordinary monsters, she was still enormous. I wasn’t sure if they could make a brush suitable for her size.","Still, when Frea-san heard my words, she suddenly started shifting her gaze nervously, looking restless.","[......M- My comrade...... from your perspective...... do I appear...... e- enormous?]","A- Ahh~~ I see now...... So it's that. Frea-san apparently had a complex about her body size, and she had reacted to my use of the word \"enormous\".","I understood that feeling very well, so of course, I’d affirm her.","[Yes, of course. Since I’m human, when Frea-san takes the form of a Dragon, I end up looking up at you, and with how dignified and powerful you look, you really do seem enormous. Honestly, when I saw your dragon form, there’s no way I would’ve thought you were only about 5 meters. You looked more like 7...... no, even 8 meters.]","[E- Eight meters is a bit of an exaggeration! S- Still, well...... from your frame of reference it would be difficult to gauge my exact over-all length, so I suppose it can’t be helped if I appeared that way!]","She looked absolutely delighted. Her voice even cracked a little, and the usually cool, dignified Frea-san looked almost adorably happy. I completely understood that feeling, when I was once mistaken for being over 170 cm tall, I was really pleased too......","[......By the way, Miyama Kaito-san, how about my dragon form? Just a simple impression will do, but how did I appear to you compared to my actual size?]","At that moment, Eingana-san also asked what impression I had of her dragon form. But here I had to tread carefully, giving the same kind of answer I gave Frea-san would be a bad move.","Frea-san had a complex about her size, so being perceived as bigger pleased her. Eingana, however, was different.","[Eingana-san’s dragon form? Of course, to me it looked tremendously huge as well, but...... How should I put it...... Maybe it’s because your face is smaller and has a sharp, refined impression, but overall you looked slender, so I feel like you actually appeared smaller than your true length.]","[......As expected of the one whom Magnawell-sama praises so highly. To so clearly perceive the truth of things, you possess truly remarkable eyes. I am deeply impressed. That is indeed a correct and most accurate impression.]","Hearing my words, Eingana-san nodded with great satisfaction and proceeded to shower me with praise. Through Sympathy Magic, I could also sense the strong joy radiating from her.","It reminded me of that time at the Hydra Kingdom’s Founding Festival...... when I learned that Eingana-san was self-conscious about the size of her face...... At the time, I thought it was unnecessary information, but I never imagined the tidbit Alice shared with me would come in handy here.","Incidentally, as for the other two of the Four Great Demon Dragons, just a hunch, but I feel like Grandireus-san would be pleased if praised for his size. Even though his smaller clone body suggests curiosity about what being small feels like, he basically takes pride in his massive body.","Fafnir, on the other hand, doesn’t seem to care much about size at all, but I think he’d be pleased if I said something along the lines of \"you have the presence of a leader\" or \"you carry yourself in a way befitting the Head Subordinate\"...... Well, that’s really just my intuition......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [This is the insight of the Conquest King, who’s raised countless flags...... the power of the Incarnation of Perfect Communication...... He’s probably right about how to deal with Grandireus and Fafnir too...... And meanwhile, Cornelia’s stomach is probably dying.]"]},{"number":2384,"title":"Chapter 2384: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 14","paragraphs":["Cornelia Sharon, eldest daughter of the Sharon County. Her capabilities as a noblewoman were somewhere between above average and slightly above that, thanks to both the solid education fitting of a high-ranking noble's daughter and her own hard work. She was more competent than most, but she did not reach the level of elites like Eris.","At the very least, she lacked Eris' depth of knowledge and ability to adapt to new information, and responding accurately to the current situation was difficult for her. Still, she had gained her own share of experience within noble society and wasn't entirely without countermeasures.","(Nidzveld-sama and Eingana-sama made remarks suggesting they were interested in the Victor Trading Company. I feel like all the blood has drained from my face. Thinking about what may happen next makes me feel like there's about to be a hole in my stomach..... but this is beyond what I can deal with right now.... I'll think about it later. Even if it's something I'll eventually have to face, sometimes turning away temporarily is necessary to protect oneself.)","Yes, Cornelia did not have the ability to neatly organize her thoughts about every possible development here and now. Thus, she decided to avert her eyes from most matters and think about them later. It was, in a sense, a form of escapism, but doing so spared her from having to dwell on what Nidzveld, Eingana, and the Victor Trading Company might mean for the future, giving her mind some much-needed breathing room.","Of course, there were times when immediate action was vital, and one couldn't simply look away. Even in this case, she would surely end up holding her head in her hands with her family once she returned to the count's mansion...... but for now, she chose to think that it was better than being tossed about by confusion and letting her mind spiral aimlessly.","(For the time being, what I should focus on is listening to Kaito-sama and the Allegra Symphony's performance. Anything that doesn't require an immediate conclusion can wait. That way, the proper course of action will become clear.)","Having pushed aside a few of her thoughts, Cornelia felt calmer. She quietly moved her gaze, checked the clock, and spoke to Kaito.","...Kaito-sama, forgive me for interrupting your conversation, but it's now about 30 minutes before the concert begins.]","[Ah, you're right. We still have a bit of time, but maybe we should start heading toward the concert hall soon.]","Indeed, they had originally stopped by this café to kill time before the concert, so they didn't have that much room for long conversations.","The concert hall was nearby enough that they could leave 15 minutes before and still arrive comfortably, but entering early was always safer, and it conveniently brought an end to their talk with the two Six Kings' Executives.","(It's quite difficult to maintain focus while conversing with Nidzveld-sama and Eingana-sama, so being able to wrap things up here is a relief. Still, Kaito-sama's conversational skill is truly remarkable. Without any sign of calculation, he naturally engages in talk that genuinely entertains them both. As someone involved in high society, I'd love to learn from it, but since it stems from genuine kindness and natural ease rather than strategy, it's not something I could ever imitate..... it's simply impossible.)","As she recalled how cheerful Nidzveld and Eingana had looked, Cornelia could only admire Kaito's extraordinary communication skills, though she knew she couldn't copy them.","Kaito tends to wear his emotions on his sleeves, but the thought process and word choices behind his speech didn't. That wasn't natural talent, it was something he'd acquired.","Beyond the growth he'd achieved through various experiences, a major factor.... was his frequent interactions, about five times a week, with a \"dangerous God\", where even a slightly misplaced word could trigger a rampage. As a result, Kaito's conversational and communication abilities had evolved to the point where he could think at high speed while maintaining a natural demeanor, something Cornelia could only admire wholeheartedly.","That said, his facial expressions still betrayed his feelings far too easily, so it wasn't as though he'd become adept at political poker faces or manipulative subtlety.","If anything, what had improved was his natural knack for conversing in ways that raised others' favor toward him, a skill that had now been polished to perfection.","As a side note, though somewhat unrelated, Kaito had once categorized Eden and Makina's rampages into distinct \"phases\" to gauge their severity, but recently, his approach had become far more precise..... It was as if he now had a \"rampage gauge\", and assuming that gauge filled completely when they go on a rampage, Kaito had nearly mastered the ability to read its current level. He could now discern the signs of an impending rampage, and even roughly estimate how close they were to reaching the breaking point.","More recently still, he had learned to recognize the earliest symptoms and divert the topic of conversation at the right time, successfully preventing a rampage from occurring.","Of course, there were cases of instantaneous rampages, situations where they couldn't be stopped once triggered, or instances where they were practically in a rampage state the moment they appeared, so his success rate was only around 30 to 40 percent.","Even so, through countless conversations that were essentially like handling live explosives, Kaito's ability to think on his feet during dialogue had grown explosively.","[Indeed. It's about time for us to head toward the concert hall as well, shall we leave the shop?]","[..... Yeah. There's still some time before the appointed hour, but we mustn't keep them waiting. It would be proper for us to arrive first and wait.]","[Quite so. I doubt they'd mind if we were a bit late, but we would feel uncomfortable about it.]","[Umu.... Well then, my comrade, we're heading out now as well. Our destination is the same concert hall. Would you like to go together? Even if we part ways here, I suspect we'd meet again soon enough.]","[Unn? I don't mind going together to the concert hall. Cornelia-san, are you okay with that?]","[Y-Yes, that's fine.]","As she replied alongside Kaito to Nidzveld's invitation to head to the concert hall together, Cornelia felt a chill of cold sweat run down her back.","That they would go together was predictable, since they were headed to the same place, there was no real reason to part ways here.","But that wasn't the problem.......","(...Just now, Nidzveld-sama said they couldn't keep someone waiting..... which means they're planning to meet someone at the concert hall, right? And from the way both Nidzveld-sama and Eingana-sama spoke, it sounded like they were referring to someone far above them in rank...... T-There's no way that's the case, right? There's no way......)","Cornelia shuddered at the implications of their earlier exchange, but at that moment, Kaito, who seemed to share her concern, voiced the",".....You said you didn't want to keep someone waiting, are you meeting up with someone?]","[Ah, yes. This time, Magnawell-sama and Megiddo-sama will also be accompanying us. We're scheduled to meet up with them in front of the concert hall.]","[Eh? Magnawell-san and Megiddo-san are here too?]","[Hyu......]","The instant those names reached her ears, Cornelia felt as though her heart had nearly stopped, her gaze turning to the sky with a face filled with","despair."]},{"number":2385,"title":"Chapter 2385: Intermission: A Terrifying Warning","paragraphs":["In a room furnished with pieces that were unmistakably high-class, a portly man dressed in what was clearly expensive clothing sat on a sofa, leisurely drinking wine.","Judging by his obvious good mood, the man, who occasionally let a self-satisfied smile slip as he tilted his glass, was the head of a certain Viscouncy within Archlesia Empire.","As he enjoyed his wine alone, a knock sounded at the door. Shortly after, a woman in her 40s wearing a fine dress, his wife, the Viscountess, entered the room.","[......Ara, aren’t you in quite the good mood today? Drinking wine in the middle of the day, did something pleasant happen, Dear?]","[Ahh, not quite yet, but soon enough. How about it, care for a drink?]","[Then I shall join you.]","Though slightly puzzled by her husband’s cheerfulness, the Viscountess accepted the offer, sat beside him, and began to drink as well. It hadn’t been some grand romance, but the two had met at a social gathering in their youth and, rather than marrying for politics, wed for love. Now, over 20 years later, the Viscount began to happily share the reason for his good mood with his beloved wife.","[Well now, I’ve come across some rather profitable information. It seems the Ritch Barony has gotten themselves into an interesting situation. I was thinking our household might as well get a piece of the pie.]","[......Ara? Are you sure that’s wise? I’ve heard a bit of that rumor myself...... isn’t it connected to that Otherworlder? Her Majesty the Emperor warned all noble households not to act carelessly in any matter involving him, did he not?]","[Hahaha! There’s no problem. It’s not as if I’m planning to do anything underhanded. I simply intend to have a little collaboration with the Ritch Barony’s industry, that’s all. I’ve done them plenty of favors already, after all, they can hardly refuse. Even if their territory borders ours, we’ve humored those paupers who can barely be called nobles. It’s only fair we reap some reward in return. Fufu, to think even a poor noble can prove useful at times.]","[Is it really that lucrative a deal?]","Perhaps influenced a little by the wine, the Viscountess smiled brightly at her husband’s gleeful tone.","[Oh yes, we stand to gain a considerable profit.]","[Ara, how lovely. Then perhaps you might buy me a new accessory?]","[Hahaha! Leave it to me! We can even replace your dresses and the magical furnishings in the room.]","[Oh my, how wonderful!]","Eyes sparkling at his words, the Viscountess set down her glass and lovingly embraced her husband. The Viscount, even more pleased, deepened his grin.","Clinging to him in a sweet show of affection, she lingered for a moment before slowly pulling back, her lips close to his ear as she whispered in a honeyed voice———–","[......The Phantasmal King No Face-sama will not permit such an act. If you intend to go through with it, be prepared to face the consequences.]","[ ! ? ! ? ]","The words were so shocking that the Viscount’s intoxication vanished in an instant. He turned toward his wife in disbelief...... only to find her looking back at him, wide-eyed and puzzled, her head tilted innocently.","[Dear? What’s wrong?]","[Y- You...... just now......]","[Just now? ......Did I perhaps say something offensive?]","[......Ah, no...... it’s...... it’s nothing......]","[Is that so? Ara, ara, Dear, you’re drenched in sweat...... Are you all right? Perhaps you’ve been drinking a bit too much?]","Sweat gushed from every pore as the Viscount felt as if the heat were draining from his body. Standing before him was undeniably his wife...... or at least, she should be his wife. Her laugh, her tone, her expression, her gestures...... everything was unmistakably that of the beloved woman with whom he’d spent over 20 years.","And yet, just a moment ago, he had undeniably heard it from her voice...... a warning......","He didn’t understand. Was the person before him truly his wife? He couldn’t tell. He understood nothing.","Was it one of the Phantasmal King’s subordinates in disguise? Or was his wife the Phantasmal King's subordinate all along? Or perhaps she had been momentarily controlled by some kind of Mental Manipulation Magic? Or maybe the warning had only been whispered to his ears, mimicking his wife’s voice? He had no idea which was the truth.","The one thing he did know for certain...... was that all his thoughts were already laid bare before the Phantasmal King, and that if he did not heed this warning, the next time it would be his head that rolled.","The wife who had been his dearest, most trusted companion had...... in an instant, turned into something unfathomable, and he trembled in an indescribable fear. With deep regret, he resolved to wipe all his schemes clean.","At that moment, he couldn't help but think that after this incident, the fact that this terror would follow him always, breeding suspicion and doubt, was itself the punishment for daring to entertain such foolish thoughts......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......That’s terrifying!]","? ? ? : [Well~~ as expected of Alice-chan, she’s great at subtle behind-the-scenes support. I don’t know about that Viscount in question, but the correct answer this time is number two, the wife was originally one of her subordinates~~]","Serious-senpai : [Honestly, that’s scarier than bringing Eden along to intimidate someone...... That’s the kind of thing that could leave you traumatized......]"]},{"number":2386,"title":"Chapter 2386: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 15","paragraphs":["It goes without saying that there’s a clear difference between the Six Kings themselves and their Executives. Even those who serve directly under the Six Kings are individuals of extraordinary ability, true elites who could be said to stand among the very best in the world. Their fame and influence are equally immense, and even a noble must tread carefully when dealing with them, for a single misstep could mean losing one’s position entirely.","However, compared to them, the Six Kings themselves exist on an entirely different plane. While, on paper, the Demon Realm respects the Human Realm under the terms of the Friendship Treaty, and the Divine Realm often interacts with humanity through blessings and divine protections, making it seem as though the Six Kings stand as equals to the Human Realm's Three Rulers, in reality, the Six Kings’ authority and stature far surpass that of any human monarch.","For Cornelia, a mere noble’s daughter, they are truly beings among the clouds, far beyond her reach. Even among the heads of noble houses, very few have ever spoken directly with one of the Six Kings, and to have any personal connection with them is, in itself, an extraordinary mark of status among the nobility.","(T- T- Two of the Six Kings are here!? N- Not only that, it's War King-sama and Dragon King-sama......)","Though all of the Six Kings possess overwhelming power and authority, some are relatively approachable, while others are nearly impossible to interact with.","First, there are those with whom contact is essentially impossible, the Death King and the Phantasmal King. With the Death King Isis, this is only natural. It was only quite recently, with the control accessory granted by Kanaris, that communication even became possible. Before that, one couldn’t so much as approach her without possessing power equal to that of a Peerage Holder. Given that, across all of Humanity, there are only about four individuals of that level, it was inevitable that no Human could normally hope to meet her.","As for the Phantasmal King, the very act of the Phantasmal King appearing before a noble almost always signified a death sentence for said noble, making any kind of \"interaction\" impossible. Nowadays, she occasionally appears thanks to Kaito’s influence, but before his arrival in Trinia, she was a presence rarely seen outside of the Festival of Heroes.","By contrast, the easiest of the Six Kings to approach are the gentle-minded Underworld King and World King. Underworld King Kuromueina serves as the de facto representative of the Demon Realm and thus often appears in public. She personally runs numerous businesses, frequently interacts with Humans, and even travels to various cities simply to sample local cuisine, making her the most approachable among the Six Kings.","World King Lillywood does not visit the Human Realm as often as Kuromueina, yet compared to the other Six Kings, she still appears as a guest at many Human events. Her kind and gentle disposition makes her another comparatively easy ruler to engage with.","On the other hand, while interaction is possible with the War King and Dragon King, it is far from easy. War King Megiddo, as one might expect, holds little fondness for nobles and has a consistent tendency to kill anyone who displeases them. As such, establishing rapport with them is exceedingly difficult. They do visit the Human Realm from time to time, and if one earns their favor, there may be a chance to interact, but approaching them carelessly carries tremendous risk.","In the case of Dragon King Magnawell, while he doesn’t present the same kind of danger as Megiddo, meeting him in person is still exceedingly difficult. His sheer size alone makes it impossible for him to visit the Human Realm outside of the Festival of Heroes. The only way to meet him directly would be to travel to the southern mountain ranges of the Demon Realm, a region teeming with monsters and considered extremely dangerous even there.","Recently, however, Magnawell has acquired a special clone body that allows him to visit the Human Realm from time to time, so that situation may change in the future, but as things stand, he remains, along with the War King, one of the Six Kings most difficult for nobles to approach.","[......U- Umm, Nidzveld-sama, Eingana-sama...... may I ask a question? I- Is it truly alright for me to accompany you...... to a place where the Six Kings themselves will be present?]","[Ahh, there’s no problem. In fact, even if you were to act separately now, you would soon end up meeting them anyway.]","[Megiddo-sama is very fond of Miyama Kaito-san. Once they realize he is nearby, they’ll almost certainly shout his name at the top of their lungs while approaching......]","Hearing Eingana’s words, Cornelia froze in dread. The image flashed through her mind, War King Megiddo loudly calling out Kaito’s name while striding toward them in front of a crowd of onlookers. The attention that would draw would be immense, and naturally, it would spill over to her as well...... Thinking about it, she began to feel that perhaps going to meet him first would actually be safer.","And sadly, resolve...... that thing people call mental preparation can sometimes be nothing more than a fragile seawall for the heart.","Had Cornelia been unaware of what awaited her, had Megiddo and Magnawell appeared before her without warning, her mental fortitude, far inferior to someone like Eris, might not have held. The shock alone could very well have caused her to faint on the spot.","But now, with prior knowledge of the meeting ahead, she was at least mentally prepared. Her stomach felt as though it had been filled with lead, heavy and painful with anxiety, but she was unlikely to lose consciousness.","......Though, in a sense, perhaps it was unlucky that she learned of it beforehand, since even the option of fainting as a form of escape had been taken from her.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Hah!? W- Wait a second! Isn’t the last chapter a serious scene!!!?]","? ? ? : [Eh? You just realized that now?]<tucrq> Fresh chapters posted on novel-fire.ɴet</tucrq>","Serious-senpai : [W- Well, I had kind of given up on the idea of any serious development happening while I was actually here...... I- I mean, it always happens conveniently when I’m not around or when I don’t see it...... So I accidentally noticed it a bit late!?]","? ? ? : [......Well, on the bright side, this finally disproves the theory that Serious-senpai is the embodiment of seriousness and therefore can’t appear when the main story gets serious. It also confirms that whether or not Serious-senpai shows up in the afterword has absolutely no effect on whether the story itself turns serious.]","Serious-senpai : [....................................]"]},{"number":2387,"title":"Chapter 2387: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 16","paragraphs":["The meeting place was a little ways away from the concert hall, in a quieter area where few people passed by, though there were still a fair number of people visible around them.","While they made small talk as they waited, Cornelia suddenly felt a faint disturbance in the air and instinctively straightened her back.","(I- It’s time......! C- Can I really do this? I don’t mean to doubt Nidzveld-sama’s words, but the thought of facing War King-sama makes my spine go cold.)","Before long, two figures approached from ahead, a tall elderly gentleman and a small girl with horns...... To a passerby, they might have looked like an ordinary grandfather and granddaughter, but the people in their path quickly moved aside.","Even though Megiddo’s human forms were quite famous, and it was known that she had several, there was one unmistakable trait that made it easy to recognize her even for those who had never met her directly.","It was her presence. Megiddo didn’t use Recognition Inhibition Magic or Information Concealment Magic, nor did she bother to suppress her immense magical power. Even when taking the form of a young girl, that vast aura remained unchanged, it was immediately clear that this was the War King in human form.","For instance, if it were someone like Kuromueina, without Recognition Inhibition Magic, there would be crowds of people gathering, eager to see her, talk to her, or get her autograph, but that never happened with Megiddo.","On the contrary, ordinary people generally avoided Megiddo. The reason was simple, if you angered her, she could quite literally kill you, so rather than calling out recklessly, people simply made way in silence. Among the Six Kings, the one most feared by the public was Isis, but Megiddo followed closely behind, which was only natural.","As the people stepped aside and the view ahead cleared, Megiddo noticed them and broke into an obviously delighted grin.","[Oh! If it isn’t Kaito! What a coincidence to run into you he———- Ouch!? Hey! What was that for!?]","[Don’t raise your voice, you fool. You’ll only attract unnecessary attention.]","[Who cares about that...... If they’re in the way, should I disperse them?]","[Stop that at once.]","Having spotted Kaito, Megiddo’s excitement rose, and her loud voice immediately earned her a fist to the head from Magnawell. Watching the scene, Cornelia pressed a hand to her stomach and stared blankly into the distance, realizing that she was about to meet two of the Six Kings in such a public place.","[Hello, Megiddo-san, Magnawell-san. I happened to run into Frea-san and Eingana-san, so I came along with them.]","[So you’re here to hear the Allegra Symphony huh? Nice choice. They’re still a bit rough, but they’re a good band.]","[It has been since your birthday celebration, has it not? Even if by chance, it pleases me to meet again like this.]","When Kaito greeted them, both Megiddo and Magnawell replied cheerfully. Immediately after, Megiddo turned her gaze toward Cornelia, who reflexively straightened her back once more.","[......So, who the hell are you?]","Just as Kaori and Akane had once experienced during Archlesia Empire’s Founding Festival, Megiddo’s voice carried such a heavy tone that, if you didn’t know her, it could easily sound like she's angry.","Since she spoke so cheerfully with Kaito, the sudden contrast in tone was startling, and Cornelia broke into a nervous sweat, panicking internally over whether she had somehow offended her.","[Megiddo-san, you’re scaring Cornelia-san.]","[Ahh? Why?]","[Like I told you before, if someone doesn’t know you, you sound angry to them...... Cornelia-san, it’s all right. Megiddo-san isn’t mad, that’s just how they normally talk.]","[I- I see...... M- My apologies.]","Thanks to Kaito stepping in, Cornelia let out a sigh of relief, gently pressing a hand to her chest.","(M- My life nearly flashed before my eyes. I thought I’d somehow offended her and drawn her wrath...... but that wasn’t the case, was it? I- I’d really prefer if only Kaito-sama did the talking from here on out, but...... that’s probably...... impossible, isn’t it......)","Trusting Kaito’s words that Megiddo wasn’t actually angry, Cornelia accepted the explanation, but she was still unsure of what to do next...... Should she introduce herself? Would that be presumptuous? As she hesitated, Kaito spoke up to Megiddo and Magnawell.","[Let me introduce her to you as well, Megiddo-san, Magnawell-san. This is Cornelia Sharon-san, a friend who came with me today.]","[Cornelia Sharon? Ahh, so you’re a few generations down from that one, and inherited the name huh...... Don’t remember seeing you at the party though. So you’re Kaito’s new woman then!]","[......I said friend, didn’t I?]","[Ahh? But you’re on a date, ain’t ya? Ah! Haven’t slept together yet, huh! Well, agreeing to a date means she’s fine with it, right?]","[Megiddo-san, please. I’ll talk to Kuro about this later, you really need some remedial lessons on romance.]","[W- What? Why!?]","The exchange itself was lighthearted and comical, but Megiddo’s voice was loud, while Kaito’s tone was normal...... Which meant that to everyone watching from a distance, Megiddo’s shout of \"Kaito’s new woman\" rang out loud and clear, whereas Kaito’s denial likely did not reach their ears.","And among those watching were several nobles...... some of whom Cornelia recognized, making her stomach twist with pain as a wave of dizziness washed over her.<vmusw> Thɪs chapter is updated by NoveI-Fire.ɴet</vmusw>","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [As always, a total muscle-headed gorilla when it comes to romance......]","? ? ? : [In any case, since her thinking is simple and she hates anything roundabout, Kuro-san had quite a hard time trying to teach her.]"]},{"number":2388,"title":"Chapter 2388: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 17","paragraphs":["It was certainly a relief that Kaito had offered a helping hand during the exchange with Megiddo, but the fact remained that she had missed the proper timing to introduce herself.","(......H- How should I handle this......? Once their conversation with Kaito-sama ends, I naturally have to greet them. But is it really okay to mention my family name? Kaito-sama is special, of course, but if I introduce myself with my family name included, it might be taken as if I expect to be treated as nobility...... No, but if I only give my first name here, it would break the flow of Kaito-sama’s introduction...... U- Uuuu, what is the correct way to do this......?)","At this point, Cornelia was allowed to meet the two of the Six Kings solely in her capacity as Kaito’s friend; she was not permitted to stand before them as a representative of Sharon County. If she gave her full name, it could be interpreted as having ulterior motives, but since Megiddo seemed to know of Sharon County, omitting the family name would also feel unnatural. Cornelia wrestled with these thoughts.","Thereupon, just as the conversation between Kaito and Megiddo reached a lull, Magnawell spoke quietly, his tone commanding.<lqybu> Follow current ɴᴏᴠᴇʟs on novel★fire.net</lqybu>","[......Now, if you are a friend of Miyama Kaito, then it is only proper for us to show the appropriate consideration. You are permitted to introduce yourself, including your family name. Megiddo, is that acceptable for you too?]","[Ahh? ......Ah, about that huh...... Sure, he’s Kaito’s buddy, so I don’t mind either.]","Sensing Cornelia’s hesitation, Magnawell granted her permission to give her full name and confirmed it with Megiddo. Despite her rough manner, Megiddo was sharp enough to immediately understand Magnawell’s intention and nodded in agreement.","[With your generous words, I am deeply grateful...... Once again, please allow me to greet the great rulers of the Demon Realm. I am Cornelia Sharon, eldest daughter of Sharon County.]","[Umu. I am Magnawell Baskus Lardo Kurtzvald, though you may call me Magnawell.]","[I'm Megiddo Argetes Kurein, best regards. You can just call me Megiddo.]","As Cornelia delivered her greeting and Magnawell and Megiddo responded, Kaito’s expression turned slightly puzzled.","[Arehh? Megiddo-san, wasn’t your family name Argetes Borgnes?]","[Unn? Nah, that’s not my family name. Borgnes is just the name I use in my usual form. This form is Kurein, and the other humanoid form Kaito has seen is named Pureshon.]","[Ahh, so it was the name of a form.]","[Yeah. Well, as long as I properly convey the name Megiddo, the rest doesn’t matter.]","Watching this exchange between Megiddo and Kaito from the side, Cornelia tried to calm her fluttering heart.","(I now truly understand the meaning behind Eris-sama’s words. Simply being Kaito-sama’s friend allows me to use my family name and even call the Six Kings by their names...... His influence is astonishing. At the very least, I have already been elevated far beyond the position of a mere noble daughter. No matter what, now that I’ve used my family name, I must act with the full awareness that everything I do from this point on will affect the reputation of Sharon County......)","Cornelia had been permitted to give her full name and had presented herself as a member of the Sharon noble family to Magnawell and Megiddo. From this moment on, her actions would reflect on the Sharon family’s reputation.","Cornelia braced herself for the weight of that responsibility...... but even she had to admit, her assumption that she could simply manage by being cautious was far too naïve.","No, her way of thinking wasn’t wrong in itself. Yet, inexperienced Cornelia had still underestimated the situation, she hadn’t fully realized just how much influence Kaito’s high regard carried......","[Hmm...... Sharon County huh...... I thought they’d been stable lately, nothing too challenging, nothing remarkable...... but I see, there’s someone in the current Sharon County that catches Kaito’s attention......]","[Eh? U- Umm, M- Megiddo-sama?]","[Fumu. Sharon County, if I recall, owns a magic tool trade company, doesn’t it? That does pique my interest a bit...... But that aside, Miyama Kaito. Did you come all the way to this city today just to hear a performance?]","A chill ran down her spine. Both Megiddo and Magnawell seemed to show interest in Sharon County simply because of Kaito’s acquaintance, and Cornelia’s stomach tightened in warning.","But her uneasy thoughts were short-lived, another shock was about to strike.","[Ahh, no, it was more like I went to the Victor Trading Company on the recommendation of Cornelia-san. They deal in monster-related goods, you see. They make specialized brushes for monsters, and apparently, they’re practically a subsidiary under Cornelia-san’s Sharon Trading Company.]","[......Hou, that is interesting...... This brush you mentioned is......]","The conversation, casually started by Kaito in response to Magnawell’s words, sent a wave of dread coursing through Cornelia, as if all the blood in her body had drained away.","(Kaito-sama? KAITO-SAMAAAA!? D- Didn’t you just phrase that strangely? The way you said it, it sounds like I hold a high position within the Sharon Trading Company! I’m just the eldest daughter of the County, and the Sharon Trading Company is the family business...... I don’t actually hold that much authority...... N- No, it’s true I haven’t explained that part to Kaito-sama in detail, so it’s understandable he might misunderstand, but still! Still!!!)","Her soul’s cry went unheard by Kaito, and with no chance to interrupt the conversation between Magnawell and Kaito, Cornelia could only wear a helpless, indescribable expression on her face.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [If you think about it, had she been able to faint in their first encounter without any prior information, all of this could’ve been avoided...... It really highlights just how devilish that Stomachache Devil was for putting in an anti-faint measure......]"]},{"number":2389,"title":"Chapter 2389: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 18","paragraphs":["Kaito’s misunderstanding was, in a sense, understandable. Setting aside Lilia, who was a family head, the only noble lady Kaito could picture at present was Eris. Naturally, she became his standard of comparison.","However, Eris and Cornelia stood on very different social ground. Eris was the heir to a Marquisdom, a prodigy from childhood who had displayed brilliance across numerous fields. She had founded several stores at a young age and even taken part in her family’s businesses. She was a person of great authority and influence.","By contrast, Cornelia was merely the eldest daughter of a County. The family’s inheritance would go to her elder brother, the legitimate heir, and Cornelia herself was expected to marry into another house for political reasons. She was not deeply involved in the family’s ventures and had little power within them.","Of course, she still had a general grasp of what her family’s business entailed, and she would sometimes offer opinions or ideas...... However, at the very least, she had almost no part in the management of the Sharon Trading Company.","The only reason she had guided Kaito to the Victor Trading Company was because she personally was friends with him, nothing more. Even though the Victor Trading Company was technically a subsidiary under her family’s influence, she held no actual authority over it.","[Hmm, I see. It’s not just Dragons, there are other races who find that ordinary brushes irritate their skin. Creating an exclusive brush sounds like a fine idea indeed.]","[Would you want an exclusive brush too, Magnawell-san?]","[No, making a brush suited to my size would be unrealistic. I use magic to clean myself, though it takes considerable skill to polish each scale properly, something few can do. Those who cannot often make use of brushes and such.]","At that moment, the conversation between Kaito and Magnawell was utterly terrifying to Cornelia. Especially because Magnawell, the Dragon King himself, seemed to show a certain level of interest in exclusive brushes.","(It doesn’t seem like Dragon King-sama...... Magnawell-sama intends to have one made for himself, but this is a terrible turn of conversation. Truly terrible...... Umm, Kaito-sama...... you remember, don’t you? Victor Trading Company is just a small trading company. If the Dragon King camp were to place a mass order, the results would be unimaginable......)","Under the Dragon King’s rule were tens of millions of monsters. Even if only a fraction were interested...... if their King, Magnawell, took a liking to these exclusive brushes, it was easy to imagine how many would want one too.","However, the Victor Trading Company had nowhere near the capacity to handle such a massive order. If that were to happen, Sharon County would have to invest enormous funds to expand the company’s operations.","That would undoubtedly bring tremendous profit to Sharon County...... but if this plan came to fruition through this very conversation...... there was no doubt who would end up at the center of it all....... Cornelia herself.","[I haven’t received mine yet since I just placed the order today, but according to Cornelia-san, their brushes are really good, so I’m looking forward to it.]","[Fumu. Then I shall ask you about its performance once you’ve tried it. If it’s satisfactory, I may recommend it to some of my subordinates who also want brushes.]","[Ahh, that would be great for Victor Trading Company’s sales.]","And then, the conversation began heading exactly in the direction Cornelia had feared.","(Kaito-sama? KAITO-SAMA!!! Magnawell-sama's camp, the Dragon King's camp is said to be second only to the Phantasmal King’s in number...... Of course, it’s not as if every single one of them would place an order, but even if only one out of a hundred did, that would still be an astronomical amount!)","Of course, this was all still hypothetical, it would only become relevant after Kaito received and used his custom brushes. There was no actual order being placed yet.","(But still, if...... if Kaito-sama ends up giving the brushes a high evaluation...... wouldn’t that lead to something absolutely catastrophic? J- Just imagining it makes my stomach......)","Just picturing the potential outcome made her stomach twist in pain. And then, right after that, Magnawell turned towards Cornelia and spoke the words that sounded like a death sentence.","[Then, should any among my subordinates desire a brush, I shall have them contact Cornelia Sharon directly...... is that acceptable?]<khsjf> ɴᴇᴡ ɴᴏᴠᴇʟ ᴄʜᴀᴘᴛᴇʀs ᴀʀᴇ ᴘᴜʙʟɪsʜᴇᴅ ᴏɴ n͟o͟v͟e͟l͟f͟i͟r͟e͟.net</khsjf>","[Y- Yesh, absholutely!]","If possible, she wanted him to contact Sharon County instead...... She really wanted that, but at the moment, Cornelia was the only one who had personal connections with both Magnawell and Kaito, and even with Nidzveld and Eingana. For now, she couldn’t possibly redirect this matter to her family.","And more than that, Magnawell, one of the Six Kings, had, even if unintentionally, personally appointed her as the point of contact. It wasn’t the sort of request someone in her position could refuse.","Thus, in that very moment, Cornelia Sharon, eldest daughter of the Sharon family...... found her future sealed, she was now destined to become Sharon County’s chief representative in all matters related to monsters.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [There’s profit in it. Without a doubt, the profit would be enormous, and for Cornelia, who until now hadn’t had any clearly defined future position and was probably just being considered for a political marriage, this could effectively secure her a very high-ranking post. ......However, the price for that is an unbearable stomachache.]","? ? ? : [And since Kaito-san doesn’t know much about business or commerce, he’s probably just thinking something simple like \"They said their sales were down, so if sales go up, they’ll be happy\", you know?]","Serious-senpai : [Isn’t that just Kaito’s good-luck correction doing its job? Like, because he’s thinking it’d make Cornelia happy if Victor Trading Company’s profits went up, the whole situation is somehow moving in that direction?]","? ? ? : [No, not yet at this point. This is still within the scope of the conversation with Magnawell-san...... If that luck correction actually kicks in, it’ll probably be after the Dragon King’s subordinates start placing orders...... and when that happens, I bet it’ll turn into a full-blown craze among the Dragon King’s camp......]"]},{"number":2390,"title":"Chapter 2390: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 19","paragraphs":["<Author's Notes>","Since I have personal matters tomorrow and won’t be able to return home, the next update will be the day after tomorrow.","Good fortune and misfortune, though they seem opposed, they can sometimes coexist. In a way, it could be called good fortune; in another, misfortune...... Such was Cornelia’s state of mind.","Cornelia was nearing her limit. Without the mental resilience that Eris possessed, the rapid torrent of events had become an enormous strain on her. She was already at the point that could only be described as a capacity overload.","If something were to push her just a little more here, Cornelia would likely have reached her limit and lost consciousness. However, that did not happen.","To begin with, the current conversation had a time limit. Yes, the time limit being the band’s performance start time......","[Magnawell-sama, forgive me for interrupting your conversation. Time-wise, it would be best if we entered soon......]","[Oh, yes, indeed. It would be quite the folly to talk for too long and end up late for the performance’s start, wouldn’t it?]","With Eingana suggesting that they should begin entering soon, the conversation came to an end. Whether this should be seen as good fortune for allowing Cornelia to avoid fainting, or misfortune for preventing her from escaping by fainting, was debatable...... but anyhow, Cornelia was simply relieved that the conversation had finally come to a pause.","[Oh, right. Kaito, where’s your seat? I plan to sit next to you.]","[Eh? No, um, aren’t the seats assigned?]","[Yeah! That’s why I’m asking for your seat number, so I can politely \"negotiate\" with whoever’s sitting beside you to swap seats.]","[......Negotiate?]","Hearing something that sounded far more like a command to switch seats than a negotiation, Kaito looked at her with a somewhat indescribable expression, while Cornelia quietly turned her thoughts over.","(My seat is next to Kaito-sama’s, so if I switched, that would be the most peaceful solution...... No, wait. In that case, I’d end up sitting in the seat Megiddo-sama was supposed to occupy...... meaning I’d be next to Magnawell-sama, wouldn’t I? T- That’s far too much...... my heart wouldn’t be able to take it......)","Since switching seats with Megiddo carried too great a risk, Cornelia decided, for the time being, to say nothing. She decided she would comply only if Megiddo himself asked her to switch......","However, Megiddo had no intention of asking Cornelia to switch. From her perspective, Cornelia was currently on a date with Kaito, and she had no intention of disturbing it. Thus, she planned to sit on the seat opposite Cornelia.","[So, where is it? If it’s an aisle seat, I’ll just sit behind......]","[Errr, it’s this seat.]","[Unn? Oh! What do you know, it’s right next to mine! That saves me the trouble!]","Seeing Megiddo nod happily, Kaito suddenly recalled Alice, the one who had sold him the ticket. Knowing her, she had likely arranged the seats with this very situation in mind. He now felt he understood the reason behind the mischievous smile she’d given him at the time.","Had he not coincidentally met Nidzveld and Eingana at the café, he would have ended up encountering Megiddo and Magnawell the moment he took his seat, which surely would have startled him. Thinking such things, Kaito entered the concert hall together with Cornelia and the others.","And from a distance, watching the scene unfold, Anne took out her hummingbird and sent an urgent message back to the Sharon County.","In the study of the Sharon County, the Count himself and Anne’s husband, his close aide, were working on matters related to their trading company.","[The Lord Trading Company has been rather active lately...... If we don’t keep an eye on them, there could be major shifts in the economy.]","[Indeed. Rumor has it they’re even considering transactions with the Hamilton Marquisdom...... Unn? Pardon me, a hummingbird message from my wife......]","[She should be accompanying Cornelia as her escort today...... Is it an emergency?]","Needless to say, Anne was an exceptionally capable maid and someone deeply trusted by Count Sharon. She would never send a private message during working hours. That meant she had judged this matter too urgent to wait until her return and deemed it necessary to report immediately, implying that the contents were of considerable importance.","[......Errr, Lady Cornelia has...... huh? Eh?]","[What is it?]","[Ah, errr, well...... Lady Cornelia has encountered War King-sama, Dragon King-sama, Sky Dragon-sama, and Sea Dragon-sama, and, with an introduction from Miyama Kaito-sama, was permitted to greet them with her family name.]","[......Wait a moment...... my brain refuses to process that...... W- W- W- What do you mean!? Cornelia was supposed to be out guiding Miyama Kaito-sama to the Victor Trading Company, wasn’t she...... How in the world did War King-sama and Dragon King=sama pop out of the story!?]","[I- I don’t know. I believe we’ll receive a detailed report in sequence soon, but......]","[F- For now, cancel all our upcoming appointments! Depending on the situation, we may have to take major action ourselves!]","The Count could not even begin to imagine how his daughter, who was supposed to be guiding Kaito to the Victor Trading Company, had ended up encountering two of the Six Kings along with two of their Executives, and even been allowed to introduce herself formally.","As a cold bead of sweat ran down his back, Count Sharon recalled a certain incident. Just a few days prior, at a meeting that had been set to take place at the Hamilton Marquisdom, he had seen Marquis Hamilton and Eris both looking deeply worried for the Ritch Barony couple...... And now, a shiver ran down his spine as he felt a dreadful premonition...... perhaps he was about to find himself in the very same position as Baron Ritch just had.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Ah, right, Anne can also not enter the concert hall and send a message back huh......]"]},{"number":2391,"title":"Chapter 2391: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 20","paragraphs":["Inside the mansion of the Hamilton Marquisdom, located in the capital of Archlesia Empire, Marquis Hamilton and Eris were in conversation. Originally, they had planned to summon the parents of the young ladies who attended the previous tea party to discuss future matters and give some guidance, but that meeting had been canceled due to the sudden and urgent return of Baron Ritch.","The reason was simple, depending on the nature of that emergency, the topics of discussion might change drastically. Hence, it was decided to hold the meeting on another day. The noble families that had gathered were each sent home using Teleportation Magic prepared by Hamilton Marquisdom.","[Ritch Barony was the first to have an incident huh...... I thought something might happen with the Sharon County first......]","[Fumu. If I recall correctly, Eris, you predicted that the ones most likely to have an inci...... or rather, to deepen their ties with Miyama Kaito-sama would be the Ritch Barony and the Sharon County, yes?]","[Yes. It’s only my impression from the tea party, but Cornelia-sama and Marie-sama seemed to have drawn Kaito-sama’s interest more than the other young ladies. They were the only two who made some sort of promise with him during the event. Marie-sama promised to gift him some ripples harvested from her Barony, while Cornelia-sama promised to guide him to the Victor Trading Company for a special monster brush...... That visit was supposed to be today, so I expected anything noteworthy to happen there......]","Eris had observed Kaito’s interactions with the young ladies during the tea party and made her own predictions about who had left a favorable impression on him.","Kaito was someone whose emotions easily appeared on his face, and Eris herself was exceptionally skilled at reading people. From that, she concluded that Cornelia and Marie had both managed to please Kaito more than the others, and her judgment was correct.","Furthermore, since Cornelia had arranged the visit to the Victor Trading Company on the spot, Eris had already been aware of the schedule. That was why she had expected anything significant to happen there, not with the Ritch Barony, making the emergency message from that direction all the more surprising.","[You’ve sent people to the city where the Victor Trading Company is located, haven’t you?]","[Yes. Not many, of course, but we have a few stationed near the company headquarters to report back should anything occur......]","The Sharon County was the most powerful noble family within the Hamilton Marquisdom after the Hamiltons themselves. Should anything significant happen there, it could easily affect the entire faction. Thus, both Eris and the Marquis remained cautious. For that reason, they had dispatched a small number of people to the trade city, not quite spies, but enough to ensure they would receive word quickly should something occur.","Just as their discussion reached that point, the door was vigorously knocked from the outside. When permission to enter was given, a flustered maid burst into the room.","[R- Reporting! An emergency message has arrived! In the trade city, we have visually confirmed the presence of War King-sama and Dragon King-sama, and they appear to be together with Miyama Kaito-sama and Cornelia Sharon-sama!]","[ [ ! ? ] ]","Both Eris and the Marquis Hamilton froze in shock at the report. Immediately, Eris pressed a finger to her brow, sinking deep into thought.","(If the scouts were able to confirm visually, it must have been outdoors. Within that trade city...... taking into account the location of Victor Trading Company's headquarters and the nearby facilities......)","Eris was a highly capable individual, and she had the city’s layout memorized perfectly. She quickly ran through in her mind the areas near the Victor Trading Company headquarters where one might plausibly encounter Megiddo or Magnawell.","[......This happened near the concert hall then?]","[Y- Yes! My apologies for not including that detail earlier, the sighting was near the concert hall.]","[......I can’t say what might have motivated Dragon King-sama's arrival, but War King-sama has a deep appreciation for music. It wouldn’t be strange for them to attend a concert. To just so happen to encounter them there, as to be expected with Kaito-sama’s luck...... In any case, it’s safe to assume that Kaito-sama introduced Cornelia-sama to the two of the Six Kings.]","[This is nad...... War King-sama alone is extraordinary, but a connection with Dragon King-sama as well? That doesn’t just affect the Sharon County...... it could influence the entire Empire. If rumors spread, it might cause quite an uproar.]","Even merely encountering two of the Six Kings was already an overwhelming event. Among them, Magnawell had particularly deep ties with the Archlesia Empire, and his influence upon the nobility was immense.","The source of this content ɪs novelꞁire.net</prmuk>","[It seems we’ll need to speak with Count Sharon before rumors spread. There’ll be a flood of inquiries directed at their County, and the benefits this will bring to the Hamilton faction are simply too great.]","[If we act too slowly, we could end up making quite a few enemies...... Still, the location is unfortunate, a concert hall, and with both War King-sama and Dragon King-sama present, neither of whom employ Recognition Inhibition Magic......]","If it had been someone like Kuromueina or Isis, who constantly used Recognition Inhibition Magic, then the spread of information could have been contained to some degree. With sufficient preparation, coordination between the Marquisdom and the County could have managed the balance of power among the nobility.","However, a delayed response might allow other noble families to move first. They wouldn’t directly target Cornelia, but they could attempt to secure marriages with the Sharon County’s younger children or even tempt the family to leave the Hamilton faction and form a new one. Either scenario would create a storm of political chaos.","In short, speed was crucial. As Eris and Marquis Hamilton reached that same conclusion almost simultaneously, the maid suddenly spoke again.","[......Well, I suppose it would be a bit pitiful to leave Cornelia-san like that, so I’ll lend her a little help.]","[ [ ! ? ! ? ] ]","Startled by the calm, almost teasing tone, both Eris and Marquis Hamilton turned toward the maid. The woman who had looked so flustered just moments ago now wore a composed smile.","[......Could it be...... Phantasmal King-sama?]","[Yeah. The seven people the Hamilton Marquisdom dispatched to that city should be making their reports within a few minutes.]","Speaking as though they were discussing the weather, Alice, who knew the exact number of agents they had sent, made both Eris and Marquis Hamilton break out in a cold sweat.","[Well, in any case, I’ll keep the spread of rumors suppressed for the next two days or so. Use that time wisely to discuss your countermeasures.]","[Understood. We are deeply grateful for your benevolence, Phantasmal King-sama...... Umm...... Phantasmal King-sama? Why are you looking at me with such pity in your eyes?]","[......Don’t worry. When your turn comes soon, I’ll make sure to help you as well.]","[Why do such gentle words sound so terrifying......?]","Alice, who had seemed like nothing more than a projection, gave Eris one last pitying glance before vanishing. Sadly, Eris had an inkling of what that meant...... After all, she herself had already made a promise...... A promise to visit Kaito’s home...... and she had also accepted his invitation to the tea party he planned to host himself.","As a vague but undeniable sense of dread welled up within her, Eris quietly pressed a hand against her stomach.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Come to think of it, Eris already got a confirmed invitation straight from Kaito himself to the tea party that Shiro’s attending, didn’t she......]"]},{"number":2392,"title":"Chapter 2392: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 21","paragraphs":["We entered the concert hall and moved to our assigned seats. As expected of such good seats, the stage was clearly visible from where we sat.","The seating order was Eingana-san, Frea-san, Magnawell-san, Megiddo-san, me, and Cornelia-san, so Cornelia-san had at least some peace of mind to relax...... I hope.","No, it was clear through Sympathy Magic that Cornelia-san was mentally exhausted from nervousness and embarrassment, but this time, handling it was surprisingly difficult.","If there had only been one other person, I could have carried the conversation myself, but with four people around, it was unavoidable that someone I wasn’t speaking with would address Cornelia-san. It was also natural for them to be curious about Cornelia-san, who hadn’t attended the ship party or the birthday party.","That said, with Megiddo-san present, avoiding any awkward encounters was...... well, impossible. In fact, it was probably better that we encountered each other before entering the concert hall. Had it happened after we took our seats, it might have drawn a lot of attention with loud voices.","Fortunately, or perhaps thanks to her straightforward personality, Megiddo-san probably wouldn’t insist on extending the conversation elsewhere after the performance.","I figured that once we listened to the music together in the hall and achieved our purpose, we’d part ways.","[Considering the size of this hall, I guess it’s kind of like an orchestra, right?]","[No, the Allegra Symphony is a bit unique. Their composition is more like a wind ensemble.]","[......I don’t really know the difference between an orchestra and a wind ensemble though......]","[It’s actually quite simple. It’s whether string instruments are included. A wind ensemble is made up of woodwinds, brass, and percussion; with no string instruments included. Sometimes a double bass is added, but that’s about it. Orchestras, on the other hand, include string instruments like violins and cellos. If violins are included, it’s an orchestra; if not, it’s a wind ensemble. That’s an easy way to remember.]","[Hehh, I see......]","Megiddo-san explained my question clearly. As expected from someone knowledgeable in the arts, her explanation was easy to understand, and in her current young girl form, there was no oddness in how she spoke.","Appearance really matters. In her usual massive Demon Beast form or muscular humanoid form, talking about art would seem strange, but in her current form as a quiet, mysterious beauty, she actually looked quite fitting...... Well, Megiddo-san's still the same with the way she speaks, of course......","[The Allegra Symphony is structured as a wind ensemble, performing bright and poppy pieces. Unlike mainstream classical performances, this ensemble plays joyfully and cheerfully, making their performances quite interesting.]","[Hehh, that sounds exciting. Megiddo-san, you know a lot about music, so do you have concert halls in your city too?]","[Yeah, got a pretty big one over there. And speaking of music, you know that otherworld singing contest back at the Harmonic Symphony? We even recently built a dedicated facility for that.]","[......R- Right, I remember you really liked that.]","I’d heard about it briefly, but it seems they really did build a facility for singing competitions. Well, even though part of me doesn’t want to recognize it as a proper singing contest, watching it is actually quite entertaining. The sight of them singing while fighting is flashy and visually impressive, so it seems likely to gain popularity.","Maybe eventually, like RINGTOSS, dedicated facilities could pop up all over the place.","When my conversation with Megiddo-san reached a lull, I leaned slightly and spoke in a low voice to Cornelia-san, who was sitting across from me.","[......Cornelia-san, are you alright?]","[Y- Yes. Though it’s embarrassing, I’ve been faced with people I normally wouldn’t have the chance to speak to, so I feel a bit uneasy, but I too am a young lady of a noble family...... I have experience speaking with people of higher status than myself. I’m a little tired, but I’m alright.]","[That would be great...... I think, knowing Megiddo-san’s personality, once we listen to the performance in the concert hall, we’ll probably just part ways normally afterward.]","Hmmm, her expression is composed, as expected of someone accustomed to aristocratic manners...... but the fatigue I sense through Sympathy Magic is significant.","Part of the reason it turned out this way is probably because of me, so if there’s any way to help her relax...... Ah, that’s right. We’re returning to the Imperial Capital of Archlesia Empire afterward, so going to Nifty there might be a good idea.","Eating something sweet is good when you’re tired, and some teas, like MK Blend with a small amount of leaves from Nebula’s World Tree, have relaxing effects...... Come to think of it, I recall Nebula mentioning that the tea leaves specially made for royal milk tea were going to be improved and sold commercially.","For now, I’ll plan to invite her to the café at Nifty later.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [How strange. Kaito is undoubtedly acting with complete goodwill, genuinely worried about Cornelia and trying to be considerate, and I can even sense his intention to help her relax, given she's mentally exhausted...... So why does it still feel like he’s \"here to punch her stomach some more\"......]"]},{"number":2393,"title":"Chapter 2393: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 22","paragraphs":["The performance of Allegra Symphony, indeed, it was really impressive. I’m not particularly knowledgeable about music, so I couldn’t really tell how it was superior compared to others, but the powerful performance by so many people, combined with the poppy, enjoyable rhythm, made me feel happy just by listening.","It was somewhere between a classical concert and a pop music live show, an enjoyable performance that made me want to hear it again.","[That was a fun and good performance, wasn’t it?]","[Yeah, though there are still some rough parts in the performance, I like how they’re trying different things to entertain the audience. Looks like they’ll continue improving, so I’m looking forward to that...... By the way, Kaito, what are you lot planning to do after this?]","[Well, we’ve more or less accomplished our goals in this city, so I think it’s about time to head back. How about Megiddo-san and the others?]","[Looks like Magnawell is interested in sightseeing. I thought we’d look around a bit more, maybe grab a meal before heading back...... Magnawell, is that fine with you?]","Personally, I was planning to invite Cornelia-san to the Nifty store afterward, but we hadn’t discussed any specific plans.","I also wanted to do a bit more sightseeing in this trade city I haven’t fully explored yet, but since Cornelia-san seems mentally fatigued, that would have to wait for another time. Even now, when I mentioned heading back, her expression didn’t show it, but her emotions transmitted through Sympathy Magic had shifted to relief, so I can tell she is indeed mentally tired.","[Umu, no problem. A place with alcohol would be good...... though I also like the snacks that go with alcohol. It’s interesting that there are so many varieties.]","[Snacks, huh. There aren’t many in this city, so we won’t go today...... But the snacks at the place run by Kaito’s woman, Kaori, were pretty good too.]","[......Hou, that’s interesting.]","Somehow, it feels like a strange situation where tragedy might befall Kaori-san is forming. If Magnawell-san comes to visit her...... wait, does Kaori-san even know about Magnawell-san’s clone body? If not, she might just think an old gentleman showed up...... Ah, but if she finds out later, it would be rough for her......","[Magnawell-san, when you go to Kaori-san’s restaurant, please contact me first. They have business hours and such.]","[Ohh, I see...... then when I visit, I’ll contact Miyama Kaito.]","Since it seemed difficult to prevent the visit entirely, I decided to go along to provide support, like the method we used when Megiddo-san came to her restaurant. Even a little, I hope I can help Kaori-san mentally......","[Frea-san and Eingana-san, thank you for today as well.]","[No, it was enjoyable for me too, being able to talk with my comrade. Thank you.]","[I’ll be looking forward to the evaluation of those brushes along with Magnawell-sama and Nidzveld. With my size, I won’t be ordering for myself, but many of my subordinates care about beauty......]","Indeed, the members of Eingana-san’s Ocean Scales did seem to have beautiful scales when I saw them at the Dragon Carnival, and perhaps many of them also pay attention to their appearance.","Chatting lightly like that, I parted ways with Megiddo-san, Magnawell-san, Frea-san, and Eingana-san. Cornelia-san and I then moved to the carriage under Anne-san’s guidance.","The natural flow would have been to head straight to the teleportation gate and disperse, but I decided to invite Cornelia-san to Nifty first.","[Cornelia-san, if you have some time, would you like to return to the Imperial Capital and visit the Nifty store? After everything that’s happened, maybe we could have some sweets and take a short break?]","[That’s a very tempting invitation, but Nifty’s café requires reservations...... Ahh, do they have something like an owner’s seat?]","[Yes, there’s that kind of dedicated seat.]","[I see. In that case, I’d be glad to join you. There are still many sweets at Nifty’s café that I haven’t tried personally......]","Cornelia-san apparently uses Nifty frequently in her daily life, as she had mentioned during the tea gathering. She seems to have become a fan, visiting the café several times with reservations, which makes me happy as well.","Perhaps because we were going to one of her favorite stores, I sensed through Sympathy Magic that her excitement had risen slightly, so inviting her was definitely the right choice.","Just like that, we could then arrived near the teleportation gate, but it would be faster to use my Teleportation Magic Tool to reach Nifty’s store. After telling Anne-san that I had invited Cornelia-san, she contacted the guards and servants waiting at the Sharon County’s estate in the Imperial Capital and instructed them to head to Nifty’s store.","Since Anne-san had tasks such as returning the carriage, we parted ways there. After receiving confirmation that the move was complete, Cornelia-san and I used the teleportation device to arrive in front of Nifty’s store.","[Oya? Miyama-dono?]","[Arehh? If it isn't Kaito! Yahho~~]","Somehow, just as we arrived in front of Nifty’s store via teleportation, Sechs-san and Tre-san came out from the store...... and well...... What a remarkable coincidence, it was.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Why?! Why can’t you give the same kind of support you show Kaori to the other Stomachache Warriors too?!]","? ? ? : [Hmmm...... I think it’s probably because Kaori-san clearly shows in her behavior that \"she’s suffering from stomachaches\". The others can hide it to some extent, and they try to stay calm......]","Serious-senpai : [......Now that you mentioned it, you also try to be considerate and even contact in advance people like Lilia, who clearly show they’re suffering from stomachaches...... So maybe showing it outwardly is actually the right move......]"]},{"number":2394,"title":"Chapter 2394: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 23","paragraphs":["Tre-san and Sechs-san came out of Nifty’s store together, a rare combination in itself, but to my surprise, four more people followed behind them.","[Cento-san and Cien-san...... and even Nove-san and Tetra-san? I’m surprised to see you all here, but this lineup is unusual too...... Ah, wait, could it be......]","[Well, if it isn’t Kaito! What are the odds of meeting you here? What’s that phrase again? A bolt from the blue, right?]","[......It’s his shop, so it’s not that strange. Just call it a coincidence.]","Nove-san and Tetra-san were both part of Kuro’s family, and both were Count-rank Demons. The two of them had fought on Neun-san’s side during the incident with Dr. Vier, and after they offered their apologies and such, we ended up on friendly terms.","The tall, bright woman with short red hair was Nove-san. You wouldn’t be able to tell from her usual appearance, but she was apparently a Harpy. Her hands were shaped like wings, but since that made daily life inconvenient, she normally kept them in a more human form.","The small, quiet woman wearing a bucket hat pulled low over her golden-blonde hair was Tetra-san. I’d heard she belonged to a very rare race capable of producing precious metals from their own bodies.","Well, both of them held important positions, Nove-san was the Special Advisor in the HR Department of the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company, while Tetra-san was the Special Advisor in the Accounting Department. So, looking closely, it seemed like most of Sedditch’s Special Advisors were gathered here...... though one person from the sales department was missing.","[Judging from the lineup, this seems related to the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company...... Is Trois-san not with you?]","[Ahh, my husband didn’t come this time. The Sales Department isn’t involved in this matter. In the first place, our original schedule’s already finished, and since we came all the way to the Imperial Capital, we just thought we might as well drop by Kaito’s store. The café part’s reservation-only, but the shop itself’s open to walk-ins right now.]","There was one more Special Advisor from the Sales Department, Trois-san, Nove-san’s husband, a man with an intelligent air. Together with him, the five of them made up the Special Advisors of the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company.","At that moment, Tre-san spoke up with a bright smile.","[The reason we’re here was, well, Kaito probably already knows this, but it’s about the project Kuromu-sama is advancing to develop magic tool technology in the Human Realm. I mentioned it briefly during the ship party, but we’ve purchased the magic crystal mines in Archlesia Empire, and we’re planning to set up manufacturing bases in the Human Realm. That’s why we’ve brought along people from the Personnel and Accounting Departments. The existing branches will handle distribution, so the Sales Department isn’t involved this time, hence why Trois didn’t come.]","[......You sure do spill company details easily, Tre.]","[Come on, it’s fine if it’s Kaito, right?]","[......Unn, he’s fine. Still, even if I know he won’t, he just feels like the type who might let something slip elsewhere, and that makes me uneasy.]","As Tre-san gave a detailed explanation, Tetra-san let out a slightly exasperated comment. Well, Tre-san was serious about work, so she wouldn’t actually say anything that truly shouldn’t be said, but I could understand that uneasy feeling all the same.","[By the way, Miyama-dono, that young lady with you...... is she not the young lady of the Sharon County?]","[Eh? Ah, yes, she came along with me...... Wait, you know her?]","[Ah no, not personally. I often attend events as Kuromu-sama’s representative, so I’ve simply memorized the names and faces of Human Realm’s noble families' heads and their relatives.]","He said it as if it were the most natural thing in the world, but honestly, being able to memorize the names and faces of every noble family head and their relatives was incredible. As expected of someone called the Great Sage of the Dead.","[Well then, it seems Sechs-san already knows her, but let me introduce her anyway. This is my friend, Cornelia Sharon-san.]","[Ohh, Sharon County...... that means she's from the Sharon Company, right?]","I turned toward Cornelia-san as I introduced her...... only to find her eyes rolled back white!?","[C- Cornelia-san? Are you alright?]","[Hah!? Ah, y- y- y- yes, I’m fine. I just froze up for a moment in surprise. It’s a pleasure to meet you. I am Cornelia Sharon, eldest daughter of the Sharon County. The Sharon Company is always indebted to Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company for your continued cooperation.]","At my call, Cornelia-san quickly recovered, giving a graceful bow as she introduced herself. As I watched her, ready to step in and help if needed...... I suddenly felt a tug at my sleeve. When I turned, Tetra-san was beckoning me slightly. I leaned down, and she brought her lips close to my ear, whispering softly.","[......You on a date? I’m so jealous. You turn down my invitations, yet here you are......]","[......No, I don’t recall ever being invited by you though?]","[......I just felt like saying it. But if I did invite you, would you stay with me until dawn for a drink?]","[If we part ways that same day, I’ll keep you company.]","[......How cold. But that part of you is cute too.]","[I really can never tell how serious you are, Tetra-san.]","[......Fufufu.]","Tetra-san was a quiet, composed woman, but every now and then she’d tease me in these strange ways...... Seemingly enjoying my reactions, she’d say things that made it impossible to tell whether she was joking or serious.","And most likely, what she just said had nothing to do with the main topic.","[So, what brings you here today?]","[......Do you plan to continue your connections with that young lady?]","[Eh? Uh, yes, I suppose so. What of it?]","[......No reason in particular. Just something I should keep in mind as an accountant. It’s important information for future dealings with the Sharon Company after all.]","[H- Huh...... I don’t really get it, but yes, I do hope to stay on good terms with Cornelia-san.]","[......Unn, that’s helpful to know, thank you. You really are always so stimulating...... I love you.]","(T/N: Not sure if that last part is \"I love you\" or \"I love it (his reactions)\". As Kaito said, she was vague with her words.)","Apparently satisfied with my answer, Tetra-san lifted the brim of her bucket hat with a finger, revealing her usually hidden silver eyes, and with a sharp wink, she pulled away.","<Afterword>","<Nove>","The Special Advisor in the HR Department of the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company, Nove is a bright and lively woman. She's a Harpy and a Count-rank Demon.","She's straightforward and genuinely kind. Her name comes from the Italian number nine.","<Tetra>","The Special Advisor in the Accounting Department of the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company. Tetra is a being evolved from a rare creature called a Gold Beast, which, like Neun, was reincarnated into a different species and became a Demon. She's quiet and usually cool, but with someone she takes a liking to, she enjoys teasing them, occasionally doing so with Kaito. Her name comes from the Greek number four.","<Trois>","The Special Advisor in the Sales Department of the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company and Nove’s husband. He's an intellectual male High Treant. The High Treant-related products Kaito uses for Bell and Lynn’s shampoo are gifts from Trois.","His name comes from the French number three."]},{"number":2395,"title":"Chapter 2395: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 24","paragraphs":["The Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company was one of the Five Great Trading Companies, in fact, it was the largest in the world. To elaborate further, while organizations like the Lord Trading Company were general trading companies, the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company dealt exclusively in magic tools, and yet it stood unrivaled at the pinnacle of all commercial enterprises. Their wealth and influence were in a league of their own.","In truth, when it came to the field of magic tools, Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company’s power and dominance were so overwhelming that it could be described as an absolute monopoly.","Even the Sharon Trading Company, run by the Sharon Count family, was considered quite large by Human standards, yet the difference in scale was so vast that it couldn’t even be called a rival.","However, Kuromueina, the founder of the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company and its honorary president, effectively its true leader, did not approve of a monopoly. She believed that progress could only come from competition, and so she generously supported other magic tool companies.","In terms of patented technologies related to magic tool creation, those with broad applicability were made public either free of charge or with very low licensing fees. She even provided educational curriculums for training magic tool engineers, and, when necessary, offered advice on business management as well.","As a result, even setting aside scale and wealth, many trading companies owed Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company great debts of gratitude, and were in no position to oppose them. The Sharon Trading Company had also received their aid countless times before. Thus, for Cornelia, this was an entity to whom she could never afford to show the slightest disrespect.","(I- I have to endure it somehow. My consciousness feels like it’s about to slip away...... T- The Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company...... and f- four of their Special Advisors are here...... I must stay strong. If I displease even one of them, the Sharon Trading Company could vanish overnight!)","The Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company, the largest trading company in the world, was overseen not only by a General Representative, but also by five Special Advisors personally appointed by Kuromueina herself, each presiding over a specific department.","These Special Advisors possessed authority surpassing even that of the Company President and wielded tremendous influence not only within the magic tools industry but across the entire economic world.","The Special Advisor of the prestigious Magic Tool Development Division, effectively the one who held the final say across numerous fields, was the one known as the \"Great Sage of the Dead\", Sechs.","The one responsible for ensuring a steady supply of what should be a rare commodity, high-purity magic crystals, and who was said to have no equal in that field, the Special Advisor of the Magic Crystal Division, \"Magic Crystal Ruler\" Tre.","With vast connections spanning the economic and social elite, from nobles to commoners alike, and the uncanny ability to instantly discern a person’s talents and assign them to their ideal position, serving as the Special Advisor of the Human Resources Division, the \"Virtuoso of Talent\" Nove.","The Special Advisor of the Accounting Department of the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company, the very cornerstone of its overwhelming financial operations, said to be capable of moving funds on the scale of a national budget with a single word, the \"Conqueror of Gold Veins\", Tetra.","And lastly, invincible and undefeated in the art of negotiation, who effortlessly secured massive contracts time and again on the front lines of magic tool sales, the Special Advisor of the Sales Division, the \"Monster of Verbal Warfare\", Trois.","Each of these individuals was a figure of such renown that anyone even remotely involved in commerce would know their names. To have four of these Special Advisors gathered in one place was an astonishing occurrence indeed.","And as Cornelia trembled in tense silence, those sharp-minded elites were quietly assessing her worth.","(Kaito’s friend huh. From a glance, her abilities as a noble seem average. Her clothes suggest she’s strong in areas like fashion or the arts, but not exceptionally so. That probably means her real strength lies in her personality. And since Kaito has an incredible eye for people, where even I’m surprised by how sharp he can be, if he values her, then there’s no harm in forming a friendly relationship.)","Nove, who oversaw the HR Division, held Kaito’s ability to judge people in extremely high regard. Because of that, she believed it would be wise to establish at least a decent relationship with anyone Kaito called a friend.","(......This will definitely have an impact. The movements of the Ritch Barony don’t really concern the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company, so I was planning to just watch from the sidelines, but this...... this involves another magic tool company. It’s bound to affect us. Strengthening ties with the Sharon Trading Company is absolutely essential.)","Tetra, on the other hand, was certain that the interaction between Kaito and Cornelia would bring about major growth for the Sharon Trading Company. Acting early, she believed, could turn that development into profit for the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company as well. She was already drafting a budget plan in her head, one that even included partial business collaborations with the Sharon Trading Company.","(Come to think about it, Kuromu-sama did mention meeting a girl from the Sharon Trading Company at a tea party. That must’ve been Cornelia-dono. Hmmm, if I recall, she wasn’t all that involved in managing the company, but with her having a connection with Miyama-dono now, then things will surely change drastically...... That said, Cornelia-dono would probably have a rough time though......)","Sechs, for his part, understood the situation clearly, including the growing stomachaches Cornelia's having, and couldn’t help but feel a little sympathy for her, knowing how busy she was about to become.","(Oh right, Kaito’s got a special reserved seat at Nifty, so he doesn’t even need to make a reservation, right? Kuromu-sama was raving about their baby castella, and I really want to try them too! I’ll have to ask him to take me there sometime!)","Meanwhile, as usual, Tre was thinking about something entirely unrelated...... but honestly, for Cornelia, that kind of reaction was probably the most comforting of them all.","Unfortunately, with Nove and Tetra already preparing to take action, even Tre’s carefree attitude wouldn’t do much to ease the stomachache Cornelia was destined to suffer.","<Afterword>","Nove (the sharp one) : [We should build a good relationship.]","Tetra (the sharp one) : [We must strengthen our ties with the Sharon Trading Company.]","Sechs (the sharp one) : [With Miyama-dono’s influence, Cornelia-dono’s going to have a tough time ahead.]","Tre (the usual Onee-chan) : [More importantly, I wanna eat baby castella.]","Serious-senpai : [......In a way, for the Stomachache Warriors, the safest one to deal with, despite her high position, might actually be Tre. She also got along easily with Aoi and Hina, and even worked smoothly with Razelia when helping Ann......]"]},{"number":2396,"title":"Chapter 2396: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 25","paragraphs":["After both Nove and Tetra had determined that Cornelia was an important person and were about to act according to their respective intentions, someone suddenly forced herself between the two of them and Cornelia.","That someone was Tre. With her usual bright smile, Tre reached out her hand for a friendly handshake as she spoke.","[I’m Tre. Since we’re both friends of Kaito, let’s get along, okay?!]","[Y- Yes, pleased to meet you, Tre-sama.]","[Oh, you don’t need to use those \"-sama\" honorifics! Let’s keep things casual! You can even call me \"Tre Onee-chan\", you know? Ah, and can I also call you Cornelia?]","[Ah, y- yes, of course. Errr...... Tre-san.]","[Unn, unn!]","Though Cornelia seemed a bit bewildered, Tre’s natural cheerfulness quickly closed the distance between them...... Watching this, Nove and Tetra, who had been slightly surprised, soon wore expressions of realization. Nove scratched her head, while Tetra gave a wry smile and shrugged her shoulders.","Though the two of them were highly capable special advisors, they were first and foremost members of Kuromueina’s family. Perhaps because of Kuromueina’s excellent leadership, they were not only intelligent but also people of good character. Seeing Tre cutting in, they seemed to reflect upon something.","(Ah...... yeah, this is one of those moments we’ll have to reflect on. Tre Onee-chan’s right, we just happened to meet a friend of Kaito’s. Judging her based on her noble status or as a potential business contact is the wrong approach. She’s clearly feeling tense, it must be scary for her~~)","Realizing that she had been interacting with Cornelia while wearing her \"Special Advisor of the HR Department\" face, Nove felt a pang of guilt. Determined to follow Tre’s example, she put on an equally bright smile and spoke to Cornelia.","[Alright then, I’ll go next after Tre Onee-chan. I’m Nove...... I know we all have our own positions and titles, but this isn’t a business meeting or a formal party, so let’s just relax and enjoy ourselves!]","[Ah, y- yes. It’s a pleasure to meet you.]","Nove’s statement that they should forget their social standings for now was meant to reassure Cornelia that her words and behavior here wouldn’t affect her relationship with Sharon County or the Sharon Trading Company. Understanding her intent, Cornelia visibly relaxed, relief softening her expression.","(......That was hasty of me. Even if I want to strengthen ties with the Sharon Trading Company, the proper way is to make a formal request to the Count’s household. Treating someone I met by chance as a point of negotiation isn’t sincere. I owe this one to Tre.)","Like Nove, Tetra also used the brief pause Tre had created to correct her slightly skewed line of thought. Once Nove finished speaking, Tetra offered a gentle smile and addressed Cornelia.","[......I’m Tetra. Same as the other two, let’s just treat this as a chance meeting between people who share a mutual friend.]","[Y- Yes, likewise, it’s a pleasure to meet you.]","Tetra, too, seemed intent on treating this meeting purely as a casual encounter between individuals who happened to share a mutual friend, Kaito. With the reassurance that nothing she said here would put the Sharon Trading Company in a difficult position, Cornelia finally let out a small sigh, her shoulders relaxing slightly as she returned the greeting in a more natural, unguarded manner.","(Good gracious, that was splendid. As expected of Tre-dono. She probably didn’t plan things to turn out that way, but by stepping in at just the right moment, she managed to throw Nove-dono and Tetra-dono off balance, forcing them to pause and rethink their approach.)","Looking impressed by how Tre had cut in at the perfect timing just as Nove and Tetra were about to act, Sechs also stepped forward to offer his greeting.","[Then I too shall greet you as just another Lich who are mutual friends of Miyama-dono. Pleased to make your acquaintance.]","[Y- Yes, pleased to meet you as well.]","[Are Liches really something you find just anywhere though?]","[Sech Nii-chan, with that scary face of yours, I was worried Cornelia-chan might get frightened.]","Given that Sechs was both tall and a literal skeleton, he certainly gave off quite the intimidating presence, prompting Tre and Nove to lightly throw retorts as he said his greetings.","[Oya, I’ll have you know I’m considered quite the dandy gentleman......]","[......Sorry to say this, Sechs, but there aren’t any Undead around here.]","Watching Tetra poke fun at Sechs’s comment, Kaito couldn’t help but think \"Come to think of it, among the Undead, Sechs-san is supposed to be quite the handsome one, isn’t he?\" to himself, recalling a conversation he went to the night market with Illness.","After that, both Cento and Cien also exchanged brief greetings with Cornelia, and at that point, Kaito spoke up.","[Are you all heading home now, everyone?]","[Unn. I actually wanted to stop by Nifty’s café too, but you need a reservation to get in...... Glance! Glance!]","[......That’s some intense hinting there. Also, are you seriously saying glance out loud? Errr, well, if I ask Canalis-san, I’m sure she can arrange a table. So, would you all like to drop by the café?]","[As expected of Kaito! Onee-chan has been waiting to hear those exact words!]","And so, the group from the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company decided to stop by Nifty’s café as well, while Cornelia, who had just managed to recover her composure a little, could only stare off into the distance once again, her expression faintly vacant.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Just when she thought she saved her from the stomachache, she ended up plunging her into more stomachache!? You really can't tell if Tre's friend or foe, Tre......]","? ? ? : [Well, if I had to guess, I don't think Tre-san really thinks that deeply about it. Outside of work, she basically lives by the flow and momentum......]"]},{"number":2397,"title":"Chapter 2397: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 26","paragraphs":["How should I say this...... If I had to put it in one phrase, I’d say things had taken a strange turn. Running into Tre-san and the others by chance was one thing, but thanks to Tre-san’s relentless enthusiasm, we ended up arranging seats for everyone at the café as well.","Well, as far as the seats were concerned, asking Canalis-san would probably solve that without issue, but I couldn’t help feeling like, in trying to help Cornelia-san relax after her mental exhaustion, we were only making her even more tired......","While I was thinking about that, the scenery around us suddenly turned gray. It looked like one of those \"time-stop\" scenes you see in anime, but I’d experienced real time-stops before, and they hadn’t looked like this.","Then, right after that, Canalis-san appeared before us.","[Alright then, as requested, here comes the appearance of your friendly neighborhood God. For first-timers’ sake, I’ve adjusted the color scheme around and the like, and yes, the world’s time is currently paused. Tahaa~~ Sorry if my considerate gestures come off as a bit too God-like!]","[Hello, Canalis-san. Sorry for calling you so suddenly.]","[No no, if it’s a summons from Kaito-sama, I’ll come running no matter where I am in my own world. I’m a God Slave...... Slave God? A God who's your slave, a position I actually enjoy very much. So please, call for me anytime, and I’ll come wagging my tail! Tahaa~~ My apologies for the peculiar kink. Ah, yes, about the seats, you can leave that to me. I am a genuine God after all, so arranging something like seats is a quick flick of the wrist...... Naturally, I can also prepare multiple layout plans to choose from.]","As always, her face was expressionless, yet her tone lively as she raised a finger and began explaining the different plans.","[First, we have the Large Table Plan, a luxurious option using Spatial Expansion Magic, perfect for accommodating large groups comfortably. Next is the Divided Table Plan, just tell me how many people per table, and I can divide it up accordingly. There are also others, like the Galaxy Observation Plan, the Amazon River Crossing Plan, and the Great Buddha Multiplication Plan, but those don’t seem relevant this time, so I’ll skip the details.]","I couldn’t help but feel curious about those last three plans...... b- but, well, it seemed that we could either have everyone share one big table or split up into smaller ones as needed.","[......That’s how it is. What do you think?]","[Ahh~~ since we can split the tables, and I’d feel bad getting in the way of Kaito’s date, I think it’d be best to have one table for Kaito and Cornelia, and another for the six of us. I just came for the baby castellas anyway. Everyone fine with that?]","[It’s fine, though honestly, the café thing wasn’t even part of the plan, you just suddenly decided on it earlier, Tre Nee-chan......]","[......Typical of your shamelessness. Well, fine, Tre can decide.]","Tre-san’s suggestion was honestly a lifesaver. Cornelia-san had clearly been at her mental limit, and since the others seemed fine with it too, we decided to go ahead and split the seating arrangements.","[Then, Canalis-san, could you please set it up so that Cornelia-san and I have a table for two, and the others have their own table?]","[Understood. Once you enter the café, a staff member will guide you to your seats~~ Now then, the world’s time will resume momentarily...... See you soon!]","As Canalis-san vanished, the gray scenery around us returned to normal. When we entered the café again, just as she’d said, a staff member approached and guided each group to their respective tables.","At Nifty’s, the tables were arranged so that you couldn’t see or hear the other groups at all, it was practically a private space once you sat down. Because of that, Cornelia-san visibly relaxed, letting out a small breath of relief.","[Cornelia-san, I’m sorry. I invited you out to help you unwind, but it somehow turned into something weird.]","[Ah, not at all. It did surprise me, yes, but everyone was so kind and well-mannered. They even made it an informal meeting, separate from matters involving the Magic Tool Trading Company or our County, which I greatly appreciated. And though the encounter was quite shocking, the Seditch Magic Tool Trading Company does have many dealings with my family’s business, so strengthening that connection is actually a blessing.]","At least it seemed that running into Tre-san and the others hadn’t been a bad thing for her, that was a relief.","[Come to think of it, the person earlier was the one rumored to be Nifty’s overseer...... errr, the Creator God from another world, right?]","[You mean Canalis-san? Yes. She calls herself a \"former god\", but she’s essentially on the same level as Shiro-san.]","[I- I- I- I see......]","For a moment, I almost mentioned Eden-san, the one who once gave a greeting...... or more accurately, a warning, to every noble in existence, but considering how traumatized some nobles were by that, I decided to use Shiro-san as the safer point of comparison.","Well, aside from her perpetually blank expression, Canalis-san really is a good person, so there shouldn’t be any problems.","......Ah, I wonder if it’s okay to call out to her mentally? Canalis-san, Cornelia-san seems mentally worn out, so could you please bring us some relaxing tea?","(Understood. I’ll bring you a tea that’s especially effective for easing stomachache.)","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [It sounds like that God’s about to bring something every Stomachache Warrior in the world would want.]"]},{"number":2398,"title":"Chapter 2398: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 27","paragraphs":["Not long after we took our seats, Canalis-san came over to our table, probably thanks to the message I had sent earlier.","[Well then, thank you for waiting. Waitress God here. You can order whichever sweets you’d like, but first, here is the tea I prepared according to Kaito-sama’s request. Now, please, have a sip and see what you think.]","With practiced grace, Canalis-san poured the tea and set the cups in front of Cornelia-san and me. Cornelia-san, with her elegant manners, examined the color and aroma of the tea, her expression turning slightly curious.","[This is...... MK Blend, isn’t it?]","[Eh? You can tell just by the color and smell?]","[Ah, well, it’s not as though I can identify every kind of tea, but I quite like MK Blend and often drink it, so I’m familiar with it......]","Cornelia-san had mentioned that she shopped frequently at Nifty, but it seemed she also often drank MK Blend, the original blend I created myself.","It was a little embarrassing, but honestly, it made me happy to have my blend appreciated.","[Yes, exactly. It’s Kaito-sama’s MK Blend, but I’ve added a little of my God Power to it...... Let’s see, if I were to name it, maybe I’d call it MK Blend: Healing Special! Tahaa~~ Sorry for the unoriginal name!]","[Healing Special...... then, if you’ll excuse me...... T- This is...... The pain in my stomach...... it’s gone?]","Cornelia-san took a sip of the MK Blend HS and looked astonished. I took a sip too, but I couldn’t tell any difference from the usual MK Blend. Well, I’m not exactly sensitive to subtle flavor changes anyway......","[Yes, this MK Blend HS was adjusted at Kaito-sama’s request to help relieve Cornelia-san’s fatigue. From what I could see, Cornelia-san's stomachache seemed mainly caused by mental exhaustion, so it’s effective only against stomachache arising from mental stress.]","[So it’s kind of like Recovery Magic?]","[Ah, no, it’s more of a conceptual thing. I used my God Power to grant the MK Blend the effect of \"soothing only stomachache caused by mental stress\". It’s not that strong though. Hmmm...... for example, if stomachache levels range from 1 to 10, this MK Blend HS would heal about 5 levels’ worth. So level 1-5 pain would be completely cured, but anything above that would just be alleviated a bit. Tahaa~~ of course, it would be great if it could heal completely, but since it’s stress-related, any stronger effect would start interfering with the mind itself.]","[I see, so it only works on stomachaches caused by mental fatigue.]","[Exactly. It doesn’t work on illnesses or other kinds of stomachaches, and it has no other effects at all. It’s purely for relieving stress-induced stomachache. Any stronger, and it might even violate my contract with Shallow Vernal, so this is the limit. Tahaa~~ sorry, it kinda fails to live up to its HS name!]","No, I don’t think it fails to live up to its name at all. In other words, if it’s a moderate level of stomachache caused by stress, it disappears the moment you drink it, and even if it’s severe, it can still ease the pain to some extent.","Of course, it’s not like the mental stress itself goes away, so the pain might return after some time. But if drinking the tea lets you forget your stomach pain for a while, then it’s probably the best kind of break for when you’re exhausted.","As I was thinking that, Cornelia-san, who had been listening, clasped her hands together in a praying gesture and bowed her head toward Canalis-san.","[......P- Please, sell this to me.]","[......You look like someone who’s seen hell in a short span of time. You’ve had quite the day, haven’t you? Hmmm, the owner is Kaito-sama, so if he has no problem with it......]","[Errr, is it actually fine to distribute something like this?]","[For anyone not suffering from stress-related stomachache, it’s just a regular MK Blend. Since the effect is added using my own God Power, no one else can really make it, but for me, it’s no trouble at all. I just grab a can of MK Blend, go \"Ei!\", and it’s done.]","[Then, umm, could you please sell some to her...... Also, if possible, I’d like a can for myself too. It’d make me really happy if you could prepare one.]","After all, today alone Cornelia-san had run into Frea-san, Eingana-san, Megiddo-san, Magnawell-san, Tre-san, Sechs-san, Nove-san, Tetra-san, Cento-san, and Cien-san. That’s two of the Six Kings, one Duke-rank, six Count-ranks, and one other, so the mental fatigue she’s accumulated must be considerable.","Even if those encounters were mostly coincidental, part of it happened because she was with me. If this tea could help her even a little, I wanted her to have it.","And while I’m at it, I’ll take one myself and give it to Lilia-san...... Though honestly, I’m probably the biggest cause of her stomachaches on a daily basis. It feels kind of like I brought a solution to a problem I myself made, but if this can at least ease that pain a bit, then it’s worth giving her.","Besides, even if I don’t do anything, Lilia-san seems to attract stomachache-inducing situations to a degree that even Kuro and Alice get astounded...... Really, even a little, I just hope this helps her......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Shouldn’t that be distributed to all the other Stomachache Warriors too?]","? ? ? : [I think, probably, in Kaito-san’s mind, most of the others don’t really fall into the category of people suffering from stomachache. Kaori-san is someone he worries about getting stomachaches, but since she doesn’t really give off the image of someone who drinks tea, he unconsciously excluded her. As for Cornelia-san, once she reached her limit and could no longer keep up appearances, like Eris-san, Kaito-san started to genuinely worry about her mental fatigue. I think it was around the time she met Megiddo-san and Magnawell-san that she entered the group of people he tries to look out for......]","Serious-senpai : [So in the end, maybe enduring it like Eris is the wrong approach. Showing that you’re suffering from stomachache might actually be the key to gaining concessions from the Stomachache Devil.]"]},{"number":2399,"title":"Chapter 2399: Purchase of Exclusive Brush 28","paragraphs":["As Cornelia began to lose her composure and Kaito started to show concern for her mental state, their break at Nifty progressed peacefully.","They sipped tea said to help with stomachaches, enjoyed refined sweets, and chatted idly. After finishing their meal, they briefly reunited with Tre and the others for a quick greeting before parting ways, then Cornelia returned to the Sharon County estate.","(......It was only supposed to be a few hours, yet it feels as though I’ve been away for days. I have much to report, such as meeting the special advisors, but if I could, I would like nothing more than to rest right away. Truly, even though Eris-sama warned me to stay on guard, I can see now how naive my awareness still was.)","She was quite exhausted, and with many pending matters yet to handle, discussions with her parents were necessary. However, since Anne had likely already sent word ahead about what happened in the commercial city, it was probable that her parents and her older brother, the heir, had already begun discussions on how to respond.","Though her position in the family might shift somewhat after this, Cornelia was simply relieved that she had managed to get through the day. Just then, Anne, who had returned ahead of her, approached.","[Welcome home, Lady Cornelia.]","[I’ve just returned. Thank you for reporting ahead, Anne...... I’d really like to rest, but I suppose we should discuss a few things first.]","[Yes, Master is waiting for you...... but before that, there’s something you must check, Lady Cornelia......]","[Check? Me?]","Cornelia tilted her head curiously at Anne’s words. Within the Sharon County, Cornelia’s authority was limited, and there were few matters for which she had decision-making power.","With her father, the head of the household, and her brother already in talks, she couldn’t think of anything that would require her confirmation before joining them.","[......Just now, a messenger from Dragon King-sama brought this for you, Lady Cornelia......]","[......A disposable magic box and a letter?]","What Anne handed her was a disposable magic box made of enchanted paper, like those used for random boxes, and a single letter. Cornelia accepted them and first unfolded the letter.","Inside was a message from Magnawell: \"Today’s exchange, including that with my subordinates, was quite meaningful. As a token of appreciation, I grant you a small reward. Use it as you see fit.\"","[I see, it seems Magnawell-sama wishes to gift me some kind of valuables as a memento of today’s meeting.]","[That’s a great honor. To receive a gift from Dragon King-sama himself, your reputation will surely rise, Lady Cornelia.]","[Indeed. We’ll have to think of an appropriate return gift, but truly, this is most generous.]","In noble society, it was common to exchange gifts under the pretense of \"commemorating a meeting\", and Cornelia had given and received such tokens many times before.","Assuming this was a similar gesture, and since she happened to be standing in the wide foyer near the entrance hall, she decided to open the disposable magic box and inspect its contents...... and in the next instant, an enormous fragment of a scale, several meters long, appeared before Cornelia and Anne.","[......................]","[......................]","Both Cornelia and Anne froze in silence, wearing the very picture of speechlessness as they stared at the massive scale. Its dazzling brilliance was one thing, but more than that, the overwhelming magic power emanating from it made its identity all too clear.","[......Ah...... A- A- Anne...... u- u- u- umm, w- what is this......?]","[......I- I believe it's a fragment of Dragon King-sama’s scale......]","To Magnawell, this was something no different from what he would casually hand to Kaito...... sent off with the same nonchalance as giving pocket money. However, the value of Magnawell’s scales was nothing short of extraordinary. After all, unless he deliberately shed them himself, his scales would never naturally molt or fall off, not unless he fought an opponent of Six Kings caliber.","In other words, aside from receiving one directly from Magnawell, there was virtually no other way to obtain such a thing. Its worth was easily on the level of building an entire castle......","Upon realizing this, Cornelia’s legs gave out and she dropped onto the floor, her face twitching.","[......A fragment of D- Dragon King-sama’s scale...... ababa...... N- No...... No more...... I just can’t handle this...... ahhyuu......]","[Lady Cornelia!? Please, compose yourself!!!]","She had just thought her exhausting duties as guide were finally over, that even if there were still matters left to address, at least nothing more shocking would happen today. And yet, here came this, an impact so tremendous it defied comprehension.","Already exhausted beyond her limits, Cornelia simply couldn’t withstand the shock. Her capacity long exceeded, her eyes rolled back, and she fainted dead away.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [The moment you let your guard down again, just like I said..... I’ve been waiting for this!!! This exact moment!!!]","≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣【K.O.】≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣≣","? ? ? : [......Well, even if you’re in a position where people worry about your stomachaches, that doesn’t mean you can avoid them. If it could be avoided that easily, Lilia-san wouldn’t have ended up like that......]","Serious-senpai : [The Stomachache Devil is way too terrifying.]"]},{"number":2400,"title":"Chapter 2400: Spreading Aftermath 1","paragraphs":["The day after I went to the trade city with Cornelia to order exclusive brushes, I received a message from Akane-san saying \"There’s something I want to ask, and I want to meet as soon as possible, so please make some time\", and I waited for her at the place she specified.","[......And why choose my shop as the meeting place then? Well, I mean, during hours when the shop isn’t open, I’m just doing prep work, so I have plenty of free time anyway.]","[Kaori-san, sorry for the sudden visit.]","[No, it’s fine. Akane-san also asked if she could use the shop, so it’s not a problem.]","Yes, the place Akane-san had specified was Kaori-san’s restaurant, Suiren, and it seemed Kaori-san had been informed in advance. As soon as we arrived, she let us inside.","[Kaori-san, are you prepping right now?]","[Ah, no, I’m just making a simple dish with leftover ingredients...... Kaito-kun, do you want some? It’s just chicken skin grilled so it doesn’t get too tough, sliced thinly and tossed with sliced onions and ponzu, really simple.]","[That sounds delicious, thank you.]","[Chicken skin tends to be leftover quite often~~]","I ate the dish that Kaori-san had placed into a small container and served to me, smiling. The tang of the ponzu matched the flavor of the chicken skin, and the texture of the sliced onions was nice, it was delicious.","[Simple, but really tasty. Maybe you could even add it to the menu?]","[This is totally a drinking snack kind of dish, so it doesn’t really fit with a set meal place. It’s easy and tasty for personal eating though...... hmm, maybe a sprinkle of shichimi would improve it.]","While Kaori-san was thinking about improvements after taking a bite of her own portion, someone knocked at the back door.","[Oh, that must be Akane-san. Heeeeeey~~ Welcome, Akane-san.]","[Sorry for intruding and borrowing your place all of a sudden. Ah, and here, a little souvenir as a token for your trouble.]","[Oh, a fancy-looking manju that seems delicious. Thanks~~]","I received the souvenir from Akane-san, who entered through the back door, and guided her to the seat next to me.","[Sorry for calling you out suddenly, Kaito.]","[Hello, Akane-san. I didn’t have any particular plans, so it’s fine...... Is Frau-san not with you today?]","[Ah, Frau was here until just now, but she said since she doesn’t need to guard me at Kaori’s restaurant, she’s going sightseeing and told me to contact her when we’re done, so she went off to tour.]","I realized why I couldn’t see Frau-san, who’s usually around, she had gone sightseeing for such a reason very typical of Frau-san.","Thereupon, Kaori-san then placed a teacup in front of Akane-san with tea and asked with a curious expression.","[Why is it that when it’s my restaurant, no guard is needed......? Here, Akane-san, tea.]","[Thanks...... Why? Well, it’s probably because of that last mock battle, right? Kaori totally beat up Frau, so I guess you feel there’s no problem since Kaori’s stronger than me.]","[I think that’s just a matter of matchup. Frau-san is a close-range type, and I have the advantage of shooting magic from mid-range.]","It seems Kaori-san is genuinely very strong. From what I saw during the Maid Olympia, Frau should also be pretty strong, but judging from Akane-san and Kaori-san’s conversation, Kaori-san must have completely dominated in the mock battle. Kuro said she was by far the strongest among the immigrants, so her strength might even be on the level of Luna-san or Sieg-san.","After some light, trivial chatter, I took the opportunity to ask Akane-san.","[......So, Akane-san, what’s up today? You said there was something you wanted to ask......]","[Ah, right, let’s get to the main point......]","After hearing my words, Akane-san took a sip of tea, then looked at me with a serious...... well, slightly angry expression.","[Lately, the merchant activity in Archlesia Empire has been unusually hectic. I even heard rumors that the Lord Trading Company, one of the five major trading companies, has started moving.]","[E- Errr......]","[It's you, right? It has to be you, there’s no one else it could be. Seriously, you need to get your act together. You keep causing strange things here and there, are you some kind of walking bomb or what?!]","What on earth...... I hadn’t even responded yet, and I was already being scolded as the culprit. But, hmmm...... well, honestly, I do have a few ideas about what she’s referring to, so it’s hard to call it completely unreasonable......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [What we should pay attention to here is, for some reason, Stomachache Warrior Kaori is also present for this talk, and the recent matter of Magnawell taking an interest in Kaori’s restaurant, which involves a stomachache factor.]"]}]);
